None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ac7af04-fb4b-52e4-8ecb-6830392d0573', 'word_count': 1312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ac7af04-fb4b-52e4-8ecb-6830392d0573'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Russia enjoys a victory in Galicia in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/01/1914-russian-army-scores-victory/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Russia enjoys a victory in Galicia in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every particle of evidence available indicates that Russia, in addition to the victories she has won over the Germans in Eastern Prussia, has inflicted a staggering defeat on the Austrian armies in Galicia. The Austrian right wing was turned and cut to pieces. The Russians took 30,000 prisoners. Along the Vistula, where the Russians attacked the Austrian left wing, fortune fluctuated for a little time, until the arrival of a strong body of reinforcements enabled the Russians to make an offensive movement of overwhelming effect and to drive back the enemy and capture a great number of cannon.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 2, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-oldsept02-russia/02iht-oldsept02-russia-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 268, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-oldsept02-russia/02iht-oldsept02-russia-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 268}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-oldsept02-russia/02iht-oldsept02-russia-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 961, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 