om/2014/09/01/ants/', 'snippet': 'From Google’s Peter Norvig: a puzzle about colliding ants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first of our challenges this week came out of a recent conversation I had with Peter Norvig, director of research at Google. (Are you on fire to learn programming? Check out Dr. Norvig’s Teach Yourself Programming in Ten Years.) This simple puzzle has plenty of room for exploration, so let’s jump in. It’s time for —', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ants on a Triangle', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norvig, Peter', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-01T16:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/547af4d8-c764-5080-8b2d-9aa9fcf62dca', 'word_count': 1579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/547af4d8-c764-5080-8b2d-9aa9fcf62dca'}, {'abstract': 'A man, 67, was killed and his wife was seriously wounded during a robbery Sunday night; the police said they had a suspect in custody.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/nyregion/staten-island-man-fatally-stabbed-during-home-invasion.html', 'snippet': 'A man, 67, was killed and his wife was seriously wounded during a robbery Sunday night; the police said they had a suspect in custody.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man was charged on Monday with killing a man and seriously injuring his wife in a home invasion on Sunday night on Staten Island, the police said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man, 20, Is Charged With Fatal Stabbing in S. I. Home Invasion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man, 20, Is Charged With Fatal Stabbing in S. I. Home Invasion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Viggiano, Dante', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gialluisi, Peter (1947-2014)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-01T16:03:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adf8c4ed-bc1b-5ded-be61-38568952668c', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adf8c4ed-bc1b-5ded-be61-38568952668c'}, {'abstract': 'An eggplant Parmesan of sorts on a bed of Israeli couscous is a good way to use the fresh tomato sauce you’ve made over the summer, though canned tomatoes will work, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/01/health/israeli-couscous-eggplant-and-tomato-gratin.html', 'snippet': 'An eggplant Parmesan of sorts on a bed of Israeli couscous is a good way to use the fresh tomato sauce you’ve made over the summer, though canned tomatoes will work, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is an eggplant Parmesan of sorts on top of a bed of Israeli couscous. If you’ve made fresh tomato sauce over the summer or you’re still finding wonderful tomatoes at the farmers’ market, use fresh tomato sauce; otherwise, use canned tomatoes for your marinara sauce. You can substitute cooked grains for the Israeli couscous; if you don’t tolerate gluten, try the recipe using cooked brown rice. I like to use Japanese or baby Italian eggplants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/02/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/01recipehealth/01recipehealth-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israeli Couscous, Eggplant and Tomato Gratin', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couscous', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-01T16:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/64aed03d-5fd5-5c8e-b076-239d078a5ff1', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64aed03d-5fd5-5c8e-b076-239d078a5ff1'}, {'abstract': 'A simple, quick dish with few ingredients and lots of flavors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/01/health/israeli-couscous-with-sauteed-cherry-tomatoes-and-basil.html', 'snippet': 'A simple, quick dish with few ingredients and lots of flavors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a simple dish with few ingredients and lots of flavor. The sauce, inspired by Melissa Clark’s Pasta with Burst Cherry Tomatoes, is incredibly sweet and wraps itself around each nugget of couscous deliciously. Cherry tomatoes break down in a hot pan in about five minutes, collapsing just enough to release some juice, which quickly thickens and caramelizes a bit. You want the tomatoes to stay mostly intact so you don’t have skins floating in sauce, but you need to cook them long enough to achieve the caramelized flavor that makes a tomato sauce sweet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimed