 couscous.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/04recipehealth/04recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/science/04recipehealth/04recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/04recipehealth/04recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/04recipehealth/04recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/04recipehealth/04recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/02/science/04recipehealth/04recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/04recipehealth/04recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romaine Salad with Couscous Confetti', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couscous', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-01T16:17:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/0adfb3bd-7641-55b8-8d3f-fb4686e3ef59', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0adfb3bd-7641-55b8-8d3f-fb4686e3ef59'}, {'abstract': 'This hearty salad, with a creamy, spicy dressing, can be made with a number of different grains.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/01/health/brown-rice-and-barley-salad-with-sprouted-red-lentils-and-green-beans.html', 'snippet': 'This hearty salad, with a creamy, spicy dressing, can be made with a number of different grains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been making iterations of this hearty whole grain salad tossed with a creamy, curry-spiced dressing since my earliest days of vegetarian cooking. My choice of grains for this version was a function of what I found in my pantry and my refrigerator: enough brown rice and barley to combine for a salad but not enough for a more substantial dish. Farro or spelt would also work. The split red lentils, soaked just long enough to soften and begin to sprout, contribute color and texture along with their grassy flavor. Tossing the grains with lemon juice while they’re still warm intensifies the flavors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/02/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/science/05recipehealth/05recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brown Rice and Barley Salad with Sprouted Red Lentils and Green Beans', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couscous', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-01T16:21:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/67afe0c1-860c-54ea-a0a3-a5b6a2ec6525', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67afe0c1-860c-54ea-a0a3-a5b6a2ec6525'}, {'abstract': 'An Oregon-based solar company is