ents so thin that doctors and nurses say their ability to properly treat serious illnesses is compromised.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HINESVILLE, Ga. — Every year, more than 25,000 Americans undergo surgery to correct a hiatal hernia, a condition in which tissue from the stomach bulges into the chest cavity through a hole in the diaphragm. The hernias often return, but major complications are rare. Hospital stays are usually short.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/us/HOSPITALS/HOSPITALS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/us/HOSPITALS/HOSPITALS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/us/HOSPITALS/HOSPITALS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/us/HOSPITALS/HOSPITALS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/us/HOSPITALS/HOSPITALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/02/us/HOSPITALS/HOSPITALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/us/HOSPITALS/HOSPITALS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Smaller Military Hospitals Said to Put Patients at Risk', 'kicker': 'Military Medicine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smaller Military Hospitals Said to Put Patients at Risk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lafraniere, Sharon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehren, Andrew W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malpractice', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T02:58:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon LaFraniere and Andrew W. Lehren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LaFraniere', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Lehren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0244cc6f-1cb9-5028-b0fd-1b31ff72d7c9', 'word_count': 4853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0244cc6f-1cb9-5028-b0fd-1b31ff72d7c9'}, {'abstract': 'River House has been a difficult place to afford and an almost impossible place to gain board approval. But with luxury rivals now blanketing the city, the place is slowly softening its image.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/nyregion/after-years-of-frostiness-a-selective-co-op-tries-a-friendlier-facade.html', 'snippet': 'River House has been a difficult place to afford and an almost impossible place to gain board approval. But with luxury rivals now blanketing the city, the place is slowly softening its image.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even two or three years ago, it would have been all but impossible to write this column. At River House, the mythic and monolithic co-op overlooking the East River, the only thing stouter than the limestone brick walls towering above East 52nd Street and Franklin D. Roosevelt Drive were the building’s standards. Those inside would call them traditions; everybody else might regard them as pretensions. Almost no one got in, and news barely escaped.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/nyregion/SUBAPPRAISAL1/SUBAPPRAISAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/nyregion/SUBAPPRAISAL1/SUBAPPRAISAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/nyregion/SUBAPPRAISAL1/SUBAPPRAISAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/nyregion/SUBAPPRAISAL1/SUBAPPRAISAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/nyregion/SUBAPPRAISAL1/SUBAPPRAISAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/02/nyregion/SUBAPPRAISAL1/SUBAPPRAISAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/nyregion/SUBAPPRAISAL1/SUBAPPRAISAL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Years of Frostiness, a Selective Co-op Tries a Friendlier Facade', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Years of Frostiness, a Selective Co-op Tries a Friendlier Facade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaban, Matt V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate Brokers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'River Club (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kips Bay (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T03:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt A.V. Chaban', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'V', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fca727f-24b8-5eda-95e2-dc42065a0014', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fca727f-24b8-5eda-95e2-dc42065a0014'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, September 2, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-tuesday-september-2-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, September 2, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“People don’t think about the fact that there are pipes under the ground that are 100 years old until one blows. You don’t hear a politician say, ‘I’m going to make your pipes work.’”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, September 2, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T03:40:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ac5bc8-6efb-5404-9f19-3eb7bdeb64b3', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ac5bc8-6efb-5404-9f19-3eb7bdeb64b3'}, {'abstract': "Next month, Joya will unveil a new perfume oil named for the odorloss Foxglove plant and inspired by Manhattan's Central Park.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/t-magazine/joya-new-perfume-oil-foxglove-inspired-by-central-park-and-new-york-city.html', 'snippet': "Next month, Joya will unveil a new perfume oil named for the odorloss Foxglove plant and inspired by Manhattan's Central Park.", 'lead_paragraph': 'As a co-founder of the international fragrance design trade show Elements, Frederick Bouchardy has sniffed countless New York-inspired scents over the years — “but I never found one that smelled like New York to me,” the Manhattan native says. Next month, Bouchardy, who is also the brains behind the Brooklyn-based fragrance studio Joya, offers his olfactory take on his hometown with the launch of a new perfume oil, Foxglove. “I grew up on the Upper West Side across the street from Central Park,” he says, “so the Park was my initial muse, and then it became an exploration of the entire botanical history of all the parks and wetlands here.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/t-magazine/02joya-park/02joya-park-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/t-magazine/