reed to sell itself to the private equity firm Thoma Bravo for about $2.5 billion, finally bowing out after years under pressure from the activist hedge fund Elliott Management.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Compuware Agrees to $2.5 Billion Buyout', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Going Private', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Compuware Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Covisint', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elliott Management Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thoma Bravo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T14:35:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gelles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d60d6b2b-07ae-5373-8bfc-dd829355a4f9', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d60d6b2b-07ae-5373-8bfc-dd829355a4f9'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A correspondent compares British and German settlements in East Africa in 1889.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/1889-british-traders-in-east-africa/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A correspondent compares British and German settlements in East Africa in 1889.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ZANZIBAR — I have just returned from Mombasa, the headquarters of the Imperial British East Africa Trading Company, and I am pleased to be able to chronicle what a difference exists in the state of affairs at that place, and at the German settlements further south. If one excepts a few turbulent spirits, the native population of Mombasa may be said to be absolutely quiet, and to be very well disposed indeed towards the Company and its servants. I attribute the excellent feeling that there predominates between natives and Europeans, at a time when the entire coast line near Zanzibar is very much disturbed, owing to the repeated aggression of the Germans. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 3, 1889', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-old03/02iht-old03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 581, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-old03/02iht-old03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 581, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-old03/02iht-old03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-old03/02iht-old03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-old03/02iht-old03-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1889: