 '_id': 'nyt://article/6776339c-a8f4-58de-b985-1bf014e4163e', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6776339c-a8f4-58de-b985-1bf014e4163e'}, {'abstract': 'The structure has become a favored spot for drug deals and neighborhood drama, angering locals who have been trying for years to get it removed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/nyregion/a-decade-on-a-sidewalk-shed-is-still-an-unwanted-shelter.html', 'snippet': 'The structure has become a favored spot for drug deals and neighborhood drama, angering locals who have been trying for years to get it removed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most nights, Roy Scott Jr. sleeps in a wheelchair, with his left arm draped over a blue scaffolding pipe, his graying curls shielded from rain by the rusting planks overhead. This is not the reason that the tunnel-like wood-and-steel structures called sidewalk sheds shroud walkways across New York City. They are supposed to catch debris from repairs overhead.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/nyregion/SCAFFOLDING1/SCAFFOLDING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/03/nyregion/SCAFFOLDING1/SCAFFOLDING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/nyregion/SCAFFOLDING1/SCAFFOLDING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/nyregion/SCAFFOLDING1/SCAFFOLDING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/nyregion/SCAFFOLDING1/SCAFFOLDING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/03/nyregion/SCAFFOLDING1/SCAFFOLDING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/nyregion/SCAFFOLDING1/SCAFFOLDING1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '10 Years On, Scaffolding in Harlem Is Still a Shelter for Noxious Acts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '10 Years On, Still a Shelter for Noxious Acts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buildings Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sidewalks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T15:01:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mueller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53a83435-9cac-5c04-b439-e3cb324c52a0', 'word_count': 987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53a83435-9cac-5c04-b439-e3cb324c52a0'}, {'abstract': '“Thieves Fall Out,” written by Gore Vidal under the name Cameron Kay and published in 1953, will come out in April in a new edition.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/new-life-for-some-pulp-fiction-by-gore-vidal/', 'snippet': '“Thieves Fall Out,” written by Gore Vidal under the name Cameron Kay and published in 1953, will come out in April in a new edition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1950s, when Gore Vidal was at the start of his career as a novelist, he did what lots of writers do to make ends meet. Between literary novels he cranked out pulp fiction, written quickly under a pseudonym – or, in Vidal’s case, three pseudonyms. As Edgar Box he wrote three mystery novels, which were reprinted with his approval during his lifetime (he died in 2012). He wrote a romance novel under the name Katherine Everard that remains a rarity. And as Cameron Kay — a name he borrowed from a great uncle — he wrote “Thieves Fall Out,” a crime thriller set in Egypt during the 1952 revolution there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/arts/02artsbeat-gore/02artsbeat-gore-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 913, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/arts/02artsbeat-gore/02artsbeat-gore-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 913}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/arts/02artsbeat-gore/02artsbeat-gore-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 673, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/arts/02artsbeat-gore/02artsbeat-gore-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1346, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/arts/02artsbeat-gore/02artsbeat-gore-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height'