rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4aa8172-5f7b-54a8-b0bb-c9a27e9e84aa', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4aa8172-5f7b-54a8-b0bb-c9a27e9e84aa'}, {'abstract': 'Our list of nine can’t-miss new places to visit between shows includes an Italian restaurant imported from the Hamptons, the best bakery in TriBeCa and much more.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/new-york-fashion-week-tribeca-where-to-eat-and-drink-coffee/', 'snippet': 'Our list of nine can’t-miss new places to visit between shows includes an Italian restaurant imported from the Hamptons, the best bakery in TriBeCa and much more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York Fashion Week unofficially kicks off tomorrow. And since the shows have become decentralized in recent seasons — with many marquee events now taking place in lower Manhattan — \xa0trekking between runway presentations and store openings also provides ample opportunity to explore what’s new on the downtown food scene. With this in mind, we rounded up the best spots below 14th Street to find the perfect croissant (hint: it’s in an arcade), drink a flat white, slurp oysters atop the deck of a 142-foot schooner, enjoy an al fresco cocktail or savor a breakfast sandwich after midnight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/t-magazine/02downtown-molvar-2/02downtown-molvar-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/t-magazine/02downtown-molvar-2/02downtown-molvar-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/t-magazine/02downtown-molvar-2/02downtown-molvar-2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/t-magazine/02downtown-molvar-2/02downtown-molvar-2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/t-magazine/02downtown-molvar-2/02downtown-molvar-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/02/t-magazine/02downtown-molvar-2/02downtown-molvar-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/t-magazine/02downtown-molvar-2/02downtown-molvar-2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Eat, Unwind and Caffeinate Downtown During New York Fashion Week', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacPherson, Sean', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T17:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kari Molvar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Molvar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e840b8f-69d2-5087-b30c-cdf4bab4f62d', 'word_count': 962, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e840b8f-69d2-5087-b30c-cdf4bab4f62d'}, {'abstract': 'We invited small-business owners who were willing to open their doors to an elected official for a day to let us know by email. Two owners did.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/meet-two-business-owners-with-opposing-views-on-minimum-wage/', 'snippet': 'We invited small-business owners who were willing to open their doors to an elected official for a day to let us know by email. Two owners did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, in a discussion about how raising the minimum wage might affect small companies, we noted that there could be more empathy among elected officials for how entrepreneurs manage their businesses. Inspired by the suggestion that members of Congress ought to try managing a small business for a week, we invited small-business owners who were willing to open their doors to an elected official for a day to let us know by email.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meet Two Business Owners With Opposing Views on Minimum Wage', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T17:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aee9e6b4-bdc9-51f1-a848-ca3429655a26', 'word_count': 1143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aee9e6b4-bdc9-51f1-a848-ca3429655a26'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A town in France prepares to host wounded soldiers in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/1914-city-prepares-for-war-wounded/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A town in France prepares to host wounded soldiers in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AIX-LES-BAINS — In spite of the deadly silence which has reigned here for more than a fortnight now, Aix has not been idle. There is hardly a person here, native or visitor, who has not done a little to help. Wonders have been achieved in all the hotels, schools and garages in establishing hospitals and ‘‘cantines,’’ and everything is now in readiness to receive the wounded. About 1,200 beds are installed, and it is touching to see how much hard work has been done and real sacrifice has been gladly made.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 3, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-oldsept03-Aix/02iht-oldsept03-Aix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-oldsept03-Aix/02iht-oldsept03-Aix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-oldsept03-Aix/02iht-oldsept03-Aix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-oldsept03-Aix/02iht-oldsept03-Aix-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1042, 'width': 1617, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-oldsept03-Aix/02iht-oldsept03-Aix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-oldsept03-Aix/02iht-oldsept03-Aix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/blogs/02iht-oldsept03-Aix/02iht-oldsept03-Aix-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1914: City Prepares for War Wounded', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T17:34:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abd048dc-af8e-5ded-a5e2-20e275030be6', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abd048dc-af8e-5ded-a5e2-20e275030be6'}, {'abstract': 'Two mentally disabled half brothers who were convicted in the rape and murder of an 11-year-old girl 30 years ago were declared innocent and ordered released by a judge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/us/2-convicted-in-1983-north-carolina-murder-freed-after-dna-tests.html', 'snippet': 'Two mentally disabled half brothers who were convicted in the rape and murder of an 11-year-old girl 30 years ago were declared innocent and ordered released by a judge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LUMBERTON, N.C. — Thirty years after their convictions in the rape and murder of an 11-year-old girl in rural North Carolina, based on confessions that they quickly repudiated and said were coerced, two mentally disabled half brothers were declared innocent and ordered released Tuesday by a judge here.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/us/JP-CAROLINA1/JP-CAROLINA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/03/us/JP-CAROLINA1/JP-CAROLINA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/us/JP-CAROLINA1/JP-CAROLINA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/us/JP-CAROLINA1/JP-CAROLINA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1078, 'width': 1586, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/us/JP-CAROLINA1/JP-CAROLINA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/03/us/JP-CAROLINA1/JP-CAROLINA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/us/JP-CAROLINA1/JP-CAROLINA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'DNA Evidence Clears Two Men in 1983 Murder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DNA Evidence Clears Two Men in 1983 Murder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Leon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCollum, Henry Lee', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCollum, Henry Lee', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T17:38:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan M. Katz and Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70a8e4a0-28fd-58e3-b786-1671967c8997', 'word_count': 1223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70a8e4a0-28fd-58e3-b786-1671967c8997'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa Rivers said she and her family were grateful for the support.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/joan-rivers-on-life-support/', 'snippet': 'Melissa Rivers said she and her family were grateful for the support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joan Rivers remains on life support on Tuesday, days after she was hospitalized in Manhattan, her daughter, Melissa Rivers, said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daughter Confirms Joan Rivers Is Still on Life Support', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivers, Joan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivers, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T17:43:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/441a0ae3-2750-5e38-a4c6-b91f5248821b', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/441a0ae3-2750-5e38-a4c6-b91f5248821b'}, {'abstract': 'Readers of Garage Magazine can examine a new virtual artwork by Mr. Koons through an app.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/a-virtual-jeff-koons-work-to-grace-garage-magazine/', 'snippet': 'Readers of Garage Magazine can examine a new virtual artwork by Mr. Koons through an app.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Garage Magazine, an art, fashion and literary magazine that publishes twice a year, will include a surprise for its readers in its seventh issue, due on Thursday: a virtual art work, created for the publication by Jeff Koons. The work, “Lady Bug,” is virtual in the sense that it can be seen only on mobile devices, by way of the Garage Mag app. Viewers will be able to use the app and their devices to walk around the piece – virtually – and see it from all angles.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/arts/02artsbeat-koons2/02artsbeat-koons2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 796, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/arts/02ar