one, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a9fb024-2a28-5af1-a4cc-811049865ec4', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a9fb024-2a28-5af1-a4cc-811049865ec4'}, {'abstract': 'In a Q. and A., Murray spoke about his role in tennis’s Big 4 and his familiarity with his U.S Open quarterfinals opponent, Novak Djokovic, whom he has played 20 times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/sports/tennis/andy-murray-reviews-his-place-among-the-big-4.html', 'snippet': 'In a Q. and A., Murray spoke about his role in tennis’s Big 4 and his familiarity with his U.S Open quarterfinals opponent, Novak Djokovic, whom he has played 20 times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Andy Murray reaches the pointy end of the draw at the United States Open, he finds a familiar face in Novak Djokovic waiting in the quarterfinals. Murray and Djokovic have met 20 times, four in Grand Slam finals (each winning twice). In his latest conversation with The New York Times, Murray discusses his role in the so-called Big 4, the four players who have dominated men’s tennis in the past 10 years. In previous interviews at the U.S. Open, Murray has discussed his perspective on this year’s tournament, female coaches in tennis, the idea of an independent Scotland and his favorite stops on the tour. This interview has been condensed and edited.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/sports/03murray/03murray-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/03/sports/03murray/03murray-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/sports/03murray/03murray-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subTy