climated. So here are a few thoughts on a\xa0cultural controversy that\xa0flared up\xa0while I was away, when a writer for Vox, Martha Nochimson, apparently\xa0got David Chase on the record\xa0saying that Tony Soprano\xa0had, in fact, survived the famous cut to black at the end of “The Sopranos” … implying\xa0that the blackout was not, in fact,\xa0a Tony’s-eye view of the gangster’s own whacking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tony Soprano Is Dead', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chase, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seitz, Matt Zoller', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York (Magazine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vox Media Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T18:55:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8751a994-82f6-576c-acbe-db37b4c6ace6', 'word_count': 1404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8751a994-82f6-576c-acbe-db37b4c6ace6'}, {'abstract': 'The owner of The Ludlow, a new hotel on the Lower East Side, talks about the city’s past and how much it has changed since the ’80s.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/video-interview-sean-macpherson-ludlow-hotel/', 'snippet': 'The owner of The Ludlow, a new hotel on the Lower East Side, talks about the city’s past and how much it has changed since the ’80s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the latest installation of our T Time video series, T’s online director Jesse Ashlock interviews Sean MacPherson, the hotelier who created the Maritime and the Jane. MacPherson talks about his new hotel, the\xa0Ludlow, located on the Lower East Side, and how the city has changed since the ’80s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sean MacPherson on His New Hotel, the Ludlow', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacPherson, Sean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T19:11:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbf4b707-66dc-5d00-b401-6303ea073c2d', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbf4b707-66dc-5d00-b401-6303ea073c2d'}, {'abstract': 'The Colts owner Jim Irsay was suspended and fined $500,000 by the N.F.L. on after he pleaded guilty Tuesday to a misdemeanor related to a March traffic stop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/sports/football/nfl-suspends-colts-owner-jim-irsay-for-six-games.html', 'snippet': 'The Colts owner Jim Irsay was suspended and fined $500,000 by the N.F.L. on after he pleaded guilty Tuesday to a misdemeanor related to a March traffic stop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'N.F.L. Commissioner Roger Goodell suspended the Indianapolis Colts owner Jim Irsay on Tuesday for six games and fined him $500,000 for violating the league’s personal conduct policy when he was arrested on the suspicion of being intoxicated while driving