s who have become quite a cheering section in Flushing Meadows in recent years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/sports/Y-OPENDAY/Y-OPENDAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/03/sports/Y-OPENDAY/Y-OPENDAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/sports/Y-OPENDAY/Y-OPENDAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/sports/Y-OPENDAY/Y-OPENDAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/sports/Y-OPENDAY/Y-OPENDAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/03/sports/Y-OPENDAY/Y-OPENDAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/sports/Y-OPENDAY/Y-OPENDAY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At 28, Peng Shuai Advances to Her First Grand Slam Semifinal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At 28, Chinese Player Advances to Her First Grand Slam Semifinal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zinser, Lynn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peng Shuai', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bencic, Belinda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bellis, Catherine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T19:54:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1f1fbab-3598-5b2b-8cd7-5f3054354474', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1f1fbab-3598-5b2b-8cd7-5f3054354474'}, {'abstract': 'Many locals have proposed Leipzig, Germany, as Europe’s new home base for voguish 20-somethings, and the city has been born anew as a cultural mecca.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/travel/new-berlin-or-not-leipzig-has-new-life.html', 'snippet': 'Many locals have proposed Leipzig, Germany, as Europe’s new home base for voguish 20-somethings, and the city has been born anew as a cultural mecca.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By 1989, Leipzig stank. The East German industrial hub was said to have the worst air in the country — if not the continent. Factories belched tons of sulfur dioxide into the skies and the polluted waterways reeked. But just a quarter-century later, Leipzig has shed its reputation as Germany’s “poverty capital” and entered safely into the realm of poverty chic; it has been born anew as a cultural mecca — and, just maybe, the “New Berlin.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-headsup-top/07-headsup-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-headsup-top/07-headsup-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-headsup-top/07-headsup-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-headsup-top/07-headsup-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-headsup-top/07-headsup-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-headsup-top/07-headsup-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-headsup-top/07-headsup-top-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘New Berlin’ or Not, Leipzig Has New Life', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hipsters Look Southward From Berlin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Leipzig (Germany)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T19:59:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Engelhart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Engelhart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f3edfce-3f4b-501d-b7f3-7458552156fd', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f3edfce-3f4b-501d-b7f3-7458552156fd'}, {'abstract': 'This year-old restaurant wears a derogatory term for Southern Italians as a badge of honor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/travel/restaurant-report-tern-in-palo-alto-calif.html', 'snippet': 'This year-old restaurant wears a derogatory term for Southern Italians as a badge of honor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Piedmontese slang, Terún is a derogatory term for Southern Italians. “It means rednecks or hicks,” said Franco Campilongo, who hails from a small town in Calabria, the toe on Italy’s boot. But rather than taking the term (pronounced tay-ROON) as an affront, Mr. Campilongo wears it as a badge of honor — as does his year-old restaurant in Palo Alto.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07BITES/07BITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07BITES/07BITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07BITES/07BITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07BITES/07BITES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', '