. 2 at the Cort Theater and open on March 5.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Fish in the Dark,” the new Broadway play written by and starring Larry David, will begin preview performances on Feb. 2 at the Cort Theater and open on March 5, the producer Scott Rudin said on Tuesday. Additional cast members were also announced: the Tony Award nominee Jayne Houdyshell (“Well”), Rosie Perez (“Fearless”), Jonny Orsini (“The Nance”), Jake Cannavale (“Basilica”), and Jerry Adler (“The Sopranos”). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/02artsbeat-larry/02artsbeat-larry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 555, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/02artsbeat-larry/02artsbeat-larry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 555, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/02artsbeat-larry/02artsbeat-larry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/02artsbeat-larry/02artsbeat-larry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/02artsbeat-larry/02artsbeat-larry-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Larry David’s ‘Fish in the Dark’ to Open on Broadway in March', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'David, Larry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T20:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f493fc13-d25c-57c6-b78c-3dcdd34ae3a1', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f493fc13-d25c-57c6-b78c-3dcdd34ae3a1'}, {'abstract': 'The first major retrospective of the filmmaker’s work opens this month in Philadelphia, where Federal Donuts will serve up sugary confections as an homage to his films.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/02/david-lynchs-doughnut-obsession/', 'snippet': 'The first major retrospective of the filmmaker’s work opens this month in Philadelphia, where Federal Donuts will serve up sugary confections as an homage to his films.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trippy dream sequences. Doppelgängers. Laura Dern. One associates them all with the fun-house mirror maze of a David Lynch project. But doughnuts? From Special Agent Dale Cooper’s insatiable sweet tooth on “Twin Peaks” to the metaphor Lynch uses in the 2012 documentary “Meditation, Creativity, Peace” (“Transcendental Meditation gives an experience much sweeter than the sweetness of this doughnut”), sugary fried rings have popped up throughout the filmmaker’s cabalistic canon. And so, Michael Solomonov, the chef and co-owner of Philadelphia’s Federal Donuts, jumped at the invite to make confections in honor of the first major retrospective of Lynch’s work, at the Pennsylvania Academy of the Fine Arts (where Lynch studied painting in the late ’60s). With names like Blue Velvet and Good Coffee — a “Twin Peaks” reference — Solomonov’s creations are an homage to the master of magical realist cinema. There’s one, though, that won’t see the light of day: the David Lynch. “I would have done a little clove and allspice, to get at the Indian-mystical thing, and a bit of malt powder since he used to have a daily milkshake,” Solomonov says. “Plus a healthy dose of windowpane LSD.” ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '80', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14mens-look-lynch/14mens-look-lynch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14mens-look-lynch/14mens-look-lynch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 491}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14mens-look-lynch/14mens-look-lynch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 839, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14mens-look-lynch/14mens-look-lynch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1318, 'width': 1609, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14mens-look-lynch/14mens-look-lynch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14mens-look-lynch/14mens-look-lynch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14mens-look-lynch/14mens-look-lynch-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'David Lynch’s Doughnut