rnational Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees ratified the contracts negotiated with the opera late last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two of the Metropolitan Opera unions represented by the International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees have ratified the contracts negotiated with the opera late last month. One of the unions, Local 1, which represents the carpenters and those responsible for the lighting, sound, props and set construction, approved a six-year agreement; the other, Local 764, representing those who work in the costume shop and who dress the singers, approved a four-year contract. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Met Opera Unions Ratify Contracts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Met Opera Unions Ratify Contracts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T21:32:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75b5c4f8-4c98-5504-bbca-ff975fea7e2d', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75b5c4f8-4c98-5504-bbca-ff975fea7e2d'}, {'abstract': 'In Ben Lerner’s latest novel, “10:04,” New York itself is more than a mere backdrop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/books/in-ben-lerners-1004-new-york-is-a-character.html', 'snippet': 'In Ben Lerner’s latest novel, “10:04,” New York itself is more than a mere backdrop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the new issue of Tin House, the literary quarterly, there’s a terrific conversation — conducted on Google Chat — between Annie Nugent Baker, the Pulitzer Prize-winning playwright, and the novelist Benjamin Baker Nugent, her brother.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/03BOOKjp/03BOOKjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/03BOOKjp/03BOOKjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 733}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/03BOOKjp/03BOOKjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 839, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/03BOOKjp/03BOOKjp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1678, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/03BOOKjp/03BOOKjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/03BOOKjp/03BOOKjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/03BOOKjp/03BOOKjp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Storms Outside, Inner Conflicts Swirl', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Storms Outside, Inner Conflicts Swirl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Dwight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lerner, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '10:04 (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-02T21:42:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a276236-9cd2-53ad-b4ea-0350b96727dd', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a276236-9cd2-53ad-b4ea-0350b96727dd'}, {'abstract': '“The Quest” combines live-action role playing with an elimination competition in a show with ogres, castles and armor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/arts/television/the-quest-a-hybrid-show-mixes-reality-and-role-play.html', 'snippet': '“The Quest” combines live-action role playing with an elimination competition in a show with ogres, castles and armor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I could have spent my television time over Labor Day weekend catching up on any number of brainy, critically beloved shows in preparation for the fall season. Instead, I was sucked into a world of inept archery and ill-fitting armor, where people who have no business trying to save a kingdom have been given the responsibility to do just that.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/03QUEST/03QUEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/03QUEST/03QUEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/arts/03QUES