02'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of looking away, Mr. Bowden chose to write deeply researched books about the borderland drug war and its many slaughters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/opinion/charles-bowden-a-writer-on-the-edge.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of looking away, Mr. Bowden chose to write deeply researched books about the borderland drug war and its many slaughters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a 1916 book about “the newspaper trade” put it, the reporter’s job is “to see for the unseeing and to become a public observer for the benefit of those who cannot observe.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charles Bowden, a Writer on the Edge', 'kicker': 'Appreciations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charles Bowden, a Writer on the Edge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowden, Charles (1945-2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Downes, Lawrence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tucson Citizen', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T00:34:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b425a7f-b0d2-5391-97ee-f7ccddc08b64', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b425a7f-b0d2-5391-97ee-f7ccddc08b64'}, {'abstract': 'Dozens of species of popular West Coast rockfish that were once so overfished that the fishing grounds were declared a federal economic disaster are now abundant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/us/revival-of-species-puts-some-fish-back-on-plates.html', 'snippet': 'Dozens of species of popular West Coast rockfish that were once so overfished that the fishing grounds were declared a federal economic disaster are now abundant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dozens of species of popular West Coast rockfish that were once so overfished that the fishing grounds were declared a federal economic disaster are now abundant. The Monterey Bay Aquarium Seafood Watch program, considered the most influential guide to hundreds of species of popular fish, on Monday issued a report encouraging consumers to eat 21 species of rockfish it had long warned cooks to avoid. Many fish sold on menus as snapper, black cod and rock cod were moved to favorable categories, along with recommendations for consumers to choose more sablefish and petrale sole. The revival of the fisheries began in earnest in 2000, when they were near collapse and fishing families were facing bankruptcy. A series of quotas, improvements in gear, better monitoring of catches and the creation of protected areas to preserve fish habitat brought improvements in stocks off the shores of California, Washington and Oregon, said Frank Lockhart of the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration’s West Coast fisheries division. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Revival of Species Puts Some Fish Back on Plates', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revival of Species Puts Some Fish Back on Plates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Othe