cted in 1983 North Carolina Murder Are Freed After DNA Tests', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T08:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1bb8996-a9c6-5f87-8763-73d93ff1481e', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1bb8996-a9c6-5f87-8763-73d93ff1481e'}, {'abstract': 'Taiwan’s main political parties have backed Hong Kong residents’ calls for a greater say in choosing their leader, following Beijing’s decision this week to limit electoral reforms in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/from-taiwan-broad-support-for-democracy-in-hong-kong/', 'snippet': 'Taiwan’s main political parties have backed Hong Kong residents’ calls for a greater say in choosing their leader, following Beijing’s decision this week to limit electoral reforms in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taiwan’s main political parties say they support Hong Kong residents’ calls for a greater say in choosing their leader following Beijing’s decision to limit electoral reforms in the semiautonomous Chinese city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/world/03sino-taiwan01/03sino-taiwan01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/03/world/03sino-taiwan01/03sino-taiwan01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u