', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/28/business/Teensjp1/Teensjp1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/business/Teensjp1/Teensjp1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Teenagers Favor Tech Over Clothes', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T08:45:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7495192-3f0a-5965-b98d-642afe06caf2', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7495192-3f0a-5965-b98d-642afe06caf2'}, {'abstract': 'In what has been the most news-filled summer in recent memory, our leaders in the media-political class “started a conversation,” whatever that means.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/magazine/bearing-witness-in-ferguson.html', 'snippet': 'In what has been the most news-filled summer in recent memory, our leaders in the media-political class “started a conversation,” whatever that means.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The spectacle began, as it often does, with a local tragedy. Last month an unarmed black teenager named Michael Brown was shot by a police officer in Ferguson, a suburb of St. Louis. In a less media-saturated time, we might have gone on to consider this serious news event on its own terms, with journalists providing facts and insights, and politicians pondering a course of action. But in the mixed-up scrum of politics and media that our so-called national conversation has become, a serious news event is only the start of the news. Soon after the shooting, the suburb of Ferguson became a roiling caldron of outside observers, all bent on “bearing witness” to the situation.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Many Outsiders Does It Take to ‘Bear Witness’ in Ferguson?', 'kicker': 'Your Fellow Americans', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let Us All Bear Witness to the Conversation!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leibovich, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Leibovich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leibovich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3987a91-dbd0-59ee-8ab1-bf2f3a8422d3', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3987a91-dbd0-59ee-8ab1-bf2f3a8422d3'}, {'abstract': 'High joblessness in the developed world results mostly from the tepid pace of recovery, data from the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/business/international/job-creation-should-be-policy-priority-oecd-report-finds.html', 'snippet': 'High joblessness in the developed world results mostly from the tepid pace of recovery, data from the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — High unemployment rates in most of the developed world are mainly a result of the tepid economic recovery, rather than a lack of appropriate skills in the work force, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said in a report on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Job Creation Should Be Policy Priority, O.E.C.D. Report Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T09:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4da7d32-4a47-564f-81b9-ff607ade2430', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4da7d32-4a47-564f-81b9-ff607ade2430'}, {'abstract': 'From the “emoji diet” to Gwyneth Paltrow’s detox, tales of diet experiments can illuminate how we eat.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/emoji-for-breakfast-dinosaur-for-lunch/', 'snippet': 'From the “emoji diet” to Gwyneth Paltrow’s detox, tales of diet experiments can illuminate how we eat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that emojis have been analyzed, debated\xa0and used as the basis of\xa0a messaging app, it’s no longer enough just to talk about them. We\xa0must eat them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emoji for Breakfast, Dinosaur for Lunch', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Tracy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lockwood, Patricia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paltrow, Gwyneth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goop.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T09:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8960c23-aef4-5345-ab65-27cb39ebf9ed', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8960c23-aef4-5345-ab65-27cb39ebf9ed'}, {'abstract': 'Did you follow the news about the death of Michael Brown and the protests in Ferguson, Mo.? If so, what reactions did you have? Do you think anything will change — either in St. Louis or nationally — as a result of the protests? Why or why not?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/will-what-happened-in-ferguson-change-anything/', 'snippet': 'Did you follow the news about the death of Michael Brown and the protests in Ferguson, Mo.? If so, what reactions did you have? Do you think anything will change — either in St. Louis or nationally — as a result of the protests? Why or why not?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Did you follow the news about the Aug. 9 death of Michael Brown and the subsequent protests in Ferguson, Mo.? If so, what reactions did you have? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None