person basis, Medicare spending is actually falling.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-medi2-1409710126918/04up-medi2-1409710126918-articleLarge.png', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-medi2-1409710126918/04up-medi2-1409710126918-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-medi2-1409710126918/04up-medi2-1409710126918-jumbo.png', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-medi2-1409710126918/04up-medi2-1409710126918-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1108, 'width': 1679, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-medi2-1409710126918/04up-medi2-1409710126918-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-medi2-1409710126918/04up-medi2-1409710126918-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-medi2-1409710126918/04up-medi2-1409710126918-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Per Capita Medicare Spending Is Actually Falling', 'kicker': 'Public Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surprise: Per Capita Medicare Spending Is Falling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanger-Katz, Margot', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T10:59:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margot Sanger-Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanger-Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/061c39b9-ab6e-5e23-a43a-41e9fd93f894', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/061c39b9-ab6e-5e23-a43a-41e9fd93f894'}, {'abstract': 'It all starts so well. You meet venture capitalists and deliver a knockout pitch. They love it, you exchange business cards, they set out the next steps – and then you fall into the trap.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/how-investors-can-kill-a-business-without-losing-money-themselves/', 'snippet': 'It all starts so well. You meet venture capitalists and deliver a knockout pitch. They love it, you exchange business cards, they set out the next steps – and then you fall into the trap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the story of a trap into which I’ve fallen twice at Posse. Investors often set the trap unknowingly – no harm is intended – while they are figuring out whether they would like to invest. Both times this happened I felt heartbroken and exhausted, with my business in turmoil. We were lucky to survive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Investors Can Kill a Business Without Losing Money Themselves', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T11:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebekah Campbell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebekah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Campbell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11cda67a-07f2-51f9-ae8a-6ffca3c1656d', 'word_count': 1175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11cda67a-07f2-51f9-ae8a-6ffca3c1656d'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Turkey considers entering WWI in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/1914-turkish-desire-for-war/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Turkey considers entering WWI in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Reports of German successes, skilfully exaggerated, have enormously reinforced the following of Enver Pasha, and telegrams from Constantinople speak of war as inevitable. Turkey would attack Russia in the Caucasus and Greece at the same time, if Bulgaria will permit the Ottoman troops to traverse her country. It is known that the Russophile party in Sofia is in the ascendant. The Bulgarians are afraid that Turkey, if victorious, would refuse to evacuate the strip of territory traversed by her troops on their way to attack Salonica. It should be added that Russia has declared at Sofia that if the passage of Turkish troops is permitted she will disembark troops at Varna.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 4, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/04iht-oldsept04-EnverPasha/04iht-oldsept04-EnverPasha-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 392, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/04iht-oldsept04-EnverPasha/04iht-oldsept04-EnverPasha-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 392, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/04iht-oldsept04-EnverPasha/04iht-oldsept04-EnverPasha-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/04iht-oldsept04-EnverPasha/04iht-oldsept04-EnverPasha-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/04iht-oldsept04-EnverPasha/04iht-oldsept04-EnverPasha-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1914: Turkish Desire for War', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ottoman Empire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T11:20:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22f39162-bbf1-56cd-a81a-972f3cf1b1d2', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22f39162-bbf1-56cd-a81a-972f3cf1b1d2'}, {'abstract': 'Most people don’t like to download mobile apps. But when they do, they spend nearly all of their time in them. A new start-up called DWNLD is promising to make it cheaper and easier for publishers to convert their sites into attractive apps.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/making-the-leap-from-web-to-mobile-apps-easier/', 'snippet': 'Most people don’t like to download mobile apps. But when they do, they spend nearly all of their time in them. A new start-up called DWNLD is promising to make it cheaper and easier for publishers to convert their sites into attractive apps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a curious paradox at the heart of mobile apps: Most people don’t like to download them. But when they do, they spend nearly all of their time in them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/technology/03bits-app1/03bits-app1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/03/technology/03bits-app1/03bits-app1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 458}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/technology/03bits-app1/03bits-app1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 782, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/technology/03bits-app1/03bits-app1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1100, 'width': 1440, 