', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/magazine/McConnellBlog1/McConnellBlog1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/02/magazine/McConnellBlog1/McConnellBlog1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/magazine/McConnellBlog1/McConnellBlog1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 716, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/magazine/McConnellBlog1/McConnellBlog1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 716, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/magazine/McConnellBlog1/McConnellBlog1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/02/magazine/McConnellBlog1/McConnellBlog1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/02/magazine/McConnellBlog1/McConnellBlog1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '9 Things You Maybe Didn’t Know About Mitch McConnell', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T14:58:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By JONATHAN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2572300-cb8f-5d12-8df9-7c800b181d70', 'word_count': 1586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2572300-cb8f-5d12-8df9-7c800b181d70'}, {'abstract': 'Kelly Barnhill’s “The Witch’s Boy” is set in an absorbing world of kingdoms and prophecies in which transformation comes through language, courage and self-awareness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/books/the-witchs-boy-by-kelly-barnhill.html', 'snippet': 'Kelly Barnhill’s “The Witch’s Boy” is set in an absorbing world of kingdoms and prophecies in which transformation comes through language, courage and self-awareness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every avid reader shares the belief that words are powerful. Words can hurt; they can heal, save, inspire, destroy and create. As Kelly Barnhill writes in “The Witch’s Boy,” her latest middle-grade novel, “a word, after all, is a kind of magic.” It’s a story with many alluring elements, including a boy who is rejected by his village after surviving an accident that killed his identical twin; a bandit king’s motherless daughter; a wolf; and a little clay pot full of magic. Barnhill (“Iron Hearted Violet,” “The Mostly True Story of Jack”) creates an absorbing world of kingdoms and prophecies in which transformation comes through language, and through courage and self-awareness as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/books/03childrens/03childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 904, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/03/books/03childrens/03childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 904}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima