word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5dd22ef-8b05-5e5f-af8d-2d90ecd62a6f'}, {'abstract': 'The fight between two liberal crusaders with profoundly divergent ideas about how to aid and educate the disempowered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/magazine/the-battle-for-new-york-schools-eva-moskowitz-vs-mayor-bill-de-blasio.html', 'snippet': 'The fight between two liberal crusaders with profoundly divergent ideas about how to aid and educate the disempowered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One afternoon this summer, Eva Moskowitz, who runs Success Academy Charter Schools, showed me her senior yearbook. “I was the editor,” she said. We sat in a half-furnished office at the construction site of her charter network’s first high school. A buzz saw shrieked in the background. She graduated in 1982 from Stuyvesant, the most selective of New York City’s public high schools. “I got completely engaged in how to take this sentimental book and make it a much bigger project.” She fought to publish photographs capturing the political protests of that time — against nuclear weapons, against American aid to the government in El Salvador. To go with the pictures, she wrote a manifesto, concluding: “We do not live in a vacuum.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '60', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07moskowitz1/07moskowitz1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07moskowitz1/07moskowitz1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07moskowitz1/07moskowitz1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07moskowitz1/07moskowitz1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07moskowitz1/07moskowitz1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07moskowitz1/07moskowitz1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07moskowitz1/07moskowitz1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Battle for New York Schools: Eva Moskowitz vs. Mayor Bill de Blasio', 'kicker': 'The Education Issue', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Class Warefare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergner, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moskowitz, Eva S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Success Academy Charter Schools', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T15:07:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Bergner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bergner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://arti