highly contentious arms deal with Russia into doubt on Wednesday over the Ukraine crisis, saying it was premature to schedule the delivery of a sophisticated French-built warship to the Russian Navy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Postpones Delivery of Warship to Russia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France Postpones Delivery of Warship to Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T16:49:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maïa de la Baume and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37c978b5-c3f2-59da-abd6-ccb5b38dcf52', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37c978b5-c3f2-59da-abd6-ccb5b38dcf52'}, {'abstract': '“On the Town” marked the Broadway debut of Leonard Bernstein, Jerome Robbins, Betty Comden and Adolph Green, a foursome known as “the kids.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/theater/fall-arts-preview-when-on-the-town-hit-the-town.html', 'snippet': '“On the Town” marked the Broadway debut of Leonard Bernstein, Jerome Robbins, Betty Comden and Adolph Green, a foursome known as “the kids.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'By November 1944, the director, producer, playwright, sometime actor and full-time theater maestro George Abbott had already exerted his legendary control over Jimmy Durante, various vaudevillians looking to go legit and even, in “Jumbo,” a live elephant. But the roomful of tyros that had assembled in rehearsals for “On the Town” posed a new challenge for the 57-year-old “Mr. Abbott,” as everyone called him.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GRODE1/07GRODE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GRODE1/07GRODE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 479}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GRODE1/07GRODE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GRODE1/07GRODE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1634, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GRODE1/07GRODE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GRODE1/07GRODE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GRODE1/07GRODE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Kids, New Kids, What a Helluva Team', 'kicker': 'The New Season', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Kids, New Kids, What a Helluva Team', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'On the Town (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Leonard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comden, Betty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Adolph', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Jerome', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T16:50:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Grode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e2f52f4-eeca-5e9c-9ade-a5650022831b', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e2f52f4-eeca-5e9c-9ade-a5650022831b'}, {'abstract': 'A Delta flight was diverted on Monday after passengers began arguing about a reclining seat–the third flight in less than two weeks that made an unscheduled landing after disputes over reclining between travelers.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/another-argument-and-diversion-over-a-reclining-seat/', 'snippet': 'A Delta flight was diverted on Monday after passengers began arguing about a reclining seat–the third flight in less than two weeks that made an unscheduled landing after disputes over reclining between travelers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A third flight in less than two weeks made an unscheduled landing Monday night because of passengers fighting over reclining seats. Delta Flight 2370, on its way from La Guardia Airport to Palm Beach International, was diverted to Jacksonville when one passenger began yelling at the woman sitting in front of her for reclining her seat, ABC News reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Argument (and Diversion) Over a Reclining Seat', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flight Attendants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR LINE PILOTS ASSN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Assn of Flight Attendants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T16:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f99e9ac-24e5-5201-9208-09d3b83f70d8', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f99e9ac-24e5-5201-9208-09d3b83f70d8'}, {'abstract': 'But those days are over. Here’s why I’m changing the way I manage.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/it-was-fun-being-the-hero-who-saves-the-day/', 'snippet': 'But those days are over. Here’s why I’m changing the way I manage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a previous post, I offered a preliminary post-mortem in which I talked about some of the things we learned from our nearly disastrous handling of one customer’s order. In this post, I want to wrap up this series of posts by talking about how my thinking about my own role at the company has changed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It Was Fun Being the Hero Who Saves the Day', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cincinnati (Ohio)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T17:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred Warmbier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warmbier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f3fb4fa-0431-57fd-95a9-843b2e3a999f', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f3fb4fa-0431-57fd-95a9-843b2e3a999f'}, {'abstract': 'Bernard Arnault will distribute to shareholders the stake he built up in Hermès. But Groupe Arnault will retain 8.5 percent of its capital, suggesting it is keeping its long-term options open, Carol Ryan of Reuters Breakingviews writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/in-hermes-agreement-a-rare-retreat-by-a-luxury-deal-maker/', 'snippet': 'Bernard Arnault will distribute to shareholders the stake he built up in Hermès. But Groupe Arnault will retain 8.5 percent of its capital, suggesting it is keeping its long-term options open, Carol Ryan of Reuters Breakingviews writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bernard Arnault has conceded defeat. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Hermès Agreement, a Rare Retreat by a Luxury Deal Maker', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARNAULT, BERNARD', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupe Arnault', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T17:08:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Ryan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27653ce7-2661-5a37-9251-26ed0fc84a96', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27653ce7-2661-5a37-9251-26ed0fc84a96'}, {'abstract': 'A first look at standout designs for spring/summer 2015, which the New York designers won’t be sending down a runway or presenting by appointment.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/new-york-fashion-week-five-best-men-collections-that-will-not-be-showing/', 'snippet': 'A first look at standout designs for spring/summer 2015, which the New York designers won’t be sending down a runway or presenting by appointment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For men’s wear, New York Fashion Week has become less a traditional week of shows and more a smattering of presentations. Some designers have elected to forgo presentations and editors’ previews altogether, including these five up-and-comers who challenge the heritage-based “all-American” aesthetic that has become typical of many New York men’s wear labels. Here T offers an exclusive first look at their spring/summer 2015 collections.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/03/t-magazine/03noshow-tudela-slide-2V2S/03noshow-tudela-slide-2V2S-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_