_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f194d71-3eb9-596c-8b7d-0a19243cee36', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f194d71-3eb9-596c-8b7d-0a19243cee36'}, {'abstract': 'The Washington Post political analyst expects Senate races to be subject to powerful local dynamics in 2014, rather than be swept up in a national wave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/upshot/chris-cillizza-plays-our-senate-forecasting-game.html', 'snippet': 'The Washington Post political analyst expects Senate races to be subject to powerful local dynamics in 2014, rather than be swept up in a national wave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are inviting political experts to play our Predict the Midterms game, and we’ll be talking to them about their entries. Our first such entrant is Chris Cillizza, founder of The Fix blog at The Washington Post.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-leofix/04up-leofix-jumbo.png', 'height': 540, 'width': 420, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-leofix/04up-leofix-superJumbo.png', 'height': 540, 'width': 420, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-leofix/04up-leofix-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/04/upshot/04up-leofix/04up-