accine. The hope was that this alternative would better protect seniors, but scientific evidence proving its effectiveness has been lacking.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Better Flu Shot', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Backs High-Dose Flu Vaccine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T19:41:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Graham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/718c4053-c817-57fa-8f59-614c087d019e', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/718c4053-c817-57fa-8f59-614c087d019e'}, {'abstract': 'Julianne Moore, who’s equally at home in indies and big-budget projects, goes out on an emotional limb with David Cronenberg’s “Map to the Stars.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/movies/fall-arts-preview-julianne-moore-plays-a-fading-diva-in-maps-to-the-stars.html', 'snippet': 'Julianne Moore, who’s equally at home in indies and big-budget projects, goes out on an emotional limb with David Cronenberg’s “Map to the Stars.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her long and enviable career, Julianne Moore has made a point of appearing in both big-budget pictures like “Non-Stop,” the recent Liam Neeson thriller, and in underfunded independent films like “What Maisie Knew,” where the costume budget was so skimpy she wound up lending the production some of her own clothes. This season, she’s in the third installment of the “Hunger Games” trilogy, which opens Nov. 21, and also in David Cronenberg’s newest film, “Maps to the Stars,” scheduled to be released before the end of the year. Though set in Hollywood, “Maps” was mostly shot in Toronto, to save money, and this time Ms. Moore had to scrounge some jewelry and handbags.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07MCGRATH1/07MCGRATH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 824, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07MCGRATH1/07MCGRATH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 824}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07MCGRATH1/07MCGRATH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 746, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07MCGRATH1/07MCGRATH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1492, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07MCGRATH1/07MCGRATH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07MCGRATH1/07MCGRATH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07MCGRATH1/07MCGRATH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘It’s Not Me, It’s the Story’ ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'pri