of Neruda’s poems at 54 Below.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/arts/music/ute-lemper-brings-nerudas-poems-to-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'The German singer Ute Lemper performed fiery renditions of Neruda’s poems at 54 Below.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The seam of feral imagery that winds through the love poems of the great Chilean writer Pablo Neruda gives them a visceral intensity that makes the romantic effusions of many English-language poets seem flowery and incorporeal. As the German chanteuse Ute Lemper sang her settings of Neruda’s works at 54 Below on Tuesday evening, her beautiful but sometimes abrasive voice bit and scratched like a lover in the throes of uncontrollable passion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04LEMPER/04LEMPER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04LEMPER/04LEMPER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04LEMPER/04LEMPER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04LEMPER/04LEMPER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1321, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04LEMPER/04LEMPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04LEMPER/04LEMPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04LEMPER/04LEMPER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Passionate Version of Love That Scratches and Bites', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Passionate Version of Love That Scratches and Bites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lemper, Ute', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T20:54:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dff4190-a182-567d-87a6-84a8165bd08b', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dff4190-a182-567d-87a6-84a8165bd08b'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer’s first New York solo show in five years captures the dark side of the American dream.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/justine-kurland-sincere-auto-care-photographs-of-men-and-cars/', 'snippet': 'The photographer’s first New York solo show in five years captures the dark side of the American dream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than a decade, Justine Kurland has taken photographs during annual cross-country journeys from New York to the Pacific Northwest that reveal the double-edged nature of the American dream. A lifelong nomad (she grew up traveling to Renaissance festivals, where her mother sold hand-sewn clothes), her tools are her 4×5 camera and her van, which allow her to dwell, briefly, in the worlds of the marginal figures she photographs. First, there were the girls she cast as runaways, forging into forests and swimming holes. Later came images of commune members in wilderness idylls and panoramas of westbound freighters and the hobos who ride them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justine Kurland’s Vivid, Haunting Photographs of Men and Cars', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kurland, Justine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T21:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Bengal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bengal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd9c7733-1467-5e58-9407-6d9a39e88be0', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd9c7733-1467-5e58-9407-6d9a39e88be0'}, {'abstract': 'Flight Tonight, a new digital application, provides travelers with a search service to find the most affordable flight leaving from a nearby airport in the next 24 hours.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/03/an-app-for-last-minute-flights/', 'snippet': 'Flight Tonight, a new digital application, provides travelers with a search service to find the most affordable flight leaving from a nearby airport in the next 24 hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Travelers who dig the spontaneity that services like Hotel Tonight afford will be happy to hear that the last-minute booking game has expanded to airline apps as well.', 'source': 'The New York 