ame': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d23efc37-afe8-56a9-ae7a-e9552e7a3d22', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d23efc37-afe8-56a9-ae7a-e9552e7a3d22'}, {'abstract': 'As cameras for animals become more readily available, pet photography is exploding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/garden/here-ansel-sit-avedon.html', 'snippet': 'As cameras for animals become more readily available, pet photography is exploding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWPORT, R.I. — It was in 2007 that Juergen Perthold, an engineer living in Anderson, S.C., strapped a tiny camera of his own design to the collar of his cat, Mr. Lee. When the images Mr. Lee captured while roaming around their neighborhood were posted online, they went, predictably, viral. Mr. Lee received a flurry of attention from the international media and became the star of a documentary, “CatCam: The Movie,” which made the film festival rounds in 2012 and even won a few awards.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/garden/04PETCAM/04PETCAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/04/garden/04PETCAM/04PETCAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/garden/04PETCAM/04PETCAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/garden/04PETCAM/04PETCAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/garden/04PETCAM/04PETCAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/04/garden/04PETCAM/04PETCAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/garden/04PETCAM/04PETCAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Here, Ansel! Sit, Avedon!', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here, Ansel! Sit, Avedon!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Penelope', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keeney, Chris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'PetCam: The World Through the Lens of Our Four-Legged Friends (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GoPro', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keeney, Chris', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T21:41:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Penelope Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Penelope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/695846d7-4ade-5603-bfdc-44da8110c05e', 'word_count': 2354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/695846d7-4ade-5603-bfdc-44da8110c05e'}, {'abstract': 'A self-appointed guardian of the neighborhood’s vanishing history turns his home into a museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/garden/in-his-basement-the-bowery.html', 'snippet': 'A self-appointed guardian of the neighborhood’s vanishing history turns his home into a museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Woodward rarely leaves his Lower East Side neighborhood, and then only grudgingly. He hates the thought of missing even the smallest change on one of the strangest and most historic thoroughfares in the country, the 400-year-old stretch of road known as the Bowery, which has seen more than its share of demolition and transformation in recent years.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In His Basement, the Bowery', 'kicker': 'House Proud', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In His Basement, the Bowery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bowery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keenan, Sandy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodward, Adam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T21:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandy Keenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3137b279-4d53-5e12-8b3d-325536481d46', 'word_count': 1536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3137b279-4d53-5e12-8b3d-325536481d46'}, {'abstract': 'In the Hamptons, a home set in an “acoustical shadow” is spared nearby traffic noise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/greathomesanddestinations/a-house-built-to-baffle.html', 'snippet': 'In the Hamptons, a home set in an “acoustical shadow” is spared nearby traffic noise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took this reporter a few minutes to realize what was missing from the house that Paul Masi, owner of the architecture firm Bates-Masi, built two years ago for his family. While their three young children played upstairs, Mr. Masi and his wife, Liz, both 42, sat at a table in the open kitchen and living area, explaining their initial concern about building on the half-acre lot in the center of town, which they bought for $840,000 in 2012. It was when Mr. Masi mentioned the proximity to the main drag that everything clicked.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A House Built to Baffle', 'kicker': 'On Location: Amagansett, N.Y.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A House Built to Baffle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAGANSETT (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bates Masi + Architects LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T21:41:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64989c6f-63a8-5826-b451-6df88c359a9e', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64989c6f-63a8-5826-b451-6df88c359a9e'}, {'abstract': 'The Minnesota State Fair is a reliable source of mind-blowing handicrafts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/garden/your-grandmas-maker-faire.html', 'snippet': 'The Minnesota State Fair is a reliable source of mind-blowing handicrafts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FALCON HEIGHTS, Minn. — In the 12 days leading up to Labor Day, more than 1.8 million visitors attended a design expo that has been held annually since 1859. Granted, most of them didn’t know they were attending a design expo; they came for the midway or the mini-doughnuts. But as a popular showcase for American vernacular design, the Minnesota State Fair wins the blue ribbon.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Grandma’s Maker Faire', 'kicker': 'Design Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Your Grandma’s Maker Faire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorello, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conventions, Fairs and Trade Shows', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T21:42:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tortorello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tortorello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/662a6571-27cf-5f8d-964f-e4c1a6902e64', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/662a6571-27cf-5f8d-964f-e4c1a6902e64'}, {'abstract': 'With movies like “Nightcrawler,” the Toronto International Film Festival finds its sweet spot among slightly complex would-be crowd pleasers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/movies/nightcrawler-with-jake-gyllenhaal-epitomizes-toronto-film-festival-fare.html', 'snippet': 'With movies like “Nightcrawler,” the Toronto International Film Festival finds its sweet spot among slightly complex would-be crowd pleasers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The actor Jake Gyllenhaal recently explained Lou Bloom, the twisted crime videographer he portrays in the movie “Nightcrawler,” which is set for a world premiere on Friday night at the Toronto International Film Festival. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04SWEETSPOT/04SWEETSPOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04SWEETSPOT/04SWEETSPOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04SWEETSPOT/04SWEETSPOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04SWEETSPOT/04SWEETSPOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1300, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04SWEETSPOT/04SWEETSPOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/04/arts/04SWEE