l will include the debut of the Argentine visual artist Fernando Rubio, and present works by Trajal Harrell and Xavier Le Roy, among others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Crossing the Line, a playful and probing interdisciplinary festival now in its eighth year, hosts an array of artists who refuse to be bottled up and labeled. The pickings are eclectic, from the debut of the Argentine director and visual artist Fernando Rubio, who places seven actresses in white beds in Hudson River Park — in 10-minute cycles, they whisper memories to audience members — to Xavier Le Roy’s sophisticated yet accessible exhibition of movement and conversation, “Retrospective,” at MoMA PS1 in Long Island City, Queens. In other words, Crossing the Line, which runs from Sept. 8 through Oct. 20 at various New York locations and is presented by the French Institute Alliance Française, is nothing if not an adventure. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07SEIBERT1/07SEIBERT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 200, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07SEIBERT1/07SEIBERT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 200}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07SEIBERT1/07SEIBERT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 318, 'width': 956, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07SEIBERT1/07SEIBERT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 318, 'width': 956, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07SEIBERT1/07SEIBERT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07SEIBERT1/07SEIBERT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fest Packed With Artists Bursting Out of the Box', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fest Packed With Artists Bursting Out of the Box', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrell, Trajal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Roy, Xavier', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-03T23:04:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daab7fc8-ec31-5c2e-b5b7-acefe57738af', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daab7fc8-ec31-5c2e-b5b7-acefe57738af'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographers Kyle Abraham and Jodi Melnick seem ready to make a splash this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/arts/dance/fall-arts-preview-premieres-ahead-from-kyle-abraham-and-jodi-melnick.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographers Kyle Abraham and Jodi Melnick seem ready to make a splash this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If much is expected of those to whom much is given, then the pressure on the choreographer Kyle Abraham is mounting. Since the 2010 debut of his first full-length piece, “The Radio Show,” the high-profile offers and lucrative prizes have been piling up. He has gotten commissions from the Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater and the ballerina Wendy Whelan. On top of many other awards, he was named — in 2013, at 36 — a MacArthur Fellow, an honor that comes with $625,000 and the connotation of “genius.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07KOURLAS/07KOURLAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07KOURLAS/07KOURLAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07KOURLAS/07KOURLAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07KOURLAS/07KOURLAS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1368, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07KOURLAS/07KOURLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07KOURLAS/07KOURLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07KOURLAS/07KOURLAS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Couple of Genius Moves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Couple of Genius Moves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abraham, Kyle (1977- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'v