son': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40a8f701-f738-5c56-bbd7-8bc647401f20', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40a8f701-f738-5c56-bbd7-8bc647401f20'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio’s campaign promised free prekindergarten for every 4-year-old, and his administration has invested mightily in quickly bringing that plan to life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/nyregion/final-touches-range-from-flowery-to-frantic-as-expanded-pre-k-awaits-start.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio’s campaign promised free prekindergarten for every 4-year-old, and his administration has invested mightily in quickly bringing that plan to life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sounds of scissors slicing through construction paper and transparent tape being torn from rolls filled every room at the Kaleidoscope Early Childhood Development Center in Ditmas Park, Brooklyn, on Wednesday. After weeks of hiring teachers, filling seats and ordering furniture, the Kaleidoscope staff was putting the finishing decorative touches on its classrooms, readying for the first day of Mayor Bill de Blasio’s signature initiative: a vast expansion of full-day prekindergarten.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/nyregion/PREK/PREK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/04/nyregion/PREK/PREK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/nyregion/PREK/PREK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_n