idents who wanted their final resting place to be in the old village cemetery, it was yet another Spanish investment plan that failed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/world/ARTSVILLAGE-2/ARTSVILLAGE-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/04/world/ARTSVILLAGE-2/ARTSVILLAGE-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/world/ARTSVILLAGE-2/ARTSVILLAGE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/world/ARTSVILLAGE-2/ARTSVILLAGE-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/world/ARTSVILLAGE-2/ARTSVILLAGE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/04/world/ARTSVILLAGE-2/ARTSVILLAGE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/world/ARTSVILLAGE-2/ARTSVILLAGE-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Lure Tourists, a Remote Village in Spain Turns Its Eye to the Arts', 'kicker': 'Genalguacil Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Lure Tourists, a Remote Village in Spain Turns Its Eye to the Arts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Genalguacil (Spain)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T00:57:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf999ce9-d038-576e-a0c7-5400b23c177f', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf999ce9-d038-576e-a0c7-5400b23c177f'}, {'abstract': 'Two new rules issued by the Securities and Exchange Commission are only modest improvements to a process that requires substantial reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/opinion/credit-rating-reform-comes-up-short.html', 'snippet': 'Two new rules issued by the Securities and Exchange Commission are only modest improvements to a process that requires substantial reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the center of the financial crisis was the corrupted process by which bad mortgages were packaged into toxic securities with stellar credit ratings. The credit rating agencies that gave out those high grades were paid by the banks, which securitized the loans and sold them to investors. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Credit Rating Reform Comes Up Short ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Credit Rating Reform Comes Up Short', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T01:07:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a56022f0-7d2d-5bd4-9c25-f79e92b46f6f', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a56022f0-7d2d-5bd4-9c25-f79e92b46f6f'}, {'abstract': 'News outlets had sought to unseal any court records that might exist for Michael Brown. Also Wednesday, Missouri’s governor lifted the orders establishing a state of emergency and activating the National Guard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/us/michael-brown-never-faced-serious-felony-charge-st-louis-officials-lawyer-says.html', 'snippet': 'News outlets had sought to unseal any court records that might exist for Michael Brown. Also Wednesday, Missouri’s governor lifted the orders establishing a state of emergency and activating the National Guard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FERGUSON, Mo. — Michael Brown, the unarmed black teenager shot and killed by a white police officer here last month, had no serious felony cases filed against him as a juvenile, a lawyer for a St. Louis County official said Wednesday.', 'print_sec