-african-sounds.html', 'snippet': 'The Ubuntu festival, featuring the trumpeter Hugh Masekela, the pianist Abdullah Ibrahim and the soprano Pretty Yende, will run from Oct. 8 through Nov. 5.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ubuntu: loosely, “I am because you are.” This fall, the Nguni Bantu term for human kindness, in usage across South Africa, becomes the rallying cry for Carnegie Hall’s festival dedicated to the music of that nation. As such, it celebrates a sense of community that has been tested for much of that country’s recent history, and that continues to be redefined today, 20 years after the arrival of democracy.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07CORINNA1/07CORINNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07CORINNA1/07CORINNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07CORINNA1/07CORINNA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07CORINNA1/07CORINNA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07CORINNA1/07CORINNA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07CORINNA1/07CORINNA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credi