rospect, long after you’ve seen them, when they’ve been absorbed into the memory to seem sweeter, wiser, more magical than anything ever does in its own time,” Vincent Canby wrote in The New York Times. “This immediate resonance is the distinguishing feature of this superb film, which is both quintessential Bergman and unlike anything else he has ever done before.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a84154f-e08b-5250-abd3-21e967b3aa67', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a84154f-e08b-5250-abd3-21e967b3aa67'}, {'abstract': 'The new season comes with five standout performances from recent Hollywood arrivals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/movies/fall-arts-preview-teyonah-parris-katherine-waterston-and-others-break-through.html', 'snippet': 'The new season comes with five standout performances from recent Hollywood arrivals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katherine Waterston, “Inherent Vice”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '58', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07FACES3/07FACES3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07FACES3/07FACES3-articleLarge.j