aph': 'The Mattress Firm Holding Corporation, one of the country’s big sellers of Sealy and Serta mattresses, has agreed to acquire a West Coast rival, the Sleep Train chain, for about $425 million, solidifying its position as the biggest mattress retailer in the country.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mattress Firm Holding to Buy Rival Sleep Train', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Buying a Rival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mattresses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mattress Firm Holding Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sleep Train', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T13:23:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gelles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0719abc5-4699-5e69-8abe-5f51f4e620a2', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0719abc5-4699-5e69-8abe-5f51f4e620a2'}, {'abstract': 'Nationwide protests took place in about 150 cities, including New York, organizers said, with workers and their labor allies demanding a $15-an-hour wage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/business/economy/fast-food-workers-seeking-higher-wages-are-arrested-during-sit-ins.html', 'snippet': 'Nationwide protests took place in about 150 cities, including New York, organizers said, with workers and their labor allies demanding a $15-an-hour wage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hundreds of fast-food workers and labor allies demanding a $15-an-hour wage were arrested in sit-ins around the country on Thursday, as the protesters used civil disobedience to call attention to their cause. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hundreds of Fast-Food Workers Striking for Higher Wages Are Arrested', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hundreds of Fast-Food Workers Striking for Higher Wages Are Arrested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenhouse, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Service Employees International Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T13:33:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/436e8680-e256-5137-b47c-1ec6b98af199', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/436e8680-e256-5137-b47c-1ec6b98af199'}, {'abstract': 'The supply of models is inexhaustible: Don’t worry; they’ll make more.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/the-genetically-blessed-of-fashion-week/', 'snippet': 'The supply of models is inexhaustible: Don’t worry; th