le', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough and Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/277875df-5878-598c-8d62-4f27e902e0e3', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/277875df-5878-598c-8d62-4f27e902e0e3'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: French tourists were not impressed with New York in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/1964-new-york-disappoints-french/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: French tourists were not impressed with New York in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — French tourists find New York not worth more than a four-day stay, the afternoon newspaper ‘‘Paris-Presse’’ said today [Sept. 4]. Among their complaints according to the paper’s New York correspondent are that they catch cold from the air-conditioning, to which they are unaccustomed, that there is nothing worth seeing in New York aside from the three major museums, that the World’s Fair is too hot and over-commercialized, that there are no bidets in hotel rooms, and that no one understands French. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 5, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: New York Disappoints French', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "World's Fair of 1964-65 (NYC)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T14:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5fdfa5f-45f5-5f17-a247-b5bcac72ff81', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5fdfa5f-45f5-5f17-a247-b5bcac72ff81'}, {'abstract': 'Mario Draghi, the European Central Bank president, announced that the bank would cut interest rates to an all-time low.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000003091292/european-central-bank-president-on-rates.html', 'snippet': 'Mario Draghi, the European Central Bank president, announced that the bank would cut interest rates to an all-time low.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mario Draghi, the European Central Bank president, announced that the bank would cut interest rates to an all-time low.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/multimedia/ecb-cuts-rates/ecb-cuts-rates-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/04/multimedia/ecb-cuts-rates/ecb-cuts-rates-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/multimedia/ecb-cuts-rates/ecb-cuts-rates-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/multimedia/ecb-cuts-rat