, whom a studio wants to digitize for posterity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/movies/robin-wright-stars-in-the-congress.html', 'snippet': 'Ari Folman’s allegorical movie “The Congress” stars Robin Wright as a midcareer actress named Robin Wright, whom a studio wants to digitize for posterity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ari Folman’s genre mash-up “The Congress” could use a freakier title, something either more appealing or appalling to go with the weird, sometimes wonderful visions flowing through it. Not that it’s all entirely strange. There’s the opening image, for starters — a close-up of Robin Wright’s face, a familiar, delicate facade that’s well enough known to ignite a chain of signification: beauty, actress, star, Sean Penn, “House of Cards,” “The Princess Bride,” middle age, under-sung, career rebirth. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/arts/05CONGRESS/05CONGRESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 323, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/05/arts/05CONGRESS/05CONGRESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 323}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/arts/05CONGRESS/05CONGRESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 551, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/arts/05CONGRESS/05CONGRESS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1076, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/arts/05CONGRESS/05CONGRESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name'