iven by a desperation that was all her own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Her delivery was like an automatic sprinkler: fast, relentless and sometimes prone to stick, soaking a comic riff into a muddy swamp.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Relentless, With No Off Switch', 'kicker': 'An Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relentless, With No Off Switch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanley, Alessandra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivers, Joan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T19:45:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'An Appraisal', '_id': 'nyt://article/69050215-6102-5720-b6d6-e4fb3a8bee9b', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69050215-6102-5720-b6d6-e4fb3a8bee9b'}, {'abstract': 'A musical adaptation of “Doctor Zhivago” is expected to begin performances at the Broadway Theater in the spring of 2015, with another new musical, “King Kong,” in discussions to move into that theater after the “Zhivago” run ends.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/doctor-zhivago-musical-coming-to-broadway/', 'snippet': 'A musical adaptation of “Doctor Zhivago” is expected to begin performances at the Broadway Theater in the spring of 2015, with another new musical, “King Kong,” in discussions to move into that theater after the “Zhivago” run ends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A musical adaptation of “Doctor Zhivago” is expected to begin performances at the Broadway Theater in the spring of 2015, with another new musical, “King Kong,” in discussions to move into that theater after the “Zhivago” run ends, according to three theater executives familiar with the plans. The Broadway, a prime house for musicals, is coming open with Wednesday’s announcement that “Rodgers & Hammerstein’s Cinderella” will close on Jan. 3.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Doctor Zhivago’ Musical Coming to Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Doctor Zhivago’ To Move to Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T19:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ecad8e6-cb42-5b13-953b-fa65d88b65de', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ecad8e6-cb42-5b13-953b-fa65d88b65de'}, {'abstract': 'Microsoft and two trade groups for German publishers said the plan to reduce Google’s dominance of the search market was inadequate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/technology/opposition-grows-in-europe-to-google-antitrust-proposal.html', 'snippet': 'Microsoft and two trade groups for German publishers said the plan to reduce Google’s dominance of the search market was inadequate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Microsoft and the German publishing industry on Thursday stepped up pressure on the European Union’s antitrust chief to make radical adjustments to a proposed antitrust settlement with Google, or effectively leave resolution of the case to his successor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/technology/05eugoogle-pic/05eugoogle-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/05/technology/05eugoogle-pic/05eugoogle-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/technology/05eugoogle-pic/05eugoogle-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/technology/05eugoogle-pic/05eugoogle-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1331, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/technology/05eugoogle-pic/05eugoogle-pic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/05/technology/05eugoogle-pic/05eugoogle-pic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/technology/05eugoogle-pic/05eugoogle-pic-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Opposition Grows in Europe to Google Antitrust Proposal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oppposition Grows in Europe to Google Antitrust Proposal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almunia, Joaquin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T19:56:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8162013-0497-57ec-a317-e6baf32c3bac', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8162013-0497-57ec-a317-e6baf32c3bac'}, {'abstract': 'Why the West’s response to Putin should draw bright lines without courting reckless war.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/for-nato-yes-for-kiev-no/', 'snippet': 'Why the West’s response to Putin should draw bright lines without courting reckless war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last few weeks, heavier Russian incursions into the Ukrainian east reversed Ukraine’s push to reclaim its separatist provinces, and over the last week\xa0the West has responded — with a French decision to (finally) suspend a promised warship sale to Russia; with news that the upcoming NATO conference will consider the creation of a new rapid reaction force for Eastern Europe; and\xa0with a forceful Obama speech\xa0this week in Tallinn, Estonia, that both condemned Russian aggression and strongly reaffirmed NATO’s official commitment to the defense of the Baltic states. And these Western steps may (or may not, who can say?) have influenced Moscow’s sudden enthusiasm for a cease-fire and peace talks … albeit, of course,\xa0on terms favorable to Vladimir Putin’s desire to keep Ukraine divided, Russian-influenced and weak.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For NATO Yes, For Kiev No', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Applebaum, Anne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mead, Walter Russell', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eastern Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Estonia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tallinn (Estonia)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Warsaw (Poland)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T19:58:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4f8af48-9daa-505a-9629-470c8170b8af', 'word_count': 1353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4f8af48-9daa-505a-9629-470c8170b8af'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s winners have tackled themes from South Africa’s post-apartheid generation to the lives of Arab women.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/getty-grants-for-personal-photo-projects/', 'snippet