ation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d6b58d6-6b81-595c-99e8-d2bf0dd9e0ad', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d6b58d6-6b81-595c-99e8-d2bf0dd9e0ad'}, {'abstract': 'In this corner of the Adirondacks, elements of modern life yield to more timeless pursuits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/travel/refuge-and-renewal-on-lake-george.html', 'snippet': 'In this corner of the Adirondacks, elements of modern life yield to more timeless pursuits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the fireflies, and the stars, that get me every time. Those winking lights, bobbing along the ground and filling up the night sky with their impossible density, signal an alternate reality to the artificially haloed urban evening I’m accustomed to in the San Francisco Bay Area. In this little corner of the Adirondack Mountains, other signals — cellphone, for one, or car headlights — are spotty, or altogether absent. Much of modern life is filtered out through the dense trees and mountains on the winding approach to Lake George. What remains — a place to run around in the woods — is time-tested and true.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-favorite-top/07-favorite-top-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-favorite-top/07-favorite-top-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-favorite-top/07-favorite-top-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/