e': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wearable Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Garmin Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T20:32:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Albert Sun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Albert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68ae1e93-5f64-539d-b6ca-7764afbf5c8d', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68ae1e93-5f64-539d-b6ca-7764afbf5c8d'}, {'abstract': 'Marin Cilic reached his first Grand Slam semifinal in four years. Bob and Mike Bryan are in the men’s doubles final, and Martina Hingis advanced to the women’s doubles final with Flavia Pennetta.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/sports/tennis/us-open-bob-and-mike-bryan-tomas-berdych-marin-cilic.html', 'snippet': 'Marin Cilic reached his first Grand Slam semifinal in four years. Bob and Mike Bryan are in the men’s doubles final, and Martina Hingis advanced to the women’s doubles final with Flavia Pennetta.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than four years have passed since Marin Cilic’s last Grand Slam semifinal appearance, an eternity in tennis years. The span included the peak of Cilic’s years as a Croatian prodigy, a player graced with size and skill, but he never seemed to live up to the promise. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/sports/tennis/05openday3/05openday3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/05/sports/tennis/05openday3/05openday3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/sports/tennis/05openday3/05openday3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/sports/tennis/05openday3/05openday3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1288, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/sports/tennis/05openday3/05openday3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/05/sports/tennis/05openday3/05openday3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/sports/tennis/05openday3/05openday3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marin Cilic Reaches U.S. Open Semifinals; Bryan Brothers and Martina Hingis Close In on Doubles Titles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rejuvenated Cilic Reaches Semifinals; Bryans Close In on 100th Title', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryan, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryan, Bob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T20:33:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c00b4e8-6e79-5276-9ad7-17aea413e933', 'word_count': 1278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c00b4e8-6e79-5276-9ad7-17aea413e933'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge on Thursday said Ohio could not cut the voting period.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/04/early-voting-in-ohio-despite-republican-objections/', 'snippet': 'A federal judge on Thursday said Ohio could not cut the voting period.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge’s decision this morning to allow early voting in Ohio is a big victory for those who think voting should be easier and more accessible. It was also a remarkable decision in purely human terms, showing a deeply compassionate understanding of the lives of the low-income people who have been the most harmed by Republican efforts to put barriers around the ballot box.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Voting in Ohio, Despite Republican Objections', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Economus, Peter C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T20:35:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0e0fb93-ff55-5bff-a326-e5c20a725570', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0e0fb93-ff55-5bff-a326-e5c20a725570'}, {'abstract': 'A show intends to criticize “Middle Eastern” and “Arab” stereotypes, but in some cases reinforces them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/arts/design/the-middle-east-revealed-a-female-perspective-and-syria-in-1940.html', 'snippet': 'A show intends to criticize “Middle Eastern” and “Arab” stereotypes, but in some cases reinforces them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The four-artist show called “The Middle East Revealed: A Female Perspective” is an apt addendum to the New Museum’s “Here and Elsewhere,” an exhibition of contemporary art from the Arab world. But this show deals in “Middle Eastern” and “Arab” stereotypes, intending to criticize them, but only, in some cases, reinforcing them.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/arts/05MIDDLEEASTGALLERY1/05MIDDLEEASTGALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/05/arts/05MIDDLEEASTGALLERY1/05MIDDLEEASTGALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/arts/05MIDDLEEASTGALLERY1/05MIDDLEEASTGALLERY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/arts/05MIDDLEEASTGALLERY1/05MIDDLEEASTGALLERY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1424, 'width': 1890, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/arts/05MIDDLEEASTGALLERY1/05MIDDLEEASTGALLERY1-thumbS