nding artist you’ve barely heard of. That thrill is currently provided by the American Folk Art Museum and its concise, electrifying survey of Willem van Genk, a Dutch self-taught outsider who died in 2005 at 78. In addition, this show is brilliantly paired with one devoted to the formidable folk painter and well-known New Yorker, Ralph Fasanella (1914-97), that focuses on what might be called his history paintings. The fertile exchange between these ambitious, encompassing visions is one of the best things you’ll see this fall.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Visionaries Inhabiting the Margins', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Visionaries Inhabiting the Margins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FOLK ART MUSEUM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fasanella, Ralph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Genk, Willem', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-04T20:52:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/613c2ed7-fe98-5987-bc28-4332a3c6a367', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/613c2ed7-fe98-5987-bc28-4332a3c6a367'}, {'abstract': 'Homes deemed unusual may be desirable for some to own, but even borrowers with excellent credit may have trouble obtaining sufficient financing to purchase them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/realestate/mortgage-problems-when-buying-outside-the-box.html', 'snippet'