are', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T00:53:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear and Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5a46168-3da5-5190-bef4-2ae257ad1bc2', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5a46168-3da5-5190-bef4-2ae257ad1bc2'}, {'abstract': 'Major League Soccer is running Chivas U.S.A. as it undergoes a rebranding and seeks a new owner and a stadium of its own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/sports/soccer/chivas-usa-trying-to-escape-mls-doldrums.html', 'snippet': 'Major League Soccer is running Chivas U.S.A. as it undergoes a rebranding and seeks a new owner and a stadium of its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARSON, Calif. — It was 20 minutes before kickoff, and the Commander stood ready. Richard Escuita, a retired Army sergeant who introduces himself by his nom de guerre, was dressed in black commando boots, military supply pants, black gloves, a black beret and a black Chivas de Guadalajara jersey. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Soccer Team Struggles to Remake Its Identity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An M.L.S. Team Struggles to Remake Its Identity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major