or the critically ill to save money on health care costs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Encouraging End-of-Life Talks', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Encouraging End-of-Life Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wills and Health Care Proxies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T01:53:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b330ef45-0f68-53e4-a27a-4a860388cb7f', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b330ef45-0f68-53e4-a27a-4a860388cb7f'}, {'abstract': 'Stouffer’s is trying to lure shoppers from the snack aisle with Mac Cups, a version of its popular macaroni and cheese in containers that are about the size of a single-serve yogurt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/business/blurring-line-between-snack-and-meal-mac-and-cheese-to-graze-on.html', 'snippet': 'Stouffer’s is trying to lure shoppers from the snack aisle with Mac Cups, a version of its popular macaroni and cheese in containers that are about the size of a single-serve yogurt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SITTING down to three square meals daily is going the way of the landline, as consumers increasingly graze throughout the day and eat what had once been standard between-meal fare like yogurt and granola bars as meals. Americans eat only snacks, including produce like fruit and cut vegetables, at mealtimes 40 percent of the time, and that is expected to increase over the next five years, according to the NPD Group, a market research firm.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/business/subAdco/subAdco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/05/business/subAdco/subAdco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/business/subAdco/subAdco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/business/subAdco/subAdco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1079, 'width': 1919, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/business/subAdco/subAdco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/05/business/subAdco/subAdco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/business/subAdco/subAdco-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blurring Line Between Snack and Meal, Mac and Cheese to Graze On', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kick