books filled with articles by and about him, photos and posters, have been donated to the Woody Guthrie Center, in Tulsa, Okla. The center is an archive and educational facility that opened in April 2013 with the goal of preserving not only Woody Guthrie’s materials – his complete archives are housed there – but also the archives of musicians and artists in other disciplines who were influenced by him.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phil Ochs Archives Go to Woody Guthrie Center', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Phil Ochs Archives Go to Guthrie Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guthrie, Woody', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ochs, Phil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tulsa (Okla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T14:42:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a4d9293-73a0-5901-af87-766937fa1862', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a4d9293-73a0-5901-af87-766937fa1862'}, {'abstract': 'The general music director, Franz Welser-Möst, cited “irreconcilable differences” for his decision and withdrew from all his scheduled performances there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/06/arts/design/vienna-state-operas-music-director-resigns.html', 'snippet': 'The general music director, Franz Welser-Möst, cited “irreconcilable differences” for his decision and withdrew from all his scheduled performances there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Vienna State Opera was thrown into turmoil just days after its new season began when its general music director, Franz Welser-Möst, abruptly resigned on Friday and withdrew from all his scheduled performances there, citing “irreconcilable differences of opinion regarding the company’s artistic planning and profile.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/arts/06OPERA/06OPERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/06/arts/06OPERA/06OPERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/arts/06OPERA/06OPERA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/arts/06OPERA/06OPERA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1289, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/arts/06OPERA/06OPERA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/06/arts/06OPERA/06OPERA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/arts/06OPERA/06OPERA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vienna State Opera’s Music Director Resigns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vienna State Opera’s Music Director Resigns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vienna State Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welser-Most, Franz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T14:43:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper and Rebecca Schmid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4cd43a1-3ad5-5be0-add1-a74015a4f807', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4cd43a1-3ad5-5be0-add1-a74015a4f807'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Italy prepares for a general mobilization in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/1914-italian-mobilization-expected/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Italy prepares for a general mobilization in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — It is said that a general mobilization is imminent, and that General Nava will immediately assume chief command of the Italian army. The order for the general mobilization has not yet been signed, but it is believed it will be signed during the day. In the meantime the mobilization is proceeding actively by means of individual orders. Throughout the kingdom enlisting is proceeding actively. On the other hand, despatches from Milan say that between Bozen and Franzens Feste travellers have noticed numerous entrenchments prepared by the Austrian army, armed with guns turned upon Italy. In the north of Venetia large Italian forces are ready to march. The despatch of an ultimatum to Austria is expected every minute. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 6, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1914: Italian Mobilization Expected', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T14:45:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18f06292-5279-5c92-8721-54c5cb2a1b67', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18f06292-5279-5c92-8721-54c5cb2a1b67'}, {'abstract': 'After the killing of a black teenager by a white police officer sparked a string of protests in Ferguson, Mo., the town is returning to a new normal as scars of the unrest remain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/us/ferguson-photos-after-the-protests.html', 'snippet': 'After the killing of a black teenager by a white police officer sparked a string of protests in Ferguson, Mo., the town is returning to a new normal as scars of the unrest remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly a month has passed since Michael Brown, an unarmed teenager, was fatally shot by a police officer, Darren Wilson, in Ferguson, Mo. The confrontation sparked a string of protests that lasted for more than a week. A small stretch of West Florissant Avenue, where businesses were looted and nightly protests would sometimes crescendo into violent clashes, became the backdrop for a national debate about racism and the militarization of police forces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wary ‘Normal’ in Ferguson, Mo.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Darren (1986- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T14:46:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Todd Heisler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Todd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heisler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd8bcb3b-5f3d-512a-929b-bf00c93bbf08', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd8bcb3b-5f3d-512a-929b-bf00c93bbf08'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to a recent review of William Deresiewicz’s “Excellent Sheep” and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/books/review/letters-poor-little-lambs.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to a recent review of William Deresiewicz’s “Excellent Sheep” and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Poor Little Lambs', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: Poor Little Lambs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 