: 'Information on sales in New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Information on sales in New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/realestate/07matrix-image/07matrix-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/realestate/07matrix-image/07matrix-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 653}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/realestate/07matrix-image/07matrix-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 941, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/realestate/07matrix-image/07matrix-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1882, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/realestate/07matrix-image/07matrix-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/realestate/07matrix-image/07matrix-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/realestate/07matrix-image/07matrix-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Home Sales Around the Region', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York Metropolitan Area', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T15:05:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/ddfb05a2-4322-5641-9b51-4d5fd739db19', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/ddfb05a2-4322-5641-9b51-4d5fd739db19'}, {'abstract': 'Frank and Ross debate the union of church and real estate in “Love Is Strange” and explore future dystopias in “The Giver.” And one columnists pleads: Stop giving actors extra credit for playing gay.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/watching-the-sun-set-on-the-summer-movie-season/', 'snippet': 'Frank and Ross debate the union of church and real estate in “Love Is Strange” and explore future dystopias in “The Giver.” And one columnists pleads: Stop giving actors extra credit for playing gay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Douthat: Now is the Indian summer of our moviegoing discontent, when the temperatures still feel appropriate to midsummer blockbusters but the studios are dumping dreck that would be more at home in the wintry graveyard of late January. (As well as satisfying the millions who were apparently clamoring for a “Forrest Gump” IMAX re-release.) But there are still interesting things to talk about, and I’ll start in with the movie that’s supposed to be the great exception to the current doldrums —\xa0“Love Is Strange,” in which John Lithgow and Alfred Molina play longtime companions who tie the knot, only to have Molina’s character lose his job as a music teacher at a Catholic school because the bishop found out about his nuptials, which forces them to sell their tastefully shabby New York apartment and crash (separately, miserably) with their relatives while they try to get on the list for a rent-controlled living situation, with various uncomfortable interpersonal consequences for everyone concerned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/MOVIE/MOVIE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/MOVIE/MOVIE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/MOVIE/MOVIE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1021, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/MOVIE/MOVIE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1662, 'width': 1667, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/MOVIE/MOVIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/MOVIE/MOVIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/04/blogs/MOVIE/MOVIE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching the Sun Set on the Summer Movie Season', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York (Magazine)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poughkeepsie (NY)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T15:10:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni and Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a160d1e5-6fe4-52a2-aa3a-bb49423dca27', 'word_count': 3026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a160d1e5-6fe4-52a2-aa3a-bb49423dca27'}, {'abstract': 'Damon Winter recently spoke about what it was like to photograph one of the wealthiest people in the world, and what it took to get him to crack a smile.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/under-cover-what-is-bill-gates-smiling-about/', 'snippet': 'Damon Winter recently spoke about what it was like to photograph one of the wealthiest people in the world, and what it took to get him to crack a smile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do an image search for Bill Gates, and you’ll find plenty of photos of him speaking at events but few formal portraits. So when Dan Winters, a photographer based in Austin, Tex., agreed to shoot Gates for the cover of the Sept. 7 Education Issue to accompany the story by Andrew Ross Sorkin, he knew he wanted to do it in classic portrait-style fashion — in a way that is “timeless and not pegged to any one time or concept,” as he put it. Recently, Winter spoke about what it took to get\xa0one of the wealthiest people in the world to crack a smile.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07cover_type/07cover_type-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07cover_type/07cover_type-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 730}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07cover_type/07cover_type-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 842, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07cover_type/07cover_type-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1683, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07cover_type/07cover_type-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07cover_type/07cover_type-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07cover_type/07cov