en Johnson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The filmmaker Ira Sachs’s two-bedroom apartment on lower Fifth Avenue, where he has lived for 15 years, is a much happier place than it used to be. He memorialized the sad times by using the art- and book-filled apartment as a primary location for his 2012 movie, “Keep the Lights On,” a fictionalized version of his tumultuous 10-year love affair with an addict.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Home and Occasional Film Set', 'kicker': 'What I Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Home and Occasional Film Set', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Ira', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fifth Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T16:19:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Shaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17399b66-42b9-5ad4-94a4-1be6dcef0aee', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17399b66-42b9-5ad4-94a4-1be6dcef0aee'}, {'abstract': 'Make Music New York will explore ethnic musical styles from around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/make-music-new-york-going-global-with-talk-series/', 'snippet': 'Make Music New York will explore ethnic musical styles from around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Make Music New York, the citywide festival that takes place on the summer and winter solstices, began experimenting in January with a new series, Make Music Monthly, at which public discussions of musical topics were presented at the Cornelia Street Café and were made available as podcasts on Make Music New York’s website.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Make Music New York Going Global With Talk Series', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Make Music New York Goes Global With Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Make Music New York (Festival)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Aaron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gutierrez, Juan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'London, Frank', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miura, Hiroya', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornelia Street Cafe', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T16:24:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/911465f4-adb9-5fd9-87b7-29c8f2c44c6d', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/911465f4-adb9-5fd9-87b7-29c8f2c44c6d'}, {'abstract': 'Scars from days of unrest remain along the main street in Ferguson, Mo., as residents and businesses try to get on with their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2014/09/05/us/FERGUSON-ss-nytnow.html', 'snippet': 'Scars from days of unrest remain along the main street in Ferguson, Mo., as residents and businesses try to get on with their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scars from days of un