': 'By Michael Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93ca67e4-8be6-5c03-8a68-674f4181f78f', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93ca67e4-8be6-5c03-8a68-674f4181f78f'}, {'abstract': 'A class from the Bear Grylls Survival Academy teaches participants tricks for negotiating the wild.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/travel/mud-worms-and-ropes-a-one-day-survival-course.html', 'snippet': 'A class from the Bear Grylls Survival Academy teaches participants tricks for negotiating the wild.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When foraging in the wild, one of the best reliable sources of protein is an earthworm. To serve: Use your fingers to wring the slime past the midsection. Snap off the bottom half — mostly intestines anyway — and put the rest in your mouth. Swallow quickly so it doesn’t wiggle on the way down. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-explorer-top/07-explorer-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-explorer-top/07-explorer-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-explorer-top/07-explorer-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/travel/07-explorer-top/07-explorer-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': '