ibery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T19:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Horowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/973660a4-17d1-5cc8-8aa6-67c5d2568f1c', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/973660a4-17d1-5cc8-8aa6-67c5d2568f1c'}, {'abstract': 'Whether they’re linked to leaked nude photos or a relatively tame bucket of ice, stunt-based philanthropic efforts have their critics.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/when-philanthropy-is-weird/', 'snippet': 'Whether they’re linked to leaked nude photos or a relatively tame bucket of ice, stunt-based philanthropic efforts have their critics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a strange week for philanthropy. Just as media outlets began assessing\xa0the effects of celebrities pouring ice on their heads for charity,\xa0Redditors\xa0decided to donate money in response to Jennifer Lawrence’s nude photos. The practice of linking charitable giving to other activities — some just odd, some ethically questionable — seems to be growing in prominence, with what some say are not entirely positive results.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/blogs/05ICE/05ICE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/05/blogs/05ICE/05ICE-