ade Me” video series by Poppy de Villeneuve, Anderer shares how his mom’s cooking and spending his junior year of college in Rome shaped his culinary sensibility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chef Nick Anderer on Rome, Pizza and His New Restaurant, Marta', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T20:15:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Poppy de Villeneuve', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Poppy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Villeneuve', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2923f731-a02a-5fb0-9bb4-f862fc293ad0', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2923f731-a02a-5fb0-9bb4-f862fc293ad0'}, {'abstract': 'Tuck, a longtime defensive standout with the Giants, is now with Oakland and will face the Jets on Sunday in East Rutherford, N.J.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/06/sports/football/justin-tuck-starting-over-in-a-familiar-setting.html', 'snippet': 'Tuck, a longtime defensive standout with the Giants, is now with Oakland and will face the Jets on Sunday in East Rutherford, N.J.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former Giant Justin Tuck wants to make the most of what may be a bleak season, starting Sunday against the Jets when he plays at MetLife Stadium for the first time as a member of the Oakland Raiders.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/sports/06jets/06jets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/06/sports/06jets/06jets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargew