lass Need?', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T21:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Altman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Altman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94e03f36-f17f-5c81-8a22-66df2327dbc6', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94e03f36-f17f-5c81-8a22-66df2327dbc6'}, {'abstract': 'They have always helped me. When I was young, my dog Poochie was my therapist.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/filling-the-empty-nest-with-animals/', 'snippet': 'They have always helped me. When I was young, my dog Poochie was my therapist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Within a week of dropping off our daughter at college, we brought home a puppy. The reason, I persuaded my husband, was to help her younger brother feel less alone — even though we already had two cats.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907CAT/0907CAT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 461, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907CAT/0907CAT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 461}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907CAT/0907CAT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 787, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907CAT/0907CAT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1575, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907CAT/0907CAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907CAT/0907CAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907CAT/0907CAT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Filling the Empty Nest With Animals', 'kicker': 'Menagerie', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Filling the Empty Nest With Animals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T21:37:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Salamon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Salamon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ea3ddc0-a170-5192-acdf-e7da305f67d9', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ea3ddc0-a170-5192-acdf-e7da305f67d9'}, {'abstract': 'Advice to help older adults avoid financial abuse from those they trust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/06/your-money/financial-schemes-against-the-elderly-are-increasing.html', 'snippet': 'Advice to help older adults avoid financial abuse from those they trust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN a longtime friend asked for a loan to help get her boyfriend back on his feet, Maria Voltl, 84, decided to help. Ms. Voltl had lent money to her friend before, and it had always been paid back. So without consulting a professional, she handed over $500,000.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/business/Retiring/Retiring-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/06/business/Retiring/Retiring-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/business/Retiring/Retiring-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/business/Retiring/Retiring-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/business/Retiring/Retiring-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStan