line': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bbf7769-4f7b-5892-8160-af85a308969a', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bbf7769-4f7b-5892-8160-af85a308969a'}, {'abstract': 'In recent years, New York-area lighthouses have been slowly rehabilitated, though in almost every case, their renovation and maintenance are being handled by people with little public funding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/nyregion/preserving-the-lighthouse-not-just-the-light.html', 'snippet': 'In recent years, New York-area lighthouses have been slowly rehabilitated, though in almost every case, their renovation and maintenance are being handled by people with little public funding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many of the people who grew up in Port Ewen, N.Y., about 100 miles north of New York City along the Hudson River, Pat Ralston has a deep affection for the Esopus Meadows lighthouse. Perched on pilings about a half-mile offshore from the neighboring town of Esopus, the squat, white-clapboard house with a red tin roof was a landmark, and its keepers — who often lived there with their families — were local celebrities.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preserving the Lighthouse, Not Just the Light', 'kicker': 'Arts | Restoration', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preserving the Lighthouse, Not Just the Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Risen, Clay', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighthouses and Lightships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and 