://slideshow/fde0597a-0199-5472-9cb1-085bc0d1a835'}, {'abstract': 'New bars, lounges and clubs that hope to lure the stylish pack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/fashion/max-fish-space-ibiza-ludlow-hotel-and-more-open-in-time-for-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'New bars, lounges and clubs that hope to lure the stylish pack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York night life is frequently maligned as sluggish and homogenized in comparison with its reckless past, but each September offers an opportunity for redemption. As usual, New York Fashion Week’s homecoming of debutantes and jet-setters coincides with a panoply of new options for depravity, each jostling for the fickle affections of the cool-kid aristocracy.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/fashion/07LAUNCH1/07LAUNCH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/fashion/07LAUNCH1/07LAUNCH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/fashion/07LAUNCH1/07LAUNCH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/fashion/07LAUNCH1/07LAUNCH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1499, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/fashion/07LAUNCH1/07LAUNCH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/fashion/07LAUNCH1/07LAUNCH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/fashion/07LAUNCH1/07LAUNCH1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Catwalk Leads to the Lounge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Catwalk Leads to the Lounge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Detrick, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September Fashion Week (2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T22:26:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Detrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Detrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28aea4a0-c4c0-545f-b3e1-ca32de20724f', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28aea4a0-c4c0-545f-b3e1-ca32de20724f'}, {'abstract': 'Two companies that bring together drivers of private cars and potential passengers have been battling over who provides insurance, and when.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/06/your-money/auto-insurance/offloading-the-risk-in-renting-a-car-ride.html', 'snippet': 'Two companies that bring together drivers of private cars and potential passengers have been battling over who provides insurance, and when.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a pervasive attitude in a prominent corner of the technology industry that goes something like this: If you’re helping people rent (not share, rent) spare bedrooms or rides in their cars, then the usual regulations and niggling insurance issues should not apply. Entrepreneurs start useful services, attract millions of users, cross their fingers and hope nobody dies before the government minders and other scolds catch up.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/business/06MONEY/06MONEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/06/business/06MONEY/06MONEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/business/06MONEY/06MONEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/business/06MONEY/06MONEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1192, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/business/06MONEY/06MONEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/06/business/06MONEY/06MONEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/business/06MONEY/06MONEY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Question of Coverage for Ride Service Drivers', 'kicker': 'Your Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Question of Coverage for Ride Service Drivers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieber, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lyft Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T22:32:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Insurance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f64e7b21-4323-52be-9e22-3124325deb9f', 'word_count': 1383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f64e7b21-4323-52be-9e22-3124325deb9f'}, {'abstract': 'The artist’s new show at Envoy Enterprises NYC includes a year’s worth of lunch and dinner napkins and sugar sculptures of body parts.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/martynka-wawrzyniak-turns-daily-meals-into-conceptual-art/', 'snippet': 'The artist’s new show at Envoy Enterprises NYC includes a year’s worth of lunch and dinner napkins and sugar sculptures of body parts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The artist Martynka Wawrzyniak has dedicated herself to “exposing and sharing very precise details of my daily private experiences,” she says. “It is up to the viewer to digest and interpret this collection of evidence and paint their own picture of my personality and lifestyle.” Beginning Sunday, her latest personal disclosure will hang from the ceiling of Envoy Enterprises NYC: a 100-foot-long polyester-cotton sculpture made from 365 dinner napkins stained with the imprint of Wawrzyniak’s lips during last year’s dinners. Nearby are 365 6-by-6-inch paper lunch napkins colored with mouth dabs following her morning consumption of vegan green juice. Both series are presented in chronological order — the fabric pieces sewn consecutively and the paper napkins framed in calendar formation. Connecting them thematically and corporally are castings of the interior of Wawrzyniak’s mouth and the hollow of her stomach made from sugar, a food that she avoids.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/t-magazine/05wawrzyniak-honigman/05wawrzyniak-honigman-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/05/t-magazine/05wawrzyniak-honigman/05wawrzyniak-honigman-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/t-magazine/05wawrzyniak-honigman/05wawrzyniak-honigman-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/t-magazine/05wawrzyniak-honigman/05wawrzyniak-honigman-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/05/t-magazine/05wawrzyniak-honigman/05wawrzyniak-honigman-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/0