': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'Christian Roman and Carrie Halperin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Carrie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Halperin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/8164f06c-3913-5db7-b2de-b77b5ed9ce33', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/8164f06c-3913-5db7-b2de-b77b5ed9ce33'}, {'abstract': 'It was a day filled with half-clothed male models, comments about shoes and tennis references. Here’s a recap of what happened, traced through the Styles staff’s Twitter feeds.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/05/new-york-fashion-week-social-media-roundup-day-2/', 'snippet': 'It was a day filled with half-clothed male models, comments about shoes and tennis references. Here’s a recap of what happened, traced through the Styles staff’s Twitter feeds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday night, celebrities, media personalities and other fashion fans gathered at spots across Manhattan to celebrate the first day of New York Fashion Week. Morning brought heat, humidity and half-clothed male models strutting down the Parke & Ronen runway, though few complained. Shoes remained a topic of conversation for our writers as the shows went on. At Jason Wu, a 3-D, living, breathing Karlie Kloss made her first appearance at Fashion Week, while at Rebecca Minkoff the entertainment factor was turned up high with unexpected props. Other shows, such as Cushnie et Ochs, Wes Gordon and Adam Selman, kept the day exciting, and tennis was on the minds of some. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Fashion Week Social Media Roundup, Day 2', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'nam