 United States Open is no longer super, with the women’s final moved to Sunday, but an afternoon of the men’s semifinals is still worthy of a pretty lofty adjective.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Open Men’s Semifinals Feature 2 Rejuvenated High Seeds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nishikori, Kei', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cilic, Marin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-05T23:41:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2957b9bb-2109-5bfd-8086-3bbbe46d1df5', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2957b9bb-2109-5bfd-8086-3bbbe46d1df5'}, {'abstract': 'A look at two books on education issues in New York City and a newly reissued 1964 guidebook.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/nyregion/lessons-in-brooklyn-harlem-and-whimsy.html', 'snippet': 'A look at two books on education issues in New York City and a newly reissued 1964 guidebook.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Think of them as back-to-school bookends to the last half-century of desperate and sometimes self-destructive debate over educational policy in New York. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank'