deral court about a meeting with former Gov. John G. Rowland that led to Mr. Rowland’s hiring as a campaign consultant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW HAVEN — When Lisa Wilson-Foley, a Republican political hopeful in Connecticut, entered the 2012 congressional race, she and her husband, Brian Foley, had lots of money but not necessarily the political seasoning of some of her rivals.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/nyregion/06ROWLAND/06ROWLAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/06/nyregion/06ROWLAND/06ROWLAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 705}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/nyregion/06ROWLAND/06ROWLAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 872, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/nyregion/06ROWLAND/06ROWLAND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1158, 'width': 985, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/nyregion/06ROWLAND/06ROWLAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/06/nyregion/06ROWLAND/06ROWLAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/nyregion/06ROWLAND/06ROWLAND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Connecticut Ex-Governor’s Trial, a Window Onto Political Strategizing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Connecticut Ex-Governor’s Trial, a Window Onto Political Strategizing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowland, John G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foley, Brian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson-Foley, Lisa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-06T02:12:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Leigh Cowan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Cowan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e445943-ab45-5e88-b228-390f9b8016d1', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e445943-ab45-5e88-b228-390f9b8016d1'}, {'abstract': 'Japan’s health minister on Friday urged the public not to panic after a popular park in central Tokyo was closed because of a rare outbreak of dengue fever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/06/world/asia/rare-outbreak-of-dengue-fever-in-japan.html', 'snippet': 'Japan’s health minister on Friday urged the public not to panic after a popular park in central Tokyo was closed because of a rare outbreak of dengue fever.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Japan’s health minister on Friday urged the public not to panic after a popular park in central Tokyo was closed because of a rare outbreak of dengue fever. The Ministry of Health said that 70 people had been found infected with the dengue virus in the past week, in what it called the first outbreak in Japan since 1945. Dengue, which causes fevers and in rare cases death, is common in tropical climates, but not in temperate Japan. Officials said global warming might be playing a role in the spread of dengue to places like Tokyo. This year, Japan had an unusually hot and humid summer. The ministry said most of the people found infected had spent time in or near Yoyogi Park, where they were most likely bitten by mosquitoes that carried the disease. On Friday, health workers sprayed pesticides in the park to kill the insects. No one has died in the outbreak. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rare Outbreak of Dengue Fever in Japan', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan: Rare Outbreak of Dengue Fever', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dengue Fever', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-06T02:14:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a7ff98e-f96e-5233-ae2b-e46cfca7bbf2', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a7ff98e-f96e-5233-ae2b-e46cfca7bbf2'}, {'abstract': 'The important news was the convergence of a NATO summit meeting, the beginnings of a cease-fire in Ukraine and the commitment to destroy ISIS.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/opinion/sunday/a-65-ton-dinosaur-as-a-distraction-from-nato-ukraine-and-isis.html', 'snippet': 'The important news was the convergence of a NATO summit meeting, the beginnings of a cease-fire in Ukraine and the commitment to destroy ISIS.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The important news was the convergence of a NATO summit meeting, the beginnings of a cease-fire in Ukraine and the commitment to destroy ISIS. Those events will shape the world. The news that won’t change anything is the discovery of a humongous dinosaur, and yet that may have been the most compelling story.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907SERGE/0907SERGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907SERGE/0907SERGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907SERGE/0907SERGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907SERGE/0907SERGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907SERGE/0907SERGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907SERGE/0907SERGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/sunday-review/0907SERGE/0907SERGE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A 65-