ments set the stage for Roberto Rossellini’s 1945 neorealist masterpiece, “Rome Open City.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/movies/rossellinis-eternal-city.html', 'snippet': 'Many elements set the stage for Roberto Rossellini’s 1945 neorealist masterpiece, “Rome Open City.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many elements set the stage for Roberto Rossellini’s 1945 neorealist\xa0masterpiece, “Rome Open City,” his portrait of the Italian resistance under the Nazis, coming to Film Forum on Friday for two weeks in a new restoration. A city pockmarked by bombs and wartime poverty offered a gritty backdrop; Rossellini assembled a formidable crew, including Federico Fellini as a screenwriter and the actors Aldo Fabrizi and Anna Magnani (both better known for comic roles at the time); and he was ready to doff studio confinements and shoot on streets and rooftops to capture a documentarylike veracity.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1466, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rossellini’s Eternal City', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film: Rossellini’s Eternal City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rossellini, Roberto', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-06T16:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5853f07-fb99-505f-b350-91e0d1b5ea45', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5853f07-fb99-505f-b350-91e0d1b5ea45'}, {'abstract': 'Calligraphy has always been the premier classical art of the Islamic world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/arts/design/calligraphy-as-visual-poetry.html', 'snippet': 'Calligraphy has always been the premier classical art of the Islamic world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Calligraphy has always been the premier classical art of the Islamic world, and it comes in many forms, some practical and workaday, others subtly expressive, reserved for religious texts and poetry. When produced by highly skilled hands, the style called “nasta’liq,” developed in Persia from the 14th to 16th centuries, is considered so beautiful as to be an aesthetic end in itself: Use it to copy a page from the phone book, and you’d still have visual poetry.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 878, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 878}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 700, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Calligraphy as Visual Poetry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art: Calligraphy as Visual Poetry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian Institution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-06T16:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_na