well before the tournament was over.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/crosswords/chess/feat-of-historic-proportions-for-an-italian-grandmaster.html', 'snippet': 'Fabiano Caruana won his first seven games at the Sinquefield Cup in St. Louis and wrapped up the title well before the tournament was over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fabiano Caruana turned in one of the most dominant performances in the game’s history at the Sinquefield Cup in St. Louis. He won his first seven games and clinched first place long before the tournament ended on Saturday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feat of Historic Proportions for an Italian Grandmaster', 'kicker': 'Chess', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feat of Historic Proportions for an Italian Grandmaster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClain, Dylan Loeb', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caruana, Fabiano', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-07T00:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86fbf316-b98a-5faf-9823-09df11f64bb5', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86fbf316-b98a-5faf-9823-09df11f64bb5'}, {'abstract': 'A day trip to a troubled district with America’s elite troops and Afghan government and military officials was characterized by the absurd and unexpected, features of the war in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/world/asia/building-good-will-in-afghanistan-but-not-without-a-fight.html', 'snippet': 'A day trip to a troubled district with America’s elite troops and Afghan government and military officials was characterized by the absurd and unexpected, features of the war in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AZRA, Afghanistan — It was hard to place the thick scent filtering into the American military helicopter as it landed here on a recent summer day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Building Good Will in a Troubled Afghan District, but Not Without a Fight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Building Good Will in a Troubled Afghan District, but Not Without a Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmed, Azam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riga, Christopher N', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afghan National Police', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-07T00:28:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/315fe68e-ffa8-55f6-a18b-752ea6c98cbc', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/315fe68e-ffa8-55f6-a18b-752ea6c98cbc'}, {'abstract': 'The hairstylist Guido Palau put a high-gloss spin on the classic gymnasium ‘do.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/06/the-trick-behind-the-sporty-ponytails-at-alexander-wang/', 'snippet': 'The hairstylist Guido Palau put a high-gloss spin on the classic gymnasium ‘do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Athletic shoes have a cultish appeal among fashion designers, and it would seem that beauty pros are similarly obsessed. Backstage at Alexander Wang this afternoon, both the hair and makeup teams talked about trainers as the inspiration behind the slicked-back, sporty looks given to the models. “It started with a fetish about sneakers,” said the makeup artist Diane Kendal of her conversation with the designer. “There were references to Stan Smith, Michael Jordan, New Balance.” The hairstylist Guido Palau ran with that concept, putting a new spin on the classic gymnasium ponytail. “It’s a bit futuristic,” he said of the low-slung style. “The tail is dry but there is a high gloss to the head.” Palau’s technique involved tightly combing back strands with generous amounts of Redken Hardwear 16 Super Strong Hair Gel around the crown, then misting Redken Diamond Oil High Shine Airy Mist (available in October) all over to provide a glistening effect. To finish, he secured hair with a simple black tie at the nape. “I can’t really move my neck too much!” joked the model Mari of the ultra-sleek result. Still, she proved to be a good sport. “But I can’t wait to see how it will look on the runway.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/t-magazine/06beauty-wang/06beauty-wang-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/06/t-magazine/06beauty-wang/06beauty-wang-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/t-magazine/06beauty-wang/06beauty-wang-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/t-magazine/06beauty-wang/06beauty-wang-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/t-magazine/06beauty-wang/06beauty-wang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/06/t-magazine/06beauty-wang/06beauty-wang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/06/t-magazine/06beauty-wang/06beauty-wang-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Trick Behind the Sporty Ponytails at Alexander Wang', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kendal, Diane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palau, Guido', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Alexander (1983- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-07T00:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kari Molvar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Molvar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reporte