life as a teenager in the United States in six episodes filmed from January through May by a group of 17- and 18-year-olds. These 15 students, including Brandon McCauley of Lebanon, Ohio, above, traveled to New York for a crash course in filmmaking from the directors Alexandra Pelosi (“Journeys With George”), Sam Pollard (“When the Levees Broke”) and Mr. Gibney. They received equipment and learned about storytelling, interviewing, cinematography, sound recording and editing. Then they returned home to document significant events and interview parents, teachers and other important people in their lives as professional producers sometimes worked alongside them to help them develop their stories.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-07T16:16:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d4fa9c7-ac0f-59ba-b007-dad3561bf83a', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d4fa9c7-ac0f-59ba-b007-dad3561bf83a'}, {'abstract': 'It is the second lockout in two years.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/the-atlanta-symphony-orchestra-locks-out-its-players-again/', 'snippet': 'It is the second lockout in two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Atlanta Symphony Orchestra began its second lockout in two years on Sunday when the ensemble’s management and its players, who accepted deep pay cuts two years ago, failed to agree on a new contract before a mi