k: Victoria Beckham Spring/Summer 2015', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckham, Victoria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-07T18:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alfredo Piola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alfredo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/726581ff-16a5-5251-bab0-2337c09ed543', 'word_count': 29, 'uri': 'nyt://article/726581ff-16a5-5251-bab0-2337c09ed543'}, {'abstract': 'The local press speculated about postings at the American Embassy in Paris in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/07/1914-french-press-misjudges-u-s-ambassadors/', 'snippet': 'The local press speculated about postings at the American Embassy in Paris in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judging from their comments, some of the French newspapers take a rather erroneous view of the arrival in Paris of Mr. W. G. Sharp and Mr. Robert Bacon. The idea seems to prevail that the United States is now represented in Paris by a sort of diplomatic triumvirate. Such an idea, of course, is amusingly inaccurate. Mr. Myron T. Herrick, the American Ambassador, is in sole charge of the Embassy, and will remain in sole charge until the end of the existing crisis. Mr. W. G. Sharp, who will take over the Embassy when conditions permit Mr. Herrick to retire, is in Paris for the purpose of arranging details connected with the preparations for his residence here. As regards Mr. Bacon, who made a host of friends during his term as Ambassador, he is visiting Paris at this time on private business. The French press, in fact, in trying to read diplomatic significance into the presence in Paris of the three eminent diplomatists, is wasting its ingenuity. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 8, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 831, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 831}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 978, 'width': 706, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 978, 'width': 706, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador/08iht-oldsept08-ambassador-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumb