', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/arts/BORDERS/BORDERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1219, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/arts/BORDERS/BORDERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/08/arts/BORDERS/BORDERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/arts/BORDERS/BORDERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Traditions Meld Deftly to the Contemporary', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Traditions Meld Deftly to the Contemporary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Schimmel, Michael, Center for the Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-07T20:32:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/73d1a296-1dab-53f6-a7a7-570c855db4e8', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73d1a296-1dab-53f6-a7a7-570c855db4e8'}, {'abstract': 'A Monet landscape is the latest lost treasure to surface in Cornelius Gurlitt’s trove of European art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/08/arts/design/suitcase-yields-a-monet.html', 'snippet': 'A Monet landscape is the latest lost treasure to surface in Cornelius Gurlitt’s trove of European art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Monet landscape is the latest lost treasure to surface in Cornelius Gurlitt’s trove of European art. The painting was recently found in a suitcase that belonged to Mr. Gurlitt, The Associated Press reported. Mr. Gurlitt died in May at 81, a little more than two years after approximately 1,280 paintings and drawings by Picasso, Chagall, Gauguin and other modern masters were confiscated from his Munich apartment.  Mr. Gurlitt had inherited the paintings from his father, Hildebrand Gurlitt, a Nazi-era art dealer. The suitcase containing the Monet was left at a hospital where Mr. Gurlitt had stayed and was turned over to a court-appointed task force handling his estate, The A.P. reported. The work, a light-blue landscape painted on paper, is estimated to have been created around 1864.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suitcase Yields a Monet', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suitcase Yields a Monet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gurlitt, Cornelius', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arts and Antiquities Looting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Munich (Germany)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gurlitt, Hildebrand (1895-1956)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monet, Claude', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-07T20:38:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'sect