mostly at night, and said marijuana had never hurt his performance answering customer calls for a Colorado satellite-television provider.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/us/MARIJUANA/MARIJUANA-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/08/us/MARIJUANA/MARIJUANA-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/us/MARIJUANA/MARIJUANA-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/us/MARIJUANA/MARIJUANA-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/us/MARIJUANA/MARIJUANA-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/08/us/MARIJUANA/MARIJUANA-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/us/MARIJUANA/MARIJUANA-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Legal Use of Marijuana Clashes With Job Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Legal Use of Marijuana Clashes With Job Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Marijuana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dish Network', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-08T00:10:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fd95717-31e3-5eda-b7c7-3872fc1b0019', 'word_count': 1208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fd95717-31e3-5eda-b7c7-3872fc1b0019'}, {'abstract': 'The Affordable Care Act will greatly affect health care costs in the next decade and beyond, but in what ways is still unclear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/08/opinion/the-ebb-and-flow-of-health-spending.html', 'snippet': 'The Affordable Care Act will greatly affect health care costs in the next decade and beyond, but in what ways is still unclear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest federal estimates of health care spending offer some good news: The growth rate for spending in 2013 will remain at a low level for the fifth straight year. But the bad news is, spending is expected to rise faster than growth in the economy over the next 10 years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ebb and Flow of Health Spending', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Ebb and Flow of Health Spending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-08T00:11:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6829ece-b0a5-5be6-9afb-16b3e29510fe', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6829ece-b0a5-5be6-9afb-16b3e29510fe'}, {'abstract': 'More must be done to improve the collection process for student loans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/08/opinion/a-fairer-shot-for-student-debtors.html', 'snippet': 'More must be done to improve the collection process for student loans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year, the federal government will pay companies that collect student loan payments about $600 million. Too often, those collectors fail to help millions of borrowers manage their accounts. Worse, some actually drive them deeper into debt. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' A Fairer Shot for Student Debtors ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fairer Shot for Student Debtors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-08T00:13:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c602bb8e-747d-50ae-9d33-4c091cc42aab', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c602bb8e-747d-50ae-9d33-4c091cc42aab'}, {'abstract': 'An absurdly strict law that accepts as proof of identity a concealed-weapon permit but not a student identification card is being challenged in court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/08/opinion/voter-id-on-trial-in-texas.html', 'snippet': 'An absurdly strict law that accepts as proof of identity a concealed-weapon permit but not a student identification card is being challenged in court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In April, a federal judge in Wisconsin invalidated that state’s voter-identification law, finding that it would disenfranchise hundreds of thousands of eligible voters in a phony attempt to prevent a problem — in-person voter fraud — that does not exist.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voter ID on Trial in Texas', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voter ID on Trial in Texas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-08T00:16:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d5493dc-293b-5778-affb-02ec8603aa68', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d5493dc-293b-5778-affb-02ec8603aa68'}, {'abstract': 'Stronger computing power, improved satellite and radar technology and more sophisticated scientific models give airlines a greater understanding of flying conditions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/08/technology/airlines-take-the-bump-out-of-turbulence.html', 'snippet': 'Stronger computing power, improved satellite and radar technology and more sophisticated scientific models give airlines a greater understanding of flying conditions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just a few years ago, airlines got their weather reports by telex. Pilots pored over reams of paper and compared the forecasts with their flight plans. Once airborne, they depended on radio communications and rudimentary radar to avoid bad weather.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/business/turbulence1/turbulence1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/08/business/turbulence1/turbulence1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/business/turbulence1/turbulence1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur