sein condemned Islamic extremism and urged international action to end conflicts in Syria and Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/world/europe/new-un-human-rights-chief-urges-action-to-end-conflicts-in-syria-and-iraq.html', 'snippet': 'Pledging to be “firm, yet always fair,” Zeid Ra’ad al-Hussein condemned Islamic extremism and urged international action to end conflicts in Syria and Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — Zeid Ra’ad al-Hussein began his tenure on Monday as the United Nations human rights chief with a strongly worded statement in which he condemned Islamic extremism and urged international action to end conflicts in Syria and Iraq.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria and Iraq Called Urgent by New U.N. Rights Chief', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria and Iraq Called Urgent by New U.N. Rights Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming-Bruce, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Zeid Ra'ad Zeid Al Hussein", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Human Rights Council', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pillay, Navi', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-08T10:44:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d89d7f82-ba2e-5f3b-82da-b43c5a37509d', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d89d7f82-ba2e-5f3b-82da-b43c5a37509d'}, {'abstract': 'Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen kick off the festivities at an unusually early hour, and the day ends with Rag & Bone and the first-ever presentation by Ralph Lauren’s Polo women’s wear.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/08/new-york-fashion-week-morning-report-day-5/', 'snippet': 'Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen kick off the festivities at an unusually early hour, and the day ends with Rag & Bone and the first-ever presentation by Ralph Lauren’s Polo women’s wear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s an early morning at New York Fashion Week. Ordinarily, key shows don’t get going until the more editor-approved hour of 10 a.m. or so, but Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen play by no one’s rules but their own. They may have the highest media profile of just about any designer showing during N.Y.F.W., but as proof of the seriousness of their intent, they’ve made an unfashionably early, unusually quiet and ruckus-proof slot their own. You can bet that top members of the industry will be in their seats at the stroke of 9.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/fashion/090714-MATTHEW/090714-MATTHEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/08/fashion/090714-MATTHEW/090714-MATTHEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 462}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/fashion/0