'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34c290a3-c6c6-5647-b68f-1ccbe3e33afa', 'word_count': 1976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34c290a3-c6c6-5647-b68f-1ccbe3e33afa'}, {'abstract': 'The brand’s play, one of fashion week’s most anticipated events, showcased a raft of celebrities and a lot of cliches.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/08/opening-ceremony-the-play-is-not-the-thing/', 'snippet': 'The brand’s play, one of fashion week’s most anticipated events, showcased a raft of celebrities and a lot of cliches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I admit that on Sunday night, when I got out of the Opening Ceremony show — which is to say, the 30-minute play “100% Lost Cotton” created by the designers Humberto Leon and Carol Lim, in conjunction with the director Spike Jonze and Jonah Hill, the co-writers — I was not happy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/fashion/09runway/09runway-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/09/fashion/09runway/09runway-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 807}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/fashion/09runway/09runway-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/fashion/09runway/09runway-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1524, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/fashion/09runway/09r