ies/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The head of the city of Brussels exchanged friendly messages with London’s Lord Mayor in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Burgomaster Max of Brussels, famed as the man who reputedly refused to hand over the keys of the city to the invading Germans in 1914, has sent the following telegram to Sir Frank Bowater, Lord Mayor of London: “When Great Britain, faithful to its promise, courageously faces the trials of war, I express to you, to the members of the Corporation of your city and to the population of London my feelings of the most enthusiastic comradeship.” The Lord Mayor has sent the following reply: “It is with heartfelt gratitude that I reply to your telegram. The citizens of London never forget the great ties uniting our city and yours, and will ever remember your generous sentiments this time.” — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 9, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09/09iht-oldsept09-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09/09iht-oldsept09-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 825}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09/09iht-oldsept09-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 989, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09/09iht-oldsept09-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 989, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09/09iht-oldsept09-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09/09iht-oldsept09-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09/09iht-oldsept09-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Letters Reaffirm City Ties', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brussels (Belgium)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-08T13:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe7944ab-bda3-57f8-8d77-3c91237b22af', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe7944ab-bda3-57f8-8d77-3c91237b22af'}, {'abstract': 'The appointment comes as Walgreen completes an acquisition of the British pharmacy chain Alliance Boots. Mr. Rosenstein will also recommend an additional director to the board.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/08/activist-investor-barry-rosenstein-to-join-walgreen-board/', 'snippet': 'The appointment comes as Walgreen completes an acquisition of the British pharmacy chain Alliance Boots. Mr. Rosenstein will also recommend an additional directo