n-in-west/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Elderly East Germans allowed to visit relatives in the West in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — East German Communist leader Walter Ulbricht announced today [Sept. 8] that elderly East Germans will be allowed to visit relatives in the West. He said his Interior Ministry has been told ‘‘to make possible’’ visits of persons of ‘‘pension age’’ to their relations in West Berlin and West Germany. East German men get old-age pensions at 65 and women at 60.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 9, 1964 ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09-berlin/09iht-oldsept09-berlin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 517, 'width': 494, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09-berlin/09iht-oldsept09-berlin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 517, 'width': 494, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09-berlin/09iht-oldsept09-berlin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09-berlin/09iht-oldsept09-berlin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/blogs/09iht-oldsept09-berlin/09iht-oldsept09-berlin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Elderly Can Visit Kin in West', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kick