nd her team sat down to dinner with American families. But what she found may be disturbing for proponents of family dinners — the meals were often\xa0times of worry\xa0and strife. And, she argues, we can’t expect moms alone to change the way America eats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Family Dinner Doesn’t Satisfy', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-08T18:47:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ba72621-c4d2-5773-8a78-9cf538e9322f', 'word_count': 1249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ba72621-c4d2-5773-8a78-9cf538e9322f'}, {'abstract': 'Zalmay Khalilzad, a former American ambassador, is suspected of tax evasion and money laundering, and his wife’s accounts in Austria have been frozen, a magazine reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/world/zalmay-khalilzad-tax-evasion-investigation.html', 'snippet': 'Zalmay Khalilzad, a former American ambassador, is suspected of tax evasion and money laundering, and his wife’s accounts in Austria have been frozen, a magazine reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Zalmay Khalilzad, a former United States ambassador to Afghanistan, Iraq and the United Nations, is under investigation by the Justice Department for possible tax evasion and money laundering, an Austrian magazine reported on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/world/09KHALILZAD/09KHALILZAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388