525afa'}, {'abstract': 'A Broadway revival of “A Funny Thing Happened on the Way to the Forum” has been postponed now that the star, James Corden, has been named the new host of “The Late, Late Show” on CBS.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/theater/forum-revival-has-been-postponed.html', 'snippet': 'A Broadway revival of “A Funny Thing Happened on the Way to the Forum” has been postponed now that the star, James Corden, has been named the new host of “The Late, Late Show” on CBS.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Broadway revival of “A Funny Thing Happened on the Way to the Forum,” which had been in the works as a vehicle for the Tony Award winner James Corden (“One Man, Two Guvnors”), below, has been postponed now that Mr. Corden has been named the new host of “The Late, Late Show” on CBS. A spokesman for the “Forum” producers said Monday that they had concluded “that time was beginning to run out to cast and produce” the revival, which was intended for the spring. The Tony Award nominee Alex Timbers (“Rocky,” “Here Lies Love”) had been on tap to direct the musical comedy, which has music and lyrics by Stephen Sondheim and won the best musical Tony in 1963. The spokesman had no additional details about a possible future for the project. Playbill.com reported the postponement on Monday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Forum’ Revival Has Been Postponed', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Forum’ Revival Has Been Postponed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corden, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Funny Thing Happened on the Way to the Forum (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Late, L