, the cerebral modernist and dean of the Yale School of Architecture, turned No. 23 into his personal laboratory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/nyregion/for-iconoclasts-of-decades-past-design-took-wing-on-secluded-beekman.html', 'snippet': 'Ashraf Pahlavi, twin sister of the shah of Iran and a crusading women’s rights advocate, found refuge in No. 29, while Paul Rudolph, the cerebral modernist and dean of the Yale School of Architecture, turned No. 23 into his personal laboratory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beekman Place is about as far off the beaten path as one can get in Manhattan. Stretching just two blocks between East 49th and East 51st Streets on a bluff overlooking the East River, it is one of the shortest streets on the island and looks like many others, with grand old townhouses and stately prewar apartment buildings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/nyregion/APPRAISALweb1/APPRAISALweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/09/nyregion/APPRAISALweb1/APPRAISALweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/nyregion/APPRAISALweb1/APPRAISALweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/nyregion/APPRAISALweb1/APPRAISALweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1298, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/nyregion/APPRAISALweb1/APPRAISALweb1-thumbStandard.j