ub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September Fashion Week (2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T00:43:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Women's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/47085cfa-2116-5f2b-a863-a93246ebe364', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/47085cfa-2116-5f2b-a863-a93246ebe364'}, {'abstract': 'An evangelical megachurch based in the Seattle area has announced that it is closing several campuses and laying off staff members because criticism of the church’s founding pastor has caused a drop in attendance and contributions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/us/washington-closings-and-layoffs-for-megachurch.html', 'snippet': 'An evangelical megachurch based in the Seattle area has announced that it is closing several campuses and laying off staff members because criticism of the church’s founding pastor has caused a drop in attendance and contributions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An evangelical megachurch based in the Seattle area has announced that it is closing several campuses and laying off staff members because criticism of the church’s founding pastor has caused a drop in attendance and contributions. The megachurch, Mars Hill Church, said it would merge three campuses in Seattle and end its affiliation with one in Phoenix; abandon a plan to open a campus in Los Angeles; and prepare to close a campus in Huntington Beach, Calif., unless fund-raising there improved. It also said it was laying off a significant but unspecified number of employees. The church has been hurt by criticism of its senior pastor, Mark Driscoll, a prominent speaker and author who has come under fire for his management style, which some found to be inappropriately bullying. Mr. Driscoll is on a voluntary leave while a church panel reviews complaints against him. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Washington: Closings and Layoffs for Megachurch', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Northwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Washington: Closings and Layoffs for Megachurch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mars Hill Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Driscoll, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T00:45:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Paulson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paulson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5e55744-17f6-5888-8391-e2cbe44e6705', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5e55744-17f6-5888-8391-e2cbe44e6705'}, {'abstract': 'At New York Fashion Week, the label creates a drama at the Met.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/fashion/edun-opening-ceremony-versus-versace-and-more-showed-at-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'At New York Fashion Week, the label creates a drama at the Met.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What was it Shakespeare said? “All the world’s a runway, and all the men