': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T03:45:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed2b5dfc-41bf-5ef2-8de8-73cd0bf5af03', 'word_count': 1488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed2b5dfc-41bf-5ef2-8de8-73cd0bf5af03'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview with David Carr, the executive editor talked about his career, the perils of war reporting, dealings with the government and other issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/insider/events/david-carr-interviews-dean-baquet.html', 'snippet': 'In an interview with David Carr, the executive editor talked about his career, the perils of war reporting, dealings with the government and other issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four months ago, Dean Baquet became executive editor after the dismissal of Jill Abramson. Last week, he was interviewed by David Carr, a media columnist, before an audience of Times Premier subscribers and their guests in the Times building.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'David Carr Interviews Dean Baquet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baquet, Dean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Insider', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'subsection_name': 'Insider Events', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erika Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizat