23e5683-21b2-59c8-b716-0756ce8b2345'}, {'abstract': 'How might scientists use similar data-rich surveillance to learn more about other insects’ behavior?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/6-qs-about-the-news-when-worker-bees-get-a-promotion/', 'snippet': 'How might scientists use similar data-rich surveillance to learn more about other insects’ behavior?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the ScienceTake video “When Worker Bees Get a Promotion,” James Gorman explains new discoveries about bee behavior. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | When Worker Bees Get a Promotion', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T08:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/392e60be-0e65-5604-9bc9-9c84b17ccba2', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/392e60be-0e65-5604-9bc9-9c84b17ccba2'}, {'abstract': 'Six years after the housing bust, the return of riskier mortgage lending may be inevitable — and welcome.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/magazine/are-subprime-mortgages-coming-back.html', 'snippet': 'Six years after the housing bust, the return of riskier mortgage lending may be inevitable — and welcome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ali and Mariluci Sleiman wanted to buy a house. The couple, who run a day care service inside their first-floor rental apartment, had outgrown their space in Taunton, a small city in southern Massachusetts. They also wanted to avoid answering to a landlord who might complain about 10 little kids running around all day. They were “desperate to buy a home,” Ali told me. And with good credit and $46,000 in joint income, they hoped they wouldn’t have a hard time getting a loan. So they were disappointed when the bank rejected their application, and then when a local credit union did too.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14economy/mag-14Economy-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14economy/14economy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14economy/14economy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14economy/14economy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Subprime Mortgages Coming Back?', 'kicker': 'It’s the Economy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Subprime Time?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appelbaum, Binyamin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c23fd7e-427b-50bb-b0c1-c3c3c2d6bd5c', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c23fd7e-427b-50bb-b0c1-c3c3c2d6bd5c'}, {'abstract': 'How seriously should teams take allegations and evidence of wrongdoing in players’ personal lives?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/do-sports-teams-have-a-responsibility-to-hold-players-to-a-standard-for-their-personal-conduct/', 'snippet': 'How seriously should teams take allegations and evidence of wrongdoing in players’ personal lives?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Baltimore Ravens dropped the star running back Ray Rice from the team after TMZ published a graphic video Monday of him punching his former fiancée, who is now his wife. Before the video had emerged, the N.F.L. had only suspended Rice in July for two games — a decision that drew immediate criticism from commentators to players to women’s advocates. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur