nts shared mattresses on the floor, the terminally ill were sent home to die because of nonexistent facilities and unclaimed corpses were buried in unadorned mass graves on the outskirts of town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1476, 'width': 2046, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/blogs/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA/20140908-lens-silva-slide-RBGA-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Witness to AIDS in South Africa', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apartheid (Policy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mbeki, Thabo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silva, Joao', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tshabalala-Msimang, Manto', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuma, Jacob G', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Johannesburg (South Africa)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T09:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joao Silva', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silva', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc80346f-5844-5583-b916-b9e9acc1e072', 'word_count': 1067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc80346f-5844-5583-b916-b9e9acc1e072'}, {'abstract': 'China Central Television used images of Condoleezza Rice in a report about a Beijing visit by Susan E. Rice, President Obama’s national security adviser.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/chinese-state-broadcaster-gets-its-american-rices-confused/', 'snippet': 'China Central Television used images of Condoleezza Rice in a report about a Beijing visit by Susan E. Rice, President Obama’s national security adviser.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China Central Television mistakenly used images of Condoleezza Rice, the former United States secretary of state who left office in 2009, in a report on Sunday about the national security adviser Susan E. Rice’s visit to Beijing, which continued on Tuesday. The state-run broadcaster quickly corrected the gaffe, however. A day later, it posted on its website a version of the English-language report complete with images of the Obama administration official, according to The South China Morning Post. (The correct Rice is pictured below.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/world/09sino-rice01/09sino-rice01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/09/world/09sino-rice01/09sino-rice01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/world/09sino-rice01/09sino-rice01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/world/09sino-rice01/09sino-rice01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/world/09sino-rice01/09sino-rice01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/09/world/09sino-rice01/09sino-rice01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/world/09sino-rice01/09sino-rice01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height'