': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T13:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Leven', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leven', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c13aab28-26e3-57f5-a5f4-a0097faec1b8', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c13aab28-26e3-57f5-a5f4-a0097faec1b8'}, {'abstract': 'With the passage of time and a sleeker cut, the leather jacket — that perennial symbol of small-town misspent youth — has grown up.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/mens-fashion-leather-jacket-salvatore-ferragamo-saint-laurent/', 'snippet': 'With the passage of time and a sleeker cut, the leather jacket — that perennial symbol of small-town misspent youth — has grown up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the passage of time and a sleeker cut, the leather jacket — that perennial symbol of small-town misspent youth — has grown up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All American', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T13:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ff66d20-c557-574b-9e6d-65204e5de64c', 'word_count': 24, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ff66d20-c557-574b-9e6d-65204e5de64c'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A Hungarian patriot drew condemnation from Berlin in 1889.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/1889-italy-to-expel-hungarian/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A Hungarian patriot drew condemnation from Berlin in 1889.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TURIN — It is announced on good authority that, at the request of the German Government, Signor Crispi has decided to expel Louis Kossuth, the Hungarian patriot, from Italy. The reasons upon which the request is founded are the visit of 800 Hungarians to Kossuth, and the speech the latter made against the policy of the Tisza Ministry. Not long after this the hero of the insurrection of 1848 said that it was greatly to be regretted that Hungary and Italy had placed themselves in a position which might force them into a war with France. This naturally gave great offence at Berlin and Vienna, and the German Foreign Office sent a note to Rome to the effect that the toleration of such language was incompatible with the conventions of the Triple Alliance. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 10, 1889', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/blogs/10iht-oldsept10-kossuth/10iht-oldsept10-kossuth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 425, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/blogs/10iht-oldsept10-kossuth/10iht-oldsept10-kossuth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 425, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/blogs/10iht-oldsept10-kossuth/10iht-oldsept10-kossuth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/10/blogs/10iht-oldsept10-kossuth/10iht-oldsept10-kossuth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/blogs/10iht-oldsept10-kossuth/10iht-oldsept10-kossuth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1889: Italy to Expel Hungarian', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hungary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T13:05:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fbb7471-3bc7-54af-a345-db05744fa998', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fbb7471-3bc7-54af-a345-db05744fa998'}, {'abstract': '“The Imitation Game,” about the mathematician Alan Turing, seemingly has all the elements of an Academy favorite.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/toronto-festival-2014-ingredients-of-an-oscar-winner/', 'snippet': '“The Imitation Game,” about the mathematician Alan Turing, seemingly has all the elements of an Academy favorite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO—How to describe “The Imitation Game,” Harvey Weinstein’s latest play in the annual Academy Awards game?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit'