By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a45bf994-f6bc-53ae-bd5a-fd73189fff64', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a45bf994-f6bc-53ae-bd5a-fd73189fff64'}, {'abstract': 'If you’ve never heard the name Lloyd J. Austin, there’s a good reason', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/at-the-helm-of-military-mission-in-iraq-an-invisible-general/', 'snippet': 'If you’ve never heard the name Lloyd J. Austin, there’s a good reason', 'lead_paragraph': 'The general overseeing America’s new military intervention in Iraq is no stranger to that battleground. In fact, he folded the tent there at the end of 2011 when the Obama administration failed to reach a deal with Baghdad to keep a small military contingent and ended an eight-year war unceremoniously.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Helm of Military Mission in Iraq, an Invisible General', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McChrystal, Stanley A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T13:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ernesto Londo&#241;o', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ernesto', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Londo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/808b9788-973