s.com/2014/09/09/readers-protest-hate-speech-in-comments-section-on-down-syndrome/', 'snippet': 'Comments on an article about a Hurricane Sandy rebuilding program provoked a similar reader response.', 'lead_paragraph': ' It started with the biologist Richard Dawkins, who on Twitter last month suggested that women have a moral obligation to abort their fetuses after they get a Down syndrome diagnosis. Responding to a question from a pregnant woman, he wrote: “Abort it and try again. It would be immoral to bring it into the world if you have the choice,” he wrote on Twitter. He said that he based this on his belief that suffering should be reduced whenever possible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Protest ‘Hate Speech’ in Comments Section on Down Syndrome', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T14:58:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1a24984-0abd-55c4-b5fa-83966933b631', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1a24984-0abd-55c4-b5fa-83966933b631'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the New York Fashion Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/new-york-fashion-week-rag-bone-spring-summer-2015/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the New York Fashion Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the New York Fashion Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Fashion Week: Rag & Bone Spring/Summer 2015', 'kicker': 'T Magazine