ey’re not always calming. A few writers and readers share what they read to relax.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/what-are-your-stress-reads/', 'snippet': 'Hate-reads can be cathartic, but they’re not always calming. A few writers and readers share what they read to relax.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If anyone — the N.S.A., say — wanted to determine my emotional state on a given day, they could probably figure it out from my browser history. At least, they’d be able to tell if I was stressed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/opinion/nyto-read/nyto-read-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/08/opinion/nyto-read/nyto-read-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/opinion/nyto-read/nyto-read-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/opinion/nyto-read/nyto-read-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1853, 'width': 1872, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/opinion/nyto-read/nyto-read-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/08/opinion/nyto-read/nyto-read-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/08/opinion/nyto-read/nyto-read-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Are Your Stress-Reads?', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T15:19:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df08fa10-f34d-5498-b99e-7aad9b194c2f', 'word_count': 2899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df08fa10-f34d-5498-b99e-7aad9b194c2f'}, {'abstract': 'Spain, a success story?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/the-structural-fetish/', 'snippet': 'Spain, a success story?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The FT has a pretty decent article on the emerging doctrine of “Draghinomics”, which looks a lot like Blanchardnomics, which looks a lot like Krugmanomics — hey, we all studied macro at MIT in the mid 1970s. But I was struck by this bit:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Structural Fetish', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T15:20:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/541b7620-28f8-5093-be1a-aa7f4678afa6', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/541b7620-28f8-5093-be1a-aa7f4678afa6'}, {'abstract': '“The Paying Guests,” the latest novel by the British author Sarah Waters, examines the years after World War I and a love affair between women from different classes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/books/the-paying-guests-by-sarah-waters-looks-at-1920s-britain.html', 'snippet': '“The Paying Guests,” the latest novel by the British author Sarah Waters, examines the years after World War I and a love affair between women from different classes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A few years ago, the British novelist Sarah Waters was playing around with ideas for her next book when she remembered a notorious 1920s trial she had once read about. Known popularly as the Thompson-Bywaters case, it featured a penny dreadful’s worth of combustible ingredients: an unexciting husband, a faithless wife, her much younger lover and a cache of racy, damning love letters.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/WATERS/WATERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/WATERS/WATERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/WATERS/WATERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/WATERS/WATERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1734, 'width': 1734, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/WATERS/WATERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/WATERS/WATERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/WATERS/WATERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weaving a Tale of Love and Death in London', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Test of Love in a Court of Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Paying Guests (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyall, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waters, Sarah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T15:27:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f50c0e83-03bc-54d4-a750-6187481ae183', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f50c0e83-03bc-54d4-a750-6187481ae183'}, {'abstract': 'Bob Dylan, Roger Daltrey, Brian Wilson and Willie Nelson are among the musicians featured on “The Art of Paul McCartney,” an album due out Nov. 18.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/09/a-star-studded-album-to-honor-paul-mccartney/', 'snippet': 'Bob Dylan, Roger Daltrey, Brian Wilson and Willie Nelson are among the musicians featured on “The Art of Paul McCartney,” an album due out Nov. 18.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tribute albums have become a sub-industry of the pop music world and collectors who snap them up, either because th