the other way. My piece tried to contextualize the grievous failure of the English authorities by linking the disaster\xa0to other high-profile cases of sexual abuse\xa0— in Roman Catholicism, of course, but also in New York’s private schools, at Joe Paterno’s Penn State, in Hollywood, elsewhere\xa0— and after the column appeared I noticed a few readers and Twitterers suggesting that as a \xa0Catholic I have an ulterior motive in generalizing about sex abuse, because generalizations are a good way to evade or minimize the particular sins of my own church.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sex Abuse Tangle', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celibacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Horace Mann School', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rotherham (England)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-09T19:08:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d17a8a7d-e398-50e5-9b6e-a54b8fa9bf78', 'word_count': 1214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d17a8a7d-e398-50e5-9b6e-a54b8fa9bf78'}, {'abstract': '“Gabriel: A Poem,” by Edward Hirsch, and “Once in the West,” by Christian Wiman, use verse to grapple with grief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/books/edward-hirschs-gabriel-and-christian-wimans-once-in-the-west.html', 'snippet': '“Gabriel: A Poem,” by Edward Hirsch, and “Once in the West,” by Christian Wiman, use verse to grapple with grief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lord of the Torrent, King of the Sudden Impulse, Emperor of the Impetuous, Clown of God. The poet Edward Hirsch’s son, Gabriel, was a handful, and the author and others had many private names for him.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 906, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 906}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 679, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1357, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-thumbL