ome a remote hope, Masahiro Tanaka is racing to return before it all ends, if only to show that he can.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tanaka Could Make a Return Before Season Ends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tanaka Could Make a Return Before Season Ends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanaka, Masahiro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T00:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab27d562-3d1e-5feb-ba54-b368f9d97a17', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab27d562-3d1e-5feb-ba54-b368f9d97a17'}, {'abstract': 'New York City officials said 10 emergency medical workers had arrived at a medical center in Manhattan after receiving a call that Ms. Rivers had gone into cardiac arrest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/nyregion/at-east-side-surgery-center-a-rush-to-save-joan-rivers.html', 'snippet': 'New York City officials said 10 emergency medical workers had arrived at a medical center in Manhattan after receiving a call that Ms. Rivers had gone into cardiac arrest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The call came in to 911 one second before 9:40 a.m. on Thursday, Aug. 28, from the staff at a clinic on East 93rd Street in Manhattan — a patient in cardiac arrest. The call was coded as “Segment 1,” the highest-level priority handled by 911, according to two New York City officials. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2