wne-vera-wang-and-more-show-at-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'At New York Fashion Week shows from Donna Karan, Maria Cornejo, Rodarte, Thom Browne and Vera Wang, even collections nominally inspired by real places had an otherworldly feel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fashion can often seem like an alternative cosmos, or a trip through the looking glass — say, when you are standing in Central Park and a three-story hologram of a runway appears, as it did Monday at the Ralph Lauren Polo show. Or when a Mad Hatter’s garden party is held, complete with girls dressed as shuttlecocks and badminton rackets and daisy chains, as it was at Thom Browne.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/fashion/10REVIEW1/10REVIEW1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/10/fashion/10REVIEW1/10REVIEW1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/fashion/10REVIEW1/10REVIEW1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/fashion/10REVIEW1/10REVIEW1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/fashion/10REVIEW1/10REVIEW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/10/fashion/10REVIEW1/10REVIEW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/fashion/10REVIEW1/10REVIEW1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Runways to Other Worlds: Donna Karan, Maria Cornejo, Rodarte, Thom Browne, Vera Wang', 'kicker': 'Fashion Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Runways to Other Worlds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September Fashion Week (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karan, Donna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rodarte', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Browne, Thom', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Vera', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cornejo, Maria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T00:50:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e770098-7db7-5c9c-900e-555800d2d3e7', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e770098-7db7-5c9c-900e-555800d2d3e7'}, {'abstract': 'The Pakistani Navy said it repelled a terrorist attack over the weekend after a six-hour exchange of fire at a naval dockyard in the southern port city of Karachi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/world/asia/pakistan-troops-fend-off-militant-attack-in-karachi.html', 'snippet': 'The Pakistani Navy said it repelled a terrorist attack over the weekend after a six-hour exchange of fire at a naval dockyard in the southern port city of Karachi.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Pakistani Navy said it repelled a terrorist attack over the weekend after a six-hour exchange of fire at a naval dockyard in the southern port city of Karachi. Two militants were killed and four were arrested when they tried to attack, a navy spokesman said. A junior ranking officer was killed, while an officer and six sailors were wounded in the clash\xa0on Saturday\xa0night, the spokesman said.\xa0The Taliban claimed responsibility\xa0on Tuesday, according to the BBC. A Taliban attack on Karachi’s international airport in June prompted a military offensive against militants in the North Waziristan tribal region. \xa0The\xa0attack on the dockyard is\xa0the second on a military facility since the offensive began. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: Troops Fend Off Militant Attack in Karachi', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Troops Fend Off Militant Attack in Karachi', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karachi (Pakistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Waziristan (Pakistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T00:54:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2e43924-d1b5-5249-b978-112a22e87be4', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2e43924-d1b5-5249-b978-112a22e87be4'}, {'abstract': 'The approval of a power-sharing government is an important building block, but hard work lies ahead for Prime Minister Abadi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/opinion/hopes-for-iraqs-new-government.html', 'snippet': 'The approval of a power-sharing government is an important building block, but hard work lies ahead for Prime Minister Abadi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Iraqi Parliament put in place an important building block of an anti-ISIS strategy on Monday when it approved, in record time, a new power-sharing government led by Prime Minister Haider al-Abadi. Harder work lies ahead as Mr. Abadi, a member of the Shiite majority, tries to manage sectarian rivals in his cabinet and unify a fractured country, all while working with the United States to eliminate a mortal threat from marauding Sunni militants who occupy a huge swath of northern Iraq.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hopes for Iraq’s New Government', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hopes for Iraq’s New Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abadi, Haider al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T00:54:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/706bc168-b36f-5405-8ac8-9f22d602fb2d', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/706bc168-b36f-5405-8ac8-9f22d602fb2d'}, {'abstract': 'Now that many tollbooths no longer take cash, some rental car companies have made a hearty business out of paying the tolls themselves. But there’s a catch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/nyregion/fighting-back-on-toll-fees-for-rental-cars.html', 'snippet': 'Now that many tollbooths no longer take cash, some rental car companies have made a hearty business out of paying the tolls themselves. But there’s a catch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that many tollbooths are no longer taking actual, physical money, some of the country’s biggest rental car companies have made a hearty business out of paying the tolls themselves. And oh, yes: There’s a service fee for that. This summer, a couple from California visiting New York hired a car from Dollar Rent A Car. They discovered that $4.88 in tolls for twice crossing the Henry Hudson Bridge — where it is impossible to pay with cash — had become a $34.88 charge from Dollar.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Back on Toll Fees for Rental Cars', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fighting Back on Toll Fees for Rental Cars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tolls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-ZPass', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hertz Global Holdings Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T00:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39edf709-1102-5988-94d3-3ac427490bc5', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39edf709-1102-5988-94d3-3ac427490bc5'}, {'abstract': 'Apple introduced a payment system that joins forces with Macy’s, Whole Foods, Visa and other retailers and major credit card companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/technology/apples-ambitious-bet-beyond-the-devices.html', 'snippet': 'Apple introduced a payment system that joins forces with Macy’s, Whole Foods, Visa and other retailers and major credit card companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tech evangelists have predicted for years a world in which people paid for retail goods with the wave of a smartphone, or the push of a smartphone button. For nearly as long, this so-called mobile wallet has yet to catch on.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Apple Pay, a Push Into Mobile Payments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ambitious Bet on More Than Devices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Virtual Currency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Commerce', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T00:54:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Isaac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isaac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7c89b55-80f8-5970-8aa3-3cf5d89c931b', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7c89b55-80f8-5970-8aa3-3cf5d89c931b'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama said in June that fixing the immigration problem was urgent. Now he says doing anything about it will have to wait.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/opinion/another-broken-promise-on-immigration.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama said in June that fixing the immigration problem was urgent. Now he says doing anything about it will have to wait.', 'lead_paragraph': '“America cannot wait forever,” said President Obama in June, when he denounced congressional paralysis on immigration reform and declared that he would soon act on his own to fix the problem. He promised to move by the end of the summer, presumably to suspend the deportations of many unauthorized immigrants — perhaps millions, though there is no way to know how many until a plan is unveiled. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Broken Promise on Immigration ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Broken Promise on Immigration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T00:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b061da14-4f8b-5449-bc00-d6040bfaa94e', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b061da14-4f8b-5449-bc00-d6040bfaa94e'}, {'abstract': 'An Australian Pentecostal megachurch powered by a recording label that dominates Christian contemporary music, Hillsong has become a phenomenon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/us/hillsong-megachurch-with-a-beat-lures-a-young-flock.html', 'snippet': 'An Australian Pentecostal megachurch powered by a recording label that dominates Christian contemporary music, Hillsong has become a phenomenon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — A toned and sunburned 32-year-old Australian with the letters F-A-I-T-H tattooed onto his biceps strode onto the stage of a former burlesque theater here and shouted across a sea of upstretched hands and uplifted smartphones: “Let’s win this city together!”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u