value': 'Houston, Brian (1954- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T00:58:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Paulson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paulson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba663267-2e3a-50ab-8127-848fc0863693', 'word_count': 1316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba663267-2e3a-50ab-8127-848fc0863693'}, {'abstract': 'Any question about how well Tim Cook is managing the reins of the world’s most valuable company will most likely be put to rest after Tuesday’s profusion of product announcements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/technology/personaltech/apple-is-back-better-than-ever.html', 'snippet': 'Any question about how well Tim Cook is managing the reins of the world’s most valuable company will most likely be put to rest after Tuesday’s profusion of product announcements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four times before in its history, at media events planned with military precision, Apple introduced a new invention that radically altered how the technology industry conceived of its future. The company hopes it did that again for a fifth time on Tuesday by unveiling the Apple Watch, a stylish smartwatch that is the company’s first advance into a new product category since it created the iPad in 2010. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/business/10STATE/10STATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/10/business/10STATE/10STATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption':