 for a domestic abuse charge, N.F.L. Commissioner Roger Goodell blundered badly and ended up harming the league and its owners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/sports/football/roger-goodell-saw-ray-rice-violence-through-a-corporate-lens.html', 'snippet': 'By prioritizing so-called league interests when initially punishing Ray Rice for a domestic abuse charge, N.F.L. Commissioner Roger Goodell blundered badly and ended up harming the league and its owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Had N.F.L. Commissioner Roger Goodell watched\xa0the chilling Ray Rice elevator video through the lens of a father whose daughter was being beaten or a brother whose sister was knocked cold or a son whose mother was dragged and dropped outside an elevator,\xa0his actions surely would have been swift,\xa0severe and, most likely, permanent. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pledging to Shield the N.F.L.’s Brand at All Costs', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pledging to Protect N.F.L.’s Brand at All Costs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Ray (1987- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Janay Palmer', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T01:31:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By William C. Rhoden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ceb8041-79e3-5df5-bb23-a9ff61fe0da6', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ceb8041-79e3-5df5-bb23-a9ff61fe0da6'}, {'abstract': 'The biggest opponent to Detroit’s blueprint for rising out of bankruptcy has reached an agreement with the city, court documents show, prompting an adjournment in a trial over the city’s plan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/us/detroit-clears-crucial-hurdle-on-bankruptcy.html', 'snippet': 'The biggest opponent to Detroit’s blueprint for rising out of bankruptcy has reached an agreement with the city, court documents show, prompting an adjournment in a trial over the city’s plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fiercest opponent to Detroit’s blueprint for erasing its debts and investing in city services has reached an “agreement in principle” with city officials, court documents filed Tuesday evening showed, clearing the way to end the city’s court fight over its future and emerge from bankruptcy far more quickly and smoothly than expected.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detroit Clears Crucial Hurdle on Bankruptcy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Detroit Clears Crucial Hurdle on Bankruptcy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walsh, Mary Williams', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syncora Guarantee Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duggan, Mike', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orr, Kevyn D', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T01:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Williams Walsh and Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46622b67-4568-5b9d-a77a-52219b1527d5', 'word_count': 1300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46622b67-4568-5b9d-a77a-52219b1527d5'}, {'abstract': 'At least 24 people were killed and seven injured when the roof of a mosque in the eastern city of Lahore collapsed Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/world/asia/pakistan-24-killed-when-mosque-roof-collapses.html', 'snippet': 'At least 24 people were killed and seven injured when the roof of a mosque in the eastern city of Lahore collapsed Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At least 24 people were killed and seven injured when the roof of a mosque in the eastern city of Lahore collapsed Tuesday. The mosque, in the Darghawala neighborhood, caved in when noon prayer had just begun. Muhamad Usman,\xa0who led\xa0the rescue operation, said that all the victims were believed to have been found but that the search would continue. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: 24 Killed When Mosque Roof Collapses', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: 24 Killed When Mosque Roof Collapses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosques', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lahore (Pakistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roofs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T01:34:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Waqar Gillani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Waqar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca71f79f-7a9a-516e-8740-2412cb159bd9', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca71f79f-7a9a-516e-8740-2412cb159bd9'}, {'abstract': 'The Israeli military arrested four fishermen early Tuesday in what Palestinian officials said was a violation of the cease-fire agreement signed last month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/world/middleeast/gaza-arrests-suggest-disagreement-on-truce-details.html', 'snippet': 'The Israeli military arrested four fishermen early Tuesday in what Palestinian officials said was a violation of the cease-fire agreement signed last month.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Israeli military arrested four fishermen early Tuesday in what Palestinian officials said was a violation of the cease-fire agreement signed last month, but that the Israelis contended was an enforcement of their restriction of fishing to within six nautical miles of the Gaza coast. Nezar Ayash of the Gaza fishermen’s union said four men were arrested less than one mile off the coast near the northern town of Beit Lahiya. He said two fishermen were arrested in a similar incident last Wednesday. The Egyptian-brokered cease-fire announced on Aug. 26 restored a 2012 agreement that the fishing zone be doubled to six nautical miles from three. A spokeswoman for the Israeli military said the four men had “deviated from the permitted fishing zone” and “were over six miles away from the shore.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaza: Arrests Suggest Disagreement on Truce Details', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gaza: Arrests Suggest Disagreement on Truce Details', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akram, Fares', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T01:36:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e536d21-45ce-5f6e-9ab2-400c1f8e65c2', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e536d21-45ce-5f6e-9ab2-400c1f8e65c2'}, {'abstract': 'Sue Donoghue, who oversaw Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s sustainability and parks blueprint, succeeds Emily Lloyd, now the head of the city’s environmental agency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/nyregion/ex-city-official-to-lead-group-that-oversees-prospect-park.html', 'snippet': 'Sue Donoghue, who oversaw Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s sustainability and parks blueprint, succeeds Emily Lloyd, now the head of the city’s environmental agency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Prospect Park Alliance, the nonprofit group that raises money for and oversees the daily operation of Brooklyn’s most visited par