n case against John G. Rowland, the former governor of Connecticut, repeatedly told the court that he had taken pains not to put anything in writing that might expose the $5,000-a-month consulting contract he had engineered with Mr. Rowland as a sham. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Witness Details a Sham in a Deal With Rowland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Witness Details a Sham in a Deal With Rowland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowland, John G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussey, Kristin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foley, Brian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson-Foley, Lisa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T02:11:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Leigh Cowan and Kristin Hussey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Cowan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kristin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hussey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf643f72-4de6-5281-b6d4-84b7cb883324', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf643f72-4de6-5281-b6d4-84b7cb883324'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and his running mate, Kathy Hochul, captured the Democratic primary over two law school professors, Zephyr Teachout and Tim Wu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytime