to pay $2.7 billion in cash for the company.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/london-stock-exchange-shareholders-approve-deal-for-russell-investments/', 'snippet': 'The stock exchange said 99.96 percent of the votes cast were in favor of acquiring the owner of the Russell 2000 stock market index. It agreed to pay $2.7 billion in cash for the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The London Stock Exchange said on Wednesday that its shareholders had voted overwhelmingly in favor of its acquisition of Russell Investments, the owner of the Russell 2000 stock market index.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Stock Exchange Shareholders Approve Deal for Russell Investments', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russell 2,000 Stock Index', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'London Stock Exchange', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Northwestern Mutual Life Insurance Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Russell Investments', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T11:25:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ebfa72f-7ba3-5fb2-99ed-f983e392c00b', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ebfa72f-7ba3-5fb2-99ed-f983e392c00b'}, {'abstract': 'Dollar General takes its bid for Family Dollar directly to shareholders. | Microsoft near a deal for the maker of Minecraft. | Fed’s newly proposed rules put pressure on banks. | Detroit clears a bankruptcy hurdle.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/morning-agenda-dollar-general-goes-hostile/', 'snippet': 'Dollar General takes its bid for Family Dollar directly to shareholders. | Microsoft near a deal for the maker of Minecraft. | Fed’s newly proposed rules put pressure on banks. | Detroit clears a bankruptcy hurdle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dollar General said on Wednesday that it was taking its $9.1 billion offer for Family Dollar directly to shareholders, DealBook’s David Gelles writes. The move could further complicate Family Dollar’s deal agreement to sell itself to Dollar Tree for $8.5 billion. In a statement, Dollar General said it was offering to acquire all of Family Dollar’s shares for $80 each. That is the same bid that Family Dollar rejected last week, contending that the deal it agreed to with Dollar Tree had a better chance of passing muster with antitrust regulators. A hostile bid is likely to, at the very least, delay any deal between Family Dollar and Dollar Tree.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Dollar General Goes Hostile', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T11:44:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b7a4712-e0bb-52b7-81e4-ea12781543ba', 'word_count': 1744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b7a4712-e0bb-52b7-81e4-ea12781543ba'}, {'abstract'