pt has been named for Mick Jagger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the name had not been bestowed by a couple of fans, Mick Jagger might have cause to take umbrage: a newly discovered extinct swamp creature has been named Jaggermeryx naida — Jagger’s water nymph — in the singer’s honor. Two of the scientists who published a study on the animal and its discovery in this month’s issue of the Journal of Paleontology, Ellen Miller, of Wake Forest University and Gregg Gunnell, of Duke University, said that the animal’s mouth structure is what brought Mr. Jagger to mind. Mr. Gunnell, in a statement, described the structure as probably “a highly innervated muzzle with mobile and tactile lips.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Think Mick Jagger Is a Fossil? So Do Some Scientists', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Think Jagger Is a Fossil? So Do Some Scientists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jagger, Mick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Jennifer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Keith', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T16:12:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/360a14eb-58f3-5fde-b3b6-6baf78a87604', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/360a14eb-58f3-5fde-b3b6-6baf78a87604'}, {'abstract': 'Central bankers have seen signs of market exuberance, but the Federal Reserve has been slow to pop the bubbles, Jesse Eisinger writes in The Trade.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/recognizing-bubbles-but-still-cautious-on-deflating-them/', 'snippet': 'Central bankers have seen signs of market exuberance, but the Federal Reserve has been slow to pop the bubbles, Jesse Eisinger writes in The Trade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Central bankers have been attacked, justifiably, for having done little to quash the great\xa0credit\xa0bubble that led to the 2008 financial crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Eisinger/Eisinger-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Eisinger/Eisinger-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Eisinger/Eisinger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Eisinger/Eisinger-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Eisinger/Eisinger-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Eisinger/Eisinger-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype