nk': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T16:26:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/231234c1-821d-5663-a498-37eb2fe8bc0c', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/231234c1-821d-5663-a498-37eb2fe8bc0c'}, {'abstract': 'The Ministry of Information dialed back an earlier assertion that Syria-based militants would soon release 45 Fijian members of a United Nations peacekeeping force.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/world/middleeast/syria-civil-war.html', 'snippet': 'The Ministry of Information dialed back an earlier assertion that Syria-based militants would soon release 45 Fijian members of a United Nations peacekeeping force.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fiji on Wednesday dialed back its assertion that 45 of its peacekeepers in the Golan Heights, captured by Syrian militants nearly two weeks ago, were about to be released.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fiji, in Clarification, Says Peacekeepers Remain Held in Golan Heights', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fiji', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Golan Heights', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Nusra Front', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T16:27:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20a40bc8-cf34-5a70-bac6-036be7f5ec9f', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20a40bc8-cf34-5a70-bac6-036be7f5ec9f'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama expanded the campaign against ISIS to include airstrikes in Syria and more American advisers in Iraq, but he sought to distinguish the new action from the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/world/middleeast/obama-speech-isis.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama expanded the campaign against ISIS to include airstrikes in Syria and more American advisers in Iraq, but he sought to distinguish the new action from the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama on Wednesday authorized a major expansion of the military campaign against rampaging Sunni militants in the Middle East, including American airstrikes in Syria and the deployment of 475 more military advisers to Iraq. But he sought to dispel fears that the United States was embarking on a repeat of the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama, in Speech on ISIS, Promises Sustained Effort to Rout Militants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Calls for Sustained Drive to Rout Militants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T16:27:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0e6b21e-fd24-5843-81c2-bfc270bbe0d4', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0e6b21e-fd24-5843-81c2-bfc270bbe0d4'}, {'abstract': 'Last night’s Sausage with Spinach and Bean Mash was easy and “therapeutic.” Tonight, pouring sauce on chicken.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/a-slower-paced-but-still-easy-wednesday-meal/', 'snippet': 'Last night’s Sausage with Spinach and Bean Mash was easy and “therapeutic.” Tonight, pouring sauce on chicken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Busy parents. Active kids. Families that arrive home every evening, starved. This week, in the series Dinner: The Boot Camp, Jenny Rosenstrach takes a recipe for chaos and coaches one family, and all of us, in the planning and preparation needed to turn it into a pleasant nightly meal. Find all the Boot Camp recipes here.Tuesday Recap', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/us/image/image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/10/us/image/image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': N