ne, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy Space Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T16:35:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'The Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7f5fda78-44d3-5a30-88f7-33731cacab00', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7f5fda78-44d3-5a30-88f7-33731cacab00'}, {'abstract': 'Producers are in talks about a New York run of the hit British plays “Wolf Hall” and its sequel “Bring Up the Bodies,” based on the historical novels by Hilary Mantel.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/wolf-hall-and-its-sequel-aiming-for-broadway-after-london-success/', 'snippet': 'Producers are in talks about a New York run of the hit British plays “Wolf Hall” and its sequel “Bring Up the Bodies,” based on the historical novels by Hilary Mantel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Broadway and London producers are in talks about a New York run of the hit British play “Wolf Hall” and its sequel “Bring Up the Bodies,” based on the historical novels by Hilary Mantel about Henry VIII and his adviser Thomas Cromwell, according to theater executives with knowledge of the discussions. No deals have been finalized, but the veteran Broadway producers Jeffrey Richards and Jerry Frankel are aiming to mount the plays in the spring, possibly at the Winter Garden Theater, said the executives, who spoke on condition of anonymity because the talks are confidential.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/16/arts/wolf/wolf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/16/arts/wolf/wolf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/16/arts/wolf/wolf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/16/arts/wolf/wolf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1271, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/16/arts/wolf/wolf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/07/16/arts/wolf/wolf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/16/arts/wolf/wolf-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Wolf Hall’ and Its Sequel Aiming for Broadway After London Success', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Wolf Hall’ and Sequel Aiming for Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mantel, Hilary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T16:46:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5bd9218-1879-5f68-b121-01d219859948', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5bd9218-1879-5f68-b121-01d219859948'}, {'abstract': 'Sylvester, the flamboyant androgyne and disco diva, has now become fodder for the latest jukebox musical.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/theater/booty-shakers-in-mighty-real-a-fabulous-sylvester-musical.html', 'snippet': 'Sylvester, the flamboyant androgyne and disco diva, has now become fodder for the latest jukebox musical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donna Summer, Gloria Gaynor, Evelyn (Champagne) King, Vicki Sue Robinson, Amii Stewart: the disco era was prime time for divas of pop. But perhaps the flashiest disco diva of them all was actually a man who, aptly enough for a diva of any era, went by a single name. I speak, of course, of Sylvester, the flamboyant androgyne whose life has now become fodder for the latest jukebox musical to splash down onstage. “Mighty Real: A Fabulous Sylvester Musical” is the brainchild of Anthony Wayne (“Pippin,” “Priscilla, Queen of the Desert”), who wrote the book, directs with Kendrell Bowman and struts the stage of the Theater at St. Clement’s in the title role. As with many another musical drawing on chart hits, the show will weave Sylvester’s finest booty shakers — “You Make Me Feel (Mighty Real),” “Do Ya Wanna Funk,” “Dance (Disco Heat)” — into his life story. And let’s not forget this bonus: The show will feature Anastacia McCleskey and Jacqueline B. Arnold as the Weather Girls. Can we hope for a singalong? (Opens Sunday, 423 West 46th Street, Clinton, 866-811-4111, fabuloussylvester.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i