Cantina and Mission Chinese shares some insights from his recent education on the cuisine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The man behind the acclaimed Mission Chinese Food restaurants in San Francisco and New York has a cameo in Jeff Gordinier’s story “In Search of the Perfect Taco” in T’s Men’s Style Issue — a culinary odyssey in which the writer traveled with the Danish chef René Redzepi to discover Mexico’s many delicious dishes. Danny Bowien, of course, has gotten into Mexican food in a major way recently since opening Mission Cantina, in which he’s sought to put his own spin on that national cuisine in the same way that he did with Sichuan food at Mission Chinese. Here, Bowien reveals what he’s learned about Mexican cooking in the last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/t-magazine/10redzepi-bowien/10redzepi-bowien-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/10/t-magazine/10redzepi-bowien/10redzepi-bowien-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/t-magazine/10redzepi-bowien/10redzepi-bowien-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/t-magazine/10redzepi-bowien/10redzepi-bowien-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/t-magazine/10redzepi-bowien/10redzepi-bowien-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail'