t, Saudi Arabia, Iraq and Kuwait pledged $30.8 million for the upkeep of the army. U.A.R. President Gamal Abdel Nasser said he would place the Sinai peninsula and the Gaza strip ‘‘at the disposal of the Palestine organization.’’ He indicated this meant the organization would be allowed to establish headquarters and training facilities in these areas but did not mean Egypt was ceding the territory. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 11, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/blogs/10iht-old11/10iht-old11-jumbo.png', 'height': 459, 'width': 541, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/blogs/10iht-old11/10iht-old11-superJumbo.png', 'height': 459, 'width': 541, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/blogs/10iht-old11/10iht-old11-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/10/blogs/10iht-old11/10iht-old11-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/blogs/10iht-old11/10iht-old11-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Palestine Exile Regime Planned', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nasser, Gamal Abdel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations'