name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T17:56:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katrin Bennhold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf149b14-e42a-54ea-a3ae-74f2df543122', 'word_count': 1320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf149b14-e42a-54ea-a3ae-74f2df543122'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama on Wednesday night is expected to describe an undertaking that would go well beyond targeted drone strikes against suspected terrorist leaders, as he has done against Al Qaeda and its affiliates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/world/middleeast/what-obama-faces-in-a-campaign-against-isis.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama on Wednesday night is expected to describe an undertaking that would go well beyond targeted drone strikes against suspected terrorist leaders, as he has done against Al Qaeda and its affiliates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama will use a prime-time address on Wednesday evening to explain to Americans his strategy for confronting the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria, the Sunni militant group. Here is a look at some of the questions that may be addressed in the speech.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Obama Faces in a Campaign Against ISIS', 'kicker': 'Q. and A.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T17:58:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2e0cf09-80f8-5601-865c-664999276a81', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2e0cf09-80f8-5601-865c-664999276a81'}, {'abstract': 'Do you think job candidates are willing to work for three months on a contract before being hired full-time?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/do-you-hire-employees-on-a-trial-basis/', 'snippet': 'Do you think job candidates are willing to work for three months on a contract before being hired full-time?', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve just published a small-business guide about business owners who “test-drive” prospective employees before hiring them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Hire Employees on a Trial Basis?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T18:10:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7449d613-6431-5df6-8844-2071ba71666b', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7449d613-6431-5df6-8844-2071ba71666b'}, {'abstract': 'Victoria Diehl, a Spanish photographer who creates haunting hybrids of flesh and stone by melding images of human models and classical marble statues, talks about how she turned Lena Dunham into marble.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/under-cover-how-we-turned-lena-dunham-into-a-neoclassical-bust/', 'snippet': 'Victoria Diehl, a Spanish photographer who creates haunting hybrids of flesh and stone by melding images of human models and classical marble statues, talks about how she turned Lena Dunham into marble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once we settled on Lena Dunham as the cover subject for this week’s Culture Issue, the question was how to capture her quirky spirit as actor, writer and director. Jake Silverstein, the magazine’s editor, wanted to evoke classical art. The magazine’s design director, Gail Bichler, suggested turning Dunham into a sculpture, and Joanna Milter, deputy photo editor, had an idea for the artist to take that on: Victoria Diehl, a Spanish photographer who creates haunting hybrids of flesh and stone by melding images of human models and classical marble statues. Diehl had been on Milter’s radar since they met a few years ago at Photo España, an international photography festival. Last month, Diehl flew in from La Coruña, Spain, to photograph Dunham at Industria Superstudio in Manhattan’s meatpacking district, and then spent the next few weeks back in Spain composing the photo illustration above. Recently, Diehl talked about what it took to turn Dunham into marble.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14cover_type/14cover_type-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14cover_type/14cover_type-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 730}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14cover_type/14cover_type-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 843, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14cover_type/14cover_type-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1685, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14cover_type/14cover_type-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14cover_type/14cover_type-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/magazine/14cover_type/14cover_type-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Cover: On Turning Lena Dunham Into a Neoclassical Bust', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diehl, Victoria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunham, Lena', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T18:34:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Fragala-Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fragala-Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization':