kets-hudson-valley/', 'snippet': 'The former bassist of Smashing Pumpkins and Hole and her filmmaker husband are luring culture-seeking Manhattanites upstate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The proposed Marina Abramovic Institute has helped burnish the ongoing, artistic renaissance of Hudson, New York, but Melissa Auf der Maur got there first. In 2008, a gabled, 19th-century warehouse caught the attention of the former bassist of Smashing Pumpkins and Hole, who, along with her husband, the filmmaker Tony Stone, became, as she puts it, the space’s “creative directors, janitors and secretaries.” From spring to fall, they host concerts, film festivals, art exhibitions, flea markets and the extremely popular Ramp Fest, held in celebration of the forageable green onion. “The building is a symbol of the region,” Auf der Maur says of Basilica Hudson, “diverse, richly historic, magical, confusing.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/t-magazine/10basilica_beddie/10basilica_beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/10/t-magazine/10basilica_beddie/10basilica_beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/t-magazine/10basilica_beddie/10basilica_beddie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/t-magazine/10basilica_beddie/10basilica_beddie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1489, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image