er of ISIS to uproarious laughter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/world/middleeast/mocking-isis-in-beirut.html', 'snippet': 'In Beirut, the band Al-Rahel Al-Kabir, or the Great Departed, has been performing a satirical hymn to the leader of ISIS to uproarious laughter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As fear of militants from the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria rises in the United States after the beheading of two American journalists, and President Obama lines up support for the use of force against ISIS, the backlash against the movement has already begun in the Arab world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mocking ISIS in Beirut', 'kicker': 'Open Source', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-10T23:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e5759aa-2d0a-59da-9b37-c9b2084f61af', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e5759aa-2d0a-59da-9b37-c9b2084f61af'}, {'abstract': 'Early reports said the Apple Watch might charge wirelessly. But wireless charging wouldn’t have worked well for the device.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/10/why-doesnt-the-apple-watch-have-wireless-charging-because-it-probably-wouldnt-work-very-well/', 'snippet': 'Early reports said the Apple Watch might charge wirelessly. But wireless charging wouldn’t have worked well for the device.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Apple Watch