t_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wearable Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T00:01:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farhad Manjoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farhad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manjoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c40a0d19-7e0f-59b8-ae9c-56e90a8ec0a1', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c40a0d19-7e0f-59b8-ae9c-56e90a8ec0a1'}, {'abstract': 'The courts should reject a perverse new challenge to the law’s health insurance subsidies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/opinion/stop-the-anti-obamacare-shenanigans.html', 'snippet': 'The courts should reject a perverse new challenge to the law’s health insurance subsidies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SO far, opponents of the Affordable Care Act have lost every major battle to repeal or invalidate it. Some of them are now urging the courts to interpret the health reform law in a way that would guarantee its failure. This is a significant threat — potentially as grave as the previous main legal challenge to the law, which the Supreme Court rejected, 5 to 4, in 2012. If the new effort succeeds, it would create total chaos. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stop the Anti-Obamacare Shenanigans', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stop the Anti-Obamacare Shenanigans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T00:03:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry J. Aaron, David M. Cutler and Peter R. Orszag', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Aaron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/09b7e285-d21c-5472-bab2-6f44a476de87', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09b7e285-d21c-5472-bab2-6f44a476de87'}, {'abstract': 'Apple’s payment system points toward a new era of commerce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/opinion/the-digital-wallet-revolution.html', 'snippet': 'Apple’s payment system points toward a new era of commerce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THIS week Apple announced two new pieces of hardware, the iPhone 6 and a “smartwatch.” But as flashy as they are, neither item is as groundbreaking as a piece of software that will accompany them: a digital wallet, allowing users to eschew cash and credit cards for a quick swipe of their device at the register. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/opi