hicle safety laws, as well as the agency’s handling of the crisis that has engulfed General Motors. The company has recalled more than 29 million cars since January and failed for more than a decade to report to regulators and the public a defective ignition that has been linked to 13 deaths.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Hearing to Examine N.H.T.S.A.’S. Recall Response', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Hearing to Examine N.H.T.S.A.’S. Recall Response', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T00:48:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ivory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/91be0901-7aef-5e8a-bd32-3b52f4670726', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91be0901-7aef-5e8a-bd32-3b52f4670726'}, {'abstract': 'Microsoft’s acquisition of Minecraft would be an acknowledgment that gaming is central to many people’s lives, serving as an engaging mode of entertainment or merely a time killer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/technology/in-hit-games-tech-giants-see-more-than-fun.html', 'snippet': 'Microsoft’s acquisition of Minecraft would be an acknowledgment that gaming is central to many people’s lives, serving as an engaging mode of entertainment or merely a time killer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parents like Minecraft because it can be a creative outlet for their children. Teachers like the game because it can bring lessons to life. And Microsoft likes the game so much that the tech giant wants to buy Minecraft’s parent company for more than $2 billion.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Minecraft1/Minecraft1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Minecraft1/Minecraft1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Minecraft1/Minecraft1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Minecraft1/Minecraft1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Minecraft1/Minecraft1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Minecraft1/Minecraft1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/business/Minecraft1/Minecraft1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Microsoft Sees More Than Fun in a Game Like Minecraft', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Hit Games, Tech Giants See More Than Fun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mojang AB', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Virtual Reality (Computers)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Minecraft (Video Game)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T00:52:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4088360-0a85-5ef6-ae1a-a246692d767f', 'word_count': 1083, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4088360-0a85-5ef6-ae1a-a246692d767f'}, {'abstract': 'Jeremy Scott and Marc by Marc Jacobs present their collections at New York Fashion Week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/fashion/new-york-fashion-week-jeremy-scott-and-marc-by-marc-jacobs-showed.html', 'snippet': 'Jeremy Scott and Marc by Marc Jacobs present their collections at New York Fashion Week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Youth is wasted on the young, but fashion has a way of yanking it back. Guests at the Marc by Marc Jacobs show arrived at a rave temple, with enormous black speakers stacked like altars and bath