 who still lives there, is his father. “Mijo,” Mr. Polendo’s father tells him, “all this is very real. It’s sad, and it’s difficult. And it’s not a story, or a play, or a myth. It’s the life of a city.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/arts/sub11JUAREZ/sub11JUAREZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/11/arts/sub11JUAREZ/sub11JUAREZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/arts/sub11JUAREZ/sub11JUAREZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/arts/sub11JUAREZ/sub11JUAREZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1066, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/arts/sub11JUAREZ/sub11JUAREZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/11/arts/sub11JUAREZ/sub11JUAREZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/arts/sub11JUAREZ/sub11JUAREZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weaving Their Tapestry of Murder and Mayhem', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weaving Their Tapestry of Murder and Mayhem', 'name': None, 'seo': None,