ew', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Sorrow Is Deeper Than Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benson, Ned (1977- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chastain, Jessica', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAvoy, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T15:19:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/aabbf1a4-ec90-57fc-a41b-c4ff5a762de4', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aabbf1a4-ec90-57fc-a41b-c4ff5a762de4'}, {'abstract': 'A spokesman said that the band would continue touring in early 2015, and that many dates would probably be rescheduled.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/zz-top-cancels-tour-after-dusty-hills-injury/', 'snippet': 'A spokesman said that the band would continue touring in early 2015, and that many dates would probably be rescheduled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When ZZ Top canceled several concerts in late August after the band’s bassist, Dusty Hill, injured his hip in a fall on the band’s tour bus, the bearded Texas bluesmen said that they expected to return to touring on Sept. 25. But Mr. Hill, 65, has not fully recovered, and on Thursday the band’s spokesman said that the rest of the autumn tour – 27 dates, through Nov. 1 – would be canceled. He said that the band would continue touring in early 2015, and that many of the dates would probably be rescheduled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ZZ Top Cancels Tour After Dusty Hill’s Injury', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ZZ Top', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T15:21:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a18cad59-7390-5f53-96f9-3b51871310af', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a18cad59-7390-5f53-96f9-3b51871310af'}, {'abstract': 'In “Bird People,” a businessman and a maid at an airport hotel abruptly seek escapes from unhappy lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/movies/in-bird-people-two-unhappy-souls-cut-their-chains.html', 'snippet': 'In “Bird People,” a businessman and a maid at an airport hotel abruptly seek escapes from unhappy lives.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Bird People” begins with a series of calm aerial views of human beings in transit: crossing the terminal concourse at Charles de Gaulle Airport, filing through the turnstiles at the nearby commuter rail station, dozing and daydreaming on the train. The images add up to an affecting composite picture of a familiar modern paradox. We never seem more alone, more adrift from one another, than when we are bustling along in impromptu crowds, migratory flocks of isolated souls. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12BIRDPEOPLE/12BIRDPEOPLE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12BIRDPEOPLE/12BIRDPEOPLE-articleLar