cusses some of the more eye-popping images.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The man looks too calm for someone getting an ax plunged into his shoulder. And the lady with crazy eyes might want to wipe the trickle of blood oozing from her mouth. Or maybe she likes it? Such is life on the cover of a Gorgon video box.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GORGON6/14GORGON6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GORGON6/14GORGON6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 937}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GORGON6/14GORGON6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 656, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GORGON6/14GORGON6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1312, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GORGON6/14GORGON6-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GORGON6/14GORGON6-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GORGON6/14GORGON6-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Return of the Boxes That Ate Your Brain!', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Return of the Boxes That Ate Your Brain!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piepenburg, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gorgon Video', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Death Spa (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Don't Look in the Basement (Movie)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T16:08:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c4d22cc-d6ab-593a-98b0-3627a99e4e37', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c4d22cc-d6ab-593a-98b0-3627a99e4e37'}, {'abstract': 'Thoughts on serving and sisterhood from the Efaw family, in which the mother, father and three daughters — so far — have gone to West Point.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/the-west-point-sisters/', 'snippet': 'Thoughts on serving and sisterhood from the Efaw family, in which the mother, father and three daughters — so far — have gone to West Point.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So far, Amy and Andrew Efaw have sent three daughters to West Point, from which they themselves graduated in 1989. Alexandra, the oldest daughter and a recent graduate who was featured in this past weekend’s magazine, was thought to be, by her mother’s admission, “not West Point material.” But that daughter, who goes by “Alix,” instead extended the family connection to the military academy. “Once Alix got in, it became more attainable,” Amy says. “The others thought, ‘Well, if Alix can get in. . . .’ ” Two more Efaw siblings are still in high school — Aimee, who goes by Kat, in eighth grade and Andrew in 10th — and, says Alix, “I could totally see my kids coming to West Point and it kind of repeating itself.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/07/magazine/07thewomenofwestpoint_ss-slide-EHE1/07thewomenofwestp