est for for the designer’s show. Here, a look at some exclusive behind-the-scenes images and tales — including which hairdo didn’t make it down the runway.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/j-mendel-beauty-new-york-fashion-week-spring-summer-2015/', 'snippet': 'T was there during the hair and makeup test for for the designer’s show. Here, a look at some exclusive behind-the-scenes images and tales — including which hairdo didn’t make it down the runway.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I like to be inspired by art, but this was really hands-on,” says Gilles Mendel, the creative director of J. Mendel. For his spring/summer 2015 collection, Mendel collaborated with the New York-based painter and visual artist Enoc Perez to create a series of graphic prints. “I started with three or four of his paintings, then found ways to transform them in my own way by changing the color palettes and molding the canvas to the shape of a woman,” Mendel explains. “It was sort of a puzzle to figure out.” It wasn’t the first time the duo had teamed up — last winter they released a book of collages — and in some ways, this collection continued the dialogue. “I sliced and collaged his prints, using these extraordinary fabrics, to create unexpected moments that aren’t entirely Enoc or me. It’s really a combination of both,” the designer contends. On the runway, Mendel wanted an equally dynamic beauty look. “The collection is really precise, slick and constructed, so I think the hair and makeup has to feel the same way,” he says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Creating the J. Mendel Beauty Look for Spring 2015', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, 