unt': 1178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33e8feea-6475-5b76-acf9-80ce2b8b5342'}, {'abstract': 'The revival of Wendy Wasserstein’s Pulitzer- and Tony-winning play will star Ms. Moss, Jason Biggs and Bryce Pinkham.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/heidi-chronicles-to-return-to-broadway-in-february-with-elisabeth-moss/', 'snippet': 'The revival of Wendy Wasserstein’s Pulitzer- and Tony-winning play will star Ms. Moss, Jason Biggs and Bryce Pinkham.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Broadway revival of Wendy Wasserstein’s play “The Heidi Chronicles” will begin performances in February with Elisabeth Moss (“Mad Men”) in the title role and, as the two men in her life, Jason Biggs (the “American Pie” movies) and Bryce Pinkham (“A Gentleman’s Guide to Love & Murder”), the producers announced on Thursday. The director will be Pam MacKinnon, who won a Tony Award last year for staging the revival of “Who’s Afraid of Virginia Woolf?,” while the actress Tracee Chimo (“Bad Jews”) will play several supporting roles.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/11artsbeat-moss/11artsbeat-moss-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/11artsbeat-moss/11artsbeat-moss-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 742}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/11artsbeat-moss/11artsbeat-moss-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 829, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/11artsbeat-moss/11artsbeat-moss-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 994, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy'