[{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef000947-ab5b-5a86-989c-24fe80f3b931', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef000947-ab5b-5a86-989c-24fe80f3b931'}, {'abstract': 'Today, it was announced that she will become the next editor-in-chief of Maxim magazine. As we revisit some of her most memorable outfits, she shares the details behind her incomparable look.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/kate-lanphear-fashion-secrets-of-t-magazine-outgoing-womens-style-director-maxim/', 'snippet': 'Today, it was announced that she will become the next editor-in-chief of Maxim magazine. As we revisit some of her most memorable outfits, she shares the details behind her incomparable look.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today, it was announced that T’s women’s style director, Kate Lanphear, will become the next editor-in-chief of Maxim magazine. Beyond her vast and varied contributions to the world of T, Lanphear has also drawn a global following for her distinctive rock-inspired look — a look that made her one of the original stars of the street-style world and continues to exert influence today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fashion Secrets of Kate Lanphear, T’s Outgoing Women’s Style Director', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T19:33:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5aa48b7-1702-5554-8b01-04a9802632dc', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5aa48b7-1702-5554-8b01-04a9802632dc'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Emerald Light in the Air,” Donald Antrim’s short story collection, absurdity is in the details of the choices his characters make.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/books/the-emerald-light-in-the-air-stories-by-donald-antrim.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Emerald Light in the Air,” Donald Antrim’s short story collection, absurdity is in the details of the choices his characters make.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Antrim is, after Thomas Pynchon, American literature’s presiding weirdo. He’s a trickster. His books are short, vivid, drastic and surreal, so much so that reading them is like driving 90 miles an hour while in third gear, in the back seat of a jalopy the author has stolen, while he disposes of his drugs by throwing them out the window.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12BOOKANTRIM/JPBOOKANTRIM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12BOOKANTRIM/JPBOOKANTRIM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12BOOKANTRIM/JPBOOKANTRIM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12BOOKANTRIM/JPBOOKANTRIM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1362, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12BOOKANTRIM/12BOOKANTRIM-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 