 'uri': 'nyt://article/db06b677-9c1c-59bb-a61f-7ff9b1c56be2'}, {'abstract': 'Even with a smaller-than-expected increase in premiums, however, the share of small businesses offering health insurance to employees declined slightly.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/small-businesses-see-only-a-small-increase-in-health-premiums/', 'snippet': 'Even with a smaller-than-expected increase in premiums, however, the share of small businesses offering health insurance to employees declined slightly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The warnings this time last year were dire and widespread: Small businesses would face a double-digit rise in health care costs in 2014. But as it turned out, premiums for small businesses barely budged. According to the Kaiser Family Foundation’s 2014 Employee Health Benefits Survey, small-group health insurance premiums for individual coverage grew by just 1 percent this year, the slowest rate of growth since 2008. Family plans increased by 2 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Small Businesses See Only a Small Increase in Health Premiums', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kaiser Family Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Federation of Independent Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T20:40:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 