34', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b64bd519-d339-5859-b266-5968d897b134'}, {'abstract': 'In “Archaeology of a Woman,” Sally Kirkland plays an ex-newspaper columnist battling dementia while a murder mystery unfolds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/movies/archaeology-of-a-woman-starring-sally-kirkland.html', 'snippet': 'In “Archaeology of a Woman,” Sally Kirkland plays an ex-newspaper columnist battling dementia while a murder mystery unfolds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not everything in a movie needs to make sense, but when almost nothing does, it’s a problem. Even so, what the publicity notes are pleased to call a “disconcerting narrative structure” is far from the only issue with “Archaeology of a Woman,” Sharon Greytak’s confounding blend of long-ago murder and present-day dementia.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1084, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN/12ARCHAELOGYWOMAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Weakness for Cops, a Crime to Solve', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Archaeology of a Woman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greytak, Sharon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkland, Sally', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Archaeology of a Woman (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T21:29:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/89e5e8c8-3b66-5260-8d1f-e68b243ee42c', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89e5e8c8-3b66-5260-8d1f-e68b243ee42c'}, {'abstract': 'The cartoonish verve of Lily van der Stokker’s irrepressible installations can sometimes disguise the originality and sharpness of her art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/arts/design/lily-van-der-stokker-huh.html', 'snippet': 'The cartoonish verve of Lily van der Stokker’s irrepressible installations can sometimes disguise the originality and sharpness of her art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cartoonish verve of Lily van der Stokker’s irrepressible installations, which consist of walls and objects painted light, feminine shades, can sometimes disguise the originality and sharpness of her art. With subtle plays of cryptic phrases, color and forms, her best efforts appear adamantly cute until they start filling up with mixed signals of longing, conflict and repressed urges. “Huh,” her current piece, meditates on the illusion of equality between the sexes, and also in relationships between artists, regardless of their sex.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 462}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1578, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6/VANDERSTOKKER-GALLERY6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '