Dubuffet: Soul of the Underground.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES/DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES/DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 728}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES/DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 844, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES/DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1455, 'width': 1199, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES/DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES/DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES/DUBUFFET1-GALLERIES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': "‘Dubuffet/Barceló'", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art in Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barcelo, Miquel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dubuffet, Jean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T21:33:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef1b34b5-7ec0-50f3-b5f4-f4500e342e6d', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef1b34b5-7ec0-50f3-b5f4-f4500e342e6d'}, {'abstract': '“Altina” tracks the life of a tobacco heiress, artist and inventor who refused to be hemmed in by convention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/movies/altina-a-documentary-about-a-schinasi-family-heiress.html', 'snippet': '“Altina” tracks the life of a tobacco heiress, artist and inventor who refused to be hemmed in by convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tobacco millionaire Morris Schinasi had three daughters. There they are, in Peter Sanders’s sassy documentary “Altina,” in their 1920s cloches and fur-collared coats in front of the family mansion at 107th and Riverside in Manhattan. Two went on to conventional heiress lives, and then there was Altina.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ALTINA/ALTINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ALTINA/ALTINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 765}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ALTINA/ALTINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 804, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ALTINA/ALTINA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1512, 'width': 1186, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ALTINA/ALTINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ALTINA/ALTINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12ALTINA/ALTINA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Money, but So Much More Than That', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Altina', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schinasi, Morris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miranda, Altina Schinasi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Altina (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T21:33:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a71c73c-ceb7-5658-ad3b-5902d272214e', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a71c73c-ceb7-5658-ad3b-5902d272214e'}, {'abstract': 'You get a sense of Conceptual Art’s mix of politics, perversity and humor in this survey of early work by Carlos Ginzburg.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/arts/design/carlos-ginzburg-the-forgotten-vintage.html', 'snippet': 'You get a sense of Conceptual Art’s mix of politics, perversity and humor in this survey of early work by Carlos Ginzburg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The early days of Conceptual Art seem long ago and far away. But you get a sense of the movement’s mix of politics, perversity and humor in this survey of early work by Carlos Ginzburg, an artist and theoretician — were the two ever really separable in Conceptualism? — who was born in Argentina in 1946 and has lived in Paris since 1972.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GINZBURG-GALLERIES4/GINZBURG-GALLERIES4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GINZBURG-GALLERIES4/GINZBURG-GALLERIES4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GINZBURG-GALLERIES4/GINZBURG-GALLERIES4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GINZBURG-GALLERIES4/GINZBURG-GALLERIES4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1529, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GINZBURG-GALLERIES4/GINZBURG-GALLERIES4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GINZBURG-GALLERIES4/GINZBURG-GALLERIES4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GINZBURG-GALLERIES4/GINZBURG-GALLERIES4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlos Ginzburg: ‘The Forgotten Vintage’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carlos Ginzburg: ‘The Forgotten Vintage’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ginzburg, Carlos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T21:34:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3810ef3-ba36-5748-ab51-9bcad959fc8b', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3810ef3-ba36-5748-ab51-9bcad959fc8b'}, {'abstract': 'Nadav Schirman’s documentary thriller “The Green Prince” tells the story of a Palestinian recruited as a spy by the Shin Bet, Israel’s internal security agency, and his Israeli handler.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/movies/the-green-prince-about-a-hamas-son-recruited-by-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Nadav Schirman’s documentary thriller “The Green Prince” tells the story of a Palestinian recruited as a spy by the Shin Bet, Israel’s internal security agency, and his Israeli handler.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The emotional core of “The Green Prince,” Nadav Schirman’s gripping documentary thriller, is the deepening relationship of Mosab Hassan Yousef, a Palestinian recruited as a spy by the Shin Bet, Israel’s internal security agency, and his Israeli handler. Mr. Yousef, whose memoir, “Son of Hamas,” inspired the film, wasn’t a Palestinian fighter infused with jihadist fervor. But because his father, Hassan Yousef, was a founder of Hamas, he was a prize catch for the Israeli agency, which manipulated him with diabolical efficiency to glean vital intelligence. In turn, he was protected from exposure.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GREENPRINCE1/GREENPRINCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GREENPRINCE1/GREENPRINCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GREENPRINCE1/GREENPRINCE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GREENPRINCE1/GREENPRINCE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1060, 'width': 1440, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/arts/12GREENPRINCE1/GREENPRINCE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/201