 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/291951f6-60fd-5fec-a183-5e7989ad06b5'}, {'abstract': 'Court documents shed light on Yahoo’s unsuccessful challenge of federal requests for warrantless surveillance of its foreign users.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/technology/documents-unsealed-in-yahoos-case-against-us-data-requests.html', 'snippet': 'Court documents shed light on Yahoo’s unsuccessful challenge of federal requests for warrantless surveillance of its foreign users.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal government was so determined to collect the Internet communications of foreign Yahoo customers in 2008 that it threatened the company with fines of $250,000 a day if it did not immediately comply with a secret court order to turn over the data.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/business/Yahoo/Yahoo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/business/Yahoo/Yahoo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/business/Yahoo/Yahoo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/business/Yahoo/Yahoo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1232, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/business/Yahoo/Yahoo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/12/business/Yahoo/Yahoo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/business/Yahoo/Yahoo-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Government’s Threat of Daily Fine for Yahoo Shows Aggressive Push for Data', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Threat of Daily Fine Shows Government’s Aggressive Push for Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-11T21:42:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vindu Goel and Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vindu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/056f1ecb-7857-5e3a-b7a8-b7b110764838', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/056f1ecb-7857-5e3a-b7a8-b7b110764838'}, {'abstract': 'The state was occupied by the Union forces for years before it started reconstruction. So why did things go so badly?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/11/louisianas-stillborn-constitution/', 'snippet': 'The state was occupied by the Union forces for years before it started reconstruction. So why did things go so badly?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Christmas Eve 1863, Abraham Lincoln wrote to Maj. Gen. Nathaniel Banks in New Orleans to reassure him that he was master “in regard to re-organizing a State government for Louisiana” and “in regard to the military matters of the Department.” Frustrated at the slow pace of Banks’s reorganization efforts, the anxious president also entreated his commander of the Department of the Gulf to “give us a free-state re-organization of Louisiana, in the shortest possible time.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Louisiana’s Stillborn Constitution', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reconstruction Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 5,