type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa7de2be-0d31-5bf9-b230-c4794e9e3da0', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa7de2be-0d31-5bf9-b230-c4794e9e3da0'}, {'abstract': 'The N.F.L.’s response against Ray Rice shows that protecting another lucrative season is all it cares about.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/opinion/the-nfls-disgraceful-response-to-the-ray-rice-case.html', 'snippet': 'The N.F.L.’s response against Ray Rice shows that protecting another lucrative season is all it cares about.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Football League will have a hard time recovering from its cavalier mishandling of the domestic abuse case against Ray Rice, the gridiron star who punched his then-fiancée unconscious in February in an elevator in Atlantic City. At first, the league sought to minimize the incident by ordering a mere two-game suspension of the Baltimore Ravens running back, despite a security video excerpt showing him dragging the limp body of Janay Palmer, the woman who is now his wife, from the elevator. A police charge of felony assault followed soon after. As controversy grew, the N.F.L. commissioner, Roger Goodell, apologized for his misjudgment and promised stronger punishments for players who attack their domestic partners. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upon Further Review', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Upon Further Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Ray (1987- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Robert S III', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T01:08:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/afe108ee-6c26-5a18-b693-86fb8faa2520', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afe108ee-6c26-5a18-b693-86fb8faa2520'}, {'abstract': 'If Congress abdicates its responsibility in this military campaign, it will allow President Obama free rein to set a dangerous precedent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/opinion/legal-authority-for-fighting-isis.html', 'snippet': 'If Congress abdicates its responsibility in this military campaign, it will allow President Obama free rein to set a dangerous precedent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Pentagon gears up to expand its fight against ISIS, a fundamentalist Sunni militant group that controls large areas of Iraq and Syria, Congress appears perfectly willing to abdicate one of its most consequential powers: the authority to declare war. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Legal Authority for Fighting ISIS', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Legal Authority for Fighting ISIS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, 