ank’s policies to guard against money laundering, and its efforts to identify transactions that might be linked to terrorists. He spoke of how Middle East terrorism hurt the bank’s business, and even how it affected his family.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Witness for Arab Bank Says Disputed Payments Were Humanitarian', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arab Bank’s Payments Called Charitable', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Arab Bank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clifford, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bishara, Shukry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T01:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df5df9ad-27a6-5ef3-a0d5-83a7b2ed5a1b', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df5df9ad-27a6-5ef3-a0d5-83a7b2ed5a1b'}, {'abstract': 'Two factors may improve Democrats’ chances: Former Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s prodigious spending for Republicans will be out, and Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo says he will be in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytime