uated along South Oyster Bay in Amityville on Long Island, the NY Kite Center has functioned as a kiteboarding school, gear shop and repair center since 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a late August afternoon, an adventurous group gathered on the second floor of a wind-battered former seaplane factory, eager to fly. They wiggled into their wet suits, tethered themselves to harnesses and inspected their winglike kites. There was only one thing left to do: wait for the wind. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiting on the Wind', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Waiting on the Wind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kiteboarding', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Sara', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NY Kite Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMITYVILLE (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pereira, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kites', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T02:23:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da724d47-e40d-53a7-82d6-8b5d987b15fc', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da724d47-e40d-53a7-82d6-8b5d987b15fc'}, {'abstract': 'The artist and designer Kate McLean led an investigative tour of sidewalk odors in Brooklyn, documenting the city’s aromas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/nyregion/the-data-for-a-map-collected-sniff-by-sniff.html', 'snippet': 'The artist and designer Kate McLean led an investigative tour of sidewalk odors in Brooklyn, documenting the city’s aromas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If smell can define a place, New York in the summertime is not exactly a meadow of flowers. In the war between a sensitive nose and the city streets, the streets have the upper hand, assailing the nose with the odors of urine, decomposing garbage and clammy armpits. Mouth breathing is not only acceptable, but often necessary.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Data for a New York ‘Smellmap,’ Collected Sniff by Sniff', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Data for a Map, Collected Sniff by Sniff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smells and Odors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McLean, Kate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smell (Olfaction)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T02:50:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5440bc30-bce3-5a0a-ad83-20e46b8742a8', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5440bc30-bce3-5a0a-ad83-20e46b8742a8'}, {'abstract': 'An investigator tasked with sorting out the N.F.L.’s handling of the Rice case will want to be as thorough as possible and not appear in any way craven to his employer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/sports/football/ex-fbi-leaders