k Sennett Collection Volume One,” a Blu-ray set from Flicker Alley, assembles 50 shorts written, directed or produced by a master of silent comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mack Sennett (1880-1960) is famous for discovering Charlie Chaplin, creating the Keystone Kops, coining the term “bathing beauty” and being, as his front-page obituary in The New York Times called him, “the film pioneer whose name was synonymous with slapstick comedy.” All true, but as demonstrated by the 50 mainly short films digitally restored and gathered in a three-disc Blu-ray set, “The Mack Sennett Collection Volume One” (Flicker Alley), he was something more.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14HOBERMAN1/14HOBERMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14HOBERMAN1/14HOBERMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14HOBERMAN1/14HOBERMAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 867, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14HOBERMAN1/14HOBERMAN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 867, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14HOBERMAN1/14HOBERMAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14HOBERMAN1/14HOBERMAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14HOBERMAN1/14HOBERMAN1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Man Who Put the K in Kops', 'kicker': 'On Video', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Man Who Put the K in Kops', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sennett, Mack (1880-1960)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Releases (Entertainment)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T13:26:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'DVD', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. Hoberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d12ea4b-2099-564c-bdcc-192d95f81814', 'word_count': 1346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d12ea4b-2099-564c-bdcc-192d95f81814'}, {'abstract': 'On “responsible” policy, unions’ “stranglehold” and military “advisers.”', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/when-one-word-might-be-the-wrong-word/', 'snippet': 'On “responsible” policy, unions’ “stranglehold” and military “advisers.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' Sometimes, as I read The Times, a word will stop me cold. That happened yesterday\xa0morning as I read the photo caption on a timely Room for Debate about the videotaped assault by Ray Rice on his wife, Janay Palmer, that has been so much in the news. The word: “altercation.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When One Word Might Be the Wrong Word', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T13:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b354ba6-f62f-5788-86fe-70c48741eeb8', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b354ba6-f62f-5788-86fe-70c48741eeb8'}, {'abstract': 'How to make pesto that doesn’t fade from bright green to olive and four new ways to use it.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/bright-green-pesto-eggs-pasta/', 'snippet': 'How to make pesto that doesn’t fade from bright green to olive and four new ways to use it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is not the first time that I’ve devoted a week of recipes to pesto genovese – basil pesto. But it is the first time that I can vouch for a basil pesto that retains a gorgeous green color. I’ve been forever flummoxed by the color problem with pesto, the way it goes from bright green to olive drab so quickly. I’ve tried this and that – been told about citric acid, covering the pesto with olive oil, or even lemon juice (which makes little sense to me because acid usually turns bright green olive). Anyway, I read up on the problem this week and decided to try blanching the leaves. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/science/12recipehealthsquashalt/12recipehealthsquashalt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/09/science/12recipehealthsquashalt/12recipehealthsquashalt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/science/12recipehealthsquashalt/12recipehealthsquashalt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/science/12recipehealthsquashalt/12recipehealthsquashalt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/science/12recipehealthsquashalt/12recipehealthsquashalt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/09/science/12recipehealthsquashalt/12recipehealthsquashalt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/science/12recipehealthsquashalt/12recipehealthsquashalt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bright Green Pesto That Won’t Fade', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T13:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b01e27c2-f05c-5339-b1bc-9cb83f0d15a3', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b01e27c2-f05c-5339-b1bc-9cb83f0d15a3'}, {'abstract': 'A soldier takes time out of uniform to pursue an MFA in writing, and discovers that what sets him apart, as a veteran at the keyboard, is not as important as the common ground he shares with other writers.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/writing-as-a-soldier-and-a-civilian/', 'snippet': 'A soldier takes time out of uniform to pursue an MFA in writing, and discovers that what sets him apart, as a veteran at the keyboard, is not as important as the common ground he shares with other writers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is 12 a.m. in the land of the midnight sun. Seventy-two hours until deployment. I should be at home with my wife, Jen, and 6-month-old son or unpacking the house we bought recently. Instead, I’m on my bike riding home from the University of Alaska, Anchorage. A rowdy group rides down another trail that merges with mine, cycling in a pack in front of me. They laugh, pull beers from messenger bags, see me and offer me one. The exchange is tour-worthy. An anonymous rider pulls out a cold Olympia and reaches toward me. His eyes remain on the trail ahead, as do mine. I extend a blind left hand, close the gap, find the front of the can. For a moment we are connected by cheap beer. Then he lets go and it is all mine. I toast the rowdies and ride ahead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/us/atwar-komatsu/atwar-komatsu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/10/us/atwar-komatsu/atwar-komatsu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/us/atwar-komatsu/atwar-komatsu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/us/atwar-komatsu/atwar-komatsu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/us/atwar-komatsu/atwar-komatsu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/10/us/atwar-komatsu/atwar-komatsu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/us/atwar-komatsu/atwar-komatsu-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Writing as a Soldier and a Civilian', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klay, Phil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Brian (1967- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Air Force', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alaska', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T13:53:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Komatsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Komatsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43cf9617-def3-5cf9-860d-cd4b12ecb1a1', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43cf9617-def3-5cf9-860d-cd4b12ecb1a1'}, {'abstract': 'The stars of the musical “The Last Five Years” discuss their roles in the film.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/toronto-festival-2014-anna-kendrick-and-jeremy-jordan-on-the-last-five-years/', 'snippet': 'The stars of the musical “The Last Five Years” discuss their roles in the film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — A couple sings its way through the exciting beginning and the difficult unraveling of a relationship in “The Last Five Years,” Richard LaGravenese’s film adaptation of Jason Robert Brown’s Off-Broadway musical. In this video, Anna Kendrick and Jeremy Jordan their roles, and their songs, in the film.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toronto Festival 2014: Anna Kendrick and Jeremy Jordan on ‘The Last Five Years’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Jason Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jordan, Jeremy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kendrick, Anna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaGravenese, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T13:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organi