o-del-toro-on-playing-pablo-escobar/', 'snippet': 'The actor discusses playing the Colombian drug lord Pablo Escobar in the film “Escobar: Paradise Lost.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — Family man, politician, ruthless drug lord. All of these sides of Pablo Escobar are explored in the thriller “Escobar: Paradise Lost,” directed by Andrea Di Stefano and featuring Benicio Del Toro as Escobar. The film follows a Canadian surfer named Nick (Josh Hutcherson), who, while spending time in Colombia, falls for Escobar’s niece (Claudia Traisac) and finds himself pulled into the drug kingpin’s dark world. In this video, Mr. Del Toro discusses his approach to the role.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toronto Festival 2014: Benicio Del Toro on Playing Pablo Escobar', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T16:46:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/745ea7c7-c80c-520b-afaa-5d27ba8bd63b', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/745ea7c7-c80c-520b-afaa-5d27ba8bd63b'}, {'abstract': 'Step and Repeat, a Saturday series which kicks off this weekend, features new-media artists, poets, dancers, rappers, musicians and comedians.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/step-and-repeat-live-performance-museum-of-contemporary-art-los-angeles/', 'snippet': 'Step and Repeat, a Saturday series which kicks off this weekend, features new-media artists, poets, dancers, rappers, musicians and comedians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Museum of Contemporary Art Los Angeles has gone through plenty of changes lately, beginning with the hiring of a new director, Philippe Vergne. One of Vergne’s first orders of business upon arriving was giving the confident staff he inherited — including the curator Bennett Simpson and the MOCAtv director Emma Reeves — the green light to move ahead with Step and Repeat, a monthlong series at the Geffen Contemporary. Over four consecutive Saturdays starting September 13 and ending October 4, the bill will be filled out with poets, DJs, bands, performance artists and comedians, including both familiar names and fledgling artists, in a kind of West Coast multimedia analog to MoMA P.S.1’s summer Warm Up series. It’s a major step forward in providing a showcase for live performance in Los Angeles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/t-magazine/11step-williams-1/11step-williams-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/11/t-magazine/11step-williams-1/11step-williams-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/t-magazine/11step-williams-1/11step-williams-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/t-magazine/11step-williams-1/11step-williams-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/t-magazine/11step-williams-1/11step-williams-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/11/t-magazine/11step-williams-1/11step-williams-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/t-magazine/11step-williams-1/11step-williams-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Live Performance Extravaganza Comes to the Museum of Contemporary Art Los Angeles', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T16:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maxwell Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maxwell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06de33ef-b5b1-554f-8ace-99e1fa58eae7', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06de33ef-b5b1-554f-8ace-99e1fa58eae7'}, {'abstract': 'Howie Karpin, 60, an official scorer for both the Mets and the Yankees, is now in his 16th full season of recording the game action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/nyregion/the-scorekeeper.html', 'snippet': 'Howie Karpin, 60, an official scorer for both the Mets and the Yankees, is now in his 16th full season of recording the game action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For those keeping score, mark it as the 901st regular season game for the man in the khakis and T-shirt settling into the press box at CitiField on Tuesday night.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm