oups that are “contradictory to Russian policy.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nations Trying to Stop Their Citizens From Going to Middle East to Fight for ISIS', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nations Working to Stop Citizens from Aiding ISIS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T17:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18260bba-f459-50b3-9fd7-a6ea26e897f6', 'word_count': 1417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18260bba-f459-50b3-9fd7-a6ea26e897f6'}, {'abstract': 'A Russian ministry spokesman said that if President Obama proceeded with a plan for air strikes in Syria against ISIS, it would violate international law.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/russia-scolds-the-u-s-over-syria/', 'snippet': 'A Russian ministry spokesman said that if President Obama proceeded with a plan for air strikes in Syria against ISIS, it would violate international law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vladimir Putin’s latest foray into the international debate over Syria took chutzpah.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Scolds the U.S. Over Syria', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T17:57:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba22203b-4e63-5c7d-8832-e63c74e46215', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba22203b-4e63-5c7d-8832-e63c74e46215'}, {'abstract': 'The artist and filmmaker has created limited-edition sets of pill-printed pajamas for Andy Spade’s line of lazywear.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/mike-mills-sleepy-jones-pajamas-collaboration/', 'snippet': 'The artist and filmmaker has created limited-edition sets of pill-printed pajamas for Andy Spade’s line of lazywear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that New York Fashion Week has ended, those involved would love nothing more than the chance to sink into a pillow and doze off. Just in time for the most exhausted moment of the year, the artist and filmmaker Mike Mills has designed a limited-edition set of pajamas for Sleepy Jones, Andy Spade’s line of stylish lazywear. The navy-and-white sets, available in men’s and women’s tops and bottoms ($74-$165), come printed with Mills’s illustrations of the various sleep aids and anxiety pills taken by his friends. “My sleep is the first to go when I start worrying, thinking too much, when life turbulence hits,” Mills says. “I let all the thoughts you don’t want to think in.” Though it’s not the first time that the prescriptions we pop have made for a pop-art-meets-fashion motif (see Damien Hirst’s pharmaceutical-studded backpack for the Row), the pill pattern, in the case of these soft cotton pieces, offers both metaphorical and literal comfort.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/t-magazine/12pajama-hartman/12pajama-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/12/t-magazine/12pajama-hartman/12pajama-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 642}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/t-magazine/12pajama-hartman/12pajama-hartman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 958, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/12/t-magazine/12pajama-hartman/12pajama-hartman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 20