2014/09/13/world/middleeast/elite-israeli-officers-decry-treatment-of-palestinians.html', 'snippet': 'In a letter sent to commanders and the prime minister, 43 veteran officers of a vaunted intelligence unit said they would refuse required reserve duty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Denouncing Israel’s treatment of Palestinians under occupation, a group of veterans from an elite, secretive military intelligence unit have declared they will no longer “take part in the state’s actions against Palestinians” in required reserve duty because of what they called “our moral duty to act.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Veterans of Elite Israeli Unit Refuse Reserve Duty, Citing Treatment of Palestinians ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Veterans of Elite Israeli Unit Refuse Reserve Duty, Citing Treatment of Palestinians', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T18:18:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b145ad2-68e8-5145-a9ea-ecdae6e6edce', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b145ad2-68e8-5145-a9ea-ecdae6e6edce'}, {'abstract': 'The statements are the league’s most unvarnished admission yet that the sport’s professional participants sustain severe brain injuries at far higher rates than the general population.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/13/sports/football/actuarial-reports-in-nfl-concussion-deal-are-released.html', 'snippet': 'The statements are the league’s most unvarnished admission yet that the sport’s professional participants sustain severe brain injuries at far higher rates than the general population.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Football League, which for years disputed evidence that its players had a high rate of severe brain damage, has stated in federal court documents that it expects nearly a third of retired players to develop long-term cognitive problems and that the conditions are likely to emerge at “notably younger ages” than in the general population.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/13/sports/13concussions/13concussions-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/13/sports/13concussions/13concussions-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/13/sports/13concussions/13concussions-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/13/sports/13concussions/13concussions-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/13/sports/13concussions/13concussions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/13/sports/13concussions/13concussions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/13/sports/13concussions/13concussions-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brain Trauma to Affect One in Three Players, N.F.L. Agrees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brain Trauma to Affect 1 in 3, N.F.L. Agrees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chronic Traumatic Encephalopathy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brody, Anita B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seau, Junior', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Segal Group Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T18:23:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05413bbf-e723-5a77-a525-e224398ffc23', 'word_count': 1434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05413bbf-e723-5a77-a525-e224398ffc23'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. O’Farrill, the Grammy Award-winning pianist and composer, spends his Sundays in a frenzy of improvisation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/nyregion/arturo-ofarrill-dont-take-five.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. O’Farrill, the Grammy Award-winning pianist and composer, spends his Sundays in a frenzy of improvisation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arturo O’Farrill, the Grammy Award-winning pianist and composer, spends his Sundays in a frenzy of improvisation. By day he directs a youth orchestra, the Fat Afro Latin Jazz Cats. By night he takes the stage himself with his own group, the Afro Latin Jazz Orchestra, at Birdland. On Sept. 20, the two groups will play together at Pueblo Harlem, a cultural festival. Mr. O’Farrill, 54, lives in Park Slope with his wife, Alison Deane, 62, a classical pianist. “I made one rule for myself, and I really try to live it: Play music you love, with people you love, for people you love,” Mr. O’Farrill said. “If I can’t be that kind of musician, I’ll drive a cab. Creating music based on art and giving away from your spirit is more important than making a living.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE1/14ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE1/14ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE1/14ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE1/14ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1604, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cr