nteresting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/dining/for-rosh-hashana-roast-chicken-with-honey.html', 'snippet': 'Honoring tradition while keeping the meal interesting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every Rosh Hashana, Jews smear honey on sliced apples and thick pieces of challah with the idea that a sweet New Year’s meal will usher in a sweet new year. It’s a symbolic ritual I’ve never questioned, since it’s also a tasty one. And who wouldn’t want to hedge their bets in such a pleasant way?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Holiday, Sweet Kisses Spice', 'kicker': 'A Good Appetite', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Holiday, Sweet Gives a Kiss to Spice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rosh Hashana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chickens', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Honey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T20:07:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41ea429a-9561-5396-9ff8-bd7263bcf0c4', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41ea429a-9561-5396-9ff8-bd7263bcf0c4'}, {'abstract': '“No Good Deed” stars Idris Elba as an escaped convict with a violent history against women, invading the house of a stay-at-home mother.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/13/movies/no-good-deed-stars-idris-elba-as-an-escaped-felon.html', 'snippet': '“No Good Deed” stars Idris E