'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ab4e7e0-f770-577a-a649-e70ce2e5cfb6', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ab4e7e0-f770-577a-a649-e70ce2e5cfb6'}, {'abstract': 'Dawn Upshaw and Gilbert Kalish headlined a performance of George Crumb’s “Ancient Voices of Children” for Nonesuch Records’ 50th-anniversary celebration at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/13/arts/music/dawn-upshaw-sings-crumbs-ancient-voices-at-bam.html', 'snippet': 'Dawn Upshaw and Gilbert Kalish headlined a performance of George Crumb’s “Ancient Voices of Children” for Nonesuch Records’ 50th-anniversary celebration at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The soprano Dawn Upshaw turned her back to the audience and leaned over the uncovered strings of a grand piano at the beginning of the second half of Thursday evening’s concert at the Harvey Theater at the Brooklyn Academy of Music. Steadying herself on the instrument’s frame with her hands, she bent over deeply and began to sing — cooing, pleading, beseeching sounds that grew more frantic and shrill until they sounded like curses and incantations. Refracted by the piano’s strings, echoes floated up from the instrument and hovered about her like an iridescent aura.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/13/arts/13UPSHAW/13UPSHAW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/13/arts/13UPSHAW/13UPSHAW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/13/arts/13UPSHAW/13UPSHAW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None