efing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T21:01:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae6553fb-9b92-5df5-8f12-c6b1a8e11b60', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae6553fb-9b92-5df5-8f12-c6b1a8e11b60'}, {'abstract': 'A new education wing, built as part of a renovation that also includes a roof terrace, reflects Carnegie’s evolution from an old-line temple of music to something of a teacher of music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/13/arts/music/resnick-education-wing-prepares-to-open.html', 'snippet': 'A new education wing, built as part of a renovation that also includes a roof terrace, reflects Carnegie’s evolution from an old-line temple of music to something of a teacher of music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The old joke held that the way to get to Carnegie Hall was to “practice, practice, practice.” Now musicians will have more places to practice once they get there: The scaffolding that has shrouded Carnegie for four years is coming down this week to reveal the hall’s new education wing, with new practice rooms, and a roof garden more than a century in the making.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/13/arts/13MUSICjp1/13MUSICjp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/13/arts/13MUSICjp1/13MUSICjp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subt