-5622-8a4f-d915d965ccc0'}, {'abstract': '“Stills,” a series of harrowing, six-and-a-half-foot-tall photographs depicting bodies falling from buildings was first created by the artist Sarah Charlesworth in 1980.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/arts/design/stills-by-sarah-charlesworth.html', 'snippet': '“Stills,” a series of harrowing, six-and-a-half-foot-tall photographs depicting bodies falling from buildings was first created by the artist Sarah Charlesworth in 1980.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Stills,” a series of harrowing, six-and-a-half-foot-tall photographs depicting bodies falling from buildings — often frozen in midair — was first created by the artist Sarah Charlesworth in 1980. Charlesworth, who died last year, was part of the so-called Pictures Generation, that group of artists who emerged in the 1970s and ’80s whose works often used existing images or carefully staged tableaus. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1126, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1126}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 546, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1092, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', '