: Film Week at the Philharmonic.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second year, the New York Philharmonic eases back into a new season with “The Art of the Score: Film Week at the Philharmonic.” The fun begins with a program dedicated to the often-sensuous scores from Cinecittà, with “La Dolce Vita: The Music of Italian Cinema.” On Tuesday and Wednesday, the Philharmonic’s music director, Alan Gilbert, conducts excerpts from the soundtracks to classics like “La Dolce Vita,” “The Leopard” and “L’Eclisse.” The violinist Joshua Bell, the soprano Renée Fleming and the singer-songwriter Josh Groban join in. (7:30 p.m., Avery Fisher Hall, nyphil.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14SUBGUIDE2/14SUBGUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14SUBGUIDE2/14SUBGUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14SUBGUIDE2/14SUBGUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14SUBGUIDE2/14SUBGUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14SUBGUIDE2/14SUBGUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14SUBGUIDE2/14SUBGUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty