ector Hou Hsiao-hsien’s films on the big screen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/movies/hou-hsiao-hsien-comes-to-the-museum-of-the-moving-image.html', 'snippet': 'Audiences in the United States get a rare opportunity to see the great Taiwanese director Hou Hsiao-hsien’s films on the big screen.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The dead stay dead, but money’s real,” says a character in “Good Men, Good Women,” a 1995 film by the great Taiwanese director Hou Hsiao-hsien. Except in “Good Men,” the dead are like the past, tethered to the present in mournful, rapt communion. Audiences in the United States don’t get many opportunities to see Mr. Hou’s movies on the big screen, which makes the Museum of the Moving Image’s retrospective “Also Like Life: The Films of Hou Hsiao-hsien” (through Oct. 17), essential viewing. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1346, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy