}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T22:49:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7cde67e-0e41-5196-b282-cff979706f12', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7cde67e-0e41-5196-b282-cff979706f12'}, {'abstract': 'The automaker will fix driver’s side air bags in about 2,000 Corvettes because they could separate from their steering wheels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/13/business/corvettes-recalled-over-air-bags-and-parking-brakes.html', 'snippet': 'The automaker will fix driver’s side air bags in about 2,000 Corvettes because they could separate from their steering wheels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'General Motors has told car dealers to stop delivery of certain 2015 Chevrolet Corvettes because they may have faulty air bags and parking brake cables. The automaker will fix driver’s side air bags in about 2,000 Corvettes because they could separate from their steering wheels. Another 800 Corvettes, most of which are at dealerships, are being held back from buyers because they may have been built with defective rear parking brake cables, increasing the risk that parked cars could roll away. Automotive News reported that G.M. was issuing two additional recalls for the vehicles, according to the stop-sales orders sent to dealers, but neither has been publicly announced. Alan Adler, a G.M. spokesman, would not confirm them. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.M. Stops Some Corvette Sales Over Air Bags', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.M. Stops Some Corvette Sales Over Air Bags', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T22:55:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ivory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/27d3b52a-ecf9-52c0-b68b-ba880f97c7c6', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27d3b52a-ecf9-52c0-b68b-ba880f97c7c6'}, {'abstract': 'A crucial issue is that whenever a state offers an incentive for a company to build a factory, the economic stimulus is rarely concentrated in the surrounding area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/13/business/nevada-woos-tesla-plant-in-tax-deal-but-economic-benefits-prompt-debate.html', 'snippet': 'A crucial issue is that whenever a state offers an incentive for a company to build a factory, the economic stimulus is rarely concentrated in the surrounding area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Nevada lured Tesla Motors to the Reno area to build a giant battery factory, a triumphant governor, Brian Sandoval, proclaimed that every dollar his state was spending in tax incentives and other subsidies would yield $80 in economic activity.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nevada Woos Tesla Plant in Tax Deal, but Economic Benefits Prompt Debate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nevada Woos Tesla Plant in Tax Deal, but Economic Benefits Prompt Debate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tesla Motors Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-12T22:56:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/406adf7b-6a02-5c2d-a922-754075eb9f91', 'word_count': 1226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/406adf7b-6a02-5c2d-a922-754075eb9f91'}, {'abstract': 'One thing highlighted at the beginning of “Rothko to Richter: Mark-Making in Abstract Painting from the Collection of Preston H. Haskell,” in Princeton, is that our concept of traditional art history has changed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/nyregion/a-review-of-rothko-to-richter-mark-making-in-abstract-painting-from-the-collection-of-preston-h-haskell-in-princeton.html', 'snippet': 'One thing highlighted at the beginning of “Rothko to Richter: Mark-Making in Abstract Painting from the Collection of Preston H. Haskell,” in Princeton, is that our concept of traditional art history has changed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been over a hundred years since abstraction was adopted in Western painting, and we’re still trying to make sense of it. Despite the rather clunky subtitle and the fact that the exhibition is drawn from a single collection, “Rothko to Richter: Mark-Making in Abstract Painting from the Collection of Preston H. Haskell” offers an excellent, compact survey of some of the key arguments.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ARTSNJ_COMBO/14ARTSNJ_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ARTSNJ_COMBO/14ARTSNJ_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ARTSNJ_COMBO/14ARTSNJ_COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ARTSNJ_COMBO/14ARTSNJ_COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1448, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ARTSNJ_COMBO/14ARTSNJ_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ARTSNJ_COMBO/14ARTSNJ_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/nyregion/14ARTSNJ_COMBO/14ARTSNJ_COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Process Behind the Painting', 'kicker': 'Art Review | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Process Behind the Painting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'maj