ank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8641abe0-4379-50c2-bb1c-ba87e30203f4', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8641abe0-4379-50c2-bb1c-ba87e30203f4'}, {'abstract': 'T. J. Lane, a 19-year-old serving life in prison for killing three students in a school cafeteria in 2012, was transferred with two other inmates to a maximum-security prison on Friday after briefly escaping a lower-security site, the Ohio Department of Rehabilitation and Correction said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/13/us/ohio-answers-sought-in-prison-break.html', 'snippet': 'T. J. Lane, a 19-year-old serving life in prison for killing three students in a school cafeteria in 2012, was transferred with two other inmates to a maximum-security prison on Friday after briefly escaping a lower-security site, the Ohio Departm...', 'lead_paragraph': 'T. J. Lane, a 19-year-old serving life in prison for killing three students in a school cafeteria in 2012, was transferred with two other inmates to a maximum-security prison on Friday after briefly escaping a lower-security site, the Ohio Department of Rehabilitation and Correction said. They were moved to the Ohio State Penitentiary in Youngstown, a day after they climbed a fence and escaped a prison in Lima, setting off a nine-hour search. The agency said it was investigating details, including a report that guards warned prison officials about an escape plot, and a panel is expected to make recommendations about improving prison procedures. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ohio: Answers Sought in Prison Break', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ohio: Answers Sought in Prison Break', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Escapes', 'rank': 3, 'ma