eart sank.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SOULCYCLE1/14SOULCYCLE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SOULCYCLE1/14SOULCYCLE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 329}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SOULCYCLE1/14SOULCYCLE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 561, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SOULCYCLE1/14SOULCYCLE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1122, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SOULCYCLE1/14SOULCYCLE1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SOULCYCLE1/14SOULCYCLE1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SOULCYCLE1/14SOULCYCLE1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At SoulCycle Tribeca, The Spinning Stops; Panic Ensues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Spinning Stops; Panic Ensues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubin, Courtney', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SoulCycle LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'TriBeCa (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-13T00:58:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Courtney Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Courtney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cabde16-fc2f-5e8b-a79f-07678c4bf7d3', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cabde16-fc2f-5e8b-a79f-07678c4bf7d3'}, {'abstract': 'The issue checks in with an eclectic mix of guys who are pursuing their passions.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/inside-the-t-mens-fall-fashion-issue/', 'snippet': 'The issue checks in with an eclectic mix of guys who are pursuing their passions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T’s fall men’s fashion issue celebrates guys who pursue their passions. On the cover is the young English actor Jack O’Connell, whose electric performances and rough-and-tumble ways have him perched on the cusp of stardom — if he can only keep it together long enough to reach the potential that many, like his “Unbroken” director Angelina Jolie, see in him. René Redzepi, owner of one of the world’s top-ranked restaurant, Noma, is a closet taco fanatic, so Jeff Gordinier follows the Scandinavian chef to Mexico in search of bold new flavors and, possibly, the next big thing in food. We travel to the rural Connecticut estate of the Picasso biographer John Richardson, which deftly mixes high and low, refined and roguish, the tasteful and the gaudy. Elsewhere, T pays a visit to the NBA’s finishing school for rookies, where draftees receive advice on fashion, sex and table manners, and are taught to repeat the mantra “I don’t want to go broke”; Marin Hopper remembers the way her father, the actor Dennis Hopper, found spiritual reckoning — and plenty of good parties — in Taos, N. M.; Alex Fury sounds off on a men’s wear moment that is, at long last, challenging notions about sexuality, power and gender politics; and Jody Rosen travels to a sprawling forensics lab in hippie Oregon to investigate the $19 billion trade in illegal wildlife, which has ties to the Russian mob and Islamic extremists. See all stories from the issue >>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14MensCover/14MensCover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14MensCover/14MensCover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 726}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14MensCover/14MensCover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 846, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14MensCover/14MensCover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1652, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14MensCover/14MensCover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14MensCover/14MensCover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazin