in pay have an insidious ripple effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Closing the persistent wage gap between men and women is important, not only as a matter of fairness but as a matter of rudimentary family economics: Women are the primary or co-breadwinner in more than 60 percent of American families. That makes it all the more urgent to address the conspicuous discrepancy that sees a woman working full-time making 77 cents on average against $1 for a man working full-time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Showdown on the Pay Gap', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Showdown on the Pay Gap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mikulski, Barbara A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-13T01:18:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6491ed8-129d-5faf-ac37-2076a3a98011', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6491ed8-129d-5faf-ac37-2076a3a98011'}, {'abstract': 'Many thought Rice received preferential treatment by prosecutors after punching his fiancée, but in most cases, domestic assaults do not lead to jail time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/13/sports/football/ray-rice-case-highlights-a-crime-often-overlooked.html', 'snippet': 'Many thought Rice received preferential treatment by prosecutors after punching his fiancée, but in most cases, domestic assaults do not lead to jail time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTIC CITY — To many who viewed the video of the N.F.L. star Ray Rice assaulting his fiancée in the elevator of a casino here, the contrast between the viciousness of his attack and the leniency of his legal punishment was both baffling and infuriating.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ray Rice Case Draws Attention to a Crime Often Obscured', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rice Case Draws Attention to a Crime Often Obscured', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Ray (1987- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kocieniewski, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Vikings', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peterson, Adrian', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-13T01:19:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 