 'nyt://article/d7d0f6a7-d1d5-58c3-882e-f818bdf61953', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7d0f6a7-d1d5-58c3-882e-f818bdf61953'}, {'abstract': 'Right now, homework is feeling like an instrument of torture designed to destroy my relationship with my children. But we go through this every September. It will get better.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/12/the-mechanics-of-homework/', 'snippet': 'Right now, homework is feeling like an instrument of torture designed to destroy my relationship with my children. But we go through this every September. It will get better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The homework wars among education wonks, teachers and parents don’t, as my friend and colleague Bruce Feiler writes in “The Homework Squabbles,” his This Life column for Sunday Styles, matter much on the scale at which most families are dealing with homework. To us, the question of how valuable homework is has to be set aside daily in the name of the backpacks, folders, binders and worksheets full of the stuff that our children actually bring home. And it’s worth noting that this idea of “too much homework” as a national problem is a myth. Instead, homework is something of an ironic twist in the American inequality story, with the more pressing problem being with the children who have too little rather than those who have too much. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mechanics of Homework', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homework', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-13T01:52:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3b9e09e-4d0e-50f8-8105-49c1193084b5', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3b9e09e-4d0e-50f8-8105-49c1193084b5'}, {'abstract': 'Since introducing her first collection in 2010, she has in short order become one of the highlights of London Fashion Week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/fashion/london-fashion-week-simone-rocha-born-to-fashion-makes-her-own-mark.html', 'snippet': 'Since introducing her first collection in 2010, she has in short order become one of the highlights of London Fashion Week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simone Rocha attended her first fashion show at the ripe age of zero, and followed up the experience no less often than every six months ever since. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SIMONE1-copy/14SIMONE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SIMONE1-copy/14SIMONE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SIMONE1-copy/14SIMONE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/fashion/14SIMONE1-copy/14SIMONE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1319, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/fas