hat Birth Control Could Let You Down?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-13T15:50:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sunday Review', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By GREGOR AISCH and BILL MARSH', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'AISCH', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARSH', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/9be3c64c-a43a-581a-a1ad-affefe1c3ee2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/9be3c64c-a43a-581a-a1ad-affefe1c3ee2'}, {'abstract': 'We need to develop a new ethic of responsible parenthood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/opinion/sunday/beyond-marriage.html', 'snippet': 'We need to develop a new ethic of responsible parenthood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARRIAGE is disappearing. More than 40 percent of new mothers are unmarried. Many young adults drift into parenthood unintentionally. They may be cohabiting at the time of their child’s birth, but about half of these couples will have split up by the time their child is 5 years old. College-educated young adults are still marrying before having children and planning their families more intentionally. The rest of America, about two-thirds of the population, is not.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond Marriage', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beyond Marriage', 'name': None, 's