atsenyuk, told a conference of security experts in Kiev.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A week into a fragile cease-fire between government troops and pro-Russian rebels in Ukraine, that country’s prime minister offered a pessimistic assessment of its chances of holding and said President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia intends eventually to conquer “all of Ukraine.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/world/UKRAINE/UKRAINE-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/world/UKRAINE/UKRAINE-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/world/UKRAINE/UKRAINE-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/world/UKRAINE/UKRAINE-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1337, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/world/UKRAINE/UKRAINE-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/world/UKRAINE/UKRAINE-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/world/UKRAINE/UKRAINE-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putin Intent on Taking ‘All of Ukraine,’ Premier Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putin Intent on Taking ‘All of Ukraine,’ Leader Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yatsenyuk, Arseniy P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-13T17:18:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9e6a0f4-f14f-5fb2-9c8e-bd95ce709ae4', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9e6a0f4-f14f-5fb2-9c8e-bd95ce709ae4'}, {'abstract': 'People keep texting when they’re behind the wheel, so an engineer has found a technological solution. The problem: He can’t do it on his own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/business/trying-to-hit-the-brake-on-texting-while-driving.html', 'snippet': 'People keep texting when they’re behind the wheel, so an engineer has found a technological solution. The problem: He can’t do it on his own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People know they shouldn’t text and drive. Overwhelmingly, they tell pollsters that doing so is unacceptable and dangerous, and yet they do it anyway. They can’t resist. So safety advocates and public officials have called for a technological solution that does an end run around free will and prevents people from texting in the first place.', 'print_section': 'BU