 that creative work survives its creator is usually empty. Shakespeare boasted that his sonnets would outlast monuments and the memory of princes, and they have. But it’s rare for an artist to keep audiences interested over generations. Most creative endeavors are ravaged by what Shakespeare called “sluttish time.” Even the list of Nobel laureates in literature is filled with now-unfamiliar names.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2114: A Library Project', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2114: A Library Project', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterson, Katie (1981- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oslo (Norway)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Twain, Mark', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Atwood, Margaret', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-13T18:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6da8109a-8d12-579c-a397-36a518a00bf3', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6da8109a-8d12-579c-a397-36a518a00bf3'}, {'abstract': 'When you enable men who beat women, you’re in danger of getting sacked.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/opinion/sunday/maureen-dowd-throw-the-bums-out.html', 'snippet': 'When you enable men who beat women, you’re in danger of getting sacked.', 'le