” without specifying what those issues were. On Saturday, George Atallah, a spokesman for the union, said the vote had authorized union negotiators “to finalize full policies with the N.F.L. as soon as possible.” ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Players Union Seeks Final Drug Agreement', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Pro Football', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.F.L. Union Seeks Final Drug Agreement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League Players Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-14T04:35:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee8cb028-515a-500e-847d-5fdda030b5df', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee8cb028-515a-500e-847d-5fdda030b5df'}, {'abstract': 'Mayweather improved to 47-0 in a welterweight rematch with Maidana that included an accusation of biting in the eighth round.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/sports/floyd-mayweather-jr-remains-unbeaten-with-decision-over-marcos-maidana.html', 'snippet': 'Mayweather improved to 47-0 in a welterweight rematch with Maidana that included an accusation of biting in the eighth round.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — In the lead-up to Saturday night’s wel