or the Baltimore Ravens running back pushed the gossip site to outmaneuver the rest of the media to get the goods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.F.L., arguably the three most powerful letters in branding, bumped into three other letters — TMZ — and was thrown for a huge loss.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/business/newdavidcarrpic/newdavidcarrpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 285, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/business/newdavidcarrpic/newdavidcarrpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 285, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/business/newdavidcarrpic/newdavidcarrpic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/27/business/newdavidcarrpic/newdavidcarrpic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/business/newdavidcarrpic/newdavidcarrpic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Ray Rice Scandal, TMZ Scores on a Fumble', 'kicker': 'The Media Equation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Ray (1987- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Janay Palmer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levin, Harvey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TMZ.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-14T13:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01421c58-ed04-5ade-b816-eddab68fd9c1', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01421c58-ed04-5ade-b816-eddab68fd9c1'}, {'abstract': 'American officials have made it clear they do not want the airstrikes to get ahead of the ground action against ISIS, which they said would take time to mass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/world/middleeast/arab-nations-offer-to-conduct-airstrikes-against-isis-us-official-says.html', 'snippet': 'American officials have made it clear they do not want the airstrikes to get ahead of the ground action against ISIS, which they said would take time to mass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration said Sunday that “several” Arab nations had offered to join in airstrikes against the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria, but any sustained military campaign does not appear imminent, and is likely to require an even more significant commitment from other nations and fighting forces in the region. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/world/JP-DIPLO/JP-DIPLO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/