': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-14T13:43:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger, Michael R. Gordon and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6d7e45c-95ce-50d1-845d-5045f498ccb5', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6d7e45c-95ce-50d1-845d-5045f498ccb5'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: An elderly man in Paris assured he would continue looking after sparrows despite the war, in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/1914-m-henri-pol-will-go-on-caring-for-paris-sparrows/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: An elderly man in Paris assured he would continue looking after sparrows despite the war, in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘‘Still here? Of course, I’m still here!’’ exclaimed M. Henri Pol, as with a wide sweep of the arm he scattered a generous handful of carefully-prepared bread pellets over the gravel path in the Tuileries Gardens. ‘‘It’s quite natural. I don’t see that there is any reason for congratulating me.’’ ‘‘These Parisian birds are unhappy enough already,’’ continued M. Pol, preparing more bread. ‘‘Nobody worries about them in the gardens, and they are growing thin and worrying because they no longer see the children playing. This is not the time to leave them, for what would become of them if the Germans came into Paris? ‘‘So I must stop here with them. In ‘70 I already passed through the upheaval of a war. But in those days I was of an age when I could shoulder a rifle, and I did not know my birds. I would have you believe that then I did not throw my powder to the sparrows.’’ ‘‘To-day, alas, I am good for nothing but to be a bird-charmer. Yet, you know, each one does what he can, and, although I am not well off, these little birdies will be assured of bread.’’ — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 15, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/blogs/15iht-old15-charmer/15iht-old15-charmer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/15/blogs/15iht-old15-charmer/15iht-old15-charmer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 434}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/blogs/15iht-old15-charmer/15iht-old15-charmer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/blogs/15iht-old15-charmer/15iht-old15-charmer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 999, 'width': 1381, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/blogs/15iht-old15-charmer/15iht-old15-charmer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/15/blogs/15iht-old15-charmer/15iht-old15-charmer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/blogs/15iht-old15-charmer/15iht-old15-charmer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1914: M. Henri Pol Will Go On Caring for Paris Sparrows', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tuileries Gardens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-14T14:22:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b50fc454-71f2-519e-9139-5e93a80daf77', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b50fc454-71f2-519e-9139-5e93a80daf77'}, {'abstract': 'Argentina may move its capital from bustling Buenos Aires to a provincial city in the sleepy north. What would this mean for the country’s infamously stormy economy and contentious political climate?', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/14/what-moving-the-capital-would-mean-for-argentina/', 'snippet': 'Argentina may move its capital from bustling Buenos Aires to a provincial city in the sleepy north. What would this mean for the country’s infamously stormy economy and contentious political climate?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a rough year for Argentina. Another economic default looms on the heels of its second sovereign debt crisis in 13 years. Inflation rates are now second highest in the world, after Venezuela. And as if things couldn’t possibly get worse, the national soccer team lost (by a hair) in the World Cup final against Germany earlier this summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Moving the Capital Would Mean for Argentina', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Cristina Fernandez de', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sasse, Benjamin E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brasilia (Brazil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buenos Aires (Argentina)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Santiago del Estero (Argentina)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South America', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-14T15:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://arti