/renewing-health-coverage-may-not-be-as-automatic-as-government-says.html', 'snippet': 'Officials are encouraging consumers to revisit the federal marketplace to compare plans and ensure that they get the right amount of financial assistance in 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Millions of consumers will soon receive notices from health insurance companies stating that their coverage is being automatically renewed for 2015, along with the financial assistance they received this year from the federal government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Law Has Caveat on Renewal of Coverage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Health Law Has Caveat on Renewal of Coverage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HealthCare.gov', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-14T16:49:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdd6bbd6-cabb-5ec7-b425-40138362f9e9', 'word_count': 1012, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdd6bbd6-cabb-5ec7-b425-40138362f9e9'}, {'abstract': 'The 43 veterans wrote that they refused to continue to be “tools” of Israel’s military rule in the occupied territories, and that information collected “harms innocent people” and “is used for political persecution.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/world/middleeast/israeli-military-threatens-to-discipline-veterans-involved-in-protest-over-intelligence-activities.html', 'snippet': 'The 43 veterans wrote that they refused to continue to be “tools” of Israel’s military rule in the occupied territories, and that information collected “harms innocent people” and “is used for political persecution.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — The Israeli military on Sunday threatened disciplinary action against a group of veterans and active reservists of a secretive military intelligence unit who declared that they would no longer participate in surveillance activities against the Palestinians.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reprisals for Israeli Soldiers Refusing to Spy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reprisals for Israeli Soldiers Refusing to Spy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conscientious Objectors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yediot Aharonot', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-14T17:10:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e085c279-9847-5b27-8