'Long, bendy locks and softly highlighted facial features spoke to the designer’s earthly vision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Backstage at Mary Katrantzou‘s spring/summer 2015 show today, the talk was of tectonic plates, the beginning of the world and not-quite-a-mermaid influences. To capture the designer’s earthly vision, the hairstylist Syd Hayes perfected a long wave with a pronounced bend in the front for additional shape. “It feels to me like she’s by the sea,” he said. “The hair is natural and clean, but there’s a bit of oil and movement.” Hayes first prepped the hair with L’Oreal Elnett Heat Protect Styling Spray Volume, then used a large barrel curler to create the soft, just woken-up waves. “There are no party curls here,” he said. “I want the hair to look as if it’s dried naturally.” He then\xa0finished with Elvive Smooth-Silk Intense Anti-Frizz Serum through the ends for definition and shine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14beauty-katrantzou-gilchrist/14beauty-katrantzou-gilchrist-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14beauty-katrantzou-gilchrist/14beauty-katrantzou-gilchrist-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14beauty-katrantzou-gilchrist/14beauty-katrantzou-gilchrist-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/t-magazine/14beauty-katrantzou-gilchrist/14beauty-katrantzou-gilchrist-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, 