nd corporate sponsors, are intended to make money for NPR.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NPR, following the lead of other news and radio organizations, is widely expanding its live stage shows, with a slate of nearly two dozen events planned nationwide in the coming months. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/business/npr1/npr1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/15/business/npr1/npr1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/business/npr1/npr1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/business/npr1/npr1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/business/npr1/npr1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/15/business/npr1/npr1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/business/npr1/npr1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': ' NPR Adds to Live Shows, With Almost 24 Planned ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'NPR Adds to Live Shows, With Almost 24 Planned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jensen, Elizabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kresge Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-14T21:24:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f01f77c-6a4e-5e29-8503-b6c638e6d460', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f01f77c-6a4e-5e29-8503-b6c638e6d460'}, {'abstract': 'The British government will donate 1.5 million pounds ($2.44 million) to the Royal Shakespeare Company to translate all of Shakespeare’s works into Mandarin for the first time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/theater/shakespeare-in-mandarin.html', 'snippet': 'The British government will donate 1.5 million pounds ($2.44 million) to the Royal Shakespeare Company to translate all of Shakespeare’s works into Mandarin for the first time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How do you say “All the world’s a stage” in Mandarin? The British government will donate 1.5 million pounds ($2.44 million) to the Royal Shakespeare Company to translate all of Shakespeare’s works into that language for the first time. The grant, announced by the Department of Culture, Media and Sport, will finance a company tour of China in 2016 and allow for select Chinese dramatic works to be translated into English. In bringing Shakespeare’s canon of plays to readers, directors and actors in China, the government hopes to forge “stronger links with China,” according to a statement by Sajid Javid, the British culture secretary. “Sharing the very best of our respective cultures is a brilliant way to make this happen,” he said. The translations continue a Shakespeare-centered cultural exchange between the two nations: In 2012, China’s National Theater performed for the first time at the Globe Theater in London, putting on “Richard III” in Mandarin. The British government will donate an additional £300,000, or about $488,000, to support exchanges between China and the British Museum. The Royal Shakespeare Company tour will coincide with the 400th anniversary of Shakespeare’s death.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shakespeare, in Mandarin', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shakespeare, in Mandarin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Shakespeare Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Translation and Interpreters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-14T21:25:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Andrew R. Chow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Chow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb1038c1-fd8d-5e17-a367-3faa35bda2f7', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb1038c1-fd8d-5e17-a367-3faa35bda2f7'}, {'abstract': 'The 4x4 Baroque Music Festival presented “The Grand Overture,” vibrant performances of orchestral suites at St. Paul’s Chapel in Lower Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/arts/music/4x4-baroque-music-festival-presents-the-grand-overture.html', 'snippet': 'The 4x4 Baroque Music Festival presented “The Grand Overture,” vibrant performances of orchestral suites at St. Paul’s Chapel in Lower Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ability of occasion and setting to enhance the power of a musical experience has been demonstrated many times, seldom more clearly, for many New Yorkers, than on Sept. 11, 2011. For the 10th anniversary of the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks, Trinity Wall Street presented a solid day of concerts alternating between Trinity Church and St. Paul’s Chapel, several blocks to the north.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/arts/subbaroque/subbaroque-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/15/arts/subbaroque/subbaroque-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/arts/subbaroque/subbaroque-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/arts/subbaroque/subbaroque-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/arts/subbaroque/subbaroque-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'c