 the judges’ table.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T04:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/06851c13-820b-5d72-bfc3-a3398b797c68', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06851c13-820b-5d72-bfc3-a3398b797c68'}, {'abstract': 'Each September, an old-timers’ battle brings together men who played in two amateur leagues in the Dominican Republic in the 1950s and ’60s: the Liga del Cine and the Liga Ozama.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/sports/baseball/alumni-of-two-dominican-amateur-baseball-leagues-play-each-september.html', 'snippet': 'Each September, an old-timers’ battle brings together men who played in two amateur leagues in the Dominican Republic in the 1950s and ’60s: the Liga del Cine and the Liga Ozama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bony, 73-year-old Dominican pitcher stood atop a mound at the northern edge of Manhattan, tossing curveballs and sliders to the rhythm of salsa music. In the batter’s box, a portly man with a white goatee, gnawing on a wad of tobacco, awaited the pitcher’s long, exaggerated delivery. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not a Young Man’s Game', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not a Young Man’s Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Base