ject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alton, Gregg H', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T10:25:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ededd042-1904-53f8-b822-5940f7052e27', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ededd042-1904-53f8-b822-5940f7052e27'}, {'abstract': 'In the wake of devastating monsoon floods in northern India and Pakistan, Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s confusing comments on climate change are troubling.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/its-a-season-of-deadly-rains-in-india-does-the-new-prime-minister-believe-in-climate-change/', 'snippet': 'In the wake of devastating monsoon floods in northern India and Pakistan, Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s confusing comments on climate change are troubling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 450 deaths were reported as monsoon floods ravaged parts of northern Pakistan and the Indian state of Jammu and Kashmir last week. The area is weathering the heaviest rainy season in more than half a century. A photo essay compiled for The Atlantic illustrates the awful scale of the devastation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Season of Deadly Rains in India, Does the New Prime Minister Believe in Climate Change?', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monsoons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T10:29:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7bd606b-77cb-5e45-96d2-1770aefc0a36', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7bd606b-77cb-5e45-96d2-1770aefc0a36'}, {'abstract': 'After charging the 81-year-old with “creating a disturbance,” officers hauled away computers and his cellphone, as well as books and periodicals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/world/asia/police-detain-tie-liu-beijing-writer-and-underground-publisher.html', 'snippet': 'After charging the 81-year-old with “creating a disturbance,” officers hauled away computers and his cellphone, as well as books and periodicals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — At 81 years old and after decades imprisoned in labor camps as a foe of the Communist Party, the Beijing writer and underground publisher Tie Liu had said that he was too old to seriously worry the security police anymore. But they raided his home over the weekend and detained him on a charge of “creating a disturbance,” his wife and friends said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Detain Tie Liu, Beijing Writer and Underground Publisher', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Dissident Writer Is Detained', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tie Liu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Yunshan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T10:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dd27bf5-1420-556f-9d7c-787480abd12a', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dd27bf5-1420-556f-9d7c-787480abd12a'}, {'abstract': 'London', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2014/09/15/fashion/runway-womens/roksanda-ilincic-spring-2015-rtw.html', 'snippet': 'London', 'lead_paragraph': 'London', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/fashion/runway-womens/roksanda-fashion-week-slide-H9Y0/roksanda-fashion-week-slide-H9Y0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 6