': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T10:53:52+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Women's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ad3e096f-3ce7-5e68-9281-3c114cb7f8f2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ad3e096f-3ce7-5e68-9281-3c114cb7f8f2'}, {'abstract': 'In the 1990s, consumers rebelled against the restrictions imposed by health maintenance organizations. There’s a risk it could happen again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/upshot/limiting-choice-to-control-health-spending-a-caution.html', 'snippet': 'In the 1990s, consumers rebelled against the restrictions imposed by health maintenance organizations. There’s a risk it could happen again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To what extent will the recent moderation in the growth of health care prices and spending continue? This is a big question, and the answer relies on many factors. But for plans offered in the new health insurance exchanges as well as a substantial minority of employer-sponsored plans, it may depend, in part, on how long consumers are willing to trade lower premiums for less choice. History offers a cautionary tale.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/upshot/16up-health/16up-health-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/upshot/16up-health/16up-health-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/upshot/16up-health/16up-health-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/upshot/16up-health/16up-health-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/upshot/16up-health/16up-health-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/16/upshot/16up-health/16up-health-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/upshot/16up-health/16up-health-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Limiting Choice to Control Health Spending: A Caution', 'kicker': 'The New Health Care', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Nineties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T10:56:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Frakt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frakt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb69499f-2058-5919-a841-1354525f034d', 'word_count': 1180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb69499f-2058-5919-a841-1354525f034d'}, {'abstract': 'Of all the dramas that entrepreneurs discuss with one another over drinks, the merging of personal relationships with business seems to cause the most pain.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/the-problem-with-going-into-business-with-a-friend/', 'snippet': 'Of all the dramas that entrepreneurs discuss with one another over drinks, the merging of personal relationships with business seems to cause the most pain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I spent a recent night consoling an associate who had fallen out with her best friend. They tried to start a business together, and she quit her high-paying job to do it. Three months in, the friend had yet to commit full-time and wasn’t pulling her weight. They couldn’t agree on how to split either the tasks or the ownership stakes. Tension built and eventually exploded, and the business died before it was born. Their 15-year friendship was over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Problem With Going Into Business With a Friend', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T11:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebekah Campbell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebekah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Campbell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96aec9cd-da52-504d-a166-cc5fdd5d4c39', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96aec9cd-da52-504d-a166-cc5fdd5d4c39'}, {'abstract': 'The Apple Watch is both a product and the embodiment of Apple’s values — taste, trust and utility — that have long guided the company’s product and design decisions.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/what-the-apple-watch-says-about-apple/', 'snippet': 'The Apple Watch is both a product and the embodiment of Apple’s values — taste, trust and utility — that have long guided the company’s product and design decisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching Timothy D. Cook last week as he introduced the Apple Watch to the world was almost touching, in his channeling of his predecessor. The back-and-forth pacing of the stage, the hand gestures, the cadence of his speech and the script unabashedly filled with superlatives\xa0— “We set out to build the best watch in the world”\xa0— were all reminiscent of the late Steven P. Jobs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/business/14bits-cookwatch/14bits-cookwatch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/14/business/14bits-cookwatch/14bits-cookwatch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/business/14bits-cookwatch/14bits-cookwatch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/business/14bits-cookwatch/14bits-cookwatch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/business/14bits-cookwatch/14bits-cookwatch-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/14/business/14bits-cookwatch/14bits-cookwatch-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/14/business/14bits-cookwatch/14bits-cookwatch-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Apple Watch Says About Apple', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPod', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cook, Timothy D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T11:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c2273cb-9f18-5c0e-9630-f70e76a4aeb9', 'word_count': 1433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c2273cb-9f18-5c0e-9630-f70e76a4aeb9'}, {'abstract': 'On Mondays, we publish a Times photo without a caption, headline or other information about its origins. Join the conversation by posting about what you see, and why. A live discussion is offered from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m. Eastern time.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/whats-going-on-in-this-picture-sept-15-2014/', 'snippet': 'On Mondays, we publish a Times photo without a caption, headline or other information about its origins. Join the conversation by posting about what you see, and why. A live discussion is offered from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m. Eastern time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated: Sept. 16, 2014', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/learning/VTS09-15-14LN/VTS09-15-14LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/11/learning/VTS09-15-14LN/VTS09-15-14LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/learning/VTS09-15-14LN/VTS09-15-14LN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/learning/VTS09-15-14LN/VTS09-15-14LN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1399, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/learning/VTS09-15-14LN/VTS09-15-14LN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/11/learning/VTS09-15-14LN/VTS09-15-14LN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/11/learning/VTS09-15-14LN/VTS09-15-14LN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Going On in This Picture? | Sept. 15, 2014', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date'