 would mean the combined companies would serve health care plans that provide coverage to about 180 million Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/outsourcing-firm-cognizant-to-buy-trizetto-for-2-7-billion/', 'snippet': 'Cognizant, a large outsourcing firm, said the deal would mean the combined companies would serve health care plans that provide coverage to about 180 million Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Cognizant Technology Solutions said on Monday that it had agreed to buy the health care information technology company TriZetto Corporation for $2.7 billion in cash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Outsourcing Firm Cognizant to Buy TriZetto for $2.7 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apax Partners LLP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cognizant Technology Solutions Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TriZetto Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T11:22:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54944b0a-e0d0-5a1d-88c8-cee2617375d2', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54944b0a-e0d0-5a1d-88c8-cee2617375d2'}, {'abstract': 'The deal would create the world’s largest integrated leisure travel business, worth 5.2 billion pounds, or about $8.5 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/tui-finalizes-terms-of-acquisition-of-britains-tui-t