d9d51-917c-5589-84d6-9c71fbb51376'}, {'abstract': 'How will the frogs breed? Check out this puzzle by Rafael Cosman and Zandra Vinegar.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/frog-2/', 'snippet': 'How will the frogs breed? Check out this puzzle by Rafael Cosman and Zandra Vinegar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks ago it was ants. Last week, bugs. This week our nature theme continues with bullfrogs, all beautifully illustrated by the Spot the Frog artist Mark Heath. The puzzle is an original collaboration by Zandra Vinegar, a recent graduate of MIT who lives, does math, builds furniture, and teaches in Berkeley, Calif., and Rafael Cosman, who is in his senior year at Stanford University, where he studies computer science.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zandra Vinegar and Rafael Cosman’s Wide-Eyed Bullfrog Puzzle', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reproduction (Biological)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cosman, Rafael', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T16:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c94790d1-ace2-53e6-ae71-09432f278840', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c94790d1-ace2-53e6-ae71-09432f278840'}, {'abstract': 'Plus: an emotional new show from Mickalene Thomas, an arts fest in the Catskills and Bryan Voltaggio’s dinner for a great cause.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/things-to-do-this-week-yayoi-kusama-voltaggio-photoville-sake-fest-mickalene-thomas/', 'snippet': 'Plus: an emotional new show from Mickalene Thomas, an arts fest in the Catskills and Bryan Voltaggio’s dinner for a great cause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tuesday, Frederick, Md.Combat child hunger by eating a meal from top chefsBryan Voltaggio has teamed up with the Washington, D.C.-based nonprofit Share Our Strength to host a fund-raising dinner\xa0at his flagship Maryland restaurant,\xa0Volt, featuring five award-winning American chefs. To date, Voltaggio has raised more than half a million dollars toward ending childhood hunger in the U.S.6 p.m., Volt restaurant, 228 N. Market St., Frederick, Maryland, ce.strength.org', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15magdaleno-agenda-1/15magdaleno-agenda-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15magdaleno-agenda-1/15magdaleno-agenda-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15magdaleno-agenda-1/15magdaleno-agenda-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15magdaleno-agenda-1/15magdaleno-agenda-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': '