s and activists, was jailed under a new law restricting protests but released by a judge who cited potential “embarrassment.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — An Egyptian court on Monday released the left-leaning activist Alaa Abd El Fattah from prison on bail in a rare example of leniency in the thousands of cases of political dissenters arrested since the military takeover last year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptian Activist Alaa Abd El Fattah Is Released on Bail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Activist Is Released on Bail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Merna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abd El Fattah, Alaa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T17:28:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Merna Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Merna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0649fe49-d581-5ff6-9128-d12a3dc383e4', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0649fe49-d581-5ff6-9128-d12a3dc383e4'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Joe discusses tech product announcements and the lull in innovation plaguing Internet 2.0.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/joe-on-wnycs-money-talking-13/', 'snippet': 'This week, Joe discusses tech product announcements and the lull in innovation plaguing Internet 2.0.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With characteristic pomp and circumstance (and a performance by U2), Apple unveiled a host of new products last week: iPhones that are bigger and slimmer; a mobile payments system that will supplant credit cards; and a smart watch that tracks fitness, updates baseball scores, and opens hotel rooms with a flick of the wrist. Oh, and it also tells time. The digital wizardry is spectacular, but are the products real game changers? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe on WNYC’s Money Talking', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T17:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Dallett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dallett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3280e73c-02a2-52f6-befb-c025097d0302', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3280e73c-02a2-52f6-befb-c025097d0302'}, {'abstract': 'For a collection inspired by the birds and the bees, Wendy Rowe created a golden flush, “tawny eyes” and brick-hued pouts.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/london-fashion-week-burberry-prorsum-spring-summer-2015-beauty/', 'snippet': 'For a collection inspired by the birds and the bees, Wendy Rowe created a golden flush, “tawny eyes” and brick-hued pouts.', 'lead_paragraph': '“This collection is all about the birds and the bees,” said the Burberry makeup artist Wendy Rowe backstage before the label’s show this morning. “How that translates to the makeup is with honey skin and a tawny eye.” Rowe used a selection of colors on the lids, depending on each model’s skin tone, to mimic the effect of a subtle shadow. She then used Burberry’s New Eyebrows (out in October) to sculpt arches. “Not only is the color amazing, you can create a shadow rather than a solid block of color,” she said. “It’s completely foolproof and doesn’t look drawn on; it’s not heavy, it’s more sophisticated.” The models’ skin, meanwhile, positively glowed under an insect- and flower-printed, greenhouse-like tent. Rowe first treated the face with Fresh Glow Luminous Fluid Base in Golden Radiance before highlighting the cheeks. “The Golden Radiance works on any skin tone and you can’t see it,” she explained. “It just gives you a lift of a tan, which we want for summer.” For lips, Burberry’s Lip Definer in Brick Red was treated with a dusting of Fresh Glow Powder for a matte finish. “Yes, the red lip can, of course, look classic,” Rowe added. “But we want to keep it modern — that’s why we kept the eyes nude and the skin slightly darker.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15beauty-buberry-cusick/15beauty-buberry-cusick-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15beauty-buberry-cusick/15beauty-buberry-cusick-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15beauty-buberry-cusick/15beauty-buberry-cusick-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15beauty-buberry-cusick/15beauty-buberry-cusick-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo'