 humans. It turns out there are small worlds of bacteria helping to guide the health of plants as well.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2014/09/16/science/16scitimes-podcast-rice.html', 'snippet': 'When we talk about the microbiome, we’re usually talking about the one inside humans. It turns out there are small worlds of bacteria helping to guide the health of plants as well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When we talk about the microbiome, we’re usually talking about the one inside humans. It turns out there are small worlds of bacteria helping to guide the health of plants as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rice Has a Microbiome', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T18:09:02+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/830deb2c-50f9-51bd-8850-26f7fddaa623', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/830deb2c-50f9-51bd-8850-26f7fddaa623'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the London fashion week diary of Alexandra Waespi.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/christopher-kane-london-fashion-week-spring-summer-2015-collection/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the London fashion week diary of Alexandra Waespi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the London Fashion Week photo diary of Alexandra Waespi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Fashion Week: Christopher Kane Spring/Summer 2015', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value'