cle/aae4a008-cd48-55e3-8ccb-aaf9a982a901', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aae4a008-cd48-55e3-8ccb-aaf9a982a901'}, {'abstract': 'Five years after losing its drummer, the Brooklyn-based act is back with a new collection of disco-inflected tracks — one of which, “You Were a Runaway,” streams here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/juan-maclean-nancy-whang-new-dance-album/', 'snippet': 'Five years after losing its drummer, the Brooklyn-based act is back with a new collection of disco-inflected tracks — one of which, “You Were a Runaway,” streams here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When John MacLean began making disco-inflected dance music for his old friend and LCD Soundsystem honcho James Murphy’s influential DFA label, he added a “The” in front of the Spanish variant of his name to ensure that his recordings could be more than just a solo project. In the 14 years since then, none of The Juan MacLean‘s many collaborators have become more central to the music than the singer and frontwoman Nancy Whang.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15maclean-dorris/15maclean-dorris-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15maclean-dorris/15maclean-dorris-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15maclean-dorris/15maclean-dorris-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/t-magazine/15maclean-dorris/15maclean-dorris-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1133, 'width': 1701, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 