ance-pilots-strike/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Please Give\xa0Marriott International\xa0is placing envelopes in more than 160,000 rooms in the United States and Canada to encourage tipping the people who clean guest rooms. (CNN)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/travel/Walkabout-Tip/Walkabout-Tip-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/15/travel/Walkabout-Tip/Walkabout-Tip-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/travel/Walkabout-Tip/Walkabout-Tip-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/travel/Walkabout-Tip/Walkabout-Tip-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1394, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/travel/Walkabout-Tip/Walkabout-Tip-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/15/travel/Walkabout-Tip/Walkabout-Tip-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/travel/Walkabout-Tip/Walkabout-Tip-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Walkabout: Marriott Encourages Tipping; Air France Pilots Strike', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T18:55:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64ad74a7-b03b-5244-843e-2fabc1b8f9a2', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64ad74a7-b03b-5244-843e-2fabc1b8f9a2'}, {'abstract': 'A throwback to a pre-digital era, the recently founded Baskerville Studio is a home to classic book arts practiced on century-old machines.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/new-orleans-printing-collective-baskerville-studio/', 'snippet': 'A throwback to a pre-digital era, the recently founded Baskerville Studio is a home to classic book arts practiced on century-old machines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a late summer downpour passes through New Orleans, Amelia Bird leans over a hulking platen press inside Baskerville Studio. An embossed plastic label that reads “Beulah, Born 1901″ identifies the apparatus, one of three, each weighing thousands of pounds, at the nonprofit printing collective located in the city’s up-and-coming Bywater neighborhood. Bird spins a wheel of the antique machine with weary pleasure, then rolls out yellow ink and puts down sheets of paper one at a time. She’s producing a poster concept by the fellow Baskerville member Jeffrey Goodman that uses digitally designed polymer plates and metal type. The end product will be distributed as a souvenir during the film exhibitor Shotgun Cinema’s upcoming screening of the Talking Heads’s 1984 documentary “Stop Making Sense” held at the nearby Marigny Opera House.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':