'original': 'By Jessica Ritz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ritz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4594bda-5038-5796-82e7-6d86333ea617', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4594bda-5038-5796-82e7-6d86333ea617'}, {'abstract': 'A videotaped statement from Pedro Hernandez, the man who confessed to killing Etan Patz in 1979, was made public for the first time on Monday. His lawyer argued that the statement is a false confession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/nyregion/in-taped-confession-in-etan-patz-case-something-just-took-over-me.html', 'snippet': 'A videotaped statement from Pedro Hernandez, the man who confessed to killing Etan Patz in 1979, was made public for the first time on Monday. His lawyer argued that the statement is a false confession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The confession came in a soft, unwavering tone. He recalled when he first spotted the boy, standing on the sidewalk outside a bodega where he worked at West Broadway and Prince Street in SoHo.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/nyregion/jpPEDRO3/jpPEDRO3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/nyregion/jpPEDRO3/jpPEDRO3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 832}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/nyregion/jpPEDRO3/jpPEDRO3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/nyregion/jpPEDRO3/jpPEDRO3-superJumb