tion is most likely caused by leaky wells rather than the process of hydraulic fracturing used to release the gas from the rock.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/us/FRACKING/FRACKING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/us/FRACKING/FRACKING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/us/FRACKING/FRACKING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/us/FRACKING/FRACKING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/us/FRACKING/FRACKING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/16/us/FRACKING/FRACKING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/us/FRACKING/FRACKING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Well Leaks, Not Fracking, Are Linked to Fouled Water', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Well Leaks, Not Fracking, Are Linked to Fouled Water', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AQUIFERS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T21:02:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/573b0746-a72a-5a2d-a2df-25edb3a0f17e', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/573b0746-a72a-5a2d-a2df-25edb3a0f17e'}, {'abstract': 'Joshua Ferris’s “To Rise Again at a Decent Hour,” shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize, is about an atheistic but Philo-Semitic dentist who has no luck with women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/books/joshua-ferriss-to-rise-again-at-a-decent-hour.html', 'snippet': 'Joshua Ferris’s “To Rise Again at a Decent Hour,” shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize, is about an atheistic but Philo-Semitic dentist who has no luck with women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Joshua Ferris’s “To Rise Again at a Decent Hour” arrived in May, there was no reason to suspect it would make history. But Mr. Ferris, along with Karen Joy Fowler (“We Are All Completely Beside Ourselves”), is one of the first two Americans with novels to be shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize in 2014. (This is the first year in which writers from the United States have been eligible.) Happily for Mr. Ferris, it is also the year he far surpassed his first two books.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/arts/BOOKFERRIS/BOOKFERRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 881, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/arts/BOOKFERRIS/BOOKFERRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 881}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/arts/BOOKFERRIS/BOOKFERRIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 698, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/arts/BOOKFERRIS/BOOKFERRIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1395, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/arts/BOOKFERRIS/BOOKFERRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/16/arts/BOOKFERRIS/BOOKFERRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/arts/BOOKFERRIS/BOOKFERRIS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Strikeout With Love and God', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Strikeout With Love and God', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferris, Joshua', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'To Rise Again at a Decent Hour (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T21:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/324f164f-5d09-5921-b1eb-39432fc94460', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/324f164f-5d09-5921-b1eb-39432fc94460'}, {'abstract': 'Now on the political side.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/replaying-the-30s-in-slow-motion/', 'snippet': 'Now on the political side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the 2008 crisis struck, anyone who knew even a bit of history had nightmares about a replay of the 1930s — not just the depth of the depression, but the downward political spiral into dictatorship and war. But this time was different: the banking crisis was contained, the plunge in output and employment leveled out, and modern Europe’s democratic political culture proved more resilient than that of the interwar years. All clear!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Replaying the 30s in Slow Motion', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T21:07:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dc49bcf-3075-52e2-9b66-5a74e9bcfdf6', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dc49bcf-3075