mes'}, 'type_of_material': 'Caption', '_id': 'nyt://article/2221502c-9ad4-54d8-8666-d28fd6ddeaa3', 'word_count': 47, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2221502c-9ad4-54d8-8666-d28fd6ddeaa3'}, {'abstract': 'The small bodyguards who defend acacia trees in Eastern Africa against elephants and giraffes are being killed off by other ants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/science/tree-protecting-ants-cant-protect-themselves.html', 'snippet': 'The small bodyguards who defend acacia trees in Eastern Africa against elephants and giraffes are being killed off by other ants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the savannas of Eastern Africa, ants live in the thorny, hollow bulbs of acacia trees and feed on the trees’ nectar. The ants also act as bodyguards, defending the trees from hungry elephants and giraffes by biting and stinging them. Now, an invasive species known as the bigheaded ant is killing the native ants. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tree-Protecting Ants Can’t Protect Themselves', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Insects: Tree-Protecting Ants Can’t Protect Themselves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Invasive Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ecology (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riginos, Corinna', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-15T22:48:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organizat