h devices but should also pass legislation to protect individual privacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even before Apple announced a smartwatch that can measure someone’s heart rate and the number of steps climbed in a day, wearable devices and mobile apps that log your every move and vital sign were growing in popularity. Apple’s size and influence as a trendsetter has now focused attention on the privacy implications of these machines and software. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smartwatches and Weak Privacy Rules', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smartwatches and Weak Privacy Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wearable Computing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T01:08:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/76c73d8a-6f14-5b04-bf7c-3ddad52d68b9', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76c73d8a-6f14-5b04-bf7c-3ddad52d68b9'}, {'abstract': 'The vote on whether to arm and train Syrian rebels should be entirely separate from the spending bill to keep the government running.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/opinion/dont-hide-the-syrian-aid-vote.html', 'snippet': 'The vote on whether to arm and train Syrian rebels should be entirely separate from the spending bill to keep the government running.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s bad enough that Congress — instead of doing its job by passing appropriations bills to finance government operations for the fiscal year that starts Oct. 1 is, once again, relying on a stopgap spending bill that will keep the lights on only through mid-December. But it’s far worse that House leaders — at the urging of the White House — are using that bill as the vehicle for a major foreign policy decision: arming and training Syrian rebels to fight against the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria, the extremist Sunni group known as ISIS.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Hide the Syrian Aid Vote', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Hide the Syrian Aid Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T01:10:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6179caf-4a16-5c07-b70a-bd66147a406f', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6179caf-4a16-5c07-b70a-bd66147a406f'}, {'abstract': 'After outrage over an email by Bruce Levenson, corporate leaders have begun a conversation about singling out demographic groups in marketing and the language used to do it.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/15/levenson-stumbles-on-the-line-between-business-and-bias/', 'snippet': 'After outrage over an email by Bruce Levenson, corporate leaders have begun a conversation about singling out demographic groups in marketing and the language used to do it.', 'lead_paragraph': '“My theory is that the black crowd scared away the whites and there are simply not enough affluent black fans to build a significant season ticket base.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/business/SORKIN-web2/SORKIN-web2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/business/SORKIN-web2/SORKIN-web2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/business/SORKIN-web2/SORKIN-web2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/business/SORKIN-web2/SORKIN-web2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1094, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': No