n said it would terminate health insurance for 115,000 people on Oct. 1 because they had failed to prove they were eligible for coverage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration said on Monday that it planned to terminate health insurance for 115,000 people on Oct. 1 because they had failed to prove that they were United States citizens or legal immigrants eligible for coverage under the Affordable Care Act. It also told 363,000 people that they could lose financial aid because their incomes could not be verified.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. to End Coverage Under Health Care Law for Tens of Thousands', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. to End Coverage Under Health Care Law for Tens of Thousands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T01:45:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4021df7a-9d9b-5a80-9d15-063450af7fe3', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4021df7a-9d9b-5a80-9d15-063450af7fe3'},