out the Affordable Care Act, though.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal government released some very reliable estimates of how many people had health insurance in the first three months of 2014. But the data won’t tell us much about how many people got insurance through the Affordable Care Act.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Estimates on Health Coverage Are Accurate but Outdated', 'kicker': 'Public Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T04:11:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margot Sanger-Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanger-Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ecf9b9e-1896-5a22-b70a-0a25dd0c947c', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ecf9b9e-1896-5a22-b70a-0a25dd0c947c'}, {'abstract': 'QuestBridge has quietly become a force in college admissions. On some elite campuses, 1 in 10 students come from the program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/upshot/a-national-admissions-office-for-low-income-strivers.html', 'snippet': 'QuestBridge has quietly become a force in college admissions. On some elite campuses, 1 in 10 students come from the program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arianna Trickey was opening a piece of mail in her bedroom during junior year of high school when a pamphlet fell out of the envelope. The pamphlet seemed to offer the impossible: the prospect of a full scholarshi