cle', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/add66fe0-7fb8-5fe2-90bb-3e567db59f72', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/add66fe0-7fb8-5fe2-90bb-3e567db59f72'}, {'abstract': 'I learned to fly airplanes. I started riding bicycles, attended music camps and took my family on great trips. Obviously, I was spending less time at the business.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/remind-me-again-why-am-i-in-business/', 'snippet': 'I learned to fly airplanes. I started riding bicycles, attended music camps and took my family on great trips. Obviously, I was spending less time at the business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It sneaked up on me about six years ago. After years of building one business and then another, I felt the need — and felt that I had earned the right — to take some “me” time and some more time with my wife and children. I decided it was time to start having more fun and to reassess my talents and my interests.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remind Me Again, Why Am I in Business?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aileron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cincinnati (Ohio)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T11:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'E