ne, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/opinion/17chappatte/17chappatte-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Anti-ISIS Coalition', 'kicker': 'Patrick Chappatte', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chappatte, Patrick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T11:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6adb8ee-7336-583b-b0d7-a6d2168fc16a', 'word_count': 5, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6adb8ee-7336-583b-b0d7-a6d2168fc16a'}, {'abstract': 'Allergan made a small measure of peace with its would-be acquirers. | Calpers said it would eliminate all of its hedge fund investments. | Fielding strong demand, Alibaba Group raised the price range for its I.P.O. | Beer brewers could be contemplating another round of deal-making.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/morning-agenda-allergans-olive-branch/', 'snippet': 'Allergan made a small measure of peace with its would-be acquirers. | Calpers said it would eliminate all of its hedge fund investments. | Fielding strong demand, Alibaba Group raised the price range for its I.P.O. | Beer brewers could be contempl...', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALLERGAN’S OLIVE BRANCH | The Botox maker Allergan on Monday night made a small measure of peace with Valeant Pharmaceuticals and Pershing Square Capital Management, the pair pursuing a $53 billion hostile takeover bid, when the three companies agreed that Allergan would hold a planned special meeting on Dec. 18, DealBook’s David Gelles reports. At the meeting, Allergan shareholders will have a chance to vote out the majority of the board, a move that could open the door to a takeover. The meeting was already set for that date, but there was a chance it could have been delayed because of litigation related to the takeover bid. Valeant and Pershing Square also agreed to drop pending litigation against Allergan in Delaware, where they had sued to force the meeting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Allergan’s Olive Branch', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T11:53:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21a390c6-1560-56f4-a727-01336a646c07', 'word_count': 1708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21a390c6-1560-56f4-a727-01336a646c07'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Williams plays a preacher with a secret in Robert O’Hara’s comedy at Playwrights Horizons.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/in-performance-lance-coadie-williams-of-bootycandy/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Williams plays a preacher with a secret in Robert O’Hara’s comedy at Playwrights Horizons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s video features a scene with Lance Coadie Williams as a preacher with a secret in “Bootycandy,” Robert O’Hara’s play about attitudes toward homosexuality in black culture. In his review, Charles Isherwood calls the show a “searing and sensationally funny” comedy from a fearless playwright “who wants to make his mark by shaking up the world, one audience at a time.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Lance Coadie Williams of ‘Bootycandy’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Hara, Robert", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Lance Coadie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playwrights Horizons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T12:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd60fdeb-dd97-5558-951e-93b050fa4d36', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd60fdeb-dd97-5558-951e-93b050fa4d36'}, {'abstract': 'In many cases, extraneous words gum up our prose. Here’s one common construction that can almost always be improved by being shortened: The [noun] is an [adjective] one.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/wasted-words/', 'snippet': 'In many cases, extraneous words gum up our prose. Here’s one common construction that can almost always be improved by being shortened: The [noun] is an [adjective] one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t subscribe to the view that good editing invariably requires the ruthless elimination of every single word that is not logically essential to a sentence. Sometimes idiom or the natural cadence of English favors phrases that aren’t stripped to the bone. There’s nothing wrong with “hurry up,” even though “hurry” means the same thing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wasted Words', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'na