s', 'value': 'West Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T14:46:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Olivia Victoria Andrzejczak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Olivia', 'middlename': 'Victoria', 'lastname': 'Andrzejczak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4132534-106d-561f-911f-cd641c132c3b', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4132534-106d-561f-911f-cd641c132c3b'}, {'abstract': 'After a few months of treating life in our new town like one big vacation, the reality of everyday life is catching up with us, and everyone — especially the kids — is a little testy.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/when-the-honeymoon-is-over-settling-into-real-life-after-a-move/', 'snippet': 'After a few months of treating life in our new town like one big vacation, the reality of everyday life is catching up with us, and everyone — especially the kids — is a little testy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my husband and I uprooted our 11-year-old son and 8-year-old daughter to move to Nashville from Atlanta, we timed it to happen over the summer. We thought it would be easier to handle the move-related chaos in a season when everything’s a little more laid back. Can’t find the box with sheets and pillows in it? That’s O.K. There’s no rush on bedtime. Don’t have an oven in the kitchen yet? No problem. Let’s throw something on the grill and eat outside.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/us/motherlode-legos/motherlode-legos-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/us/motherlode-legos/motherlode-legos-articleLarge