/the-power-of-fearing-the-worst/', 'snippet': 'A psychologist argues that if you use it right, pessimism can work to your advantage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Worriers, rejoice. Your fears may actually be the makings of your success.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/opinion/nyto-fear/nyto-fear-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/15/opinion/nyto-fear/nyto-fear-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/opinion/nyto-fear/nyto-fear-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/opinion/nyto-fear/nyto-fear-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2027, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/opinion/nyto-fear/nyto-fear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/15/opinion/nyto-fear/nyto-fear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/15/opinion/nyto-fear/nyto-fear-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Power of Fearing the Worst', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T15:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f20aae3b-e2af-5dbf-a90b-a937a3fc05e0', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f20aae3b-e2af-5dbf-a90b-a937a3fc05e0'}, {'abstract': 'A new compilation featuring tracks by José González (which premieres exclusively at T), Robyn and Hot Chip pays tribute to the pioneering experimental and dance musician.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/arthur-russell-jose-gonzalez-red-hot-pop-music/', 'snippet': 'A new compilation featuring tracks by José González (which premieres exclusively at T), Robyn and Hot Chip pays tribute to the pioneering experimental and dance musician.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though he’s not widely known, Arthur Russell — the avant-garde multi-instrumentalist who bridged classical, dance and experimental music in the 1970s and ’80s before succumbing to AIDS in 1992 — has been one of the most influential forces in popular music. A new compilation, “Master Mix: Red Hot + Arthur Russell” — the latest in the 24-year-old Red Hot + series dedicated to raising money to fight HIV/AIDS — is helping to voice that legacy by putting his compositions in the hands of artists like Robyn, Devendra Banhart and Hot Chip.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16russell-diehl/16russell-diehl-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16russell-diehl/16russell-diehl-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16russell-diehl/16russell-diehl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16russell-diehl/16russell-diehl-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16russell-diehl/16russell-diehl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16russell-diehl/16russell-diehl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16russell-diehl/16russell-diehl-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Appreciating Arthur Russell, Pop Music’s Most Influential Unknown Star', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, Jose', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T15:30:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By MATT DIEHL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DIEHL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55df19c6-4f7c-5ae9-b774-7d86366c51e8', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55df19c6-4f7c-5ae9-b774-7d86366c51e8'}, {'abstract': 'As Mayor Bill de Blasio and his surrogates continue to issue barbs at Michael R. Bloomberg, former Bloomberg administration officials have increasingly moved to defend him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/nyregion/at-city-hall-a-tussle-over-bloombergs-legacy.html', 'snippet': 'As Mayor Bill de Blasio and his surrogates continue to issue barbs at Michael R. Bloomberg, former Bloomberg administration officials have increasingly moved to defend him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mayor Bill de Blasio’s administration unveiled a promotional video this summer in its bid to lure the Democratic National Convention to Brooklyn in 2016, most viewers saw a slick, breezy collage of a pulsing New York City — schoolchildren and Citi Bikes, culinary wonders and brochure-worthy parks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/nyregion/billvsmike_promo/billvsmike_promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/nyregion/billvsmike_promo/billvsmike_promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/nyregion/billvsmike_promo/billvsmike_promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/nyregion/billvsmike_promo/billvsmike_promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/nyregion/billvsmike_promo/billvsmike_promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height