'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/world/middleeast/isis-airstrikes-united-states-coalition.html', 'snippet': 'Remarks by Gen. Martin E. Dempsey, the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, open the door to a riskier, more expansive American combat role than the president has publicly outlined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama’s top military adviser said Tuesday that he would recommend deploying United States forces in ground operations against Islamic extremists in Iraq if airstrikes proved insufficient, opening the door to a riskier, more expansive American combat role than the president has publicly outlined. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. General Open to Ground Forces in Fight Against ISIS in Iraq', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. General Open to Ground Force as Option in Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Jeremy W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint Chiefs of Staff', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T15:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler and Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84218ee5-24a0-5b23-9a98-fcc71efb69d9', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84218ee5-24a0-5b23-9a98-fcc71efb69d9'}, {'abstract': 'The company is sharing videos that feature dancers, as well as behind-the-scenes reports.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/american-ballet-theater-starts-a-youtube-channel/', 'snippet': 'The company is sharing videos that feature dancers, as well as behind-the-scenes reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In line with a growing trend among ballet companies, American Ballet Theater has created its own YouTube channel, the company announced. “With our initial phase of videos, we hoped to give users a sampling of the content,” said a spokeswoman, adding that the channel would be continually refreshed with new material. Most of the videos currently posted date back to May and June. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Ballet Theater Starts a YouTube Channel', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T15:59:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/519118a8-