illion people worldwide do not get enough to eat, even as the world produces more than twice as much food as it needs, according to new figures released Tuesday by the United Nations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '800 Million People Still Malnourished, U.N. Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Food Program', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Millennium Development Goals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T16:02:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f13db5e5-0027-5dfb-a4bc-a11fc97fedeb', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f13db5e5-0027-5dfb-a4bc-a11fc97fedeb'}, {'abstract': 'Tech upgrades for small businesses. How to use Instagram to promote products. Should we ban states and cities from offering tax breaks for jobs?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/today-in-small-business-the-case-against-tipping/', 'snippet': 'Tech upgrades for small businesses. How to use Instagram to promote products. Should we ban states and cities from offering tax breaks for jobs?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Small Business: The Case Against Tipping', 'kic