iquita.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Chiquita Brands International and Fyffes said on Tuesday that they were in discussions with European regulators about a series of possible concessions to obtain clearance for their proposed inversion deal. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-chiquita/dbpix-chiquita-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-chiquita/dbpix-chiquita-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-chiquita/dbpix-chiquita-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-chiquita/dbpix-chiquita-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1089, 'width': 1665, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-chiquita/dbpix-chiquita-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-chiquita/dbpix-chiquita-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-chiquita/dbpix-chiquita-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chiquita Offers Concessions to European Regulators for Fyffes Merger', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Banana Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chiquita Brands International Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cutrale Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fyffes PLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Safra Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T16:38:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d7a0b22-8e43-5da2-acb3-22e4ffabc6bc', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d7a0b22-8e43-5da2-acb3-22e4ffabc6bc'}, {'abstract': 'A response to the Texas senator’s defenders in the Middle East Christians debate.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/a-last-word-on-the-cruz-affair/', 'snippet': 'A response to the Texas senator’s defenders in the Middle East Christians debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column used Ted Cruz’s now-famous performance at a summit organized to raise awareness of Christian persecution in the age of ISIS as a window into the difficulties that the Middle East’s swiftly-disappearing Christians have finding patrons in the American political scene. The column didn’t have space to do justice to the various arguments raised in defense of Cruz’s provocations\xa0— the most notable of which was his\xa0challenge to a mostly-Arab audience to acknowledge that “Christians have\xa0no greater ally than the Jewish state,” which prompted boos and sent things\xa0spiraling downhill. So let me say a word about those arguments here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Last Word on the Cruz Affair', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zionism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coptic Orthodox Church of Alexandria', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T16:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'perso