y at the London Design Festival, including the Tube, which looks like a glowing light saber.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/garden/may-the-force-be-with-you.html', 'snippet': 'Four lamps from Lee Broom are on display at the London Design Festival, including the Tube, which looks like a glowing light saber.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On display at the London Design Festival this week is Nouvel Rebel: four lamps, a set of candlesticks and a martini glass all designed by Lee Broom in marble, crystal or some combination of both. The collection features two styles of pendant lamps with Carrara marble centers encased in lead crystal, and a globular table lamp with a crystal hemisphere. But the most impressive of the lot may be an exceedingly thin (5 mm) marble tube with a single strip of LEDs inside. When lit, the lamp, called Tube (shown), looks like a glowing light saber. It “was inspired by the very basic fluorescent tube light you would get in factories or warehouses,” said Mr. Broom, a former theater designer based in the East End. “I wanted to create something very industrial, but very hand crafted.” Tube is about 35 inches long and 2.75 inches in diameter, and costs about $5,310. The Future Perfect design store is taking advance orders. Information: 212-473-2500 or thefutureperfect.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/garden/16lighting/16lighting-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/garden/16lighting/16lighting-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 744}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/garden/16lighting/16lighting-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 826, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'sup