ifferences with the company’s management.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Vienna State Opera continues to bleed conductors. Less than two weeks after the surprise resignation of its music director, Franz Welser-Möst, the French conductor Bertrand de Billy announced this week that he was canceling his upcoming performances there because of differences with the company’s management.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bertrand de Billy Cancels Vienna State Opera Appearances', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vienna Opera Conductor  Cancels His Performances', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vienna State Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T17:43:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ca3c766-6a92-537e-859d-7cc52857f2c5', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ca3c766-6a92-537e-859d-7cc52857f2c5'}, {'abstract': 'After a drop in visitors during this summer’s Gaza conflict, tourism officials are looking for a rebound.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/travel/hoping-war-weary-tourists-will-return-to-israel.html', 'snippet': 'After a drop in visitors during this summer’s Gaza conflict, tourism officials are looking for a rebound.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent afternoon in the Old City of Jerusalem, while fighting raged in Gaza, Bilal Abu Khalaf hosted a group of Israeli tourists at his textile store in the Christian Quarter — one of Jerusalem’s tourist gems.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'pr