 start a long-term project by filming three Shakespeare plays in HD and showing them in movie theaters and on television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve been meaning to catch some of the Stratford Festival’s renowned Shakespeare productions but haven’t been able to get up to Ontario, the festival has a remedy at hand. As the first installment of a long-term project, in which the festival hopes to document its productions of the entire Shakespeare canon, three of this year’s stagings will be filmed in HD. The films will be screened in cinemas around the world in 2015 and television broadcasts by the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation will follow, as will on-demand digital releases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stratford Festival to Offer Shakespeare in Movie Theaters and on TV', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stratford Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stratford Shakespeare Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ontario (Canada)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T17:55:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d3326da-3921-533e-bb26-7cc70a971313', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d3326da-3921-533e-bb26-7cc70a971313'}, {