'snippet': 'On Twitter and Facebook, and in comments to The Times, undecided Scottish readers talked about their concerns over which way to vote on independence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Public opinion polls show Scotland’s independence referendum is too close to call ahead of the Sept. 18 vote, which could come down to those still undecided — at least 6 percent of potential voters have not made up their mind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/world/17scotland-social/17scotland-social-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/world/17scotland-social/17scotland-social-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/world/17scotland-social/17scotland-social-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/world/17scotland-social/17scotland-social-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1247, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/world/17scotland-social/17scotland-social-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/17/world/17scotland-social/17scotland-social-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/world/17scotland-social/17scotland-social-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scottish Referendum Could Hinge on the Undecided', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T19:21:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hanna Ingber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ingber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7f9691c-9c0b-53d8-af0e-396ff976ab52', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7f9691c-9c0b-53d8-af0e-396ff976ab52'}, {'abstract': 'A Dutch artist faked a trip to Southeast Asia through a series of carefully manipulated Facebook photos, demonstrating the power and ubiquity of deception in the digital age.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/how-to-fake-your-next-vacation/', 'snippet': 'A Dutch artist faked a trip to Southeast Asia through a series of carefully manipulated Facebook photos, demonstrating the power and ubiquity of deception in the digital age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zilla van der Born, a Dutch national, spent five weeks traveling through Southeast Asia and documented the trip in photos on Facebook. She\xa0posed for pictures while dining\xa0on dumplings, snorkeling among colorful fish in azure waters and visiting ornately decorated Buddhist temples — compiling the lot into a series of videos for her Vimeo account. All in all, Ms. van der Born seemed to have enjoyed a busy, albeit conventional, trip to Phuket, Luang Prabang or some other regional tourist hub.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', '