'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/multimedia/laura/laura-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Excerpt: ‘The Mysteries of Laura’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T20:27:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'NBC', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nbc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/cbf8fffd-fba3-5f20-a3f0-ce80ae47f12d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cbf8fffd-fba3-5f20-a3f0-ce80ae47f12d'}, {'abstract': '“Let’s Dance Raw,” the follow-up to his cult-classic 2011 solo debut, is out today — and can be listened to in its entirety here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/japan-indie-rock-star-shintaro-sakamoto-profile-new-album-stream/', 'snippet': '“Let’s Dance Raw,” the follow-up to his cult-classic 2011 solo debut, is out today — and can be listened to in its entirety here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Japan, Shintaro Sakamoto is a bona fide star. His former psychedelic-rock trio, Yura Yura Teikoku, sold out large venues whenever they played; they even toured the United States with the indie stalwarts Yo La Tengo. But since disbanding the group in 2010, he has favored a more low-key approach, eschewing live shows and retreating to the studio to produce his first solo album, “How to Live with a Phantom,” in 2011. That release, a mellow affair with jazzy guitar, Latin percussion and soft sax, called to mind the chilled-out feel of ’70s yacht rock and the sonic perfectionism of Steely Dan. When the label arm of the influential New York record emporium Other Music issued it in the United States, it became a cult classic. (The former Girls frontman and Hedi Slimane muse Christopher Owens, for one, has professed his love in multiple interviews.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16sakamoto-hadis/16sakamoto-hadis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16sakamoto-hadis/16sakamoto-hadis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16sakamoto-hadis/16sakamoto-hadis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16sakamoto-hadis/16sakamoto-hadis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16sakamoto-hadis/16sakamoto-hadis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16sakamoto-hadis/16sakamoto-hadis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16sakamoto-hadis/16sakamoto-hadis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stream the New Album From Japan’s Original Indie Rock Star, Shintaro Sakamot