r rival, Auxilium Pharmaceuticals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drug Maker That Did an Inversion Seeks to Block One', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Auxilium Bid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T21:40:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gelles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91499a9d-0f2c-503c-9d3b-6ee071e6ab7f', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91499a9d-0f2c-503c-9d3b-6ee071e6ab7f'}, {'abstract': 'The Argento Chamber Orchestra and the JACK Quartet played around with Mahler’s Ninth on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/arts/music/jack-quartet-and-argento-riff-on-mahlers-ninth.html', 'snippet': 'The Argento Chamber Orchestra and the JACK Quartet played around with Mahler’s Ninth on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mahler’s great, valedictory Ninth Symphony, about 90 minutes long and prevailingly intense, is more often than not left to fill an evening by itself. But the Argento Chamber Ensemble and the JACK Quartet built an ambitious program around it on Monday evening in the Music Mondays series at Advent Lutheran Church on the Upper West Side, adding two shortish contemporary works more or less based on the Ninth.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17ARGENTO/17ARGENTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17ARGENTO/17ARGENTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17ARGENTO/17ARGENTO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17ARGENTO/17ARGENTO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 835, 'width': 1544, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17ARGENTO/17ARGENTO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17ARGENTO/17ARGENTO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17ARGENTO/17ARGENTO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Great Symphony, and Then Two More Takes on It', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Great Symphony, and Then Two More Takes on It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JACK Quartet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Argento Chamber Ensemble', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T21:43:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/04e2c4e0-b547-5971-b480-75191a367ac9', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04e2c4e0-b547-5971-b480-75191a367ac9'}, {'abstract': 'The Bed-Stuy Veterans did a lunch-hour brukup show on Friday as part of the third annual BEAT Festival in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/arts/dance/brukup-from-the-bed-stuy-veterans-at-beat-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Bed-Stuy Veterans did a lunch-hour brukup show on Friday as part of the third annual BEAT Festival in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday afternoon at MetroTech Commons in Downtown Brooklyn, the mercurial dancer known as Ghost came out of character for a minute to address the crowd assembled around a small outdoor stage. Surrounding him were fellow members of the Bed-Stuy Veterans, a dance crew devoted to the Jamaican-born style brukup, which migrated from Caribbean dance halls to Brooklyn streets in the mid-1990s. The lunch-hour show was part of the third annual BEAT Festival, an eclectic series of theater, music and dance throughout Brooklyn.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17MASHUP/17MASHUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17MASHUP/17MASHUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17MASHUP/17MASHUP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17MASHUP/17MASHUP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17MASHUP/17MASHUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17MASHUP/17MASHUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17MASHUP/17MASHUP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Changing States of Matter, and a Whole New Meaning to Vaping', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changing States of Matter, and a Whole New Meaning to Vaping', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bed-Stuy Veterans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T21:44:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a177da53-91b1-5dab-a52f-b8b62ed93a0d', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a177da53-91b1-5dab-a52f-b8b62ed93a0d'}, {'abstract': '“The Fatal Weakness,” which ran on Broadway in 1946 and is being restaged at the Mint Theater, is a domestic comedy with a twist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/theater/the-fatal-weakness-is-revived-at-the-mint.html', 'snippet': '“The Fatal Weakness,” which ran on Broadway in 1946 and is being restaged at the Mint Theater, is a domestic comedy with a twist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes a play is more interesting in the future than in its own time. “The Fatal Weakness,” a domestic comedy with a drama at its core, was apparently unloved in its day; its 1946 Broadway premiere ran for only 119 performances despite having Ina Claire, a prominent stage actress, in the lead role. But here in 2014, the Mint Theater Company is making this George Kelly work an amusing, affecting reminder that the institution of marriage has been under siege for much longer than we tend to think.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17FATAL/17FATAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17FATAL/17FATAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17FATAL/17FATAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 980, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17FATAL/17FATAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 980, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17FATAL/17FATAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17FATAL/17FATAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank':