uest,” written by Simon Barrett and featuring Dan Stevens and Maika Monroe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Wingard narrates a sequence from his film “The Guest,” written by Simon Barrett and featuring Dan Stevens and Maika Monroe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/multimedia/guest-anatomy/guest-anatomy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/multimedia/guest-anatomy/guest-anatomy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/multimedia/guest-anatomy/guest-anatomy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/multimedia/guest-anatomy/guest-anatomy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1153, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/multimedia/guest-anatomy/guest-anatomy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/16/multimedia/guest-anatomy/guest-anatomy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/multimedia/guest-anatomy/guest-anatomy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anatomy of a Scene | ‘The Guest’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wingard, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Simon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, Dan (1982- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Guest (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T22:50:41+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/99fa9d56-d56c-526a-a618-416f5dc3a075', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/99fa9d56-d56c-526a-a618-416f5dc3a075'}, {'abstract': 'Really a five-day marathon, the second leg of fashion month continued with shows from brands like Burberry and Tom Ford. Here’s a recap of what happened, traced through the Styles staff’s Twitter feeds.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/london-fashion-week-social-media-roundup/', 'snippet': 'Really a five-day marathon, the second leg of fashion month continued with shows from brands like Burberry and Tom Ford. Here’s a recap of what happened, traced through the Styles staff’s Twitter feeds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though short in terms of time (it lasts exactly five days), London Fashion Week packs a punch. Just ask Alexandra Jacobs, who developed an entirely new phobia from the sheer stress of dashing from show to show: F.O.N.G.T.O.T., or Fear of Not Getting There On Time — #fongtot for those who are on Twitter. Fortunately, hashtags and acronyms didn’t slow the critics down too much as they surveyed the offerings both of megabrands like Burberry and Tom Ford, and of less established designers like Simone Rocha, Margaret Howell and Hunter. The truncated week brimmed with moments: unexpected ones (Birkenstocks at Burberry), unnerving ones (a moving runway at Anya Hindmarch) and even political ones (Vivienne Westwood’s comment on the Scottish referendum). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Fashion Week Social Media Roundup', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September Fashion Week (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Bradley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westwood, Vivienne', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Birkenstock Footprint Sandals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Burberry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marchesa', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T22:55:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valeriya Safronova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valeriya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Safronova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/294b4776-e528-5471-911a-6880ed89e07d', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/294b4776-e528-5471-911a-6880ed89e07d'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Guest,” a man with suspect intentions ingratiates himself with a dead soldier’s family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/movies/the-guest-stars-dan-stevens-as-a-sinister-interloper.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Guest,” a man with suspect intentions ingratiates himself with a dead soldier’s family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As one of the sharper young horror directors working today, Adam Wingard likes to take familiar genre setups — the serial killer or the home invasion — and warp them just enough to pique our interest. Together with the writer Simon Barrett, whose canny scripts flip and swerve at unexpected moments, Mr. Wingard is building a résumé that pays at least as much attention to character and story as it does to scares and body count.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17GUEST/17GUEST-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17GUEST/17GUEST-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17GUEST/17GUEST-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17GUEST/17GUEST-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 993, 'width': 1403, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17GUEST/17GUEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17GUEST/17GUEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/arts/17GUEST/17GUEST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dangerous Visitor Makes Himself at Home', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dangerous Visitor Makes Himself at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Guest (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, Dan (1982- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wingard, Adam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Simon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-16T22:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcb1294b-ae9d-5542-b82d-1c184001abbb', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcb1294b-ae9d-5542-b82d-1c184001abbb'}, {'abstract': 'The practice was popular in the Victorian era, but there is only one artist seriously pursuing it today. Matthew Killip’s short film “The Diatomist,” which premieres exclusively with T, explores his unusual world.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/diatomist-film-matthew-killip-premiere/', 'snippet': 'The practice was popular in the Victorian era, but there is only one artist seriously pursuing it today. Matthew Killip’s short film “The Diatomist,” which premieres exclusively with T, explores his unusual world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps you’ve never done much thinking about the beauty of algae, but the Victorians did. Microscopists of the era used to arrange diatoms — single-cell organisms encased in jewel-like glass shells that likely date to the Jurassic Period — into stunningly beautiful mosaics that resemble stained glass in miniature. The last surviving diatomist is an Englishman named Klaus Kemp, who became fascinated with the practice as a teenager. Because the Victorians left no records behind, Kemp had to figure it out for himself. He’s still at it today, supporting himself by selling his creations to a small but avid group of collectors. The filmmaker Matthew Killip spent an afternoon with Kemp at his home in England in December of 2013, documenting his unique practice at the intersection of science and art. Killip’s film, “The Diatomist,” premieres exclusively here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16diatomist/16diatomist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 586, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16diatomist/16diatomist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 586}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16diatomist/16diatomist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 976, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16diatomist/16diatomist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 976, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16diatomist/16diatomist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/16/t-magazine/16diatomist/16diatomist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheigh