, 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T01:05:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54905e32-7de3-5881-abc8-ddc3d385c5c0', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54905e32-7de3-5881-abc8-ddc3d385c5c0'}, {'abstract': 'Pedro Hernandez’s confession to murdering Etan Patz has details that seem to be at odds with what is known about that day 35 years ago, but, for now, the focus of the case is on whether Mr. Hernandez made a truly voluntary decision in waiving his right to silence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/nyregion/in-etan-patz-killing-testing-the-weight-of-threadbare-confessions.html', 'snippet': 'Pedro Hernandez’s confession to murdering Etan Patz has details that seem to be at odds with what is known about that day 35 years ago, but, for now, the focus of the case is on whether Mr. Hernandez made a truly voluntary decision in waiving his ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'All that kept the orange Rikers Island jumpsuit from swallowing Pedro Hernandez whole were the hand-rolled pants cuffs, turned high enough to clear his canvas shoes. Accused of murdering a child named Etan Patz 35 years ago, Mr. Hernandez stood not much taller than the shoulders of the shortest of the court officers who led him into State Supreme Court in Manhattan this week. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Patz Killing, Testing the Weight of Threadbare Confessions', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Testing the Weight of Threadbare Confessions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Pedro (1961- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patz, Etan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Confessions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T01:08:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1889ef81-7886-5612-9ace-2c4825d88d62', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1889ef81-7886-5612-9ace-2c4825d88d62'}, {'abstract': 'The United States and other countries need to hasten medical assistance if they hope to contain the rapidly expanding epidemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/opinion/an-urgent-campaign-against-ebola.html', 'snippet': 'The United States and other countries need to hasten medical assistance if they hope to contain the rapidly expanding epidemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s announcement of a more aggressive campaign against the Ebola outbreak in West Africa on Tuesday shows the administration is starting to recognize the severity of the crisis in Guinea, Liberia and Sierra Leone. The question now is whether ramped-up medical assistance from the United States and other countries will arrive fast enough to change the course of the rapidly expanding epidemic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Urgent Campaign Against Ebola', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Urgent Campaign Against Ebola', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T01:09:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b45cf5a-dea9-5eed-98e9-829eaab37310', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b45cf5a-dea9-5eed-98e9-829eaab37310'}, {'abstract': 'Testimony from the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff raises questions about U.S. policy on fighting ISIS only a week after President Obama explained it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/opinion/is-us-policy-on-fighting-isis-already-changing.html', 'snippet': 'Testimony from the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff raises questions about U.S. policy on fighting ISIS only a week after President Obama explained it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A week ago, President Obama stood before the American people and promised that the expanding fight against the Islamic State — a vicious Sunni militant group known as ISIS or ISIL that is terrorizing parts of Iraq and Syria — would not mean a commitment of American ground troops. “As I have said before, these American forces will not have a combat mission,” he said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Slippery Slope Begins', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Slippery Slope Begins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint Chiefs of Staff', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T01:12:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4d0c84d-e6b6-5a25-bc7f-78dd621e80ad', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4d0c84d-e6b6-5a25-bc7f-78dd621e80ad'}, {'abstract': 'Income for most Americans has not recovered since the recession ended, and, at the recent rate of progress, it won’t for a long time, if ever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/opinion/new-data-old-story.html', 'snippet': 'Income for most Americans has not recovered since the recession ended, and, at the recent rate of progress, it won’t for a long time, if ever.', 'le