at-the-heart-of-bolivias-identity.html', 'snippet': 'A silver-rich mountain — seen by many Bolivians as a potent national symbol — is caving in after centuries of mining, but many of the men who work on the mountain do not want to move.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POTOSÍ, Bolivia — The silver in this mountain helped finance the Spanish empire. It created vast fortunes for some and misery for many more. It fueled the early growth of European capitalism, setting the stage for the modern era.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Miners, Increasing Risk on a Mountain at the Heart of Bolivia’s Identity', 'kicker': 'Potosi Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Miners, Increasing Risk on a Mountain at the Heart of Bolivia’s Identity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bolivia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Potosi (Bolivia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mountains', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Silver', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T01:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cafb393-5309-5e5e-9fb7-609a686c4a7d', 'word_count': 1336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cafb393-5309-5e5e-9fb7-609a686c4a7d'}, {'abstract': 'Even though the $4 billion hedge fund investment being dropped by the California Public Employees’ Retirement System is minuscule by industry standards, Calpers has long been a trendsetter among public pension plans.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/with-calpers-quitting-hedge-funds-other-investors-reflect/', 'snippet': 'Even though the $4 billion hedge fund investment being dropped by the California Public Employees’ Retirement System is minuscule by industry standards, Calpers has long been a trendsetter among public pension plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hedge funds were once the domain of the rich. Today, it is the teachers, firefighters and other public employees in the country’s biggest pension funds who are among the industry’s main investors.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/HEDGE/HEDGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/business/HEDGE/HEDGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/HEDGE/HEDGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/HEDGE/HEDGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/HEDGE/HEDGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_