 59E59 Theaters, a woman afflicted with AIDS prepares to die in a South Africa beset by bleak realities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/theater/ndebele-funeral-set-in-south-africa-at-59e59-theaters.html', 'snippet': 'In “Ndebele Funeral,” at 59E59 Theaters, a woman afflicted with AIDS prepares to die in a South Africa beset by bleak realities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daweti (Zoey Martinson), a former university intellectual moldering in a Soweto shack, takes an unusual approach to home décor. She calls the dirt and trash littering her floor essential elements of feng shui, and used some government-supplied wood to build a coffin. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/theater/17ndebele/17ndebele-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/theater/17ndebele/17ndebele-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/theater/17ndebele/17ndebele-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/theater/17ndebele/17ndebele-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/theater/17ndebele/17ndebele-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/17/theater/17ndebele/17ndebele-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/theater/17ndebele/17ndebele-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Will to Live, Fading Fast in Soweto', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Will to Live, Fading Fast in Soweto', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinson, Zoey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Timpo, Awoye', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Yusef', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '59E59 THEATERS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Ndebele Funeral (Play)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Soweto (South Africa)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T02:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Soloski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soloski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c92a449-47c3-56f5-94eb-7254a556af2e', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c92a449-47c3-56f5-94eb-7254a556af2e'}, {'abstract': 'This puzzle by Zhouqin Burnikel and Don Gagliardo is definitely not for the birds.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/16/drink-made-with-jameson/', 'snippet': 'This puzzle by Zhouqin Burnikel and Don Gagliardo is definitely not for the birds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY’S PUZZLE — I’d like to personally thank Zhouqin Burnikel and Don Gagliardo for the IRISH COFFEE they’ve left for us. Last week was a rough one, the weather is getting cooler, and a warm beverage is just what I needed. Just be careful when you lift the cup to your mouth and don’t get stung.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drink Made With Jameson', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T02:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/128659c3-a8ea-5c58-bbc8-04c5f7886e1c', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/128659c3-a8ea-5c58-bbc8-04c5f7886e1c'}, {'abstract': 'The Canadian company has posted an operating loss of $2.4 billion over the last five years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/business/us-steels-canada-subsidiary-files-for-creditor-protection.html', 'snippet': 'The Canadian company has posted an operating loss of $2.4 billion over the last five years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'U.S. Steel Canada was granted creditor protection on Tuesday, the latest chapter in its tumultuous recent history. U.S. Steel said that the Canadian company, known as Stelco before its purchase in 2007, has posted an operating loss of $2.4 billion over the last five years. With the filing, the Canadian unit’s results will no longer be included in U.S. Steel’s financial statements. In 2009, U.S. Steel shut down the Canadian operation and locked out its workers while demanding pension changes. That prompted a lawsuit from the government of Canada, charging that the company had failed to live up to foreign investment laws. An agreement to make further investments in Canada ended that action, although the company continues to battle unions. A lawyer for U.S. Steel Canada told the Ontario Superior Court that it had liabilities of between 3.86 billion and 4.3 billion Canadian dollars ($3.52 billion and $3.9 billion), and assets worth between 1.9 billion and 2.3 billion Canadian dollars, according to The Globe and Mail. The largest creditor is U.S. Steel, which the court was told is owed 1.6 billion Canadian dollars. It will provide the subsidiary with up to 185 million Canadian dollars to keep it operating until the end of 2015. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Steel’s Canada Subsidiary Files for Creditor Protection', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Steel’s Canada Subsidiary Files for Creditor Protection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Steel Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T02:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/21d7f6b2-fd92-5d20-9ec2-f7c8ebd0d52c', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21d7f6b2-fd92-5d20-9ec2-f7c8ebd0d52c'}, {'abstract': 'A former Brooklyn prosecutor was questioned about the handling of a 1991 case in which two teenagers were quickly convicted of murdering a police officer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/nyregion/convictions-involving-louis-scarcella-revisited-by-court-and-brooklyn-district-attorneys-office.html