k with their employees who want to cash out of their shares.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/new-broker-seeks-role-in-secondary-sales-of-private-stock/', 'snippet': 'The brokerage firm, Battery East, which officially opened on Wednesday, wants to persuade start-ups to let it work with their employees who want to cash out of their shares.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It used to be that technology companies of reasonable size would sell shares to the public in an initial public offering. No longer. Today, some of the most talked-about companies, like Uber and Airbnb, are privately held despite having multibillion-dollar valuations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Broker Seeks Role in Secondary Sales of Private Stock', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohn, Barrett', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sobel, Michael P', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Battery East', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T11:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/398bf38c-0c1d-5796-b6f1-deb69a2ace57', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/398bf38c-0c1d-5796-b6f1-deb69a2ace57'}, {'abstract': 'A district procurator’s declaration allows the police to continue holding Jaycee Chan and investigati