'uri': 'nyt://article/8bcf86fb-b706-56e1-8a92-f1bf04d3051c'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The war slowed automobile trade in Paris in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/1914-paris-auto-trade-stalls/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The war slowed automobile trade in Paris in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In common with so many other businesses, the automobile industry has been brought almost to a standstill by the war. A walk up the Champs-Elysées is sufficient to prove this. Hoardings block nearly all the window fronts of the numerous auto shops. Other shops have been turned into workrooms, where scores of women may be seen sewing diligently. One of the few auto firms still doing business in Paris is the Packard Company. An advertisement in the Herald announces that Packard automobiles may be hired for journeys in France at 1 franc 50 per kilomètre. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 18, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/blogs/18iht-oldsept18-packard/18iht-oldsept18-packard-articleLarge.png', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/18/blogs/18iht-oldsept18-packard/18iht-oldsept18-packard-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/blogs/18iht-oldsept18-packard/18iht-oldsept18-packard-jumbo.png', 'height': 576, 'width': 771, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/blogs/18iht-oldsept18-packard/18iht-oldsept18-packard-superJumbo.png', 'height': 576, 'width': 771, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'sup