e Williams, 50, had expressed a desire to scale back the number of weeks he spent on the road, a plan that did not appeal to Adam Scott.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Scott is in the market for a caddie after parting with Steve Williams, who helped guide him to his only major championship, the 2013 Masters, and to the world No. 1 ranking during their four-year partnership.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adam Scott Splits With Caddie, Who Hopes to Travel Less', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scott Splits With Caddie, Who Hopes to Travel Less', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Adam (1980- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Steve (1963- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T14:29:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/063e8064-3f03-5937-b300-f45f4f5f090f', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/063e8064-3f03-5937-b300-f45f4f5f090f'}, {'abstract': 'Gen. Ray Odierno, the Army chief of staff, said “rooting out” militants on the ground would be necessary, but he did not say it had to be done by Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/world/middleeast/general-odierno-isis-iraq-nato.html', 'snippet': 'Gen. Ray Odierno, the Army chief of staff, said “rooting out” militants on the ground would be necessary, but he did not say it had to be done by Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIESBADEN, Germany — The United States general who beat back Islamic extremists in Iraq in 2007 suggested on Wednesday that the battle against Islamic State jihadis would only succeed with the use of ground forces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/world/18GENERAL/18GENERAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/18/world/18GENERAL/18GENERAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 752}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/world/18GENERAL/18GENERAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 818, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/world/18GENERAL/18GENERAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1635, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/world/18GENERAL/18GENERAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/18/world/18GENERAL/18GENERAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/world/18GENERAL/18GENERAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Army Chief Says Ground Troops Will Be Needed Against ISIS', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Odierno, Raymond T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T14:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc96e723-6c34-5b03-9209-f60fabd81ecb', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc96e723-6c34-5b03-9209-f60fabd81ecb'}, {'abstract': 'As the conflict escalates, Congress is about to shut its doors for the election season and head home.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/will-congress-bother-to-debate-war-against-isis/', 'snippet': 'As the conflict escalates, Congress is about to shut its doors for the election season and head home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the American war against the Islamic State escalates, Congress is about to shut its doors for the election season and head home. The most it will do is authorize some limited assistance to Syrian rebels, but the Senate will probably not even take a vote on that, instead burying the aid inside an emergency spending bill so that its members won’t have to be held accountable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Congress Bother to Debate War Against ISIS?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiff, Adam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T14:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d308b828-af47-5add-8b2f-4c1edc8fb073', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d308b828-af47-5add-8b2f-4c1edc8fb073'}, {'abstract': 'Money market funds played a central role in Lehman Brothers’ failure and helped spread the contagion. But, Jennifer Taub, of Vermont Law School, says, the problems remain unsolved.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/post-lehman-money-market-fund-protections-still-weak/', 'snippet': 'Money market funds played a central role in Lehman Brothers’ failure and helped spread the contagion. But, Jennifer Taub, of Vermont Law School, says, the problems remain unsolved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jennifer Taub is a professor at Vermont Law School. Her book “Other People’s Houses” was published in May by Yale Press.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-lehman/dbpix-lehman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-lehman/dbpix-lehman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-lehman/dbpix-lehman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/dbpix-lehman/d