n': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1402f2e-e14a-57f4-b779-d0518e6a78f3', 'word_count': 1213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1402f2e-e14a-57f4-b779-d0518e6a78f3'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The Soviet Union attacked Poland in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/1939-soviets-invade-poland/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The Soviet Union attacked Poland in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Soviet Union entered the war at dawn yesterday by invading Poland along its entire 500-mile eastern frontier, an hour after the Polish Ambassador in Moscow had refused to receive a note of explanation from the Soviet government. Violent fighting between Polish and Russian troops was reported at Molodeczno, sixty-five miles southeast of Vilna. At almost the same time, German artillery and planes began a day-long bombardment of the center of Warsaw. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 18, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/blogs/18iht-oldsept18-poland/18iht-oldsept18-poland-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/18/blogs/18iht-oldsept18-poland/18iht-oldsept18-poland-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/blogs/18iht-oldsept18-poland/18iht-oldsept18-poland-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/blogs/18iht-oldsept18-poland/18iht-oldsept18-poland-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo'