e': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/5f5cd5f2-deec-5c6f-83e6-5f7d60b41788', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/5f5cd5f2-deec-5c6f-83e6-5f7d60b41788'}, {'abstract': 'Volunteer medical organizations said the vaccine afflicted dozens of children in insurgent-held areas of Idlib Province.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/world/middleeast/syrian-children-die-after-vaccinations.html', 'snippet': 'Volunteer medical organizations said the vaccine afflicted dozens of children in insurgent-held areas of Idlib Province.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An improperly mixed or possibly sabotaged measles vaccine has killed as many as 50 children in insurgent-held areas of northwestern Syria, volunteer medical organizations and physicians reported Wednesday, forcing the suspension of a large-scale United Nations vaccination campaign intended to stop the spread of measles, rubella and polio.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bad Vaccine Kills Dozens of Children Inside Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bad Vaccine Kills Dozens of Children Inside Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Measles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'German Measles (Rubella)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poliomyelitis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mumps', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T18:28:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone and Hwaida Saad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hwaida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aea5f18-b6c3-53b6-a71c-f7f3c2f2f09f', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aea5f18-b6c3-53b6-a71c-f7f3c2f2f09f'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Milan Fashion Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/alberta-ferretti-milan-fashion-week-spring-summer-2015-collection/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Milan Fashion Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the Milan Fashion Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Fashion Week: Alberta Ferretti Spring/Summer 2015', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferretti, Alberta', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T18:30:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alfredo Piola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alfredo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94fb40f3-b681-5223-b01b-86b1755815f4', 'word_count': 27, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94fb40f3-b681-5223-b01b-86b1755815f4'}, {'abstract': 'New rules could reduce the number of men who would be prescribed the medicines, as well as coverage from insurance companies for their use.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/health/testosterone-drugs-fda.html', 'snippet': 'New rules could reduce the number of men who would be prescribed the medicines, as well as coverage from insurance companies for their use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HYATTSVILLE, Md. — An expert panel voted overwhelmingly on Wednesday for the Food and Drug Administration to impose strict new limitations on the multibillion-dollar testosterone drug industry, recommending that the agency tighten labels for the medicines so they are not prescribed to men who only have problems related to aging, such as low energy and libido. The F.D.A. often takes the advice of such panels. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Panel Backs Limits on Testosterone Drugs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Panel Backs Limits on Testosterone Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Testosterone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hormones', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T18:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bc54f0a-9086-5786-9f38-a607869488d0', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bc54f0a-9086-5786-9f38-a607869488d0'}, {'abstract': 'The commission found that the two companies violated the Children’s Online Privacy Protection Act, known as Coppa.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/f-t-c-fines-yelp-and-tinyco-for-violating-childrens-privacy-rules/', 'snippet': 'The commission found that the two companies violated the Children’s Online Privacy Protection Act, known as Coppa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | WASHINGTON – Tiny Pets, Tiny Zoo, Tiny Monsters and other mobile apps aimed at children have been downloaded more than 34 million times, often – not surprisingly – by children. But TinyCo, the maker of the apps, failed to recognize that strict rules apply to collection of information from children online, according to federal regulators.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/technology/17bits-ftc/17bits-ftc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 568, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/technology/17bits-ftc/17bits-ftc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 568, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/technology/17bits-ftc/17bits-ftc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/17/technology/17bits-ftc/17bits-ftc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/technology/17bits-ftc/17bits-ftc-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name'