s.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/deborah-kass-craig-martin-outdoor-art-mall-chestnut-hill-florida/', 'snippet': 'Art Production Fund has installed the works of Deborah Kass and Jessica Craig-Martin in advertising spaces at a pair of high-end shopping centers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the daughter of two art collectors — the fashion designer Lisa Perry and the hedge fund manager Richard Perry — Samantha Perry David grew up surrounded by Jeff Koons sculptures and Andy Warhol paintings. Now the head of upMarkets, a division of the retail real estate firm WS Development, David realized there was a\xa0dearth of public art at two of its properties, the luxury shopping center The Street in Chestnut Hill, Mass., and Hyde Park Village in Tampa, Fla. So she called on two of her mother’s friends, Yvonne Force Villareal and Doreen Remen of Art Production Fund,\xa0to do something about it.\xa0“We were compelled by this notion because there is no public art within that community,” Force Villareal says, “and we always strive to bring the vision of contemporary artists to new audiences that have little exposure to such projects.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/t-magazine/17binlot-hartman/17binlot-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/t-magazine/17binlot-hartman/17binlot-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/t-magazine/17binlot-hartman/17binlot-hartman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/t-magazine/17binlot-hartman/17binlot-hartman-superJumbo.jpg', 'h