.com/2014/09/17/lawsuit-aims-to-put-an-end-to-gay-conversion-therapy-in-china/', 'snippet': 'China decriminalized homosexuality in 1997 and declassified it as a mental illness in 2001, but clinics promising to “convert” gay people abound in a country where pressure to join the heterosexual mainstream is high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 30-year-old man going by the pseudonym Xiao Zhen has attracted attention in recent months as the first person in China to file a lawsuit against a clinic offering “gay conversion therapy,” treatments aiming to change sexual orientation that many medical experts criticize as ineffective and harmful. With the help of the Beijing LGBT Center, an organization representing gay, bisexual and transgender people, Xiao Zhen has sued the Xinyupiaoxiang Counseling Center in Chongqing, as well as Baidu, China’s leading Internet search engine, for posting the ads that led him there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Xiao Zhen on Trying to End ‘Gay Conversion Therapy’ in China', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baidu Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T22:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Becky Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Becky', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb265fb1-8c91-595a-bc3a-bcab685ef3af', 'word_count': 1471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb265fb1-8c91-595a-bc3a-bcab685ef3af'}, {'abstract': 'To prevent another recall debacle, Congress badly needs to strengthen the federal agency responsible for investigating auto defects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/opinion/avoiding-the-next-auto-safety-failure.html', 'snippet': 'To prevent another recall debacle, Congress badly needs to strengthen the federal agency responsible for investigating auto defects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is one clear lesson from the General Motors recall debacle: Congress badly needs to strengthen the federal agency responsible for investigating auto defects. Reports released this week paint a disturbing picture of how regulators failed to identify an ignition defect in millions of G.M. cars that has now been linked to at least  19 deaths and could be responsible for many more.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Total Failure on Auto Safety ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Total Failure on Auto Safety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T22:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/59899ef1-ff56-5316-9e7c-e73169626f20', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59899ef1-ff56-5316-9e7c-e73169626f20'}, {'abstract': 'Is there a disagreement over the kind of strategy needed to succeed against ISIS?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/on-ground-troops-in-iraq-obama-and-his-generals-appear-at-odds/', 'snippet': 'Is there a disagreement over the kind of strategy needed to succeed against ISIS?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Speaking to military personnel at CENTCOM in Tampa on Wednesday, President Obama was unequivocal about his unwillingness to deploy ground troops again in Iraq.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Ground Troops in Iraq, Obama and his Generals Appear at Odds', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T22:11:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ernesto Londo&#241;o', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ernesto', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Londo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d12ea1c8-ca76-5c34-bd03-934dae6b530d', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d12ea1c8-ca76-5c34-bd03-934dae6b530d'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers would like to improve transparency before prominent think tanks’ scholars testify on Capitol Hill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/us/politics/house-proposal-would-require-think-tanks-to-disclose-foreign-funding.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers would like to improve transparency before prominent think tanks’ scholars testify on Capitol Hill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Expressing concern that prominent think tanks may be covertly trying to push the agendas of foreign government donors, the House of Representatives is considering a rule that would require that their scholars testifying on Capitol Hill disclose any such support — a proposal that won immediate bipartisan endorsement on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Proposal Would Require Think Tanks to Disclose Funding by Foreign Governments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proposal Would Require Think Tanks to Disclose Funding by Foreign Governments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Think Tanks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Speier, Jackie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookings Institution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic Council', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Strategic and International Studies', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T22:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lipton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2eb7bc9-72