 {'original': 'Compiled by Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e160da4d-c9b8-5a4b-a353-a635d405fd21', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e160da4d-c9b8-5a4b-a353-a635d405fd21'}, {'abstract': 'With Americans’ fears about a terrorist attack on the rise, a New York Times/CBS News poll finds the public is questioning President Obama’s strategy for combating the militant organization calling itself the Islamic State.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/us/politics/for-first-time-most-americans-disapprove-of-obamas-handling-of-terrorism.html', 'snippet': 'With Americans’ fears about a terrorist attack on the rise, a New York Times/CBS News poll finds the public is questioning President Obama’s strategy for combating the militant organization calling itself the Islamic State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time in his presidency, more Americans disapprove of President Obama’s handling of terrorism than approve of it, as discontent about his management of foreign affairs and the fight against Sunni militants in Iraq and Syria weighs on an anxious and conflicted public, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News Poll.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Faulted in Terror Fight, New Poll Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Faulted in Terror Fight, New Poll Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Julie Hirschfeld', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sussman, Dalia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T22:31:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Hirschfeld Davis and Dalia Sussman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'Hirschfeld', 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Dalia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sussman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ca307af-1d56-572c-b332-eb5631d9bbff', 'word_count': 1369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ca307af-1d56-572c-b332-eb5631d9bbff'}, {'abstract': 'On gay marriage, Judge Richard Posner’s journey from “no” to “maybe but not yet” to “yes and now” suggests he is a stand-in for many of us.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/opinion/the-moment-at-hand.html', 'snippet': 'On gay marriage, Judge Richard Posner’s journey from “no” to “maybe but not yet” to “yes and now” suggests he is a stand-in for many of us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two stories appeared on the website of The New York Times within hours of each other early this month. One reported that the drugstore giant CVS had stopped selling tobacco products in its 7,700 stores. The other announced: “Gay Groups to March in St. Patrick’s Day Parade as a Ban Falls.” These two developments had nothing obvious in common beyond their newsworthiness. And yet to anyone who has spent the past couple of decades living on planet Earth, the two stories conveyed the same powerful message: Look how times have changed. What was scarcely imaginable not too many years ago has come to pass.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Moment at Hand', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eskridge, William N Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posner, Richard A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Souter, David H', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T22:33:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/18669c92-f44e-5948-8863-26fc8f00c9b2', 'word_count': 1864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18669c92-f44e-5948-8863-26fc8f00c9b2'}, {'abstract': 'Marilynne Robinson, Elizabeth McCracken and Phil Klay are among the writers whose work is on the 2014 fiction long list for the National Book Awards.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/national-book-awards-fiction/', 'snippet': 'Marilynne Robinson, Elizabeth McCracken and Phil Klay are among the writers whose work is on the 2014 fiction long list for the National Book Awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The long list of nominees for the 2014 National Book Award f