lead_paragraph': 'Federal agencies have taken legal action to shut down two networks of online payday lenders, saying they made fraudulent loans to unwitting consumers and then used the loans as a pretext to withdraw millions of dollars from their bank accounts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Courts Close 2 Payday Lenders Accused of Fraud', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payday Loans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-17T23:13:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ec04426-9bd5-51b0-8711-59d36f1ef5d3', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ec04426-9bd5-51b0-8711-59d36f1ef5d3'}, {'abstract': 'Galerie Kreo exhibits deceptively humble works of design in its new London space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/garden/where-old-friends-show-off.html', 'snippet': 'Galerie Kreo exhibits deceptively humble works of design in its new London space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In May, the Paris-based Galerie Kreo, which is known for experimental contemporary design and flashy clients like Karl Lagerfeld and Azzedine Alaïa, opened a London outpost near Berkeley Square in Mayfair. For its latest exhibition in the new space, Kreo is showing off rare works by old friends, including Jasper Morrison, Pierre Charpin and Ronan and Erwan Bouroullec. The exhibition, called “Des Formes Utiles,” explores the relationship between function and form with restrained interpretations of mirrors, tables, lights and ladders, including Studio Wieki Somers’s flowerlike “Aoyama Lamp” ($42,000, edition of six), and Konstantin Grcic’s “London Calling” a Shaker-pure set of oak library steps (about $46,000, edition of eight).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/garden/18CURR1/18CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/18/garden/18CURR1/18CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/garden/18CURR1/18CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/garden/18CURR1/18CURR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/garden/18CURR1/18CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/18/garden/18CURR1/18CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/garden/18CURR1/18CURR1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thum