 {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breeding of Animals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Birds of Pandemonium, The (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T00:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandy Keenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/212cdf24-50b7-5cdc-8160-714b56a72ab1', 'word_count': 1487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/212cdf24-50b7-5cdc-8160-714b56a72ab1'}, {'abstract': 'The government said Wednesday that it would seek to revoke the citizenship of the actress Maria Conchita Alonso, left, a fervent critic of its socialist-inspired policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/world/americas/venezuela-move-to-revoke-actresss-citizenship.html', 'snippet': 'The government said Wednesday that it would seek to revoke the citizenship of the actress Maria Conchita Alonso, left, a fervent critic of its socialist-inspired policies.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The government said Wednesday that it would seek to revoke the citizenship of the actress Maria Conchita Alonso, left, a fervent critic of its socialist-inspired policies. Ms. Alonso was born in Cuba and moved to Venezuela as a child, becoming a naturalized citizen. She has lived for years in the United States. The Interior Ministry will take judicial action to revoke her citizenship, according to the Information Ministry website. In May, Ms. Alonso said in an interview with the Voice of America, “I wish that the United States would invade with bullets to remove all those wretched communists from Venezuela.” Venezuela is mired in an economic crisis, with inflation of 63 percent a year and shortages of basic goods, problems for which the government frequently blames its opponents. Ms. Alonso competed in the Miss Venezuela pageant in 1975 and has appeared in many films, including “Predator 2.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/18/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 901}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 931, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/18/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Move to Revoke Actress’s Citizenship', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Move to Revoke Actress’s Citizenship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alonso, Maria Conchita', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T00:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f07b6930-6490-50f6-a230-265ded9ad3d8', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f07b6930-6490-50f6-a230-265ded9ad3d8'}, {'abstract': 'Twitter reacts to the talents of the new Miss America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/17/style/miss-new-yorks-red-cup-juggling.html', 'snippet': 'Twitter reacts to the talents of the new Miss America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, the Miss America pageant crowned its latest winner, Kira Kazantsev, the third consecutive winner from New York (labeled a “three-peat” by Twitter users). For the talent portion, Ms. Kazantsev sang Pharrell Williams’s “Happy” while tapping and flipping a red plastic cup, a routine that some assumed was inspired by the 2012 musical comedy “Pitch Perfect,” starring Anna Kendrick as an a cappella singer. Others thought it looked like a college drinking game. Making matters worse, the following tidbit appeared on the screen during her performance: “Loves anything Jane Austin.” This misspelling of the renowned author’s name added to the barrage of tweets.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miss New York’s Red-Cup Juggling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Well, It Wasn’t Beer Pong', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Safronova, Valeriya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty Contests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miss America Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T00:12:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valeriya Safronova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valeriya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Safronova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d29bad2-de1f-56d0-81a2-93bab71c24aa', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d29bad2-de1f-56d0-81a2-93bab71c24aa'}, {'abstract': 'Speakers at a hearing sought the Council’s support for a union campaign for pension payments from owners of six jazz clubs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/nyregion/city-council-hears-push-for-benefits-by-jazz-veterans.html', 'snippet': 'Speakers at a hearing sought the Council’s support for a union campaign for pension payments from owners of six jazz clubs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the middle of a City Council committee hearing at City Hall on Wednesday, notes began to stream, slowly and unexpectedly, from a flugelhorn, alternating between blares and warbles, but unmistakably forming the spiritual “Nobody Knows the Trouble I’ve Seen.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/subJAZZMEN/subJAZZMEN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'su