N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Owens, Jimmy (1943- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T00:14:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tatiana Schlossberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tatiana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schlossberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/216c1be2-5adb-5f00-8dc1-ff360e612c31', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/216c1be2-5adb-5f00-8dc1-ff360e612c31'}, {'abstract': 'Opponents of a law requiring voters to provide photo ID asked a federal appeals court to reconsider a ruling last week that cleared the way for the law to take effect for the Nov. 4 elections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/us/wisconsin-full-court-asked-to-halt-voter-id-law.html', 'snippet': 'Opponents of a law requiring voters to provide photo ID asked a federal appeals court to reconsider a ruling last week that cleared the way for the law to take effect for the Nov. 4 elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opponents of a law requiring voters to provide photo ID asked a federal appeals court on Wednesday to reconsider a ruling last week that cleared the way for the law to take effect for the Nov. 4 elections. Arguing that the abrupt reinstatement of the requirement would create chaos and confusion and prevent some residents from voting, the opponents, including the American Civil Liberties Union, asked that judges from the United States Court of Appeals for the Seventh Circuit re-examine the decision last week by a three-judge panel of the court. The law was first approved by lawmakers and signed by Gov. Scott Walker, a Republican, in 2011, though it has been delayed since 2012 as legal fights play out in state and federal courts. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisconsin: Full Court Asked to Halt Voter ID Law', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wisconsin: Full Court Asked to Halt Voter ID Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T00:18:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e162901d-9039-5fd8-82bc-698c60e6bb02', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e162901d-9039-5fd8-82bc-698c60e6bb02'}, {'abstract': 'A trial on Detroit’s plan for erasing debts and remaking city services will be delayed for a week, a federal bankruptcy judge said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/us/michigan-one-week-delay-ordered-in-bankruptcy-trial.html', 'snippet': 'A trial on Detroit’s plan for erasing debts and remaking city services will be delayed for a week, a federal bankruptcy judge said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A trial on Detroit’s plan for erasing debts and remaking city services will be delayed for a week, a federal bankruptcy judge said on Wednesday. The delay, which will halt testimony in the case for all of next week, is to give the remaining critics of Detroit’s plan a chance to rework their legal case after another critic, Syncora Guarantee, a bond insurer, unexpectedly dropped its objections and settled with the city. The trial over the exit plan proposed by Detroit, the largest city ever to seek bankruptcy protection, began on Sept. 2 and is scheduled to run into October. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: One-Week Delay Ordered in Bankruptcy Trial', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: One-Week Delay Ordered in Bankruptcy Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T00:24:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f2e8bd1-9d61-5a66-a3e2-43abd46fc695', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f2e8bd1-9d61-5a66-a3e2-43abd46fc695'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s hard-core drinking joints are threatened by gentrification.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/fashion/a-sobering-future-for-new-yorks-dive-bars.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s hard-core drinking joints are threatened by gentrification.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a dive bar should, the Subway Inn smelled like stale beer and sweat one Thursday last month as a throng of well-wishers crowded three deep for a last hurrah.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/fashion/18ZDIVEBAR1/18zDIVEBAR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/18/fashion/18ZDIVEBAR1/18zDIVEBAR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'x