': 'subject', 'value': 'In Vitro Fertilization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T01:34:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86c5f93f-b993-5f26-9404-813f4697831d', 'word_count': 2320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86c5f93f-b993-5f26-9404-813f4697831d'}, {'abstract': 'In an era of only televisions, radios and phonographs, he was the industry’s top salesman and spread electronics fever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/business/jack-wayman-inventor-of-consumer-electronics-show-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'In an era of only televisions, radios and phonographs, he was the industry’s top salesman and spread electronics fever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jack Wayman, a sales executive who saw the future and said it was consumer electronics, organized the industry’s first trade show in the era of black-and-white television and fought Hollywood’s endeavor to smother the videocassette-recorder business, died on Aug. 30 in Boulder, Colo. He was 92.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/business/WAYMAN-obit/WAYMAN-obit-1410994373320-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/18/business/WAYMAN-obit/WAYMAN-obit-1410994373320-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 696}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/business/WAYMAN-obit/WAYMAN-obit-1