ed Ambien — and spelling it out is the only way to clarify things. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Places Where You Can Hear a Pin Drop', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spelling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T02:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a73760e-0158-58a8-95dc-d8a29c74d117', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a73760e-0158-58a8-95dc-d8a29c74d117'}, {'abstract': 'Women around the country expressed disillusionment this week as the N.F.L. desperately tried to stanch the public backlash to several controversial cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/sports/football/women-disillusioned-by-nfl.html', 'snippet': 'Women around the country expressed disillusionment this week as the N.F.L. desperately tried to stanch the public backlash to several controversial cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This time of year, families throughout the Chicago area schedule their weekends around the Bears. Nearly half the city’s televisions tune in to Bears games when they play, and an empty seat is rarely seen at Soldier Field.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/sports/CITY-JP-WOMEN-3/CITY-JP-WOMEN-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xla