 Robyn Davidson’s memoir about her 1,700-mile walk across the Australian desert in 1977, accompanied only by four camels, a dog and the occasional National Geographic photographer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/movies/mia-wasikowska-plays-robyn-davidson-in-tracks.html', 'snippet': '“Tracks” is based on Robyn Davidson’s memoir about her 1,700-mile walk across the Australian desert in 1977, accompanied only by four camels, a dog and the occasional National Geographic photographer.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Tracks,” a high-mileage, low-energy story about an Australian woman, her trusty dog, four charming camels and the siren call of adventure, comes coated in a layer of sand. At times, the sand rolls on and on like an endlessly unfurling, magically variegated carpet that shifts from blood red to burnt sienna, pale pink and dung brown. At other times, it violently rises off the desert floor, swirling and churning into dusty whirlpools. The adventurer, Robyn Davidson (Mia Wasikowska), may blink — at the sandy dust and one deranged hallucination — but she keeps going, at times with nothing other than some cloth between her and a seemingly asphyxiating end. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I’d Walk 1,700 Miles With a Camel ', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I’d Walk 1,700 Miles With a Camel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curran, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wasikowska, Mia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davidson, Robyn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Tracks (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T14:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/946b2776-c29e-5371-8b9a-f59868c991bc', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/946b2776-c29e-5371-8b9a-f59868c991bc'}, {'abstract': 'With thousands of bridges in New York State deemed structurally deficient, there are two choices: repair or rebuild. The 60-year-old Tappan Zee Bridge and the Brooklyn Bridge are the latest examples.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000003118059/living-city-a-tale-of-two-bridges.html', 'snippet': 'With thousands of bridges in New York State deemed structurally deficient, there are two choices: repair or rebuild. The 60-year-old Tappan Zee Bridge and the Brooklyn Bridge are the latest examples.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With thousands of bridges in New York State deemed structurally deficient, there are two choices: repair or rebuild. The 60-year-old Tappan Zee Bridge and the Brooklyn Bridge are the latest examples.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/Tappanzeeweb3/Tappanzeeweb3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/Tappanzeeweb3/Tappanzeeweb3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/Tappanzeeweb3/Tappanzeeweb3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/Tappanzeeweb3/Tappanzeeweb3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, '