 '_id': 'nyt://article/5f56d7ef-4504-50f0-949f-ace7563ad144', 'word_count': 1343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f56d7ef-4504-50f0-949f-ace7563ad144'}, {'abstract': 'Less than a year after construction began, the new bridge is making progress toward the opening of its first span, in 2016. Includes a video: two ways to deal with an old bridge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/nyregion/new-tappan-zee-bridge-begins-to-take-shape-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Less than a year after construction began, the new bridge is making progress toward the opening of its first span, in 2016. Includes a video: two ways to deal with an old bridge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TARRYTOWN, N.Y. — The shape of the new Tappan Zee Bridge is emerging from the green-gray waters of the Hudson River.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/TAPPANZEEweb2/TAPPANZEEweb2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/TAPPANZEEweb2/TAPPANZEEweb2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/TAPPANZEEweb2/TAPPANZEEweb2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/TAPPANZEEweb2/TAPPANZEEweb2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/TAPPANZEEweb2/TAPPANZEEweb2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/TAPPANZEEweb2/TAPPANZEEweb2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/18/nyregion/TAPPANZEEweb2/TAPPANZEEweb2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Skeleton of Tappan Zee Bridge’s Successor Begins to Surface in the Hudson', 'kicker': '21st-Century Span', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bridge’s Skeleton Begins to Surface in Hudson River', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berger, Joseph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tappan Zee Bridge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York State Thruway Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tappan Zee Constructors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Nyack (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tarrytown (NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T14:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30bc2012-aa95-5e43-a6c3-50a9c6e6248f', 'word_count': 1444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30bc2012-aa95-5e43-a6c3-50a9c6e6248f'}, {'abstract': 'Referendum-day thoughts on the case for Scottish independence.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/scotland-self-interest-and-self-government/', 'snippet': 'Referendum-day thoughts on the case for Scottish independence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the perspective of America’s national interest, the prospect of an independent Scotland\xa0— which could, though probably won’t, become a reality after today’s referendum vote — has relatively\xa0little to recommend it. Scottish secession would hardly be disastrous for the U.S., but it would come with all sorts of modest downsides: It would weaken\xa0our most reliable ally for the long term and create an immediate (if likely manageable) crisis at a time when the world is quite sufficiently unstable already; it would lead to various military and strategic headaches\xa0(again: none insurmountable, but not ideal right now); and it would sow further instability in secession-prone regions across Europe where political differences might not be settled quite so civilly (including one within the British Isles themselves).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scotland, Self-Interest and Self-Government', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T14:17:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifie