d Adam Driver.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/tracks/tracks-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/tracks/tracks-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/tracks/tracks-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/tracks/tracks-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/tracks/tracks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/tracks/tracks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/tracks/tracks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clip: ‘Tracks’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T17:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f2611477-8257-5328-8cc4-70547aba861f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f2611477-8257-5328-8cc4-70547aba861f'}, {'abstract': '“Thread Lines” at the Drawing Center includes textile-art titans like Louise Bourgeois and Sheila Hicks, and emerging talents.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/thread-lines-drawing-center-group-exhibition-fiber-art-evolution-louise-bourgeois-sheila-hicks-sam-moyer/', 'snippet': '“Thread Lines” at the Drawing Center includes textile-art titans like Louise Bourgeois and Sheila Hicks, and emerging talents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the Drawing Center seems a strange place for a sweeping show about textile art, consider the concept of the line. The distance between two points is, as the artist Sheila Hicks says, from her Paris studio, “the mother thinker of all form-making, whether it be two- or three-dimensional. It is the direct conductor from brain to materialization.” Rendered in fiber, that line is just pulled a little tighter, and the tension is on full display in “Thread Lines,” opening Sept. 19.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Group Exhibition Traces the Evolution of Fiber Art', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On View: Common Threads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bourgeois, Louise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hicks, Sheila', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moyer, Sam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drawing Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T17:36:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Su Wu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Su', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db75a541-162f-5755-822d-666306317724', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db75a541-162f-5755-822d-666306317724'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: In 1964, Martin Luther King Jr. obtained endorsement from the Vatican for his struggle.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/1964-dr-king-gets-papal-pledge/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: In 1964, Martin Luther King Jr. obtained endorsement from the Vatican for his struggle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — The Rev. Martin Luther King Jr. said today [Sept. 18] that Pope Paul VI promised him he would publicly denounce racial segregation. ‘‘Pope Paul was very open and forthright in his statements on the situation,’’ the U.S. Negro leader told reporters after a 25- minute talk with the pope. ‘‘He said he was a friend of the Negro people and that he was following our struggle in the United States. The pope told me that he would make a personal and public declaration against racial segregation. However, he said he could not accept violence and I made it clear that we did not support violence either,’’ he said. Dr. King said before meeting the Pope that he felt a statement reaffirming Roman Catholic opposition to racial segregation would be ‘‘a profound help for us.’’\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 19, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/blogs/19iht-oldsept19-pope/19iht-oldsept19-pope-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 485, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/blogs/19iht-oldsept19-pope/19iht-oldsept19-pope-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600,