ion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gucci', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marc Jacobs International LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T18:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54631fc9-77da-5b9a-a32f-3d5b41bef200', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54631fc9-77da-5b9a-a32f-3d5b41bef200'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Ward Sutton on the elements that inspired his design for a play about three men who think they are Jesus Christ.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/18/behind-the-poster-3-christs/', 'snippet': 'The artist Ward Sutton on the elements that inspired his design for a play about three men who think they are Jesus Christ.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three paranoid schizophrenics, each of whom thinks he is Jesus Christ, come together in the play “3 Christs,” now being staged at Judson Memorial Church by the Peculiar Works Project. The show recreates a University of Michigan experiment by Dr. Milton Rokeach, who had the men live and work together to see what would happen. Rokeach’s published study, “The Three Christs of Ypsilanti,” is the basis for the stage adaptation by S. M. Dale and Barry Rowell.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/10/theater/10three-sutton/10three-sutton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xl