 the countries who helped the Islamic State grow into a global threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one has presented a more articulate case for Iran to Western audiences than the foreign minister, Mohammad Javad Zarif. He and President Hassan Rouhani proved that last year when they attended their first United Nations General Assembly after Mr. Rouhani’s election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran and the ‘Coalition of Repenters’', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zarif, Mohammad Javad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T18:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1058c150-a4d2-5151-8858-dd9d902aa46c', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1058c150-a4d2-5151-8858-dd9d902aa46c'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration’s measures are part of the first major federal effort to confront a public health problem that takes at least 23,000 lives a year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/health/us-lays-out-strategy-to-combat-crisis-of-antibiotic-resistance.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration’s measures are part of the first major federal effort to confront a public health problem that takes at least 23,000 lives a year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration on Thursday announced measures to tackle the growing threat of antibiotic resistance, outlining a national strategy that includes incentives for the development of new drugs, tighter stewardship of existing ones, and improvements in tracking the use of antibiotics and the microbes that are resistant to them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/science/19antibiotics/19antibiotics-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/19/science/19antibiotics/19antibiotics-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/science/19antibiotics/19antibiotics-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/science/19antibiotics/19antibiotics-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1263, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/science/19antibiotics/19antibiotics-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/19/science/19antibiotics/19antibiotics-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/science/19antibiotics/19antibiotics-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Aims to Curb Peril of Antibiotic Resistance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Aims to Curb Peril of Antibiotic Resistance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Science and Technology Policy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holdren, John P', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T19:01:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1ceeb32-8839-5ae6-8ece-bebb210b2671', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1ceeb32-8839-5ae6-8ece-bebb210b2671'}, {'abstract': 'A proposal aims to address the problem of studies that go unpublished even though their findings can be important.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/upshot/to-get-more-out-of-science-show-the-rejected-research.html', 'snippet': 'A proposal aims to address the problem of studies that go unpublished even though their findings can be important.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2013, the federal government spent over $30 billion to support basic scientific research. These funds help create knowledge and stimulate greater productivity and commercial activity, but could we get an even better return on our investment?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subty