}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b380d028-b458-5184-b719-6d1f824baf39', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b380d028-b458-5184-b719-6d1f824baf39'}, {'abstract': 'The primary attraction of this show is the New York debut of the artist’s final work, “Parallel I-IV.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/arts/design/harun-farocki-parallel.html', 'snippet': 'The primary attraction of this show is the New York debut of the artist’s final work, “Parallel I-IV.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The death of the German filmmaker and writer Harun Farocki this summer at 70 was a huge loss. Few artists of his international standing so consistently combined formal daring and probity with an agitator’s temperament. Beginning in the 1960s, his films, using images old and new, staged and documentary, concentrated on examining mechanisms of political control embodied in the chemical weapons industry, the prison system, consumer culture and surveillance or other electronic technology.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/19SUBFAROCKI-GALLERIES/SUBFAROCKI-GALLERIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/19SUBFAROCKI-GALLERIES/SUBFAROCKI-GALLERIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/19SUBFAROCKI-GALLERIES/SUBFAROCKI-GALLERIES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/arts/19SUBFAROCKI-GALLERIES/SUBFAROCKI-GALLERIES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'c