s swarming with workers busily getting ready for the season’s opening night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trucks pulled in behind the Metropolitan Opera House, and stagehands began unloading sets for Bizet’s “Carmen,” hauling them onto a mammoth elevator, similar to those on aircraft carriers, and storing the disassembled pieces of Spain below the stage between a patch of Scotland from Verdi’s “Macbeth” and bits of Paris from Puccini’s “La Bohème.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Labor War Over, Met’s Operatic Army Mobilizes ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Labor War Over, Met’s Operatic Army Mobilizes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netrebko, Anna', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T22:44:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3051c9a-485b-54e9-9c9a-e3a57dec8b4f', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3051c9a-485b-54e9-9c9a-e3a57dec8b4f'}, {'abstract': 'Isabelle Adjani tries to weather the St. Bartholomew Day’s Massacre in Patrice Chéreau’s “Queen Margot.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/movies/homevideo/portraits-of-aristocracy-in-queen-margot-and-blanche.html', 'snippet': 'Isabelle Adjani tries to weather the St. Bartholomew Day’s Massacre in Patrice Chéreau’s “Queen Margot.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A roistering spectacle, heavy on intrigue, murder and fabulous brocaded gowns, Patrice Chéreau’s “Queen Margot” (1994) returns on Blu-ray and DVD (courtesy of the Cohen Film Collection), restored to the original 159-minute director’s cut awarded the third-place Jury Prize at the 1994 Cannes Film Festival. The Palme d’Or went to “Pulp Fiction,” a title that could have fit Chéreau’s blood-soaked, lustful chef d’oeuvre as well.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21HOBERMAN1/21HOBERMAN1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21HOBERMAN1/21HOBERMAN1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21HOBERMAN1/21HOBERMAN1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21HOBERMAN1/21HOBERMAN1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1153, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21HOBERMAN1/21HOBERMAN1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21HOBERMAN1/21HOBERMAN1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21HOBERMAN1/21HOBERMAN1-thum