https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/arts/television/hack-my-brain-self-improvement-on-science-channel.html', 'snippet': 'In “Hack My Brain,” the host Todd Sampson submits himself to assorted exercises that are supposed to improve his mental prowess.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A whole industry has materialized to exploit the fear that we’re all much stupider than we need to be. Supposed brain-workout apps like Elevate. Pills that claim to improve memory and concentration. On Friday night, the Science Channel works the same territory with a three-part dose of nonsense called “Hack My Brain,” an Australian import in which a guy you’ve probably never heard of submits himself to assorted exercises that are alleged to improve neuro-this-and-that.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Were They Thinking? ', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Were They Thinking?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hack My Brain (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-18T22:55:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c84ae6e-c875-5447-bb0d-91247f320501', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c84ae6e-c875-5447-bb0d-91247f320501'}, {'abstract': 'Georgian cinema is exotic, and can be forbidding as well as fiercely beautiful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/movies/a-survey-celebrates-georgias-rich-film-tradition.html', 'snippet': 'Georgian cinema is exotic, and can be forbidding as well as fiercely beautiful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Squeezed between the Black and Caspian Seas, as it was among the Roman and Persian, and Ottoman and Russian empires, Georgia is a small realm with a spectacular natural setting and a proud past. “I am a representative of the last living Mediterranean culture that has its roots in antiquity,” the self-exiled Georgian filmmaker Otar Iosseliani once told an interviewer in a bit of patriotic hyperbole.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GEORGIA1/21GEORGIA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GEORGIA1/21GEORGIA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GEORGIA1/21GEORGIA1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GEORGIA1/21GEORGIA1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GEORGIA1/21GEORGIA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GEORGIA1/21GEORGIA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GEORGIA1/21GEORGIA1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width