 the city is also a breeding ground for new designers and brands. Set apart from the commercial pressures and intense competition of design capitals like Milan, London has an anything-goes attitude that attracts some of the best and brightest. And in various projects there — including the Airbnb-sponsored project “A Place Called Home” centered in Trafalgar Square — top-shelf names can share the spotlight with those just building their portfolios. Here, a few standout rising talents we spotted this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19ldf-rubinstein-1/19ldf-rubinstein-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19ldf-rubinstein-1/19ldf-rubinstein-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19ldf-rubinstein-1/19ldf-rubinstein-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19ldf-rubinstein-1/19ldf-rubinstein-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19ldf-rubinstein-1/19ldf-rubinstein-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19ldf-rubinstein-1/19ldf-rubinstein-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19ldf-rubinstein-1/19ldf-rubinstein-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Rising Talents Spotted at the London Design Festival', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Rubinstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubinstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b32a766-e76b-5944-a280-8108111639e2', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b32a766-e76b-5944-a280-8108111639e2'}, {'abstract': "There's no reason to wait until next year to sport this very wearable 'do (take it from Cara Delevingne and Kate Moss).", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/t-magazine/loose-waves-parted-down-the-middle-the-ultimate-spring-2015-hairstyle.html', 'snippet': "There's no reason to wait until next year to sport this very wearable 'do (take it from Cara Delevingne and Kate Moss).", 'lead_paragraph': 'During New York Fashion Week, we were convinced that braids would be the ultimate spring/summer 2015 beauty look (Donna Karan, Michael Kors, Suno). But today, it’s become clear that long, loose waves parted down the middle will be the way to wear your hair when the weather warms up again next year. (Or, for that matter, right now.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19trend-hair-beddie/19trend-hair-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy