he New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Muddled Message in ISIS’ Latest Agitprop Video', 'kicker': 'The TV Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantlie, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T04:08:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e858dfa-37a8-502d-990a-166f2b085076', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e858dfa-37a8-502d-990a-166f2b085076'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/arts/television/whats-on-tv-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (E!) FASHION POLICE: CELEBRATING JOAN Melissa Rivers leads a 90-minute tribute to her mother, Joan Rivers, above, who died Sept. 4, in which the “Fashion Police” team of Kelly Osbourne, Giuliana Rancic and George Kotsiopoulos narrates behind-the-scenes footage and outtakes from the show and recounts personal stories. The special crowns an all-day marathon, from 7 a.m. to 7 p.m., of “Fashion Police” episodes, including Ms. Rivers’s 80th-birthday celebration and her last stints dissecting the good, the bad and the downright ugly at the MTV Video Music Awards and Primetime Emmys.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s on TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/069469d3-c539-57e1-8954-686dfe3645fc', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/069469d3-c539-57e1-8954-686dfe3645fc'}, {'abstract': 'Prediction markets give much more reliable forecasts than pollsters, as do surveys of what voters expect will happen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/upshot/scotlands-no-vote-a-loss-for-pollsters-and-a-win-for-betting-markets.html', 'snippet': 'Prediction markets give much more reliable forecasts than pollsters, as do surveys of what voters expect will happen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thursday’s Scottish referendum was interesting not just for what it said about Britain, but also for what it said about the state of political forecasting. I’m calling it a loss not only for the pro-independence movement — the “No” campaign won 55.3 percent of the vote — but also for the pollsters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/upshot/20up-predict/20up-predict-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/19/upshot/20up-predict/20up-predict-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19