laimed novels, whether they’re set in the Victorian period (“Tipping the Velvet”) or in the 1940s (“The Night Watch”), the tectonic plates beneath the storytelling are formed by British society — how its attitudes shift, how they don’t. Along class lines. About lesbian sex. Concerning the place of women.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/0921-bks-ANSHAW/0921-bks-ANSHAW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/0921-bks-ANSHAW/0921-bks-ANSHAW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/0921-bks-ANSHAW/0921-bks-ANSHAW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/0921-bks-ANSHAW/0921-bks-ANSHAW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1191, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/0921-bks-ANSHAW/0921-bks-ANSHAW-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/0921-bks-ANSHAW/0921-bks-ANSHAW-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/0921-bks-ANSHAW/0921-bks-ANSHAW-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 