llustrator Maira Kalman sketches her observations from a trip in search of history — and espresso.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/09/19/travel/muse-maira-kalman-lewis-and-clark-trail.html', 'snippet': 'The author and illustrator Maira Kalman sketches her observations from a trip in search of history — and espresso.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The author and illustrator Maira Kalman sketches her observations from a trip in search of history — and espresso.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/travel/21-kalman-promo/21-kalman-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 460, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/travel/21-kalman-promo/21-kalman-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 460}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/travel/21-kalman-promo/21-kalman-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/travel/21-kalman-promo/21-kalman-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 806, 'width': 1052, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/travel/21-kalman-promo/21-kalman-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/travel/21-kalman-promo/21-kalman-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/travel/21-kalman-promo/21-kalman-promo-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Lewis and Clark Trail', 'kicker': 'Muse', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lewis and Clark National Historic Trail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T15:49:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By MAIRA KALMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maira', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KALMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/b7def0b6-d38c-5b26-8e2d-37656784c188', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b7def0b6-d38c-5b26-8e2d-37656784c188'}, {'abstract': 'Ian McEwan, whose novel “The Children Act” is No. 4 on the hardcover fiction list, keeps a tally on his website of academic dissertations and theses discussing his work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Ian McEwan, whose novel “The Children Act” is No. 4 on the hardcover fiction list, keeps a tally on his website of academic dissertations and theses discussing his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ijan Makjuan: The British novelist Ian McEwan — whose latest book, “The Children Act,” hits the hardcover fiction list at No. 4 — keeps a tally on his website of academic dissertations and theses discussing his work. There are dozens of them, as befits a writer of McEwan’s stature, and their titles should give even unversed readers a fair sense of his interests (as well as the interests of literary scholars today): “Pervasive Perspectives: Gender Relationships in the Fiction of Ian McEwan”; “The Child in Time: Postmodern Representations of Childhood in the Novels of Ian McEwan”; “A Mind With a View: Cognitive Science, Neuroscience and Contemporary Literature”; “The Epistemology of Evil in Ian McEwan’s Novels.” Sex, childhood, postmodernism, science, the nature of evil: Yep, that’s \xadMcEwan. (The paper about evil was written by a Serbian philosopher, Zorica Djergovic-Joksimovic, who later expanded her research into a book with the wonderful title “Ijan Makjuan: Polifonija Zla,” or “Ian McEwan: The Polyphony of Evil.”) McEwan recently told The Wall Street Journal that fans sometimes stop him in the street. “But literary fame is quite delightful compared to Hollywood fame or rock ’n’ roll fame or footballer fame,” he said, “because the kind of people who like literary fiction tend to come up blushing or squirming with embarrassment, trying to make themselves disappear but just wanting to tell you before they fade away that your work has meant a great deal to them. And then they vanish before you can even say thank you.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/21mcewan/21mcewan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 456, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/21mcewan/21mcewan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 456, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/21mcewan/21mcewan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/21mcewan/21mcewan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/books/review/21mcewan/21mcewan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T15:51:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41f99c4a-5023-5651-b0a2-1fb8be31d79c', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41f99c4a-5023-5651-b0a2-1fb8be31d79c'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JONATHAN SWIFT: His Life and His World,  by Leo Damrosch. (Yale University, $22.) Swift (1667-1745) distinguished himself as novelist (“Gulliver’s Travels”), satirist (“A Modest Proposal”), essayist, poet and political pamphleteer. Damrosch’s commanding biography aims at sweeping away misconceptions about Swift’s parentage, love life and moral and religious views — many of which were encouraged by Swift himself.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'mai