, 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/137ba33d-b3d9-532d-bdf4-53b7be1af29b', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/137ba33d-b3d9-532d-bdf4-53b7be1af29b'}, {'abstract': 'A new book offers suggestions on how organizations can reinvent themselves, and a first step is putting trust in employees, Tony Schwartz writes in the Life@Work column.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/putting-soul-back-into-business/', 'snippet': 'A new book offers suggestions on how organizations can reinvent themselves, and a first step is putting trust in employees, Tony Schwartz writes in the Life@Work column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most important and inspiring business book I’ve ever read was written by a first-time author from Belgium who self-published his book in March. It’s called “Reinventing Organizations: A Guide to Creating Organizations Inspired by the Next Stage of Human Consciousness,” and the author’s personal story is nearly as inspiring as the content of the book. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/business/dbpix-schwartz-book/dbpix-schwartz-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 336, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/business/dbpix-schwartz-book/dbpix-schwartz-book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 336, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/business/dbpix-schwartz-book/dbpix-schwartz-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/19/business/dbpix-schwartz-book/dbpix-schwartz-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 7