nside The New York Times Book Review: ‘Cosby: His Life and Times’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T16:17:33+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/5b8adb2d-8f36-5693-85aa-4f585989fb94', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/5b8adb2d-8f36-5693-85aa-4f585989fb94'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes both parties to a dispute have right on their side, but they still can’t both win.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/dont-make-me-land-this-plane/', 'snippet': 'Sometimes both parties to a dispute have right on their side, but they still can’t both win.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day, not too long ago, my two daughters, seated in the same room, found themselves at a standoff. One wished to watch a Rainbow Loom video. The other wanted to read in a quiet, video-free room. Things escalated, as these things do; there were available compromises, but it seems one couldn’t be reached. After a period of loud dispute, both were ejected from the room by the authorities, and not without harsh words. Both eventually resumed their activities in other locations. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/us/motherlode-plane/motherlode-plane-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/19/us/motherlode-plane/motherlode-plane-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/us/motherlode-plane/m