 in the Arctic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Exxon Mobil announced on Friday that it was winding down its $700 million exploration in Russia’s Kara Sea, the first major sign that Western sanctions are biting into the company’s ambitious plans to explore for oil and gas in the Arctic Ocean.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exxon Halts Oil Drilling in Waters of Russia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exxon Halts Oil Drilling in Waters of Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exxon Mobil Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rosneft', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T16:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68a76ba8-c2da-5b9c-88f1-e2300b5416ac', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68a76ba8-c2da-5b9c-88f1-e2300b5416ac'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Milan Fashion Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/etro-milan-fashion-week-spring-summer-2015-collection/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Milan Fashion Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the Milan Fashion Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Fashion Week: Etro Spring/Summer 2015', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Etro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T16:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alfredo Piola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alfredo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0b7a3fe-89b2-5681-b52b-6220d9043d6f', 'word_count': 27, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0b7a3fe-89b2-5681-b52b-6220d9043d6f'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Joe discusses Alibaba’s massive IPO and what it will mean for China.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/joe-on-wnycs-money-talking-14/', 'snippet': 'This week, Joe discusses Alibaba’s massive IPO and what it will mean for China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alibaba is the name on every trader’s lips today as shares of the e-commerce giant — which raised nearly $21.8 billion in its initial public offering yesterday — began trading on the New York Stock Exchange. The Hangzhou-based company opened at an astonishing $92.70, making it roughly the size of J.P. Morgan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe on WNYC’s Money Talking', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alibaba Group Holding Ltd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T16:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Dallett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dallett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2beea15-2638-58c6-9241-37680a73d4f8', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2beea15-2638-58c6-9241-37680a73d4f8'}, {'abstract': 'For the cautious majority, the allure of self-rule failed to quell the real advantages of union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/opinion/scotlands-pro-unity-vote.html', 'snippet': 'For the cautious majority, the allure of self-rule failed to quell the real advantages of union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the end, Scottish voters stepped back from breaking with the rest of Britain. The decision to maintain the 307-year-old union was the right one. Scotland already enjoys a significant degree of autonomy, and Britain’s prime minister, David Cameron, has promised more. Besides, separation would have been a plunge into a dangerous unknown. But this will not be the end of the dream of independence — not for the Scots, nor for the Catalans, Flemish, Basques and other people who nurture the dream. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scotland’s Pro-Unity Vote ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scotland’s Pro-Unity Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salmond, Alex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T16:41:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_