 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/058dc139-e0df-5ae7-a204-a9bd02951dd6', 'word_count': 29, 'uri': 'nyt://article/058dc139-e0df-5ae7-a204-a9bd02951dd6'}, {'abstract': 'American conservatives have found a lot to like about our northern neighbor, but they should be careful exactly what they wish for.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/upshot/the-new-conservative-love-affair-with-canada.html', 'snippet': 'American conservatives have found a lot to like about our northern neighbor, but they should be careful exactly what they wish for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may remember your liberal friends threatening to move to Canada after George W. Bush was re-elected. But something surprising has happened in the last few years: Conservatives have fallen in love with Canada. The conservative journalist John Fund wrote in National Review this month that Canada is becoming “more American than America.” That’s the same John Fund who wrote a 1995 Wall Street Journal staff editorial calling Canada “an honorary member of the third world.” A lot can change in two decades.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/upshot/21up-canada/21up-canada-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/upshot/21up-canada/21up-canada-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/upshot/21up-canada/21up-canada-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/upshot/21up-canada/21up-canada-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1678, 'width': 1678, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/upshot/21up-canada/21up-canada-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/upshot/21up-canada/21up-canada-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/upshot/21up-canada/21up-canada-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Conservative Love Affair With Canada', 'kicker': 'Opposites Attract', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Conservatives Fall in Love With Canada', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barro, Josh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fund, John H', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T17:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Barro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a71fc970-88df-5a77-8c68-365c32332973', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a71fc970-88df-5a77-8c68-365c32332973'}, {'abstract': 'Visitors at Jane Austen’s House Museum in Chawton, Hampshire, can see the 11 booklets that formed “The Watsons,” a novel Austen abandoned, as well as a needle case and other domestic tools belonging to the writer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/rare-jane-austen-manuscript-goes-on-exhibit/', 'snippet': 'Visitors at Jane Austen’s House Museum in Chawton, Hampshire, can see the 11 booklets that formed “The Watsons,” a novel Austen abandoned, as well as a needle case and other domestic tools belonging to the writer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Jane Austen news just keeps coming.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rare Jane Austen Manuscript Goes on Exhibit', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rare Austen Manuscript Goes on Display', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Manuscripts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Jane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Austen's, Jane, House Museum (Chawton, England)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bodleian Libraries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hampshire (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T17:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acad2520-1e9c-55f9-9dbf-e677704204c3', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acad2520-1e9c-55f9-9dbf-e677704204c3'}, {'abstract': 'Employers have the option of letting participants carry over as much as $500 to the next plan year, rather than forfeit it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/your-money/rule-changes-increase-flexibility-in-pretax-health-care-accounts.html', 'snippet': 'Employers have the option of letting participants carry over as much as $500 to the next plan year, rather than forfeit it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS open enrollment season approaches for those with workplace health benefits, employees may want to take a fresh look at health care flexible spending accounts, if their employers offer them, because the rules for the accounts have changed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rule Changes Increase Flexibility in Pretax Health Care Accounts', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rule Changes Increase Flexibility in Pretax Health Care Accounts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T17:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/051a82f6-9745-5d29-9805-d9af44f1f5a8', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/051a82f6-9745-5d29-9805-d9af44f1f5a8'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Bloomberg, a mayor turned U.N. climate envoy, explains what cities can do to blunt climate change and its impacts.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/michael-bloomberg-now-a-u-n-climate-envoy-presses-the-case-for-urban-action/', 'snippet': 'Michael Bloomberg, a mayor turned U.N. climate envoy, explains what cities can do to blunt climate change and its impacts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently had a chance to ask former New York City Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg about the fresh push he’s making for urban action to blunt climate impacts and greenhouse gas emissions as the new United Nations Special Envoy for Cities and Climate Change. He’ll be a very busy man next week, as the city hosts the People’s Climate March, a U.N. “summit” on climate change and Climate Week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/nyregion/20cityroom-poll/20cityroom-poll-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/11/21/nyregion/20cityroom-poll/20cityroom-poll-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/nyregion/20cityroom-poll/20cityroom-poll-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/nyregion/20cityroom-poll/20cityroom-poll-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/nyregion/20cityroom-poll/20cityroom-poll-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/11/21/nyregion/20cityroom-poll/20cityroom-poll-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/11/21/nyreg