” is one of the latest efforts to create a show that will appeal to an English-speaking Hispanic audience and a wider viewership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance, the protagonist of “Jane the Virgin” bears little resemblance to any other character on television, never mind any viewer.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21JANE2/21JANE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21JANE2/21JANE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21JANE2/21JANE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21JANE2/21JANE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1270, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21JANE2/21JANE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21JANE2/21JANE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21JANE2/21JANE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Jane the Virgin’ Aims Beyond Its Latin Ethnicity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Human Types, Not Stereotypes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Jane the Virgin (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CW Television Network', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T19:21:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8fac7c9-02d9-577b-85b7-91fbf44f7815', 'word_count': 1330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8fac7c9-02d9-577b-85b7-91fbf44f7815'}, {'abstract': 'Pace University’s second season of Voce: Rising Opera Stars in Recital opens with the soprano Julia Bullock and the tenor Joseph Kaiser', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/arts/music/voce-opera-recital-returns-to-pace.html', 'snippet': 'Pace University’s second season of Voce: Rising Opera Stars in Recital opens with the soprano Julia Bullock and the tenor Joseph Kaiser', 'lead_paragraph': 'The song recital, which requires attention and patience from both performers and audiences, is perpetually an endangered species. (Full-scale opera, with its costumes and grandeur, comes across as rather more fun.) But since they value intimacy, textual specificity and communicative ability, recitals remain crucial proving grounds for young artists. Voce: Rising Opera Stars in Recital, a series at Pace University started last year by the veteran impresario Matthew Epstein, has already been a valuable addition to the vocal scene. This season’s first concert, on Sunday, features the potent combination of the soprano Julia Bullock, a star at the Juilliard School in recent productions of Massenet’s “Cendrillon” and Janacek’s “The Cunning Little Vixen,” and the tenor Joseph Kaiser, over the past few years a Met stalwart in Mozart, Handel and Britten. (3 p.m., Schimmel Center for the Arts, 3 Spruce Street, between Park Row and Gold Street, Lower Manhattan, 212-346-1715, schimmel.pace.edu.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GUIDE4/21GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GUIDE4/21GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1536}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GUIDE4/21GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 400, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GUIDE4/21GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GUIDE4/21GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GUIDE4/21GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/arts/21GUIDE4/21GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Proving Ground For Young Stars', 'kicker': 'Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_