militants operating in Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/world/middleeast/bomb-kills-2-lebanese-soliders-near-border-with-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The attack on a Lebanese Army convoy took place near the town of Arsal, the scene of battles that erupted last month between the army and militants operating in Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Two Lebanese Army soldiers were killed and two were wounded on Friday when their convoy was hit by a roadside bomb outside the town of Arsal, near the border with Syria. The town was the scene of battles that erupted last month between the army and militants from the group Islamic State and the Nusra Front, which is affiliated with Al Qaeda.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bomb Kills 2 Lebanese Soldiers Near Border With Syria', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lebanon: 2 Soldiers Killed Near Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Nusra Front', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T19:35:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/451297fd-321d-5c2a-9422-6d52b6c2cf06', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/451297fd-321d-5c2a-9422-6d52b6c2cf06'}, {'abstract': 'In a conciliatory gesture after years of tensions, Prime Minister Shinzo Abe of Japan sent a letter to President Park Geun-hye of South Korea proposing the meeting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/world/asia/japans-premier-seeks-summit-meeting-with-south-korean-president.html', 'snippet': 'In a conciliatory gesture after years of tensions, Prime Minister Shinzo Abe of Japan sent a letter to President Park Geun-hye of South Korea proposing the meeting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The office of President Park Geun-hye said on Friday that Prime Minister Shinzo Abe of Japan had sent a letter proposing a summit meeting, a conciliatory gesture after years of tensions between America’s most important allies in Northeast Asia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s Premier Seeks Summit Meeting With South Korean President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea: Japan Proposes a Meeting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Geun-hye', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T19:39:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bac0f844-5ad5-5ddc-96e1-38058666a710', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bac0f844-5ad5-5ddc-96e1-38058666a710'}, {'abstract': 'You’re all bums on welfare.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/john-boehners-theory-of-the-leisure-class/', 'snippet': 'You’re all bums on welfare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And, I’m back — I’ve been in a grueling battle against deadlines, which is not quite over, so blogging may remain scarce for a while longer. But I’m sticking my toe in for the moment — and whaddya know, oops, he did it again. John Boehner says that unemployed Americans are pretty clearly malingerers, bums on welfare who have decided that they don’t feel like working:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John Boehner’s Theory of the Leisure Class', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T19:44:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d65e2905-4e9c-562f-89a7-643601225602', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d65e2905-4e9c-562f-89a7-643601225602'}, {'abstract': 'Practice and careful measurement will assure that you always have the pastry ready for a tart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/24/dining/mastering-the-pastry-shell-dough.html', 'snippet': 'Practice and careful measurement will assure that you always have the pastry ready for a tart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If I have a sweet pastry shell in the freezer, I know I’m ready to entertain. A dinner party requires a dessert, and what is more pleasing than a beautiful fruit or lemon tart?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/