name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6225e275-0134-5453-981b-b4515e58b571', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6225e275-0134-5453-981b-b4515e58b571'}, {'abstract': 'The radiant models exuded youthful sophistication on this morning’s runway in Milan.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/blumarine-milan-fashion-week-how-to-get-the-fresh-faced-glow/', 'snippet': 'The radiant models exuded youthful sophistication on this morning’s runway in Milan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This morning in Milan, fresh-faced models stepped into Blumarine’s spring 2015 collection of garden-party frocks, skirts and coats (no pants in sight!). Sure, they had just gotten a good night’s sleep. But the makeup artist Tom Pecheux helped enhance their bright and even complexions with a mix of skin-care products, foundation, concealer, blush and bronzer. “The inspiration is youth,” he said, explaining that he aimed to create the “superfresh and young girl that acts like a woman.” On the runway, models’ eyes were wide and bright thanks to a bit of shimmer on the inside corner of the eye, some gloss on the brushed eyebrows and the absence of dark mascara. The finishing touch was the sexy and easy-to-pull-off-in-real-life hairstyle that seems to be dominating runways this season: relaxed waves, parted down the middle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19beauty-blumarine-col/19beauty-blumarine-col-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19beauty-blumarine-col/19beauty-blumarine-col-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19beauty-blumarine-col/19beauty-blumarine-col-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19beauty-blumarine-col/19beauty-blumarine-col-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19beauty-blumarine-col/19beauty-blumarine-col-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19beauty-blumarine-col/19beauty-blumarine-col-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19beauty-blumarine-col/19beauty-blumarine-col-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Get the Fresh-Faced Glow at Blumarine', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T19:50:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chiara Da Col', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chiara', 'middlename': 'Da', 'lastname': 'Col', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43d4bd4a-cc46-5976-9ab9-40d90a0962d1', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43d4bd4a-cc46-5976-9ab9-40d90a0962d1'}, {'abstract': 'A partnership between Expedia and HomeAway will offer more than 100,000 home rentals.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/expedia-and-homeaway-expand-rental-partnership/', 'snippet': 'A partnership between Expedia and HomeAway will offer more than 100,000 home rentals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Expedia and HomeAway have decided to expand a pilot partnership begun last year offering HomeAway listings through Expedia’s website.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Expedia and HomeAway Expand Rental Partnership', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Booking.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Expedia Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hilton Worldwide Holdings Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HomeAway Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TripAdvisor.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T19:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c3b4cb4-3257-5841-91f9-30ca344f3d45', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c3b4cb4-3257-5841-91f9-30ca344f3d45'}, {'abstract': 'Several days after the storm, the American military, the State Department and the Mexican authorities continued to airlift stranded tourists from the Cabo San Lucas area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/world/americas/us-and-mexico-aid-tourists-stranded-after-hurricane-odile.html', 'snippet': 'Several days after the storm, the American military, the State Department and the Mexican authorities continued to airlift stranded tourists from the Cabo San Lucas area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — Several days after a powerful hurricane hit one of Mexico’s most popular Pacific resorts, the American military, the State Department and the Mexican authorities continued to airlift stranded tourists from an area afflicted by looting and still lacking electricity and potable water.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. and Mexico Aid Tourists Stranded After Hurricane Odile', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Stranded Tourists Evacuated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Archibold, Randal C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cabo San Lucas (Mexico)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T19:55:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27c3b7cf-79c8-52e8-a7c1-9733821790f6', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27c3b7cf-79c8-52e8-a7c1-9733821790f6'}, {'abstract': 'Apple not of my eye.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/phoney-baloney-personal-and-trivial/', 'snippet': 'Apple not of my eye.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just to say: What is it with the huge lines waiting for the new iPhone? Yes, smartphones are quite useful and sometimes even fun; I’m not a heavy app user, but I’m still on the thing many times a day. But even if the iPhone 6 has nifty new features, how can you get so excited over something that is, when all is said and done, an incremental change?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phoney Baloney (Personal and Trivial)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T19:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7030b116-38e4-5673-a16f-5a93308b1e80', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7030b116-38e4-5673-a16f-5a93308b1e80'}, {'abstract': 'A joint venture between the Chinese company and Broadway Worldwide aims to screen between two and four shows a year, including in the Asian market.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/chinese-media-company-signs-on-to-broadcast-broadway-shows/', 'snippet': 'A joint venture between the Chinese company and Broadway Worldwide aims to screen between two and four shows a year, including in the Asian market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Broadway has been slow to embrace the high-definition broadcasts increasingly beamed out by performing arts organizations around the world. A new venture hopes to speed that up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Media Company Signs On To Broadcast Broadway Shows', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T19:58:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lorne Manly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lorne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/591d707d-706f-583a-9aac-cd702cd8cc19', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/591d707d-706f-583a-9aac-cd702cd8cc19'}, {'abstract': 'In the same colors and patterns as the clothes, silk scarves completed the label’s breezy spring 2015 collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/19/missoni-spring-2015-milan-summery-turbans/', 'snippet': 'In the same colors and patterns as the clothes, silk scarves completed the label’s breezy spring 2015 collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were swaths and swaths of silk on Missoni’s spring 2015 runway — even on the models’ heads, where hair was wrapped up in an array of silk scarves printed with the same colors and patterns as the clothes. The turbans lent an extra summery feel to the light, breezy collection.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19do-missoni-gilchrist/19do-missoni-gilchrist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/19/t-magazine/19do-missoni-gilchrist/19do-missoni-gilchrist-articleLar