//article/2da159d3-e455-50ea-833f-176cfcc18a61'}, {'abstract': 'A valuable muscle car collection seized by the United States Marshals Service was auctioned in a few-frills affair in Lodi, N.J., netting about $2.5 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/automobiles/seized-and-sold-the-marshal-holds-a-muscle-car-auction.html', 'snippet': 'A valuable muscle car collection seized by the United States Marshals Service was auctioned in a few-frills affair in Lodi, N.J., netting about $2.5 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LODI, N.J. — The first car offered was a 1970 Ford Mustang, a rare 21,000-mile Boss 429 model in Grabber Green. Not that anyone could tell the color — the lighting, a splotchy mess of glare and shadow, was that bad. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seized and Sold: The Marshal Holds a Muscle Car Auction ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seized and Sold: The Marshal Holds a Muscle Car Auction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marshals Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-19T21:32:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathan Laliberte', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Laliberte', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43ba49e6-0e07-5a04-b13e-75cfe63e8478', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43ba49e6-0e07-5a04-b13e-75cfe63e8478'}, {'abstract': 'An analysis by the Union of Concerned Scientists showed that, for the majority of the country, electric vehicles are cleaner than even the most efficient hybrids.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/automobiles/coal-fades-so-electrics-get-cleaner.html', 'snippet': 'An analysis by the Union of Concerned Scientists showed that, for the majority of the country, electric vehicles are cleaner than even the most efficient hybrids.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost as soon as modern mass-market electric vehicles became available, skeptics began asking if they actually delivered an environmental benefit. After all, they argued, charging batteries from a generating plant that burns fossil fuels simply relocates the greenhouse gas emissions to someone else’s neighborhood.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/automobiles/subELECTRIC/subELECTRIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/automobiles/subELECTRIC/subELECTRIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/automobiles/subELECTRIC/subELECTRIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 671, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/automobiles/subELECTRIC/subELECTRIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 671, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail