_id': 'nyt://article/d38e73e9-0f97-57ab-a2ef-a178c598d401', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d38e73e9-0f97-57ab-a2ef-a178c598d401'}, {'abstract': 'To account for concerns raised by small brewers, cheese producers and others, the agency revised provisions for water testing, manure, compost and spent grains.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/business/fda-plans-to-revise-food-safety-rules.html', 'snippet': 'To account for concerns raised by small brewers, cheese producers and others, the agency revised provisions for water testing, manure, compost and spent grains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration on Friday proposed changes to new rules that will govern food safety in the United States. In an effort to account for concerns raised by small brewers, artisanal cheese producers and other food producers, the agency revised provisions for water testing, as well as those on manure, compost and spent grains. Brewers had objected to rules requiring them to write food safety plans for the spent grain they sell as animal feed. The changes will be open to public comment for 75 days; final rules are to be issued in 2015. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Plans to Revise Food Safety Rules', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Plans To Revise Food Safety Rules ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T00:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlena