growth that is “job-rich and inclusive” is possible in theory; politically, not so much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unhappy economies, it turns out, are all unhappy in the same way. A recent report on job markets globally showed that too few jobs are being created worldwide, and even fewer good jobs are. Wages are flat or falling in all major economies as corporate profits claim an increasing share of productivity gains. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Big Unhappy Economy ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Big Unhappy Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T00:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa5548e6-6e2c-5155-a865-1f51263f5490', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa5548e6-6e2c-5155-a865-1f51263f5490'}, {'abstract': 'A decision to go forward with a controversial production is a win for the principle of artistic freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/opinion/the-death-of-klinghoffer-must-go-on.html', 'snippet': 'A decision to go forward with a controversial production is a win for the principle of artistic freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'True to its artistic mission, the Metropolitan Opera remains firmly committed to presenting “The Death of Klinghoffer,” the widely praised opera that has drawn the scorn of protesters who plan to demonstrate outside the Met’s season opening on Monday at Lincoln Center. The Met’s board of directors and Peter Gelb, its general manager, are entirely correct in insisting the opera must proceed as planned next month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Met Opera Stands Firm', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Met Opera Stands Firm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, John (1947- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelb, Peter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinghoffer, Leon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Death of Klinghoffer (Opera)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T00:34:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d5cbb80-ad5e-5118-a2be-2e6547a5a964', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d5cbb80-ad5e-5118-a2be-2e6547a5a964'}, {'abstract': 'The surfing community in this Sandy-battered enclave is flourishing, happy with the upside of another hurricane season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/opinion/hurricane-watch-in-the-rockaways.html', 'snippet': 'The surfing community in this Sandy-battered enclave is flourishing, happy with the upside of another hurricane season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Midway through the hurricane season, an interesting breed of aquatic New Yorkers — surfers — are religiously scrolling apps for the most promising waves. They could not resist dropping by Rockaway Beach this week to ride the remnants of Hurricane Edouard pounding the Atlantic beachfront of Queens. “We’re rooting for Edouard — up to a point,” said Conrad Karl, an obsessive surfer who is happy to frolic at a hurricane’s farther edges.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hurricane Watch in the Rockaways', 'kicker': 'Editorial Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hurricane Watch in the Rockaways', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surfing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockaway Beach (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T00:38:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7b68943-6b8a-5588-a1c4-2cee72ef6efc', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7b68943-6b8a-5588-a1c4-2cee72ef6efc'}, {'abstract': 'A complaint alleges that the agency failed to stop workplace harassment and sexual abuse and retaliated against women who reported it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/us/