}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T02:43:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5a7a5a7-90b8-5d7b-91ba-9fc2f656ecf3', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5a7a5a7-90b8-5d7b-91ba-9fc2f656ecf3'}, {'abstract': 'Subtitled Oyster Bar & Grill, Ocean House, in Croton-on-Hudson, has offerings including a variety of oysters and the latest catch, served in a small, spare space reminiscent of the New England shore.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/nyregion/a-review-of-ocean-house-in-croton-on-hudson.html', 'snippet': 'Subtitled Oyster Bar & Grill, Ocean House, in Croton-on-Hudson, has offerings including a variety of oysters and the latest catch, served in a small, spare space reminiscent of the New England shore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite its out-of-the-way location and its history as a funky diner, the Ocean House restaurant has transformed its deficits, and without nets and ships’ wheels. Colonial-blue trim suggests an old fisherman’s cottage on a briny New England shore. But it’s the Hudson River that runs beyond the front door of Ocean House in Croton-on-Hudson. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/nyregion/21DINEWE2/21DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/nyregion/21DINEWE2/21DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty