t': 'Initially suspended for the first half against No. 22 Clemson, the Heisman-winning quarterback will now sit the entire game for making an obscene comment in the student union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Florida State reversed course late Friday, suspending quarterback Jameis Winston for the whole game, instead of the first half, against No. 22 Clemson on Saturday night.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/sports/20jameis/20jameis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/sports/20jameis/20jameis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/sports/20jameis/20jameis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/sports/20jameis/20jameis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/sports/20jameis/20jameis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/sports/20jameis/20jameis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/sports/20jameis/20jameis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jameis Winston Out for Entire Game as Florida State Extends Ban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winston Out for Game as F.S.U. Extends Ban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tracy, Marc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winston, Jameis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T04:12:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1b7cca4-6922-51d5-994a-d9e82d992a38', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1b7cca4-6922-51d5-994a-d9e82d992a38'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7 P.M. (HBO) THE SECRET LIFE OF WALTER MITTY (2013) Ben Stiller, who also directed this adaptation of the James Thurber short story, stars as Walter, a dutiful drone in the photography department of Life magazine who finds himself on a caper far beyond his wildest imagination when the negative for the publication’s final print edition goes missing. Kristen Wiig plays the crinkly-nosed co-worker on whom Walter has a crush; Adam Scott is the leader of the new tech-jerk bosses who have Walter’s job on the line. And Sean Penn is the mysterious photographer behind Walter’s travels to Iceland, Afghanistan and other stunning far-off places. “Though it is a celebration of modesty, there is also quite a lot of vanity in ‘The Secret Life of Walter Mitty,’\xa0” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. There is also a contradiction: “An ordinary fellow should not have to be quite so special to win our admiration. And this version of Walter Mitty undermines some of the democratic whimsy that has made his story such an appealing and durable modern myth. He used to be one of us: a self-deluded dreamer charmed by his unruly creative powers, a willing prisoner of his appetite for escapism. But now our identification gives way to envy, and he is another one of those enchanted people the rest of us can only dream of becoming.” The movie is followed at 9 by “On the Run Tour: Beyoncé and Jay Z,” a concert special filmed on Sept. 12 and 13 at the Stade de France, near Paris, featuring performances of more than 40 songs during the couple’s only stop outside North America on the tour.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/948b1c3f-094a-56d2-b982-8536ad0c5acd', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/948b1c3f-094a-56d2-b982-8536ad0c5acd'}, {'abstract': 'Tomas Maier for Bottega Veneta, maker of those very subtle, extremely expensive woven purses, shows at 9 a.m.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/milan-fashion-week-morning-report-day-4/', 'snippet': 'Tomas Maier for Bottega Veneta, maker of those very subtle, extremely expensive woven purses, shows at 9 a.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To put things in sports terms (sort of) in case you clicked here by mistake: Today the two opposing teams of Italian fashion — colorful flamboyance and understated tailoring — clash helmets on the gridiron.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Fashion Week Morning Report, Day 4', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cavalli, Roberto', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maier, Tomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Armani, Giorgio, SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bottega Veneta', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jil Sander AG', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T05:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9758adc0-5e5b-5ad5-ad2d-603562d407e0', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9758adc0-5e5b-5ad5-ad2d-603562d407e0'}, {'abstract': 'After a Texas man with a knife made it into the entrance of the first family’s residence, the Secret Service said there would be increased patrols and surveillance while the episode was scrutinized.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/us/politics/intruder-white-house.html', 'snippet': 'After a Texas man with a knife made it into the entrance of the first family’s residence, the Secret Service said there would be increased patrols and surveillance while the episode was scrutinized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The director of the Secret Service ordered an internal review of its security procedures around the White House after a man armed with a knife who jumped the fence at 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue on Friday night managed to make his way through the front door of President Obama’s home before being stopped, officials said Saturday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breach Prompts Review of White House Security', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Review Ordered of White House Security', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Secret Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House Building (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenny, Steve', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, Omar J (1972- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T05:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and Steve Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6881d509-01b6-5cf0-b49e-388e666a9c00', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6881d509-01b6-5cf0-b49e-388e666a9c00'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on September 20, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/pageoneplus/corrections-september-20-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on September 20, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: September 20, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T05:43:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/829eba0f-e576-5745-9500-997853788137', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/829eba0f-e576-5745-9500-997853788137'}, {'abstract': 'Omar J. Gonzalez, 42, of Copperas Cove, Tex., was arrested after jumping the White House fence and making it through the North Portico doors on Friday night, the Secret Service said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/us/politics/intruder-gets-through-white-house-doors-before-arrest.html', 'snippet': 'Omar J. Gonzalez, 42, of Copperas Cove, Tex., was arrested after jumping the White House fence and making it through the North Portico doors on Friday night, the Secret Service said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Texas man who jumped the White House fence made it through the North Portico doors on Friday night before being apprehended, the Secret Service said. The intruder, Omar J. Gonzalez, 42, of Copperas Cove, Tex., was arrested and taken to George Washington University Hospital after complaining of chest pains, said Ed Donovan, a Secret Service spokesman. None of the Obamas were home when the security breach occurred, about 7:20 p.m., but White House staff members were evacuated as a precaution, Mr. Donovan said. Mr. Gonzalez was not armed, he added, and the incident was being reviewed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intruder Gets Through White House Doors Before Arrest', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Intruder Gets to White House Doors Before Arrest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenny, Steve', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House Building (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, Omar J (1972- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Secret Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T08:23:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/85f6bd92-555d-51ba-8972-62294a023cdb', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85f6bd92-555d-51ba-8972-62294a023cdb'}, {'abstract': 'The reconstituted Replacements kicked up a solid ruckus Friday night, as a fervent crowd took its non-hit oldies to heart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/arts/music/the-replacements-play-at-forest-hills-stadium.html', 'snippet': 'The reconstituted Replacements kicked up a solid ruckus Friday night, as a fervent crowd took its non-hit oldies to heart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Better late than never, in a way. More than 20 years after the Replacements initially broke up, leaving behind a fervent cult following but disappointing album sales, the reconstituted band had a stadium singing along on Friday night. Yes, Forest Hills Stadium is a fairly small stadium. But the crowd’s voices were loud through both verses and choruses, song after song.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i