eft Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muggings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T15:25:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dba69661-4c75-5b39-aacb-d7e100c52194', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dba69661-4c75-5b39-aacb-d7e100c52194'}, {'abstract': 'For spring 2015, designers make a statement with the humble knot.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/milan-fashion-week-spring-2015-twists-and-ties-of-fabric-liven-up-simple-silhouettes/', 'snippet': 'For spring 2015, designers make a statement with the humble knot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trending on spring 2015 runways: knotted garments. We saw it first in New York at The Row, where Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen turned sleek silhouettes into interesting shapes with the addition of knots or crossed lengths of fabric in either the front or the back of dresses and shirts. Then in Milan, the Sportmax collection was all about tied-up skirts, trousers and sarong-like dresses. And again today in Milan, almost all the looks in Bottega Veneta’s laid-back, luxurious collection — loose trenches and cashmere leggings — were cinched at the waist. The styling was at its best in its most exaggerated form: a hooded sweatshirt with an oversize knot in the middle that looked almost like a corsage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/20/t-magazine/20knots_trendnew/20knots_trendnew-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/20/t-magazine/20knots_trendnew/20knots_trendnew-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 512}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/20/t-magazine/20knots_trendnew/20knots_trendnew-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 874, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/20/t-magazine/20knots_trendnew/20knots_trendnew-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1748, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/20/t-magazine/20knots_trendnew/20knots_trendnew-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/20/t-magazine/20knots_trendnew/20knots_trendnew-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/20/t-magazine/20knots_trendnew/20knots_trendnew-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Twists and Ties of Fabric Liven Up Simple Silhouettes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None