o a lot more to alert readers about conflicts of interests of sources used by the paper.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/public-editor/new-york-times-public-editor-on-conflicts-of-interest.html', 'snippet': 'The Times could do a lot more to alert readers about conflicts of interests of sources used by the paper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE article ran above the fold on the front page early this month, a Times investigation into the influence of foreign money within American research organizations.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hidden Interests, Closer to Home', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hidden Interests, Closer to Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Margaret M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Editor (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Think Tanks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transparify', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Belfer Center for Science and International Affairs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaffer, Brenda', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbett, Philip B', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chan, Sewell', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keane, John M', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T18:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e7acbcc-d630-591d-8c3d-7fb3697d6df6', 'word_count': 1027, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e7acbcc-d630-591d-8c3d-7fb3697d6df6'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s why the no vote in Scotland was a good thing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/opinion/sunday/thomas-l-friedman-three-cheers-for-pluralism-over-separatism.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s why the no vote in Scotland was a good thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — THIS was an interesting week to visit Britain and Spain — first to watch the Scottish separatists push for independence and then to watch Basque and Catalan separatists watching (with disappointment) the outcome of the vote. One reaction: I’m glad a majority of Scots rejected independence. Had they not, it would have clipped the wing of America’s most important wingman in the world: Britain. Another reaction: God bless America. We have many sources of strength, but today our greatest asset is our pluralism — our “E pluribus unum” — that out of many we’ve made one nation, with all the benefits that come from mixing cultures and all the strengths that come from being able to act together. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'super