', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/472999d4-a4fb-5d9a-bb44-704aaa5bb849', 'word_count': 1224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/472999d4-a4fb-5d9a-bb44-704aaa5bb849'}, {'abstract': 'The opposition has long demanded the release of the official, Iván Simonovis, who was jailed in connection with the killing of protesters in 2002, but the Supreme Court said that he would be returned to jail once his health improved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/world/americas/venezuela-simonovis-house-arrest.html', 'snippet': 'The opposition has long demanded the release of the official, Iván Simonovis, who was jailed in connection with the killing of protesters in 2002, but the Supreme Court said that he would be returned to jail once his health improved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — A jailed former police official whose nearly decade-long stay in prison has become a rallying cry for the political opposition was moved to house arrest, his wife and court officials announced on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela Moves Jailed Former Police Official to House Arrest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela Moves Jailed Former Police Official to House Arrest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simonovis, Ivan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T19:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2e0f588-6803-5ec8-86c6-065a80b53f19', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2e0f588-6803-5ec8-86c6-065a80b53f19'}, {'abstract': 'Parker Conrad’s start-up, which helps small businesses navigate employee benefits, has shown phenomenal growth. Yet he is anything but sure of its success.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/business/zenefits-leader-is-rattling-an-industry-so-why-is-he-stressed-out.html', 'snippet': 'Parker Conrad’s start-up, which helps small businesses navigate employee benefits, has shown phenomenal growth. Yet he is anything but sure of its success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parker Conrad’s start-up, Zenefits, is thought to be one of the fastest-growing companies in recent Silicon Valley history, and his investors and associates describe him as an uncommonly talented software visionary. But lately, Mr. Conrad often finds himself petrified, his days a series of white-knuckled attempts to escape the clutches of sudden, inadvertent failure. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-ZENEFITS/21-ZENEFITS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1295, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-ZENEFITS/21-ZENEFITS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1295}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-ZENEFITS/21-ZENEFITS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 475, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-ZENEFITS/21-ZENEFITS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1919, 'width': 889, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-ZENEFITS/21-ZENEFITS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-ZENEFITS/21-ZENEFITS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-ZENEFITS/21-ZENEFITS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Zenefits’ Leader Is Rattling an Industry, So Why Is He Stressed Out?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Guy Is Rattling an $18 Billion Industry by Giving People What They Want. So Why Is He Stressed Out?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manjoo, Farhad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zenefits Insurance Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conrad, Parker', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Employee Fringe Benefits', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T19:17:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farhad Manjoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farhad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manjoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/082e591e-0656-5417-843f-bdfc3e1df1b8', 'word_count': 2776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/082e591e-0656-5417-843f-bdfc3e1df1b8'}, {'abstract': 'Attributing unemployment to benefits that don’t exist anymore.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/20/return-of-the-bums-on-welfare/', 'snippet': 'Attributing unemployment to benefits that don’t exist anymore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thinking some more about John Boehner’s resurrection of the notion that we’re suffering weak job growth because people are living the good life on government benefits, and don’t want to work. It has long seemed to me that the issue of unemployment benefits is where the debate over economic policy in a depression reaches its purest essence. If you’r on the right, you believe — you more or less have to believe — that unemployment benefits hurt job creation, because you’re “paying people not to work.” To admit that depression conditions are different, that the economy is suffering from an overall lack of demand and that putting money into the pockets of people likely to spend it would increase employment, would mean admitting that the free market sometimes fails badly. And of course disdain for the unemployed helps a lot if you want to oppose any kind of aid for the unfortunate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Return of the Bums on Welfare', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T19:18:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43f57615-04d7-5638-9f16-67f21865ef35', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43f57615-04d7-5638-9f16-67f21865ef35'}, {'abstract': 'The independence movement in Scotland was another sign of widespread dissatisfaction with an established order that has failed to deliver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/upshot/in-scotland-and-beyond-a-crisis-of-faith-in-the-global-elite.html', 'snippet': 'The independence movement in Scotland was another sign of widespread dissatisfaction with an established order that has failed to deliver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Scotland this week, a measure to become an independent country and end the United Kingdom as we know it failed, but it would have succeeded with a swing of just 5 percent of the vote. Earlier in the week, a right-wing anti-immigration party in Sweden claimed its largest-ever share of parliamentary votes. And in the United States, new census data released this week showed that middle-income American families made 8 percent less last year, adjusted for inflation, than they did in 2007.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-UP-ELITE3SUB/21-UP-ELITE3SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-UP-ELITE3SUB/21-UP-ELITE3SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-UP-ELITE3SUB/21-UP-ELITE3SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-UP-ELITE3SUB/21-UP-ELITE3SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1156, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-UP-ELITE3SUB/21-UP-ELITE3SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-UP-ELITE3SUB/21-UP-ELITE3SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-UP-ELITE3SUB/21-UP-ELITE3SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Scotland and Beyond, a Crisis of Faith in the Global Elite', 'kicker': 'Pulse of the People', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Crisis of Faith in the Global Elite', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irwin, Neil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Parliament', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T19:20:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Irwin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Irwin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16958c8a-0a61-5349-8229-4cf230563ecc', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16958c8a-0a61-5349-8229-4cf230563ecc'}, {'abstract': 'The Museum of Modern Art will present what curators say is the earliest extant footage of a feature film with a black cast, featuring the vaudeville star Bert Williams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/nyregion/coming-soon-a-century-late-a-black-film-gem.html', 'snippet': 'The Museum of Modern Art will present what curators say is the earliest extant footage of a feature film with a black cast, featuring the vaudeville star Bert Williams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, the seven reels from 1913 lay unexamined in the film archives of the Museum of Modern Art. Now, after years of research, a historic find has emerged: what MoMA curators say is the earliest surviving footage for a feature film with a black cast. It is a rare visual depiction of middle-class black characters from an era when lynchings and stereotyped black images were commonplace. What’s more, the material features Bert Williams, the first black superstar on Broadway. Williams appears in blackface in the untitled silent film along with a roster of actors from the sparsely documented community of black performers in Harlem on the cusp of the Harlem Renaissance. Remarkably, the reels also capture behind-the-scenes interactions between these performers and the directors. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/nyregion/WILLIAMS/WILLIAMS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/nyregion/WILLIAMS/WILLIAMS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/nyregion/WILLIAMS/WILLIAMS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/nyregion/WILLIAMS/WILLIAMS-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/nyregion/WILLIAMS/WILLIAMS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/nyregion/WILLIAMS/WILLIAMS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/nyregion/WILLIAMS/WILLIAMS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming Soon, a Century Late: A Black Film Gem', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coming Soon, a Century Late: A Black Film Gem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Felicia R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Bert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T19:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed32d3c2-70d5-5b0a-b529-dafba8c2426d', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed32d3c2-70d5-5b0a-b529-dafba8c2426d'}, {'abstract': 'The annual cost of a checking account can range from zero to more than $700, according to a WalletHub survey. The biggest fees may fall on those who overdraw their accounts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/your-money/in-checking-accounts-the-less-you-have-the-more-you-may-pay.html', 'snippet': 'The annual cost of a checking account can range from zero to more than $700, according to a WalletHub survey. The biggest fees may fall on those who overdraw their accounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Financial complexity doesn’t happen only on Wall Street. Even a basic checking account is often no longer simple, because account rules and fees can vary widely — so widely, in fact, that the annual cost can range from zero to more than $700, according to the 2014 survey of checking account costs by WalletHub, a consumer finance information and social networking site. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Checking Accounts, the Less You Have, the More You May Pay', 'kicker': 'Datapoints', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Less You Have, the More You Pay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Checks and Checking Accounts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-20T19:23:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Bernasek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernasek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0ed890f-82d4-533d-8cc3-fdd07509cf1c', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0ed890f-82d4-533d-8cc3-fdd07509cf1c'}, {'abstract': 'An ambitious plan to create a better-informed marketplace for education doesn’t take into account how public universities are funded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/upshot/why-federal-college-ratings-wont-rein-in-tuition.html', 'snippet': 'An ambitious plan to create a better-informed marketplace for education doesn’t take into account how public universities are funded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'College costs have been rising for decades. Slowing — or even better, reversing — that trend would get more people into college and help reduce student debt. The Obama administration is working on an ambitious plan intended to rein in college costs, and it deserves credit for tackling this tough job.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-VIEW/21-VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/business/21-VIEW/21-VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo'