port-day-5-marni-salvatore-ferragamo-dolce-gabbana/', 'snippet': 'As Milan winds down, there still will be plenty of action today at Marni, Salvatore Ferragamo, Dolce & Gabbana and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Put your Marni where your mouth is!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/fashion/21runway-B/21runway-B-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/fashion/21runway-B/21runway-B-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/fashion/21runway-B/21runway-B-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/fashion/21runway-B/21runway-B-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1499, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/fashion/21runway-B/21runway-B-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/21/fashion/21runway-B/21runway-B-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/fashion/21runway-B/21runway-B-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Fashion Week Morning Report, Day 5', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September Fashion Week (2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castiglioni, Consuelo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferragamo, Salvatore, Italia SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marni Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-21T06:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48c10faa-c3f1-5ddd-8dec-67b6c345fabd', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48c10faa-c3f1-5ddd-8dec-67b6c345fabd'}, {'abstract': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/arts/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'lead_paragraph': '8:30 P.M. (CBS) MADAM SECRETARY Téa Leoni stars as Elizabeth McCord, a college professor and former C.I.A. analyst turned newly appointed secretary of state, who battles office politics and circumvents protocol as she navigates issues in the White House and abroad. Then there are matters with her husband and two children at home. Tim Daly plays her supportive spouse; Bebe Neuwirth is her chief of staff; Geoffrey Arend is her speechwriter; Keith Carradine is the president, and her former mentor; and Zeljko Ivanek (above left, with Mr. Carradine and Ms. Leoni) is his Dick Cheney-esque chief of staff. “Hillary Rodham Clinton is the obvious inspiration, but this is Hillary with a human face: Téa Leoni, who has a husky voice and a loose, engaging manner, is an unusually likable beauty,” Alessandra Stanley wrote in The New York Times. “As Elizabeth McCord, she has all the brains and determination of the original and none of the political ambition and baggage.” Ms. Stanley added that a closer model for Mrs. Clinton can be found in the character of Alicia Florrick, the wife of a politician brought down by a sex scandal in “The Good Wife.” That show’s sixth season begins at 9:30, with Alicia refusing to run for state’s attorney. “She stands by his side for a while, then leaves him and restarts her legal career from scratch,” Ms. Stanley said. Of the two series, “\xa0‘The Good Wife’ stands out because it strikes the right balance of network-mandated virtue and cable-inspired vice. ‘Madam Secretary’ has some good moments, but it would be better if its heroine were just a little bit worse.” ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-21T06:50:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cbdce30-81d5-58de-b1f6-91a792bb907d', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cbdce30-81d5-58de-b1f6-91a792bb907d'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on September 21, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/21/pageoneplus/corrections-september-21-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on September 21, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: September 21, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections