e, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88b7fa9f-2e0b-5908-96a1-f4df473c0e4b', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88b7fa9f-2e0b-5908-96a1-f4df473c0e4b'}, {'abstract': '“Mighty Real” is a slender but musically vibrant show about the androgynous pop star Sylvester.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/theater/mighty-real-a-musical-about-the-pop-star-sylvester.html', 'snippet': '“Mighty Real” is a slender but musically vibrant show about the androgynous pop star Sylvester.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A disco ball the size of a small house twirls over the stage at the Theater at St. Clement’s, where “Mighty Real,” a slender but musically vibrant show about the androgynous pop star Sylvester, has audience members shaking their booties in their seats. There are two more disco balls, of slightly more modest size, shaking their own booties above the audience, speckling the auditorium with dizzying dots.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' Exulting in His Fabulous Moment, a Spangled Disco Diva at Fever Pitch', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exulting in His Fabulous Moment, a Spangled Disco Diva at Fever Pitch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wayne, Anthony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Sylvester Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowman, Kendrell', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCleskey, Anastacia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arnold, Jacqueline B', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mighty Real: A Fabulous Sylvester Musical (Play)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-21T20:14:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4188d7f2-ce2f-53ff-b0ac-55bea2c44416', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4188d7f2-ce2f-53ff-b0ac-55bea2c44416'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic performed Charlie Chaplin’s original score during a screening of a restored print of “Modern Times.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/arts/music/philharmonic-plays-score-at-screening-of-modern-times.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic performed Charlie Chaplin’s original score during a screening of a restored print of “Modern Times.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'After its sorry gala concert to open the season last Tuesday night, a slick tribute to music from Italian cinema titled “La Dolce Vita,” the New York Philharmonic resuscitated its artistic pedigree and proved how rewarding its venture into performing film scores can be on Friday night at Avery Fisher Hall. As part of the series The Art of the Score, a beautifully restored print of Charlie Chaplin’s classic 1936 comedy “Modern Times” was screened as the Philharmonic performed Chaplin’s original score, meticulously reconstructed by the composer and conductor Timothy Brock, who led the orchestra in his impressive Philharmonic debut. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/arts/PHIL/PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xla