eneral-assembly/2014/09/21/the-69th-session-of-the-united-nations-general-assembly/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times will provide real-time coverage of the 69th session of the United Nations General Assembly, including reports from the United Nations Climate Summit, to begin Tuesday, and the Security Council meeting on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times will provide real-time coverage of the 69th session of the United Nations General Assembly, including reports from the United Nations Climate Summit, to begin Tuesday, and the Security Council meeting on Wednesday. In addition to video of key speeches by world leaders, readers can find analysis from Times reporters on issues being discussed at the United Nations, including international efforts to fight Ebola, the battle against the militant Islamic State group and attempts to manage conflicts in Ukraine, Iraq and Syria. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 69th Session of the United Nations General Assembly', 'kicker': 'United Nations General Assembly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-21T20:19:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/021d9cbc-84ce-5fe6-977a-7077b8272ce6', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/021d9cbc-84ce-5fe6-977a-7077b8272ce6'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations will convene a summit meeting on climate issues to begin on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/un-general-assembly/2014/09/21/push-for-new-climate-change-pact-as-u-n-summit-approaches/', 'snippet': 'The United Nations will convene a summit meeting on climate issues to begin on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The United Nations is convening on Tuesday the largest gathering of world leaders ever devoted to climate change, and some bold proclamations are expected,” report Justin Gillis and Coral Davenport. “Africa will promise a clean-energy corridor stretching from Cairo to Cape Town. Pledges will be made to halve the destruction of the world’s forests by 2020 and stop it by 2030. The World Bank will lead a big push to put a global price on emissions of greenhouse gases.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Push for New Climate Change Pact as U.N. Summit Approaches', 'kicker': 'United Nations General Assembly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-21T20:23:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea61edc8-2d54-5d7b-938c-18eca1ebb212', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea61edc8-2d54-5d7b-938c-18eca1ebb212'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants played proficiently against Houston, with the new-look offense running the ball more effectively and the defense forcing three turnovers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/sports/new-york-giants-stabilize-season-cruising-past-houston-texans.html', 'snippet': 'The Giants played proficiently against Houston, with the new-look offense running the ball more effectively and the defense forcing three turnovers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Although it was a new year, the Giants’ 2014 season, through two games, looked and felt no different from the team’s disastrous start a year ago.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Thrash Texans and Shake Off Gloom', 'kicker': 'Giants 30, Texans 17', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants Thrash Texans and Shake Off Gloom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Victor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Texans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jennings, Rashad (1985- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-21T20:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46739f70-e630-572c-a1eb-fb49630ca56a', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46739f70-e630-572c-a1eb-fb49630ca56a'}, {'abstract': 'Account assignments, executive appointments and miscellaneous news from advertising agencies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/business/media/news-from-the-advertising-industry-.html', 'snippet': 'Account assignments, executive appointments and miscellaneous news from advertising agencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Accounts', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News From the Advertising Industry ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'News From the Advertising Industry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MillerCoors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levy, Maurice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WPP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hearst Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dentsu', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Y&R', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saatchi & Saatchi', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-21T20:46:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fda27ebf-a41c-5cf6-8491-b56217899ade', 'word_count': 1043, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fda27ebf-a41c-5cf6-8491-b56217899ade'}, {'abstract': 'The Andrew W. Mellon Foundation will contribute $750,000 to Gibney Dance to support its Dance in Process residency program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/arts/dance/750000-grant-for-gibney-dance.html', 'snippet': 'The Andrew W. Mellon Foundation will contribute $750,000 to Gibney Dance to support its Dance in Process residency program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Andrew W. Mellon Foundation will contribute $750,000 to Gibney Dance to support its Dance in Process residency program, bolstering an impressive fund-raising year for the organization, which operates a dance company, two dance centers and a community action program for victims of domestic abuse. In January, the Agnes Varis Trust announced a $3 million gift that allowed Gibney Dance to take over and renovate a 36,000-square-foot space at 280 Broadway, next to City Hall, that Dance New Amsterdam relinquished when it declared bankruptcy a year ago. Over three years, the Mellon gift will provide 30 artists with a three-week residency at Gibney’s other Manhattan space, 890 Broadway in the Flatiron district, where the company has been based since its founding in 1991. In 2011 the company significantly expanded its footprint in the building with additional studios; with the Mellon grant, it is establishing a choreographic center there. The Dance in Process program has been in pilot mode for the past two years with virtually no financial backing. “The Mellon support will give it real depth and will really ground it,” Gina Gibney, the chief executive and artistic director of Gibney Dance, said in an interview. “We will be able to support these dance artists at a whole new level.” The residency will focus specifically on midcareer artists, a demographic often left out of major funding support in favor of so-called established or emerging artists.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$750,000 Grant  For Gibney Dance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '$750,000 Grant for Gibney Dance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mellon Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibney, Gina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gibney Dance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-21T21:02:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Schaefer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaefer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/00697a18-0234-5631-ac56-06bbc67148e4', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00697a18-0234-5631-ac56-06bbc67148e4'}, {'abstract': 'Listeners who click thumbs-up on a song on the Internet radio service could be treated to a live personal performance by the artist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/business/media/a-thumbs-up-brings-musicians-to-life-for-pandora-listeners-.html', 'snippet': 'Listeners who click thumbs-up on a song on the Internet radio service could be treated to a live personal performance by the artist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR fans of Pandora Media, the Internet radio service that plays music based on preferences for genres, artists and songs, no element is more familiar than tapping the thumbs-up or thumbs-down icon. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/adco/adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/21/business/adco/adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/business/adco/adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/21/