 year unless Congress agrees to extend it. Bills are pending in both the House and the Senate to extend financing for four years, to 2019. Congress should approve the extension in the lame-duck session after the midterm elections so that families and state officials will know what the future holds. The program needs to be maintained amid uncertainty as to whether other good coverage will be available for these children. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Children’s Health Insurance at a Crossroads', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Children’s Health Insurance at a Crossroads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "State Children's Health Insurance Program (S-CHIP)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T01:06:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/36b2b9c7-ed3b-5bd0-9fcf-8d7bfdb4f237', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36b2b9c7-ed3b-5bd0-9fcf-8d7bfdb4f237'}, {'abstract': 'A brokered solution to the electoral dispute was far from democratic but sets the stage for a milestone: a peaceful transfer of power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/opinion/a-shaky-step-forward-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'A brokered solution to the electoral dispute was far from democratic but sets the stage for a milestone: a peaceful transfer of power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Afghans got a new president on Sunday, following a bitter fight over the fraud-plagued runoff election on June 14. The outcome was a brokered political accommodation that was far from democratic, but it nonetheless set the stage for an important milestone: a transfer of power that gives the government a fighting chance of containing the Taliban and mending a nation scarred by decades of war. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shaky Step Forward in Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Shaky Step Forward in Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghani, Ashraf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABDULLAH, ABDULLAH', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T01:10:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f1a379b-3d2d-5c08-9d99-51cdb80d1a93', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f1a379b-3d2d-5c08-9d99-51cdb80d1a93'}, {'abstract': 'In the town near Gleneagles, where the Ryder Cup will begin Friday, people have swapped the political passions of last week for the breezier enthusiasms of preparing for one of golf’s greatest events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/sports/gol