ad6b1c2'}, {'abstract': 'After voters rejected independence from the United Kingdom, politicians quickly began bickering over how to transfer more powers to Scotland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/world/europe/promises-of-greater-home-rule-for-scots-turn-contentious.html', 'snippet': 'After voters rejected independence from the United Kingdom, politicians quickly began bickering over how to transfer more powers to Scotland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — When more home-rule powers were offered to Scotland in the heat of the country’s independence referendum campaign, the promises came with rare and unqualified support from the three main British political parties, all desperate to avert a Scottish breakaway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Promises of Greater Home Rule for Scots Turn Contentious', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labour Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T03:14:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89fad638-f0d5-54de-8f40-45659f536be0', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89fad638-f0d5-54de-8f40-45659f536be0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Poli received harsh criticism after the Professional Air Traffic Controllers Organization went on strike in 1981 as President Ronald Reagan responded by dismissing 11,500 controllers in what is now viewed as a seminal moment in the decline of organized labor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/us/robert-e-poli-leader-of-pivotal-strike-by-air-traffic-controllers-is-dead-at-78.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Poli received harsh criticism after the Professional Air Traffic Controllers Organization went on strike in 1981 as President Ronald Reagan responded by dismissing 11,500 controllers in what is now viewed as a seminal moment in the decline of ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert E. Poli, who led the tumultuous 1981 air traffic controllers’ strike, which prompted President Ronald Reagan to dismiss 11,500 controllers and is viewed as a pivotal moment in the decline of organized labor, died on Sept. 15 at his home in Meridian, Idaho. He was 78. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/us/poli-obit/poli-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/22/us/poli-obit/poli-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/us/poli-obit/poli-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/us/poli-obit/poli-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1259, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {