s', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cce197e-13f4-5b79-b6de-e95645d56993', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cce197e-13f4-5b79-b6de-e95645d56993'}, {'abstract': 'The recent conviction of the “accountant of Auschwitz” reinvigorated the debate about prosecuting aging Nazi war criminals.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/should-we-continue-to-prosecute-nazi-war-criminals/', 'snippet': 'The recent conviction of the “accountant of Auschwitz” reinvigorated the debate about prosecuting aging Nazi war criminals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recent conviction of a 93-year-old Auschwitz guard reignited a debate about prosecuting the remaining few Nazi war criminals. Most observers call for a no-holds-barred hunt for the Holocaust perpetrators who have evaded justice for decades, but others\xa0point to their old age, legal issues and difficulty in proving the crimes, arguing that after nearly 80\xa0years, the pursuit should come to a conclusion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should We Continue to Prosecute Nazi War Criminals?', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T10:13:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hanna Kozlowska', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozlowska', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e995d702-c0ad-5e48-aa14-46f89b97cf1c', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e995d702-c0ad-5e48-aa14-46f89b97cf1c'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese authorities have tightened censorship over Internet traffic in recent weeks, and Google and its services are particularly affected.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/daily-report-chinas-great-firewall-toughens-for-googl