all things Washington and elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After eight years, five campaign cycles and nearly 20,000 items, The Caucus on Monday suspended its campaign. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus Ends Its Campaign', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T11:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8409cc0f-02f8-50e8-928a-8a66a43afa5e', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8409cc0f-02f8-50e8-928a-8a66a43afa5e'}, {'abstract': 'But a researcher who produced the data could not explain why.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/study-finds-small-business-health-plans-are-cheaper-on-shop/', 'snippet': 'But a researcher who produced the data could not explain why.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, in a post answering basic questions about how the Affordable Care Act affects small business, we raised the issue of how insurance premiums purchased on the marketplaces set up for small businesses, known as SHOP exchanges, compare to premiums for insurance purchased off the exchanges. It was something of an unsatisfying discussion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Finds Small-Business Health Plans Are Cheaper on SHOP', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}]