_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc734ff4-4a20-5417-818c-242061f337dc'}, {'abstract': 'Gillibrand’s Weight Watcher Revealed, and a Presidential Nominee Is Sunk', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/09/22/gillibrands-weight-watcher-revealed-and-a-presidential-nominee-is-sunk/', 'snippet': 'Gillibrand’s Weight Watcher Revealed, and a Presidential Nominee Is Sunk', 'lead_paragraph': 'PhotoCredit Left, Jim Watson/Agence France-Presse — Getty Images; right, Christopher Gregory/The New York Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gillibrand’s Weight Watcher Revealed, and a Presidential Nominee Is Sunk', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillibrand, Kirsten E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inouye, Daniel K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T11:19:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb497bbe-8357-55b2-b156-dc6dbde6ed6b', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb497bbe-8357-55b2-b156-dc6dbde6ed6b'}, {'abstract': 'Alibaba soared in its public market debut. | Siemens agreed to buy the Dresser-Rand Group. | EMC weighed a deal with H.P. | Public pension funds may be souring on hedge funds.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/morning-agenda-alibabas-i-p-o-aftermath/', 'snippet': 'Alibaba soared in its public market debut. | Siemens agreed to buy the Dresser-Rand Group. | EMC weighed a deal with H.P. | Public pension funds may be souring on hedge funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALIBABA’S I.P.O. AFTERMATH | For months, investors eagerly awaited the Alibaba Group’s public market debut. Now, with the Chinese e-commerce giant’s first day of trading solidly in the rearview mirror, nearly everyone is likely breathing a sigh of relief. After pricing at $68 a share, Alibaba’s stock finished Friday up 38 percent, at $93.89, giving the company a market value of $231 billion, DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced writes. The company officially set the record for the biggest initial public offering ever, after its bankers on Friday decided to exercise a so-called green shoe option, allowing them to increase the size of the deal by 15 percent, from $21.8 billion to $25 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Alibaba’s I.P.O. Aftermath', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T11:23:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ac89c84-4402-5597-9710-f388a2e0cf89', 'word_count': 1887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ac89c84-4402-5597-9710-f388a2e0cf89'}, {'abstract': 'When inflation and the cost of old insurance markets are considered, the premiums available to consumers willing to shop around are remarkably low.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/upshot/in-context-health-premium-increases-dont-actually-look-like-increases.html', 'snippet': 'When inflation and the cost of old insurance markets are considered, the premiums available to consumers willing to shop around are remarkably low.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Affordable Care Act marketplaces, which now serve 7.3 million Americans, some premiums are going up while others are going down. Based on data available so far, we reported last week that the average premiums for last year’s most popular plans would rise 8.4 percent, but that people willing to switch plans could get much better deals — an average 1 percent increase, and even decreases in some markets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/20/upshot/23premiumchart-1411163717684/23premiumchart-1411163717684-articleLarge.png', 'height': 135, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/20/upshot/23premiumchart-1411163717684/23premiumchart-1411163717684-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 135}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/20/upshot/23premiumchart-1411163717684/23premiumchart-1411163717684-jumbo.png', 'height': 231, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/20/upshot/23premiumchart-1411163717684/23premiumchart-1411163717684-superJumbo.png', 'height': 379, 'width': 1679, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/20/upshot/23premiumchart-1411163717684/23premiumchart-1411163717684-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/20/upshot/23premiumchart-1411163717684/23premiumchart-1411163717684-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/20/upshot/23premiumchart-1411163717684/23prem