ial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca08c586-27ea-5739-be93-c10f10fdb418', 'word_count': 1145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca08c586-27ea-5739-be93-c10f10fdb418'}, {'abstract': 'After Epiq Systems, a software company that provides legal documents for bankruptcy and class-action cases, rejected a $1.1 billion take-private offer from P2 Capital Partners, the hedge fund increased its stake in the company to 17 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/p2-capital-partners-raises-pressure-on-epiq-a-maker-of-legal-software/', 'snippet': 'After Epiq Systems, a software company that provides legal documents for bankruptcy and class-action cases, rejected a $1.1 billion take-private offer from P2 Capital Partners, the hedge fund increased its stake in the company to 17 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After several months of discussions, Epiq Systems, a software company that provides legal documents for bankruptcy and class-action cases and discovery, rejected a $1.1 billion offer from the hedge fund P2 Capital Partners to take the company private.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'P2 Capital Partners Raises Pressure on Epiq, a Maker of Legal Software', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pressure on Epiq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EPIQ Systems Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'P2 Capital Partners LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T14:14:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3e083a6-32d9-50cf-a7db-386312dba3ba', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3e083a6-32d9-50cf-a7db-386312dba3ba'}, {'abstract': 'A brief history of the White House’s North Portico.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/09/22/the-white-house-front-door-when-entered-properly/', 'snippet': 'A brief history of the White House’s North Portico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House door that a knife-carrying fence jumper waltzed through on Friday night, prompting a review of procedures by the Secret Service, is not just the entrance to one of the nation’s most supposedly secure facilities. It is also one of the most famous entryways anywhere, where world leaders are greeted and departing presidents meet their successors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The White House Front Door, When Entered Properly', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Secret Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T14:18:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e0fffd4-2d3f-50ca-91c8-170223e833db', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e0fffd4-2d3f-50ca-91c8-170223e833db'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Concepts for high-speed rail travel were discussed in 1889.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/1889-five-miles-a-minute/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Concepts for high-speed rail travel were discussed in 1889.', 'lead_paragraph': ' After the telephone and the phonograph one can believe almost any imaginable electrical miracle, and therefore the claim that an electric railway motor has been invented which, on a specially constructed road, can whisk passengers and freight along at the rate of 300 miles an hour does not seem incredible. In fact, it is asserted that a speed of 180 miles an hour has already been attained on an experimental road. Should the invention prove successful, it will bring London within an hour of Paris — exclusive of the Channel passage — and will enable the Londoner to do business in the city and to sleep in the Scottish Highlands every night. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 23, 1889 ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1889: Five Miles a Minute', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Speed Rail Projects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T14:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a3cd327-1cf8-5c17-b537-21e009afd91d', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a3cd327-1cf8-5c17-b537-21e009afd91d'}, {'abstract': 'As the shows came to a close, the conversations continued.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/milan-fashion-week-carla-bruni-sarkozy-jimmy-choo-air-franceo-know-from-milan/', 'snippet': 'As the shows came to a close, the conversations continued.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The reports have been written, the reviews are in, but after the sensory extravaganza that was Milan Fashion Week, some outstanding questions may still be niggling. In an effort to wipe the slate clean and to allow us all a fresh start in Paris, here are four questions that bubbled up in conversations from the catwalk to cocktails, and responses to keep you in the know:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/fashion/22runway-A/22runway-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/22/fashion/22runway-A/22runway-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/fashion/22runway-A/22runway-A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/fashion/22runway-A/22runway-A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/fashion/22runway-A/22runway-A-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop