cs Help Line', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T14:38:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b41d3686-1aaf-5a56-a1c7-1a4ec29f150d', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b41d3686-1aaf-5a56-a1c7-1a4ec29f150d'}, {'abstract': 'Ban Ki-Moon, the United Nations secretary general, will open the international Climate Summit and the 69th session of the General Assembly this week with some of the most difficult challenges of his tenure dominating the agenda including Ebola and ethnic violence around the world that is driving populations from their homes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/un-general-assembly/2014/09/22/secretary-general-ban-ki-moon-to-open-united-nations-meetings/', 'snippet': 'Ban Ki-Moon, the United Nations secretary general, will open the international Climate Summit and the 69th session of the General Assembly this week with some of the most difficult challenges of his tenure dominating the agenda including Ebola and...', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday at the United Nations, the first world conference on indigenous peoples began, the day before Ban Ki-Moon, the United Nations secretary general, opened the Climate Summit. Wednesday, the secretary general opens the 69th session of the General Assembly. It has been an important week for the United Nations, and for Mr. Ban, who will speak before the General Assembly meeting. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/world/UNGA-MOON/UNGA-MOON-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/19/world/UNGA-MOON/UNGA-MOON-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/world/UNGA-MOON/UNGA-MOON-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/world/UNGA-MOON/UNGA-MOON-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1153, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/world/UNGA-MOON/UNGA-MOON-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/19/world/UNGA-MOON/UNGA-MOON-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/19/world/UNGA-MOON/UNGA-MOON-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Secretary General Ban Ki-moon to Open United Nations Meetings', 'kicker': 'United Nations General Assembly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Millennium Development Goals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T14:48:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/109c2be3-f3e8-5386-bbd7-248a84322b8e', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/109c2be3-f3e8-5386-bbd7-248a84322b8e'}, {'abstract': 'Adrian Peterson shouldn’t sell himself short. He is where he is today in spite of his father, not because of him, and what he learned from him now threatens his career and his family.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/spanking-isnt-culture-its-a-cycle-of-abuse/', 'snippet': 'Adrian Peterson shouldn’t sell himself short. He is where he is today in spite of his father, not because of him, and what he learned from him now threatens his career and his family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the debate rages over Adrian Peterson’s child abuse charges, his defenders, including Charles Barkley, have suggested that this particular kind of discipline — lashing a child with a switch — is “cultural” and therefore beyond reproach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/17nytnow-peterson2-pm/17nytnow-peterson2-pm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/17/business/17nytnow-peterson2-pm/17nytnow-peterson2-pm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/17nytnow-peterson2-pm/17nytnow-peterson2-pm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/17nytnow-peterson2-pm/17nytnow-peterson2-pm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/17nytnow-peterson2-pm/17nytnow-peterson2-pm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/17/business/17nytnow-peterson2-pm/17nytnow-peterson2-pm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/17/business/17nytnow-peterson2-pm/17nytnow-peterson2-pm-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spanking Isn’t Culture. It’s a Cycle of Abuse.', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGER (EMOTION)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Negl