5ee3-4bfd-5663-97ab-8d2a88b4796f', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a015ee3-4bfd-5663-97ab-8d2a88b4796f'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Plans for the partition of Poland were revealed in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/1939-line-of-demarcation-decided/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Plans for the partition of Poland were revealed in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Following the departure from Moscow yesterday morning of a German military mission charged with the negotiation for the partition of Poland between Germany and Russia, the D.N.B., official German news agency, announced that both governments ‘‘had fixed the line of demarcation between the German and Russian armies,’’ a Havas dispatch from Berne said. According to the D.N.B. communiqué, Germany abandons the idea of re-establishing the German and Russian occupation zones agreed upon in the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk in 1917. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 23, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/blogs/23iht-oldsept23-map/23iht-oldsept23-map-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/23/blogs/23iht-oldsept23-map/23iht-oldsept23-map-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 711}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/blogs/23iht-oldsept23-map/23iht-oldsept23-map-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 864, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/blogs/23iht-oldsept23-map/23iht-oldsept23-map-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1728, 'subType': 'superJumbo', '