/', 'snippet': 'The bucket list encourages us to seek activities for their novelty. But how might we travel in a way that encourages meaningful experience?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wherefore the bucket list? Rebecca Mead recently wrote a blog post for The New Yorker about “Kicking the Bucket List,” a plea for abolishing the practice of seeking experiences for the sake of accomplishment. Instead, Ms. Mead lobbies in favor of an approach to life that engages deeply with a smaller range of experiences.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-travelsub/nyto-travelsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-travelsub/nyto-travelsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-travelsub/nyto-travelsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-travelsub/nyto-travelsub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2001, 'width': 2020, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-travelsub/nyto-travelsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-travelsub/nyto-travelsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-travelsub/nyto-travelsub-thu