8-b546-531a-9f2c-4cf8d318654f'}, {'abstract': 'Venezuela may represent the Latin American and Caribbean nations – and sit right next to the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/theatrics-to-come-on-the-u-n-security-council/', 'snippet': 'Venezuela may represent the Latin American and Caribbean nations – and sit right next to the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There could be major drama on the United Nations Security Council next year if, as widely expected, Venezuela gets a seat adjacent to that of its nemesis, the United States, to represent Latin American and Caribbean nations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theatrics to Come on the U.N. Security Council', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Power, Samantha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T15:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ernesto Londo&#241;o', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ernesto', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Londo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02507605-315d-53e6-b6de-384f339a22e6', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02507605-315d-53e6-b6de-384f339a22e6'}, {'abstract': 'Hotels, cruise lines and tour companies are now creating activities for travelers who like to sleep.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/what-wake-up-call-catering-to-sleepers-in/', 'snippet': 'Hotels, cruise lines and tour companies are now creating activities for travelers who like to sleep.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The travel industry is geared toward early risers: activities and tours tend to begin in the morning, and breakfast is usually served for a limited time. That’s finally changing with more hotels, cruise lines and tour companies catering to travelers who like to sleep in or want a leisurely start to their day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Wake-up Call? Catering to Sleepers-In', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T15:41:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/469c800c-cc6d-58a6-865d-360043c49a99', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/469c800c-cc6d-58a6-865d-360043c49a99'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of demonstrators, protesting what they said was capitalism’s influence over environment-harming practices, struggled to get to their destination. About 100 were arrested.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/nyregion/climate-change-protesters-wall-street.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of demonstrators, protesting what they said was capitalism’s influence over environment-harming practices, struggled to get to their destination. About 100 were arrested.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 100 climate change protesters were arrested on Monday as hundreds marched through the streets of Lower Manhattan, at one point clashing with the police as they tried to push through barricades sealing off Wal