ght': 2048, 'width': 1583, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/business/22adnews-pic1/22adnews-pic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/22/business/22adnews-pic1/22adnews-pic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/business/22adnews-pic1/22adnews-pic1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Initiative for Special Olympics Aims for More Spontaneity, Less Marketing', 'kicker': 'Campaign Spotlight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Olympics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Y&R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T16:57:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc4575be-d732-5a46-9059-a3ef02b89594', 'word_count': 1429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc4575be-d732-5a46-9059-a3ef02b89594'}, {'abstract': 'The last piano George Gershwin owned will be part of a concert at the University of Michigan’s music school in October.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/michigan-music-school-concert-to-feature-gershwins-piano/', 'snippet': 'The last piano George Gershwin owned will be part of a concert at the University of Michigan’s music school in October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last piano George Gershwin owned and performed on – a Steinway Model A, made in 1933 and delivered to Gershwin in January, 1934 – will make its 21st-century public debut in a free concert at the University of Michigan’s School of Music, Theater & Dance, in Ann Arbor, Mich., on Oct. 10, the university announced.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan Music School Concert to Feature Gershwin’s Piano', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gershwin, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T16:59:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13fbd3e9-ac76-5579-9ac0-2c1e806d0b7e', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13fbd3e9-ac76-5579-9ac0-2c1e806d0b7e'}, {'abstract': 'Heavenly Rembrandt is a temporary restaurant serving up fine cuisine and lectures from a 35th-floor boardroom installed with the artist’s etchings.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/amsterdam-rembrandt-pop-up-restaurant-opens/', 'snippet': 'Heavenly Rembrandt is a temporary restaurant serving up fine cuisine and lectures from a 35th-floor boardroom installed with the artist’s etchings.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Cooking is like painting with taste, so I was fascinated by the idea of creating a menu based on Rembrandt’s work,” says the Dutch chef Wilco Berends, explaining why he chose to head the kitchen at Heavenly Rembrandt, a pop-up dinner-only restaurant that is set to be one of the most intriguing events in Amsterdam this fall. The interdisciplinary project, which opens tonight, is a collaboration between the Het Rembrandthuis museum, which occupies the house where the painter lived and worked from 1639 to 1658; Berends, who normally cooks at his Michelin-starred De Nederlanden restaurant in Vreeland; and the Rembrandt Tower boardrooms, a plush suite of private meeting rooms atop the 35-story, 500-foot-tall Rembrandt Tower, the city’s tallest building.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/t-magazine/22rembrandt-lobrano/22rembrandt-lobrano-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/22/t-magazine/22rembrandt-lobrano/22rembrandt-lobrano-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/t-magazine/22rembrandt-lobrano/22rembrandt-lobrano-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/t-magazine/22rembrandt-lobrano/22rembrandt-lobrano-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/t-magazine/22rembrandt-lobrano/22rembrandt-lobrano-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/20