s offering a training course on how to “win with the media,” which promises “numerous practical tips for handling the media in an officer-involved shooting.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Comment Necessary: ‘Officer-Involved Shooting – You Can Win With the Media’', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T17:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14365a7c-d868-5404-8272-3283c54c1dc3', 'word_count': 42, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14365a7c-d868-5404-8272-3283c54c1dc3'}, {'abstract': 'Lt. Col. George Bivens said investigators were “following up very aggressively” on tips regarding the whereabouts of Eric M. Frein, the focus of an intensive manhunt now in its 10th day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/us/pennsylvania-police-say-they-are-close-to-capturing-suspect-in-troopers-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'Lt. Col. George Bivens said investigators were “following up very aggressively” on tips regarding the whereabouts of Eric M. Frein, the focus of an intensive manhunt now in its 10th day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BLOOMING GROVE, Pa., — Pennsylvania authorities said Monday that they believed they were closing in on a self-taught survivalist accused of killing one state trooper and wounding a second during an ambush earlier this month outside a police barracks in the Pocono Mountains.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image