: 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efe79977-3111-50a0-9a62-3b26c626869e', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efe79977-3111-50a0-9a62-3b26c626869e'}, {'abstract': 'Israel’s occupation of Arab lands and its standoff with the Palestinians have become so divisive that many rabbis say it is impossible to have a civil conversation about Israel in their synagogues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/us/rabbis-find-talk-of-israel-and-gaza-a-sure-way-to-draw-congregants-wrath.html', 'snippet': 'Israel’s occupation of Arab lands and its standoff with the Palestinians have become so divisive that many rabbis say it is impossible to have a civil conversation about Israel in their synagogues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the war in Gaza still raging, Rabbi Sharon Kleinbaum offered an unusual prayer for peace last month during a Friday night service at the large predominantly gay synagogue she leads in New York. Cautioning her flock not to “harden our hearts” against any who had suffered, she wove throughout the prayer the names of young Israeli soldiers — as well as Palestinian children — who were killed in Gaza.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/us/23RABBIS-hp/23RABBIS-hp-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/23/us/23RABBIS-hp/23RABBIS-hp-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/us/23RABBIS-hp/23RABBIS-hp-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/us/23RABBIS-hp/23RABBIS-hp-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1233, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/us/23RABBIS-hp/23RABBIS-hp-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/23/us/23RABBIS-hp/23RABBIS-hp-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/us/23RABBIS-hp/23RABBIS-hp-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Talk in Synagogue of Israel and Gaza Goes From Debate to Wrath to Rage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talk in Synagogue of Israel and Gaza Goes From Debate to Wrath to Rage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rabbis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T17:22:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Goodstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b4cf2a4-4e68-5e63-a973-a44c159cff24', 'word_count': 1406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b4cf2a4-4e68-5e63-a973-a44c159cff24'}, {'abstract': 'Riccardo Muti will not conduct two scheduled performances at Teatro dell’Opera di Roma this season, saying that conditions at the theater did not “guarantee the serenity I need.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/muti-withdraws-from-rome-opera-performances/', 'snippet': 'Riccardo Muti will not conduct two scheduled performances at Teatro dell’Opera di Roma this season, saying that conditions at the theater did not “guarantee the serenity I need.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Riccardo Muti will not conduct two operas scheduled for the upcoming season at the Teatro dell’Opera di Roma, citing “recent, persistent problems” at the storied — and strike-plagued — theater. Carlo Fuortes, the opera’s general manager, announced the split on Sunday, citing a personal letter by the maestro stating that conditions at the theater did not “guarantee the serenity I need to ensure the success of the performances.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Muti Withdraws From Rome Opera Performances', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muti, Riccardo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T17:35:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70411621-2c5c-5672-9c1b-b0c90bc8db91', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70411621-2c5c-5672-9c1b-b0c90bc8db91'}, {'abstract': 'White House outlines President Obama’s speech to the U.N. Climate Summit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/09/22/if-nothing-else-a-speech-from-obama-on-climate/', 'snippet': 'White House outlines President Obama’s speech to the U.N. Climate Summit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When President Obama addresses the United Nations Climate Summit on Tuesday, he won’t be announcing a breakthrough on environmental policy. Opposition in Congress to carbon taxes remains high, and expectations for progress around the world are low, as rich and poor countries continue to clash over long-simmering environmental disputes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If Nothing Else, a Speech From Obama on Climate', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T17:42:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1e94473-90f6-5910-948c-a68ac146ee35', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1e94473-90f6-5910-948c-a68ac146ee35'}, {'abstract': 'Investors should take note of the path taken last week by Calpers, a financial adviser writes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/your-money/asset-allocation/picking-the-right-hedge-fund-involves-more-than-looking-in-the-past.html', 'snippet': 'Investors should take note of the path taken last week by Calpers, a financial adviser writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in my career, I worked at a large brokerage firm. My job included answering calls from people with questions. One question kept coming up: What does your Individual Retirement Account return? The first few times, I thought it was a joke. But it didn’t take long for me to realize that people just didn’t understand the difference between an I.R.A. and the investments held in an I.R.A.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/business/092214bucks-carl-sketch/092214bucks-carl-sketch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/22/business/092214bucks-carl-sketch/092214bucks-carl-sketch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/business/092214bucks-carl-sketch/092214bucks-carl-sketch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/business/092214buc