 an agreement in line with other retailers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/amazon-workers-walk-off-the-job-in-germany-over-wage-dispute/', 'snippet': 'A total of 2,000 workers refused to show up for their shifts on Monday in an effort to force Amazon to accept an agreement in line with other retailers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN —\xa0Amazon employees in Germany, frustrated by the company’s refusal to hold wage talks, walked off their jobs Monday in a coordinated strike at four of the company’s distribution centers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Workers Walk Off the Job in Germany Over Wage Dispute', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T19:07:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/246d84d2-555b-5a47-bd5b-230fc4d6b0e6', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/246d84d2-555b-5a47-bd5b-230fc4d6b0e6'}, {'abstract': 'The jeweler created this gold-and-jade design to commemorate its 140th anniversary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/piaget-watch-jade-gold-diamond-cuff/', 'snippet': 'The jeweler created this gold-and-jade design to commemorate its 140th anniversary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there ever was an object that perfectly captured the louche sexiness and that somehow tremendously appealing drab green of the ’70s, this Piaget watch is it. Inspired by similar designs in its archive, the Swiss jeweler has created this decadent cuff to commemorate its 140th anniversary. The watch has a natural jade dial and is set in a gold cage with 236 brilliant-cut diamonds that give the illusion of rising from the wrist like a great pyramid.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '78', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28design-qual-thing/28design-qual-thing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28design-qual-thing/28design-qual-thing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28design-qual-thing/28design-qual-thing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28design-qual-thing/28design-qual-thing-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28design-qual-thing/28design-qual-thing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28design-qual-thing/28design-qual-thing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28design-qual-thing/28design-qual-thing-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Piaget’s Groundbreaking 1970s Cuff Watch, Renewed', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Thing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T19:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Bobb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bobb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9adf192d-acfc-565d-825d-a7c39e95bd1b', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9adf192d-acfc-565d-825d-a7c39e95bd1b'}, {'abstract': 'Netflix will soon be streaming all seven seasons of “Gilmore Girls.” Why has the show, which concluded its run in 2007, garnered such a cultish following?', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/why-are-we-so-obsessed-with-gilmore-girls/', 'snippet': 'Netflix will soon be streaming all seven seasons of “Gilmore Girls.” Why has the show, which concluded its run in 2007, garnered such a cultish following?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the WB series “Gilmore Girls” concluded in 2007, I gradually managed to acquire all seven seasons on DVD, unable to part with the quirky but infinitely relatable characters, the charming small town I wanted to live in and the lightning-speed dialogue peppered with references waiting to be decoded. As soon as I had the entire collection, the 42 discs started disappearing in my friends’ homes. To this day, they claim innocence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-gilmore/nyto-gilmore-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-gilmore/nyto-gilmore-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-gilmore/nyto-gilmore-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-gilmore/nyto-gilmore-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1775, 'width': 1792, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-gilmore/nyto-gilmore-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-gilmore/nyto-gilmore-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/opinion/nyto-gilmore/nyto-gilmore-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Are We So Obsessed With ‘Gilmore Girls’?', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bledel, Alexis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Heather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Melissa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WB Television Network', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T19:12:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hanna Kozlowska', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozlowska', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41896c19-a398-5ab5-b5cf-59602474c80f', 'word_count': 992, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41896c19-a398-5ab5-b5cf-59602474c80f'}, {'abstract': 'Beetroots, whether roasted, steamed or raw, easily find their way into new salads, side dishes and main dishes. The greens are interchangeable with other mild-tasting greens like Swiss chard and spinach.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/beets-recipe-ideas/', 'snippet': 'Beetroots, whether roasted, steamed or raw, easily find their way into new salads, side dishes and main dishes. The greens are interchangeable with other mild-tasting greens like Swiss chard and spinach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I sometimes wonder when I’ll run out of ideas for beets, as year after year around this time I’ve devoted a week’s worth of Recipes for Health to beets and their greens. But it hasn’t happened yet. Beetroots, whether roasted, steamed or raw, easily find their way into new salads, side dishes and main dishes. They are friendly with Mediterranean seasonings of all kinds: Greek, Middle Eastern, North African, Italian and Provençal. The greens are interchangeable with other mild-tasting greens like Swiss chard and spinach; one bunch of beets gives you two vegetables to work with. With the beets and their greens you get two sets of nutrients: anthocyanins and betalains, known for their antioxidant properties, from the beetroots, and vitamins K and A, as well as other phytonutrients – lutein and zeaxanthin – from the greens. Both are excellent sources of folate, and beets are a very good source of manganese, potassium and copper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/25recipehealthbeetsalt/25recipehealthbeetsalt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/23/science/25recipehealthbeetsalt/25recipehealthbeetsalt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/25recipehealthbeetsalt/25recipehealthbeetsalt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/25recipehealthbeetsalt/25recipehealthbeetsalt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/25recipehealthbeetsalt/25recipehealthbeetsalt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/23/science/25recipehealthbeetsalt/25recipehealthbeetsalt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/25recipehealthbeetsalt/25recipehealthbeetsalt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beauty in the Beets', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T19:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bdc67d6-6eea-5835-a40b-f558edbfb5aa', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bdc67d6-6eea-5835-a40b-f558edbfb5aa'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Caramanica and Ben Ratliff discuss Chris Brown and the challenges of appraising a polarizing figure.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/popcast-what-we-talk-about-when-we-talk-about-chris-brown/', 'snippet': 'Jon Caramanica and Ben Ratliff discuss Chris Brown and the challenges of appraising a polarizing figure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chris Brown’s new album, “X,” has been a long time coming — it was first announced a year ago, before he served a few months of jail time unrelated to his 2009 felony charges for assaulting his then-girlfriend, Rihanna. Jon Caramanica wrote about “X” this week, but our Popcast conversation is less about the album than the complicated task of writing about Mr. Brown as a music critic. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, '