e: The World Shaped by Us (Book)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T20:05:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8168405-1ff7-59f9-9253-69470213dadc', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8168405-1ff7-59f9-9253-69470213dadc'}, {'abstract': 'It was unclear whether President Petro O. Poroshenko would travel\u200b to New York to deliver his address as scheduled on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/un-general-assembly/2014/09/22/poroshenkos-presence-at-u-n-general-assembly-is-in-doubt/', 'snippet': 'It was unclear whether President Petro O. Poroshenko would travel\u200b to New York to deliver his address as scheduled on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The foreign minister of Ukraine said Monday that it was unclear whether President Petro O. Poroshenko would travel\u200b to New York to deliver his scheduled address before the United Nations General Assembly on Thursday. It is possible, Foreign Minister Pavlo Klimkin told reporters, “there will be a change in the program.” He offered no details except to say that the crisis in the country could compel Mr. Poroshenko to remain in Ukraine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poroshenko’s Presence at U.N. General Assembly Is in Doubt', 'kicker': 'United Nations General Assembly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poroshenko, Petro Olekseyevich', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T20:07:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a0088a9-8dc1-56ca-8621-956d48125c3f', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a0088a9-8dc1-56ca-8621-956d48125c3f'}, {'abstract': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll is based on telephone interviews conducted September 10 through 14 with 1,000 adults throughout the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/science/how-the-poll-was-conducted.html', 'snippet': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll is based on telephone interviews conducted September 10 through 14 with 1,000 adults throughout the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll is based on telephone interviews conducted September 10 through 14 with 1,000 adults throughout the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Poll Was Conducted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T20:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cbe4216-906d-5db0-93d3-dca0e87ec2dd', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cbe4216-906d-5db0-93d3-dca0e87ec2dd'}, {'abstract': 'Many of the Mexican chefs moving into the limelight are male, but it was the women of the country who forged the extraordinary recipes in the new Phaidon tome “Mexico: The Cookbook.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/mexican-cookbook-phaidon-secret-history/', 'snippet': 'Many of the Mexican chefs moving into the limelight are male, but it was the women of the country who forged the extraordinary recipes in the new Phaidon tome “Mexico: The Cookbook.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my taco pilgrimage through Mexico with the Danish chef René Redzepi of Noma was winding to a close in the languorous city of Mérida, I was starting to worry that we were going to miss out on one of the dishes I was most looking forward to. By then we had chewed and slurped our way through everything from the tasting menu at Pujol, chef Enrique Olvera’s gastronome-magnet in Mexico City, to fresh coconuts bought by the side of a jungle road. But we still hadn’t had cochinita pibil.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/t-magazine/22Gordinier-Ashlock2/22Gordinier-Ashlock2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/22/t-magazine/22Gordinier-Ashlock2/22Gordinier-Ashlock2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/t-magazine/22Gordinier-Ashlock2/22Gordinier-Ashlock2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/t-magazine/22Gordinier-Ashlock2/22Gordinier-Ashlock2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'hei