meetings during the United Nations General Assembly this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/09/22/obama-to-meet-with-netanyahu-at-white-house/', 'snippet': 'The White House said Monday that President Obama would hold a series of bilateral meetings during the United Nations General Assembly this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House said Monday that President Obama would meet with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel on Oct. 1 in Washington.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama to Meet With Netanyahu at White House', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T20:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f228303-3b81-5d31-87dc-44184f2e4e69', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f228303-3b81-5d31-87dc-44184f2e4e69'}, {'abstract': 'More than half of Americans said global warming was caused by human behavior, the highest level ever recorded by The New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/science/global-warming-concerns-grow.html', 'snippet': 'More than half of Americans said global warming was caused by human behavior, the highest level ever recorded by The New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While few Americans regard the environment as the nation’s foremost challenge, most say it should be a priority, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll. And more than half say global warming is caused by human behavior, the highest level ever recorded by the national poll.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Global Warming Concerns Grow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Global Warming Concerns Grow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connelly, Marjorie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T20:19:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39ef2618-4a58-5985-aa7f-71f88c17a755', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39ef2618-4a58-5985-aa7f-71f88c17a755'}, {'abstract': 'The Arctic is changing — fast. Two experts who have spent decades working there believe that the marine mammals who call the high latitudes home are now locked into a human-forced ecological game of chance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2014/09/23/science/23scitimes-podcast-climate-seaice.html', 'snippet': 'The Arctic is changing — fast. Two experts who have spent decades working there believe that the marine mammals who call the high latitudes home are now locked into a human-forced ecological game of chance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Arctic is changing — fast. Two experts who have spent decades working there believe that the marine mammals who call the high latitudes home are now locked into a human-forced ecological game of chance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Animal Gamble in the Arctic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC OCEAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Walruses', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whales and Whaling', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seals (Animals) and Sealing', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T20:23:29+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/23adbc31-f07f-5ac9-ab10-61d260494841', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/23adbc31-f07f-5ac9-ab10-61d260494841'}, {'abstract': 'A Canadian traveler, Nyesha McPherson, was charged after the authorities discovered the weapons and 33 pounds of the drug in her checked luggage on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/nyregion/woman-arrested-at-kennedy-airport-with-marijuana-and-guns-officials-say.html', 'snippet': 'A Canadian traveler, Nyesha McPherson, was charged after the authorities discovered the weapons and 33 pounds of the drug in her checked luggage on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 24-year-old woman was arrested at Kennedy International Airport on Sunday morning after the authorities discovered two handguns, hundreds of rounds of ammunition and 33 pounds of marijuana concealed in her luggage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/nyregion/ARRESTweb/ARRESTweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 417, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/nyregion/ARRESTweb/ARRESTweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 417, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/nyregion/ARRESTweb/ARRESTweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/23/nyregion/ARRESTweb/ARRESTweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/nyregion/ARRESTweb/ARRESTweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman Arrested at Kennedy Airport With Marijuana and Guns, Officials Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy International Airport (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T20:25:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bfbb9d2-5f35-56b6-b792-c9775232335c', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bfbb9d2-5f35-56b6-b792-c9775232335c'}, {'abstract': 'When the Anasazi abandoned the cities they had worked so long to build on the Colorado Plateau, it had something to do with climate, but drawing lessons from their opaque past may be as difficult as predicting our clouded future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/science/a-future-as-clouded-as-their-past.html', 'snippet': 'When the Anasazi abandoned the cities they had worked so long to build on the Colorado Plateau, it had something to do with climate, but drawing lessons from their opaque past may be as difficult as predicting our clouded future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We won’t ever know what the Anasazi were thinking on the eve of the 13th century when they abandoned the cities they had worked so long to build on the Colorado Plateau. The reasons had something to do with climate — a great drought and, perhaps on top of that, a mini ice age. If that wasn’t enough to defeat a thriving culture, there was the turmoil that came from just not knowing. Why were the sky and earth behaving so strangely? Why wasn’t the old magic working anymore?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23JOHN/23JOHN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23JOHN/23JOHN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23JOHN/23JOHN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1021, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23JOHN/23JOHN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1648, 'width': 1653, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23JOHN/23JOHN-thumbSt