_paragraph': 'Some of the most spellbinding dancing New York has seen all year occurred last week during Trajal Harrell’s seven-part series, “Twenty Looks or Paris Is Burning at the Judson Church.” The series also contained other performances that were extraordinary in nondance ways. Four dancers (Rob Fordeyn, Thibault Lac, Stephen Thompson, Ondrej Vidlar) were phenomenal, redefining grace before our eyes, and the drag artist François Chaignaud, though at his worst when dancing, compellingly and bewilderingly demonstrated multiple layers of identity. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/TRAJAL/TRAJAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/TRAJAL/TRAJAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/TRAJAL/TRAJAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/TRAJAL/TRAJAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/TRAJAL/TRAJAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/TRAJAL/TRAJAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/TRAJAL/TRAJAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Marathon Mash-Up of Two Creative Worlds ', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Marathon Mash-Up of Two Creative Worlds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrell, Trajal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T21:45:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/df7b9773-35c8-52a9-8502-1bbc362e8883', 'word_count': 1049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df7b9773-35c8-52a9-8502-1bbc362e8883'}, {'abstract': 'Stylish hordes moved forth from England to Italy for the third week of fashion month. Here’s a recap of what happened, traced through the Styles staff’s Twitter feeds.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/milan-fashion-week-social-media-roundup/', 'snippet': 'Stylish hordes moved forth from England to Italy for the third week of fashion month. Here’s a recap of what happened, traced through the Styles staff’s Twitter feeds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not 24 hours after London Fashion Week concluded, the fashion crowd had already migrated to Italy for Milan Fashion Week. As the world hurtled forward at a look-there-or-you’ll-miss-it pace driven by the Scottish referendum, the Alibaba I.P.O. and the release of the latest iPhone, Italian designers slowed down and plumbed the past for inspiration — out of nostalgia for the heyday of Italian fashion, perhaps? Not all were looking backward: Fendi existed distinctly in the moment, and a contemporary Barbie seemed to be Jeremy Scott’s latest muse at Moschino. One change in attendance was notable and noticed: Though celebrity models like Naomi Campbell and Kendall Jenner stalked the catwalk, actual celebrities were mostly missing from the front row. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Fashion Week Social Media Roundup', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September Fashion Week (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Amy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Naomi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenner, Kendall', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Jeremy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T21:45:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valeriya Safronova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valeriya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Safronova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a99dde3-9e2c-59a9-946c-ccfe88d98f81', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a99dde3-9e2c-59a9-946c-ccfe88d98f81'}, {'abstract': 'After two incidents involving security breaches at the White House over the weekend, President Obama said he was grateful for the Secret Service and the protection it provides.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000003131519/obama-defends-the-secret-service.html', 'snippet': 'After two incidents involving security breaches at the White House over the weekend, President Obama said he was grateful for the Secret Service and the protection it provides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After two incidents involving security breaches at the White House over the weekend, President Obama said he was grateful for the Secret Service and the protection it provides.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/multimedia/obama-secret-service/obama-secret-service-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/22/multimedia/obama-secret-service/obama-secret-service-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/multimedia/obama-secret-service/obama-secret-service-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/multimedia/obama-secret-service/obama-secret-service-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/multimedia/obama-secret-service/obama-secret-service-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/22/multimedia/obama-secret-service/obama-secret-service-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/22/multimedia/obama-secret-service/obama-secret-service-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Defends the Secret Service', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Secret Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T21:49:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'Reuters', 'person': [], 'organization': 'Reuters'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/bc191b9e-b200-5ae2-87a5-c7e78fb110e6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/bc191b9e-b200-5ae2-87a5-c7e78fb110e6'}, {'abstract': 'Several opera singers brought their talents to French art music and some American works at the Schimmel Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/arts/music/the-voce-series-with-french-songs-at-the-schimmel-center.html', 'snippet': 'Several opera singers brought their talents to French art music and some American works at the Schimmel Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are certain styles that are difficult to convey well: Most competent pianists, for example, can play Chopin decently, but it takes a more particular gift to win over an audience with Bach or Boulez. On the vocal front, the intimate, enigmatic French art song — a genre (like chamber music) that is often best suited to salon-style formats — can be challenging to render convincingly. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/RISING/RISING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/RISING/RISING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidt