decision about running for president sometime next year. But from the sound of things, she might be trying out a campaign slogan already.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeding a Slogan? Clinton Talks Up Choice and Chance in Email Blast', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T22:10:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dea27592-cad6-5c48-9132-7ef617202614', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dea27592-cad6-5c48-9132-7ef617202614'}, {'abstract': 'The band’s guitarist is also a longtime photographer. His collected shots are the subject of a new Rizzoli book — and included in a new Jeffrey Deitch-curated exhibition.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/blondie-40th-anniversary-photographs-chelsea-chris-stein/', 'snippet': 'The band’s guitarist is also a longtime photographer. His collected shots are the subject of a new Rizzoli book — and included in a new Jeffrey Deitch-curated exhibition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since Blondie formed 40 years ago, one thing has remained constant: if the band’s co-founder Chris Stein isn’t onstage with a guitar slung around his neck, chances are he’s off somewhere with a camera, taking pictures. Now, the results of his four-decade-long hobby have been compiled in a new book, “Chris Stein/Negative: Me, Blondie, and the Advent of Punk” (out tomorrow from Rizzoli), and will appear in an exhibition curated by Jeffrey Deitch at the Chelsea Hotel’s Storefront Gallery alongside band memorabilia and images by the likes of Annie Leibovitz and Robert Mapplethorpe. “I was just in the middle of this milieu and I took pictures,” Stein says matter-of-factly on the phone from Vienna, a recent stop on Blondie’s anniversary tour.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Blondie Turns 40, a Look Back Through Chris Stein’s Lens', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gallery: Behind the Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harry, Deborah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blondie (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T22:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Bengal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bengal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6962437e-fd73-5ad8-a583-a22b7d1dbd24', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6962437e-fd73-5ad8-a583-a22b7d1dbd24'}, {'abstract': 'Climate change may impact even the smallest organisms, like photosynthesizing microbes that play a critical role in the desert and scrub environments in the Southwest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/science/on-warmer-planet-range-of-soil-microbes-may-change.html', 'snippet': 'Climate change may impact even the smallest organisms, like photosynthesizing microbes that play a critical role in the desert and scrub environments in the Southwest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEMPE, Ariz. — Even the microbes, it seems, may be on the move.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Microscopic Issue of Unknown Consequences', 'kicker': 'Nature in the Balance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Microscopic Reactions to Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia-Pichel, Ferran', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T22:17:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f50f7120-3ba2-556c-b395-a374561b3562', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f50f7120-3ba2-556c-b395-a374561b3562'}, {'abstract': 'The rapper Stitches, whose video “Brick in Yo Face” has gone viral, performed on Sunday at the Amityville Music Hall on Long Island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/arts/music/stitches-the-transgressive-rapper-plays-amityville.html', 'snippet': 'The rapper Stitches, whose video “Brick in Yo Face” has gone viral, performed on Sunday at the Amityville Music Hall on Long Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMITYVILLE, N.Y. — “I’m gonna pick one person,” Stitches said. Out in the Sunday night crowd at the Amityville Music Hall here, several young men — and one or two young women — were thrusting their hands to the sky, clamoring for a shot at immortality. Or at least a chance at touching a modern starburst, which here meant having Stitches — the Miami rapper whose manic, pneumatic-intensity video for “Brick in Yo Face” has been one of this year’s most unlikely viral phenomena — throw a brick in their face, and have it explode in a puff of powder. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/STITCHES/STITCHES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/STITCHES/STITCHES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/STITCHES/STITCHES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/STITCHES/STITCHES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/STITCHES/STITCHES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/23/arts/STITCHES/STITCHES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images