: [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cochrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc7756bd-7d2d-5027-81f2-b1370f6ffd7a', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc7756bd-7d2d-5027-81f2-b1370f6ffd7a'}, {'abstract': 'The rules would make it more difficult for American companies to lower their tax bills by relocating overseas and would wipe out the benefits for those that do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/business/treasury-creates-new-hurdles-to-inversion-moves.html', 'snippet': 'The rules would make it more difficult for American companies to lower their tax bills by relocating overseas and would wipe out the benefits for those that do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Treasury Secretary Jacob J. Lew announced rules on Monday that are aimed at making it more difficult for American companies to lower their tax bills by relocating overseas and that would wipe out the benefits for those that do. It is the administration’s latest move to sidestep a paralyzed Congress and tackle a politically charged element of President Obama’s agenda.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/business/INVERSIONS/INVERSIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 301, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/23/business/INVERSIONS/INVERSIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 301}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/business/INVERSIONS/INVERSIONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 514, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '