'A study, supported by the United Nations women’s agency, found that movies released in the 10 most profitable markets worldwide exhibited evidence of “deep-seated discrimination and pervasive stereotyping of women and girls by the international film industry.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/un-general-assembly/2014/09/22/for-most-women-in-film-their-roles-are-silent/', 'snippet': 'A study, supported by the United Nations women’s agency, found that movies released in the 10 most profitable markets worldwide exhibited evidence of “deep-seated discrimination and pervasive stereotyping of women and girls by the international fi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Women are more seen than heard in movies worldwide. A tiny fraction of them are cast as lawyers or doctors. Women and girls are twice as likely as men and boys to be shown on screen naked, partially clothed or in sexually revealing clothes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Most Women in Film, Their Roles Are Silent', 'kicker': 'United Nations General Assembly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Southern California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T23:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c9ad608-7321-5940-a34b-61720e2dec42', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c9ad608-7321-5940-a34b-61720e2dec42'}, {'abstract': 'Winters and summers that have grown more extreme imperil a country’s herding tradition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/science/its-not-genghis-khans-mongolia.html', 'snippet': 'Winters and summers that have grown more extreme imperil a country’s herding tradition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ULAN BATOR, Mongolia — For all of his victories and skills, Genghis Khan always insisted that the god Tengri — the Eternal Blue Sky — deserved the credit for his triumphant success in uniting the vast Mongol Empire in the early 13th century. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23MONG/23MONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23MONG/23MONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23MONG/23MONG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23MONG/23MONG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23MONG/23MONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/23/science/23MONG/23MONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, '