t 450 employees and annual sales of about $77 million in Venezuela. Clorox, which is based in California, said in a statement that for nearly three years it had to sell more than two-thirds of its products at prices fixed by the government, even as high inflation caused its costs to rise sharply. It said recent price increases “were nowhere near sufficient.” Clorox sells bleach and other household cleaning products in Venezuela. Venezuela suffers from inflation of more than 60 percent a year and shortages of many basic goods, a situation that could be exacerbated by Clorox’s exit. President Nicolás Maduro, a socialist, says the economic woes are caused by capitalists and political opponents waging an economic war against the country. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Clorox Plans to Leave Over Price Controls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Clorox Plans to Leave Over Price Controls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cleansers, Detergents and Soaps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clorox Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-22T23:29:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c10837d-358b-50c8-af6c-99380ce5f607', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c10837d-358b-50c8-af6c-99380ce5f607'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Pareles, music critic for The New York Times, reviews Senator Bernard Sanders’s recently unearthed folk al