 — and thrilling for a merger-happy Wall Street.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/magazine/how-a-lopsided-recovery-fueled-the-dollar-store-wars.html', 'snippet': 'Times have been tough for discount retailers and their customers — and thrilling for a merger-happy Wall Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matthew Guzman has been shopping at the FamilyDollar store in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn, since he was a kid, but lately something feels different. The service has gotten worse, the lines have grown longer and shoppers have responded accordingly. “It used to be packed here,” Guzman told me on a recent Saturday. “But it died out.” Guzman, who finished high school this year and makes $9.50 an hour as an assistant manager at an outsourcing company, ought to be right in Family Dollar’s core customer group. But that day, he opted out. Cringing at the $4.25 price tag on a broom, he walked across the street to a local 99-cent store instead.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/magazine/28economy/28economy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/magazine/28economy/28economy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 761}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/magazine/28economy/28economy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 808, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/magazine/28economy/28economy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1772, 'width': 1397, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'