 Annexation', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-23T11:18:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70908d0c-7721-5eef-9933-8764ab3e1f04', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70908d0c-7721-5eef-9933-8764ab3e1f04'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama heads to New York on Tuesday morning to address world leaders just hours after opening a new front in the war against Islamic extremists with an aerial barrage in Syria. The fight against the Islamic State and his climate change policy will be high on Mr. Obama’s agenda this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/09/23/obama-faces-the-world-after-bombs-fall-in-syria/', 'snippet': 'President Obama heads to New York on Tuesday morning to address world leaders just hours after opening a new front in the war against Islamic extremists with an aerial barrage in Syria. The fight against the Islamic State and his climate change po...', 'lead_paragraph': 'PhotoFighters from the Nusra Front among destroyed buildings south of Damascus, Syria, on Monday. Airstrikes were focused on fighters from the Nusra Front in northern Idlib Province. Credit Rami Al-Sayed/Agence France-Presse — Getty Images', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Faces the World After Bombs Fall in Syria', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': Non