at.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/in-performance-andrew-rannells-and-stephen-trask-of-hedwig-and-the-angry-inch/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rannells, who plays the title character in the Broadway musical, sings the number “Midnight Radio,” accompanied by the show’s composer, Stephen Trask, on guitar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s video features the number “Midnight Radio” from the Broadway musical “Hedwig and the Angry Inch,” performed by the actor Andrew Rannells with the show’s composer, Stephen Trask, on guitar. Mr. Rannells, who replaced Neil Patrick Harris in the title role, is scheduled to star through Oct. 12, after which he will be replaced by Michael C. Hall. The show is at the Belasco Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Andrew Rannells and Stephen Trask of ‘Hedwig and the Angry Inch’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rannells, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trask, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-23T12:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a06893b9-d31c-544d-82f4-7e793cf5eb9f', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a06893b9-d31c-544d-82f4-7e793cf5eb9f'}, {'abstract': 'Numbers are among the most basic facts we report — and many corrections could be avoided if writers and editors took more care to make sure the numbers are right.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/do-the-math/', 'snippet': 'Numbers are among the most basic facts we report — and many corrections could be avoided if writers and editors took more care to make sure the numbers are right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like names and dates, numbers are among the most basic facts The Times reports — and getting those facts right is the foundation of our journalism. Many errors, and many blows to The Times’s credibility, could be avoided if writers and editors took more care to make sure the numbers are right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do the Math', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-23T12:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1571c28f-74da-564e-857e-ef251f69659c', 'word_count': 1570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1571c28f-74da-564e-857e-ef251f69659c'}, {'abstract': 'Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. will announce Tuesday that the federal government will end its fiscal year next week with 4,800 fewer prisoners, the first time since 1980 that the inmate population has declined from year to year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/09/23/federal-prison-population-drops-for-first-time-in-34-years/', 'snippet': 'Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. will announce Tuesday that the federal government will end its fiscal year next week with 4,800 fewer prisoners, the first time since 1980 that the inmate population has declined from year to year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal government will end its fiscal year next week with 4,800 fewer prisoners, the first time since 1980 that the inmate population has declined from year to year. Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. will trumpet the decline Tuesday and release Justice Department figures projecting a continued decline of 2,000 prisoners next year and 10,000 the following year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federal Prison Population Drops for First Time in 34 Years', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-23T12:01:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Apuzzo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Apuzzo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/109a991e-594b-5dae-8249-1be9dd73b54a', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/109a991e-594b-5dae-8249-1be9dd73b54a'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama will speak Tuesday morning regarding the strikes in Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/09/23/obama-to-speak-this-morning-on-syria/', 'snippet': 'President Obama will speak Tuesday morning regarding the strikes in Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 10:32 a.m. | President Obama on Tuesday hailed the American-led coalition that conducted airstrikes in Syria against the Islamic State on Monday night, declaring that “we’re going to do what is necessary to take the fight to this terrorist group.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Will Do ‘What Is Necessary’ to Fight ISIS, Obama Says', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': Non