anya Tagaq, an Inuit throat singer. The prize is 30,000 Canadian dollars (about $27,000). The four-hour concert can be seen on YouTube.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/arts/23artsbeat-polaris/23artsbeat-polaris-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/24/arts/23artsbeat-polaris/23artsbeat-polaris-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/arts/23artsbeat-polaris/23artsbeat-polaris-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/arts/23artsbeat-polaris/23artsbeat-polaris-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1393, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/arts/23artsbeat-polaris/23artsbeat-polaris-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/24/arts/23artsbeat-polaris/23artsbeat-polaris-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/arts/23artsbeat-polaris/23artsbeat-polaris-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tanya Tagaq Wins Canada’s Polaris Prize', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inuit Throat Singer Tops Drake, Arcade Fire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tagaq, Tanya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-23T16:58:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baaa8587-cefd-5cff-99ff-aeccb69f7691', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baaa8587-cefd-5cff-99ff-aeccb69f7691'}, {'abstract': 'The three companies said they would change practices like marketing to encourage less consumption of calorie-heavy drinks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/24/business/big-soda-companies-agree-on-effort-to-cut-americans-drink-calories.html', 'snippet': 'The three companies said they would change practices like marketing to encourage less consumption of calorie-heavy drinks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The three largest soda companies — Coca-Cola, PepsiCo and the Dr Pepper Snapple Group — have pledged to cut the number of sugary drink calories that Americans consume by one-fifth in about a decade, through a combination of marketing, distribution and packaging.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/business/BEVERAGE/BEVERAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1107, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/24/business/BEVERAGE/BEVERAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1107}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/business/BEVERAGE/BEVERAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 