nk': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beverages', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Snapple Beverage Corp', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-23T17:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/414cf84d-2bc0-570d-983e-f5d08b373cfc', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/414cf84d-2bc0-570d-983e-f5d08b373cfc'}, {'abstract': 'A few different ways of looking at our intervention.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/into-syria/', 'snippet': 'A few different ways of looking at our intervention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There isn’t that much to say, now that bombing has officially begun, that I didn’t say in my skeptical blog post following the president’s initial announcement of a wider war, and my skeptical Sunday column on the same subject. You can read Dan Drezner and Jeffrey Goldberg for cautiously pessimistic and cautiously optimistic takes, respectively; my colleagues David Kirkpatrick and Omar Al-Jawoshy have a not-entirely encouraging take on the tactical state of play in Iraq;\xa0Daniel Trombly and Yasir Abbas have a very interesting piece in The Daily Beast on what it would actually mean to degrade the Islamic State’s fighting capacity; and\xa0Dexter Filkins on the Kurds in the\xa0New Yorker is the higher-level must-read of the week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Into Syria', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense a