 shifts during Shakespeare’s “Antony and Cleopatra.” In a staging directed by Emily Mann at the McCarter Theater Center in Princeton, the only constant is the production itself — it’s always beautifully bold. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28NJARTS/28NJARTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28NJARTS/28NJARTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28NJARTS/28NJARTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28NJARTS/28NJARTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28NJARTS/28NJARTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28NJARTS/28NJARTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28NJARTS/28NJARTS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When in Love With an Egyptian Queen, Go Bold', 'kicker': 'Theater Review | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When in Love With an Egyptian Queen, Go Bold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaworowski, Ken', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McCarter Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Nicole Ari', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pritchett, Esau', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mann, Emily', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'ANTONY AND CLEOPATRA (PLAY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Princeton (NJ)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-23T18:43:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Jaworowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaworowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/69baa40b-dff9-5e7d-88ad-2cf10b5ac706', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69baa40b-dff9-5e7d-88ad-2cf10b5ac706'}, {'abstract': 'The hairstylist and photographer credit their early collaborative years as the starting-off point of their careers. Today, they celebrate their latest book, “Hair,” and talk to T about the evolution of their creative landscape, style gangs and fantasy hair.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/23/guido-palau-david-sims-interview-fashion-photography/', 'snippet': 'The hairstylist and photographer credit their early collaborative years as the starting-off point of their careers. Today, they celebrate their latest book, “Hair,” and talk to T about the evolution of their creative landscape, style gangs and fan...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fashion world often revolves around creative alliances. And in the case of the British photographer and T contributor David Sims and the hairstylist Guido Palau, early collaborations proved to be the spark that ignited their careers. Both hail from similar backgrounds, having grown up around “not sophisticated London,” as Palau describes it, listening to a lot of David Bowie, punk and New Wave music. They formed an easy friendship in the mid ’80s and soon teamed up behind the lens, building a portfolio of test pictures that would define their respective styles: Sims would often cast lanky kids off the street, letting them do whatever they felt like in front of the camera, while Palau created “non-hair” that was usually messy, unwashed and always offhandedly cool. The look was a precursor to grunge and quickly caught the attention of Calvin Klein, who hired the duo to shoot his CK campaign featuring Kate Moss in 1993. It was a pivotal moment for Sims and Palau, yet neither realized it at the time. “I didn’t think even for a minute we’d end up making anything like a living from it,” says Sims. “Or be successful,” adds Palau.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/t-magazine/23guido-molvar/23guido-molvar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/23/t-magazine/23guido-molvar/23guido-molvar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/t-magazine/23guido-molvar/23guido-molvar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/23/t-magazine/23guido-molvar/23guido-molvar-superJumbo.jpg'