says-beijing-paid-him-1-42-million/', 'snippet': 'Rafael Hui Si-yan, Hong Kong’s former chief secretary, testified that he received the money in late 2007 from a friend who said it was from “someone from Beijing” but refused to identify the donor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is being called one of the biggest corruption trials in Hong Kong’s history turned up an unexpected element when the city’s former No. 2 official said he received a secret payment of 11 million Hong Kong dollars, or $1.42 million, from Beijing, the local news media reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/world/24sino-HUI/24sino-HUI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/24/world/24sino-HUI/24sino-HUI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/world/24sino-HUI/24sino-HUI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/world/24sino-HUI/24sino-HUI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1456, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/world/24sino-HUI/24sino-HUI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/24/world/24sino-HUI/24sino-HUI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/world/24sino-HUI/24sino-HUI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height'