ate 225 years of legal history in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is one of the oldest, unofficial legal fraternities in the United States: lawyers who either currently or once worked as a federal prosecutor in Manhattan. And on Tuesday night, more than 700 former and current prosecutors got together for a birthday party that also posed a bit of security challenge for law enforcement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29BOOKSHELF/29BOOKSHELF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29BOOKSHELF/29BOOKSHELF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29BOOKSHELF/29BOOKSHELF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29BOOKSHELF/29BOOKSHELF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 991, 'width': 1480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29BOOKSHELF/29BOOKSHELF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29BOOKSHELF/29BOOKSHELF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29BOOKSHELF/29BOOKSHELF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Birthday Party, of Sorts, for U.S. Prosecutors in New York', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Courts (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Attorneys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bharara, Preet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comey, James B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuliani, Rudolph W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Mary Jo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T10:40:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fd12428-82ac-5295-abeb-a91846eb9e1b', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fd12428-82ac-5295-abeb-a91846eb9e1b'}, {'abstract': 'As one group of Kurds desperately flees from ISIS and into Turkey, another hopes with equal urgency to go in the other direction and fight the militants in Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/world/middleeast/syria-isis.html', 'snippet': 'As one group of Kurds desperately flees from ISIS and into Turkey, another hopes with equal urgency to go in the other direction and fight the militants in Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SURUC, Turkey — Turkish tanks dot the hills here, guarding against Islamic State militants advancing just across the Syrian border. Lines of police officers fan out across fields, brandishing shields to stem the flow of Syrian Kurds fleeing the militants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/25/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/25/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid a Maze of Alliances, Syrian Kurds Find a Thorny Refuge at the Border ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid a Maze of Alliances, Syrian Kurds Find a Thorny Refuge at the Border', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T10:54:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ced670d6-ed3e-566d-9e9f-1f32bb256ad1', 'word_count': 1283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ced670d6-ed3e-566d-9e9f-1f32bb256ad1'}, {'abstract': 'Denver students protesting a proposed anti-protest curriculum-review committee appear to have learned lessons about the value of questioning authority, and irony.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/24/civil-disorder-out-of-the-curriculum-and-into-the-streets/', 'snippet': 'Denver students protesting a proposed anti-protest curriculum-review committee appear to have learned lessons about the value of questioning authority, and irony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you tried yet to teach your children how to change the world? Told them stories of world changers, like Mohandas K. Gandhi or the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King, and how they led others in protest against the injustices they saw and believed society could not abide? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/us/ML-DENVER/ML-DENVER-articleLarge-v2.jpg',