 Heritage Foundation analysis claiming, among other things, that the plan would drive the unemployment rate down to 2.8 percent. (Heritage then tried, unsuccessfully, to send its nonsense down the memory hole and pretend it never happened.) Ryan defenders tried to claim that the plan didn’t actually rely on that Heritage stuff; but as some of us tried to explain, the plan actually didn’t add up, relying on a multi-trillion-dollar magic asterisk on tax receipts. And we predicted that sooner or later Ryan would embrace magical theories about how tax cuts increase revenue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charlatans and Cranks Forever', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T13:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f793b2c-3561-57d1-b757-8a39c3e0d562', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f793b2c-3561-57d1-b757-8a39c3e0d562'}, {'abstract': 'A new picture book says goodnight in a blissful pastoral setting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/24/books/go-to-sleep-little-farm-by-mary-lyn-ray.html', 'snippet': 'A new picture book says goodnight in a blissful pastoral setting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To be a modern bedtime story is to exist in the shadow of “Goodnight Moon.” That laconic little 1947 book is so indelible that after reading it to a child night after night for a few weeks, you feel Margaret Wise Brown’s cadences burrowed into your brain. It’s so subtly forceful that the flagrant red-and-green of Clement Hurd’s illustrations somehow never makes you think of Christmas, evoking instead the book’s own peculiar yet comforting universe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/books/24childrens/24childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 270, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/24/books/24childrens/24childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 270}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/books/24childrens/24childrens-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 461, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/books/24childrens/24childrens-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 922, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/books/24childrens/24childrens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/24/books/24childrens/24childrens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/books/24childrens/24childrens-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The World at Night', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ray, Mary Lyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neal, Christopher Silas', 'rank': 