like Burning Man,” explained the makeup maestro Peter Philips about the Dries Van Noten beauty look this morning. “She’s a little alternative and she loves nature.” His earthy vision — totally clean skin, “no mascara, no eyebrows and no blush” — worked harmoniously with the nearly 120-foot-long moss-inspired carpet that spanned the runway, not to mention the wild fauna prints that surfaced over breezy, bohemian silhouettes. There was, however, “one subtle beauty element,” he said. “It’s a subtle golden line drawn down the center of the lip that resembles a lip piercing when it catches the light.” Safer and far less painful than the real thing, Philips’ faux-metal adornment simply requires a slick of Make Up For Ever’s Aqua Liner in Diamond Gold, applied via a fine MAC eyeliner brush. Looking back to the Rodarte runway, where eyebrows were studded with clip-on hoops, it seems piercings are making their mark for spring 2015.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/t-magazine/24beauty-dries-rigg/24beauty-dries-rigg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/24/t-magazine/24beauty-dries-rigg/24beauty-dries-rigg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/t-magazine/24beauty-dries-rigg/24beauty-dries-rigg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/t-magazine/24beauty-dries-rigg/24beauty-dries-rigg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non