'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Reporters Working on Pool End-Around', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'White House Correspondents Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T18:46:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed73a514-a909-5c8b-804e-42b54d9c6ee0', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed73a514-a909-5c8b-804e-42b54d9c6ee0'}, {'abstract': 'A decision to punt or kick on fourth-and-short often means you have to face a tougher fourth-down play later in the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/upshot/a-lesson-in-risk-management-in-a-jets-defeat.html', 'snippet': 'A decision to punt or kick on fourth-and-short often means you have to face a tougher fourth-down play later in the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in the fourth quarter of Monday night’s game between the Jets and the Bears, Coach Rex Ryan found himself with a difficult fourth-down decision. The Jets were down by 8 points and facing a fourth-and-2 at the Bears’ 24-yard line. There were 9 minutes 56 seconds remaining — plenty of time. Ryan did what coaches do more than 80 percent of the time in those situations: He sent out his kicker. Nick Folk kicked the field goal successfully, cutting the Bears’ lead to 5.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/upshot/25up-b