ling countries to “prevent” and “suppress” their citizens from traveling abroad to join terrorist organizations. President Obama, who led the meeting, said it was only the sixth time since the Council first met in 1946 that it held a session with so many member states’ top leaders. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Security Council Passes Resolution to Thwart Foreign Fighters', 'kicker': 'United Nations General Assembly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T20:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d363d17-bf27-5bcc-8056-72013f23cb30', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d363d17-bf27-5bcc-8056-72013f23cb30'}, {'abstract': 'The suspension is for Rosh Hashana.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/24/new-york-parking-alert-alternate-side-rules-suspended-thursday-and-friday/', 'snippet': 'The suspension is for Rosh Hashana.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because of Rosh Hashana, alternate-side street-cleaning regulations will be suspended in New York City on Thursday and Friday. Other regulations will remain in effect.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Parking Alert: Alternate-Side Rules Suspended Thursday and Friday', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rosh Hashana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_