ous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grass', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T20:43:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Barro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/360f5097-1568-5719-9fd7-3b5941e12cf3', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/360f5097-1568-5719-9fd7-3b5941e12cf3'}, {'abstract': 'The creative director Alessandro Dell’Acqua’s ’70s-inspired frocks were paired with the most laid-back of hairstyles on today’s spring 2015 runway.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/24/paris-fashion-week-spring-2015-rochas-ponytail/', 'snippet': 'The creative director Alessandro Dell’Acqua’s ’70s-inspired frocks were paired with the most laid-back of hairstyles on today’s spring 2015 runway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the spring 2015 Rochas fashion show in Paris today, the brand’s creative director, Alessandro Dell’Acqua, unveiled dreamy designs, including printed white dresses that look like they could have been plucked from the late ’70s (the way it looked in Sofia Coppola’s “Virgin Suicides”). Against all the embroidered flowers and lacy details, the simple ponytails — parted to the side and tied low on the back of the head — felt appropriately laid-back and youthful.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/t-magazine/24do-rochas-gilchrist/24do-rochas-gilchrist-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/24/t-magazine/24do-roc