nited-nations/', 'snippet': 'Competing speeches at the United Nations by various Middle Eastern rivals that are also United States allies underscored the Obama administration’s delicate task in balancing competing interests in the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether they bumped into each other back stage could not be confirmed. But the General Assembly on Wednesday afternoon saw a parade of regional rivals coming in quick succession to the podium. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Middle East Rivals Trade Rhetorical Jabs at United Nations', 'kicker': 'United Nations General Assembly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T20:48:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e62aa007-2d06-5183-9d81-a8113780de45', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e62aa007-2d06-5183-9d81-a8113780de45'}, {'abstract': 'The insider trading case against Michael A. Lucarelli, a former executive at Lippert/Heilshorn and Associates, was relatively minor. But he got attention for running barefoot from the court in August.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/24/ex-investor-relations-executive-pleads-guilty-to-insider-trading/', 'snippet': 'The insider trading case against Michael A. Lucarelli, a former executive at Lippert/Heilshorn and Associates, was relatively minor. But he got attention for running barefoot from the court in August.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael A. Lucarelli, a former executive at an investor relations agency, admitted on Wednesday to insider trading based on information in news releases that had not yet been released.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/business/dbpix-lucarelli/dbpix-lucarelli-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/25/business/dbpix-lucarelli/dbpix-lucarelli-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/business/dbpix-lucarelli/dbpix-lucarelli-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/business/dbpix-lucarelli/dbpix-lucarelli-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/business/dbpix-lucarelli/dbpix-lucarelli-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/25/business/dbpix-lucarelli/dbpix-lucarelli-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/business/dbpix-lucarelli/dbpix-lucarelli-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Investor Relations Executive Pleads Guilty to Insider Trading', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bharara, Preet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucarelli, Michael A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lippert/Heilshorn and Associates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T20:48:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3eaf99d-fc1f-53c3-9115-c66baa11eba5', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3eaf99d-fc1f-53c3-9115-c66baa11eba5'}, {'abstract': 'The former “Jersey Shore” star Mike Sorrentino, who was indicted on tax fraud charges, did plenty of things to avoid taxes that were perfectly legal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/upshot/what-the-indictment-of-the-situation-tells-us-about-the-tax-code.html', 'snippet': 'The former “Jersey Shore” star Mike Sorrentino, who was indicted on tax fraud charges, did plenty of things to avoid taxes that were perfectly legal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Somehow, the most shocking thing about the indictment of Michael Sorrentino for tax fraud is not that the “Jersey Shore” star may have been less than punctilious about paying the taxman. After all, Mr. Sorrentino, known as “The Situation,” has never projected the levelheaded public image you’d associate with careful income tax compliance. (Here is a video in which he slams his head into a wall. Here is the 911 call from when he was in a brawl at a tanning salon).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/upshot/25up-situatio