roit-designs-and-pride.html', 'snippet': 'Michele Varian honors her Detroit roots with a pop-up shop selling Motor City merchandise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michele Varian is hosting a pop-up shop in the basement of her Howard Street store, left, featuring goods from about 20 Detroit companies. A Detroit native, Ms. Varian said her origins have always been a “point of pride, before it was cool to the rest of the world.” The designs for sale include furniture by Alex Drew & No One; vessels by Adora Bella Ceramics, bottom right; metalwork from Smith Shop, top right; and terrariums by Lead Head Glass. Simply being made in Detroit did not qualify an object for admission, Ms. Varian emphasized; the goods also had to meet her rigorous style standards. “Everything in the show is something I’d buy for the store,” she said.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR8/25CURR8-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR8/25CURR8-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR8/25CURR8-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR8/25CURR8-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1445, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR8/25CURR8-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR8/25CURR8-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR8/25CURR8-thumbLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of Detroit, Designs and Pride', 'kicker': 'Currents: Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out of Detroit, Designs and Pride', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suqi, Rima', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Varian, Michele', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Built (Manhattan, NY, Retail Store)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop-Up Stores and Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T22:13:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fca0999-5286-55cc-a912-98ebe54123ee', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fca0999-5286-55cc-a912-98ebe54123ee'}, {'abstract': 'The Nova duvet cover from Crane & Canopy succeeds in simplifying a tedious chore.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/garden/fewer-hero-points-for-bed-making-husbands.html', 'snippet': 'The Nova duvet cover from Crane & Canopy succeeds in simplifying a tedious chore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having lived in Switzerland, where he mastered the domestic arts by osmosis, my husband is a superior bed maker. I put him in charge of testing the Crane & Canopy Nova duvet cover, which promises to cut the time it takes to make your bed by 80 percent. The sample we received, Hayes Nova Grey, unfolded into a lustrous field of 400-thread-count, charcoal-colored cotton with white piping. A white panel about a foot wide was layered over the top, mimicking the look of a folded flat sheet while concealing a zipper. Using the standard inversion method, my husband turned the fabric envelope inside out, reached inside, plucked two corners of our duvet and gave a mighty shake. A tuck, a zip, a toss and some smoothing, and the bed was made, looking far more finished than usual. Time: 1 minute 44 seconds. A queen-size cover is $149; king, $169; matching shams, $60 a pair. Information: 888-686-8586 or craneandcanopy.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR2/25CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR2/25CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR2/25CURR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR2/25CURR2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR2/25CURR2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR2/25CURR2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR2/25CURR2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fewer Hero Points for Bed-Making Husbands', 'kicker': 'Currents: Road Test', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fewer Hero Points for Bed-Making Husbands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beds and Bedding', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crane & Canopy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T22:13:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0232570-9a97-5527-9250-ec5f15c11378', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0232570-9a97-5527-9250-ec5f15c11378'}, {'abstract': 'Stair Galleries in Hudson, N.Y., is auctioning highlights from the collections of Ashton Hawkins and Johnnie Moore.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/garden/art-from-classic-to-quirky.html', 'snippet': 'Stair Galleries in Hudson, N.Y., is auctioning highlights from the collections of Ashton Hawkins and Johnnie Moore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday, Stair Galleries in Hudson, N.Y., will offer highlights from the wildly diverse collections of Ashton Hawkins, the Metropolitan Museum of Art’s former counsel, and his husband, Johnnie Moore, from the couple’s homes in Manhattan and Athens, N.Y. The trove includes 18th- and 19th-century Russian silver, classical bronzes, Victorian and modern furniture and contemporary works by Jasper Johns, Alfred Stieglitz, Helen Frankenthaler, Paul Cadmus and David Hockney. On the block will be a screen-printed Campbell’s Soup Can T-shirt signed by Andy Warhol, a gift from the artist that is estimated to fetch $1,000 to $1,500; “Sin,” an unusual screen print ($6,000 to $10,000) by Ed Ruscha; a quirky portrait of Alfred Hitchcock by Hunt Slonem ($4,000 to $6,000); and Alfred Stieglitz’s “Steerage,” a large-format photogravure dated 1907 that has been hailed as one of the finest and earliest works of modernism in photography ($12,000 to $18,000). Information: 518-751-1000 or stairgalleries.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR3/25CURR3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR3/25CURR3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 660}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR3/25CURR3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 931, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR3/25CURR3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1817, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR3/25CURR3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR3/25CURR3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/garden/25CURR3/25CURR3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art, From Classic to Quirky', 'kicker': 'Currents: Events', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art, From Classic to Quirky', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawkins, Ashton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Johnnie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stair Galleries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T22:14:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Mason', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mason', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6f68de4-47f5-5bb5-a0bb-fed45d003020', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6f68de4-47f5-5bb5-a0bb-fed45d003020'}, {'abstract': 'For “Not I,” one of three solo Beckett pieces she will perform in Brooklyn, Lisa Dwan performs while immobilized in straps and metal brackets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/theater/lisa-dwan-performs-solo-at-bam-in-3-beckett-plays.html', 'snippet': 'For “Not I,” one of three solo Beckett pieces she will perform in Brooklyn, Lisa Dwan performs while immobilized in straps and metal brackets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMBRIDGE, ENGLAND — First comes a layer of thick black grease, applied from the neck to just below the eyes. The lips are carefully painted red. Then a blindfold, then clinging black fabric wrapped around the head. At that point, Lisa Dwan is guided up steps to a wooden board, her arms pinioned through metal brackets on each side, her head fitted into a small opening and secured in place by thick straps that cover her ears. Unable to see, unable to hear, she takes a deep breath and opens her mouth.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DWAN1/28DWAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DWAN1/28DWAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 668}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DWAN1/28DWAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DWAN1/28DWAN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2002, 'width': 1799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DWAN1/28DWAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DWAN1/28DWAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DWAN1/28DWAN1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 15