oor until the sun was starting to rise,” he told his audience, adding that he “passed out to the gentle vibrations of thumping electronic music for three to four hours.”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' The Progeny of Burning Man ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Progeny of Burning Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Burning Man Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meditation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-24T22:38:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Allison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd92aafc-957e-5590-90a1-677bd61d3d4d', 'word_count': 1353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd92aafc-957e-5590-90a1-677bd61d3d4d'}, {'abstract': 'Rabbis serve in remote areas during High Holy Days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/fashion/rabbis-who-travel-to-remote-congregations-on-the-high-holy-days.html', 'snippet': 'Rabbis serve in remote areas during High Holy Days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rabbi Rami Schwartzer, a Connecticut-born fourth-year rabbinical student at Jewish Theological Seminary in New York, won’t be spending the High Holy Days as he usually does. Instead, he has traveled nearly 1,600 miles to spend the Jewish New Year, which began Wednesday evening, in Cypress, Tex., leading services for