one, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d3c98b2-1907-502a-b42e-9249c33b65ea', 'word_count': 1207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d3c98b2-1907-502a-b42e-9249c33b65ea'}, {'abstract': 'Israel experiments with modern observances of the Jewish “shmita,” a traditional rest period for farmers that comes every seventh year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/world/middleeast/25israel.html', 'snippet': 'Israel experiments with modern observances of the Jewish “shmita,” a traditional rest period for farmers that comes every seventh year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — The printers at Energiya Global sit idle as the company, which promotes solar power in developing countries, tries to go paperless. Energiya is also throwing open the doors to its funky, colorful headquarters for yoga workshops and Talmud classes. And instead of ordering in for the weekly staff lunch, employees this year will rotate cooking duties, donating the savings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Israel, Values of a Holy Respite Are Adapted for a High-Tech World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Israel, Values of a Holy Respite Are Adapted for a High-Tech World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-25T00:16:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middl