ment', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-25T00:31:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ivory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/445c9fb8-486b-5911-ac16-3e609de8641b', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/445c9fb8-486b-5911-ac16-3e609de8641b'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio of New York, a virtual unknown not so long ago, is now determined to cultivate a profile on the international stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/nyregion/de-blasio-walks-tightrope-between-municipal-politics-and-international-influence.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio of New York, a virtual unknown not so long ago, is now determined to cultivate a profile on the international stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He has bonded with the socialist mayor of Paris, tutoring her on the nuances of the American term “retrofit.” He has met with Italy’s foreign minister three times in the past four months. This week, he walked in the People’s Climate March in Manhattan alongside the United Nations secretary general and talked shop with the leaders of Buenos Aires, Melbourne and Rio de Janeiro.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/nyregion/DEBLASIO/DEBLASIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/25/nyregion/DEBLASIO/DEBLASIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/25/nyregion/DEBLASIO/DEBLASIO-ju