rticle/8e584ea1-4fa5-5c53-bb12-ea536e392442'}, {'abstract': 'The Treasury Department announced sanctions on 11 individuals and one organization it said helped finance the flow of fighters for terrorist groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/world/middleeast/treasury-imposes-terrorism-sanctions-on-those-linked-to-islamic-state.html', 'snippet': 'The Treasury Department announced sanctions on 11 individuals and one organization it said helped finance the flow of fighters for terrorist groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Treasury Department on Wednesday imposed sanctions on 11 people and one entity it said were sending financial and other support to terrorist groups, including the Islamic State. The sanctions are aimed at the funding streams that have allowed the terrorist organizations to flourish and recruit fighters from the Middle East, Europe and North Africa.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Imposes Terrorism Sanctions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Imposes Terrorism Sanctions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Julie Hirschfeld', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jemaah Islamiyah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Batirashvili, Tarkhan Tayumurazovich', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-25T00:45:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Hirschfeld Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'Hirschfeld', 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d70996d1-b461-59d4-89cd-a93fcb67b884', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d70996d1-b461-59d4-89cd-a93fcb67b884'}, {'abstract': 'Islamic State militants on Wednesday blew up an important site in early Christianity known as the Green Church in Tikrit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/world/middleeast/iraq-militants-destroy-historic-church.html', 'snippet': 'Islamic State militants on Wednesday blew up an important site in early Christianity known as the Green Church in Tikrit.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Islamic State militants on Wednesday blew up an important site in early Christianity known as the Green Church in Tikrit. The group, also known as ISIS, has driven thousands of Christians and other religious minorities from their homes as it has consolidated its hold on a broad section of Syria and Iraq. It has destroyed or defaced several historic churches as well as many Muslim shrines that it considers prohibited by its puritanical version of Islam. After capturing the city of Mosul this summer, the Islamic State’s fighters took a sledgehammer to the tomb of the biblical figure Jonah. It replaced the cross above the historic St. Ephrem’s Cathedral in Mosul with its black jihadi flag, and it also destroyed a statue of the Virgin Mary. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Militants Destroy Historic Church', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Militants Destroy Historic Church', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tikrit (Iraq)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Churches (Buildings)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-25T00:56:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/283e83fd-9e88-5dba-b2a4-98986f6baee4', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/283e83fd-9e88-5dba-b2a4-98986f6baee4'}, {'abstract': 'Climate change is the new unmentionable these days on Capitol Hill and in state capitols.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/opinion/gail-collins-the-politics-of-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'Climate change is the new unmentionable these days on Capitol Hill and in state capitols.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Miami Beach, rising sea levels have interesting consequences. The ocean periodically starts bubbling up through local drainpipes. By the time it’s over, the concept of “going down to the water” has extended to stepping off the front porch. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': '