op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/readers-respond-on-long-term-unemployment/', 'snippet': 'Readers wrote on parables, responsibility and balance in comments on Paul Krugman’s Op-Ed “Those Lazy Jobless.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Given the almost religious fervor, it might have been a debate about old-fashioned creation theology.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Respond: On Long-Term Unemployment', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-25T15:36:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marie Tessier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tessier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6367a5a6-61a3-5afe-b772-5cdc63f7bd82', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6367a5a6-61a3-5afe-b772-5cdc63f7bd82'}, {'abstract': 'The search engine Yossarian is supposed to increase creativity. I decided to test it out.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/i-tried-to-make-a-search-engine-write-me-a-poem/', 'snippet': 'The search engine Yossarian is supposed to increase creativity. I decided to test it out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before I started writing this, I took a creativity test. Many different such tests exist, but I took one of the best-known ones: Guilford’s Alternative Uses Task, which simply requires that you come up with as many applications for a particular object as possible. I picked a paper coffee cup. After 10\xa0minutes (an amount of time I’d arbitrarily chosen), I had 39 uses, from the prosaic (“hold coffee”) to the probably impractical (“poke holes in the bottom and it could be a shower head for a short amount of time before it collapses”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mul