011fa'}, {'abstract': 'City epidemiologists, who interviewed stricken employees and analyzed blood samples, discovered that The Times had come down with Legionnaires’ disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/09/25/1985-an-illness-at-the-times/', 'snippet': 'City epidemiologists, who interviewed stricken employees and analyzed blood samples, discovered that The Times had come down with Legionnaires’ disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the era of meta media coverage, it wasn’t surprising when problems this week with the filtered water system at The Times’s Manhattan headquarters — problems linked to three employees’ brief illnesses — earned the notice of news sites like Gawker and Daily Intelligencer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/blogs/water1/water1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 554, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/24/blogs/water1/water1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 554}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/blogs/water1/water1-jumbo.png', 'height': 599, 'width': 649, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/blogs/water1/water1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 599, 'width': 649, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/blogs/water1/water1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/24/blogs/water1/water1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge',