0-8421-5ba3-8cad-c86fcfc944f3'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Kenya struggles with Somali guerrillas in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/1964-kenya-battling-somali-rebels/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Kenya struggles with Somali guerrillas in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GARISSA, Kenya — A few hundred armed fanatics have paralyzed normal life in almost half of Kenya since it attained independence in December. These tough guerrillas are Somalis, bent on forcing the Kenya government to cede to the neighboring Somali Republic the Somali-occupied northeastern part of Kenya in which about 250,000 of their countrymen live. There is no doubt in Nairobi that the Somali government in Mogadishu provided the terrorists with arms, ammunition and other supplies. There are about 800 of these so-called ‘‘Shifta,’’ operating in small groups of 30 or 40 men. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 26, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Kenya Battling Somali Rebels', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nairobi (Kenya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-25T17:14:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cbddbe9-8e5d-505f-9559-ccf2957ba215', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://articl