-5be0-81f7-428e51ebf8e8', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f87e17f7-c329-5be0-81f7-428e51ebf8e8'}, {'abstract': '“Lilting” centers on a young man’s attempts to communicate with a Cambodian-Chinese woman whose son, who recently died, was his lover.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/movies/lilting-about-a-divide-between-bereaved-strangers.html', 'snippet': '“Lilting” centers on a young man’s attempts to communicate with a Cambodian-Chinese woman whose son, who recently died, was his lover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lachrymose British drama “Lilting” pivots on the prickly relationship between two people who are mourning a third. Junn (Cheng Pei Pei) is a Cambodian-Chinese woman who can’t understand English, and Richard (Ben Whishaw) is a plaster saint who struggles and struggles to be understood. With infinite patience, moist eyes and trembling lips and lashes, Richard attempts to overcome the differences — linguistic, cultural, generational and temperamental — between him and Junn, who doesn’t grasp that he also loved her dead son, Kai (Andrew Leung). ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stubborn Mother and Her Supplicant', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stubborn Mother and Her Supplicant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khaou, Hong', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whishaw, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lilting (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-25T21:24:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organizatio