', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37b27a4e-b31b-55cc-a8cd-7a047777235d'}, {'abstract': 'Victoria Siddall will become director of the Frieze art fairs in New York and London; the co-founders Amanda Sharp and Matthew Slotover will “explore new projects for Frieze.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/25/frieze-art-fair-founders-step-aside-for-a-new-director/', 'snippet': 'Victoria Siddall will become director of the Frieze art fairs in New York and London; the co-founders Amanda Sharp and Matthew Slotover will “explore new projects for Frieze.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In a surprise move, Frieze art fair announced on Thursday that in 2015 Victoria Siddall will become director of Frieze London and Frieze New York.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frieze Art Fair Founders Step Aside for a New Director', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frieze Art Fairs Choose New Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frieze Art Fair', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-25T21:39:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2ce9d23-4440-5903-9d83-fd078fc7bccd', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2ce9d23-4440-5903-9d83-fd078fc7bccd'}, {'abstract': 'Opening with “Gone Girl,” the New York Film Festival includes a 3-D film by Godard and many other provocative titles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/movies/a-brief-look-at-10-new-york-film-festival-features.html', 'snippet': 'Opening with “Gone Girl,” the New York Film Festival includes a 3-D film by Godard and many other provocative titles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each of the world’s major film festivals has a special flavor and purpose. Some arrange the crown jewels of world cinema in a fancy European setting. Others line up horses for the Oscar race or parade indie darlings through the snow. The New York Film Festival, whose 52nd edition begins on Friday, takes its name and inspiration from the world capital of talk, and its clear and consistent ambition has been to start as many arguments as possible.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grab Some Popcorn, Settle Down, Start Debating', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grab Some Popcorn, Settle Down, Start Debating', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Film Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-25T21:41:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a881f0f-ccd5-5860-9d9a-c1b6358ec7ac', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a881f0f-ccd5-5860-9d9a-c1b6358ec7ac'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary “Print the Legend” follows tech-savvy entrepreneurs in the world of 3-D printers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/movies/print-the-legend-looks-at-3-d-printers.html', 'snippet': 'The documentary “Print the Legend” follows tech-savvy entrepreneurs in the world of 3-D printers