-led airstrikes in Syria, it was increasingly uncertain whether the United States could punish terrorist groups without aiding President Bashar al-Assad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/world/middleeast/clashing-goals-in-syria-strikes-put-us-in-fix.html', 'snippet': 'On the third day of American-led airstrikes in Syria, it was increasingly uncertain whether the United States could punish terrorist groups without aiding President Bashar al-Assad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — President Obama said the American-led airstrikes in Syria were intended to punish the terror organizations that threatened the United States — but would do nothing to aid President Bashar al-Assad of Syria, who is at war with the same groups.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clashing Goals in Syria Strikes Bedevil Obama', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clashing Goals in Syria Strikes Bedevil Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United Arab Emirates', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T01:06:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Hubbard and Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6168f945-c4b5-559a-a645-801d8864ffe8', 'word_count': 1434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6168f945-c4b5-559a-a645-801d8864ffe8'}, {'abstract': 'The city leaders agreed that Kevyn D. Orr, Detroit’s emergency manager, would continue his role until bankruptcy proceedings were done, but that he would cede the rest of his authority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/us/detroits-leaders-regain-some-power.html', 'snippet': 'The city leaders agreed that Kevyn D. Orr, Detroit’s emergency manager, would continue his role until bankruptcy proceedings were done, but that he would cede the rest of his authority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — The mayor and City Council of Detroit regained most of their decision-making authority on Thursday, a symbolic milestone in a financially beleaguered city that cleared the way for an end to nearly 18 tense months of oversight by a state-appointed emergency manager.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/us/DETROIT/DETROIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/26/us/DETROIT/DETROIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/us/DETROIT/DETROIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name':