acquisition spree to help reinvent itself and regain relevance. But the company’s previous takeover efforts have yielded few obvious gains, leaving shareholders more eager to receive the bulk of the cash rather than see it used for acquisitions. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Yahoo’s Decision Point', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T11:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c4891be-a56f-56ce-b8ca-1bd6a8ce0f04', 'word_count': 2129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c4891be-a56f-56ce-b8ca-1bd6a8ce0f04'}, {'abstract': 'Some recommendations from the students of Jan Bone, an 83-year-old New York Times reader who has been teaching for 42 years — the last two online.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/nytlnreads-recommendations-from-students-in-an-online-course-at-roosevelt-university/', 'snippet': 'Some recommendations from the students of Jan Bone, an 83-year-old New York Times reader who has been teaching for 42 years — the last two online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We recently introduced a new feature, NYTLNreads, and are inviting teachers and students everywhere to participate by simply telling us what you’ve been reading in The Times recently, and why you’d recommend it to others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/learning/RooseveltNYTLN/RooseveltNYTLN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name':