elationship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/movies/talking-to-justin-kauflin.html', 'snippet': 'The rising pianist Justin Kauflin talks about this mentor, the trumpeter Clark Terry, and a documentary detailing their relationship.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Dear Justin,” an elderly man recites, “challenges are a part of life, as you know. Your mind is a powerful asset. Use it for positive thoughts and you’ll learn what I learned. I believe in your talents and I believe in you.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28SUBSNAPSHOT/28SUB-SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28SUBSNAPSHOT/28SUB-SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28SUBSNAPSHOT/28SUB-SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28SUBSNAPSHOT/28SUB-SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28SUBSNAPSHOT/28SUB-SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28SUBSNAPSHOT/28SUB-SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28SUBSNAPSHOT/28SUB-SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Something in Common With His Mentor ', 'kicker': 'Snapshot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Something in Common With His Mentor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shattuck, Kathryn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hicks, Alan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T12:10:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Kathryn', 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20194f97-10b0-5a9b-ba29-eff218e18c78', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20194f97-10b0-5a9b-ba29-eff218e18c78'}, {'abstract': 'As “The Good Lie,” a film about Lost Boys who begin new lives in America, finally opens, one of the actors reflects on his own long, strange trip from Sudan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/movies/the-actor-ger-duany-reflects-on-his-journey-from-sudan.html', 'snippet': 'As “The Good Lie,” a film about Lost Boys who begin new lives in America, finally opens, one of the actors reflects on his own long, strange trip from Sudan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST HOLLYWOOD, Calif. — By the age of 14, Ger Duany had wandered barefoot for hundreds of miles through his native Sudan, spent four years in Ethiopian refugee camps and fought as a child soldier. On one occasion, he walked for so long that all his toenails fell off; on another, he fled from soldiers by swimming across a river choked with corpses. But Mr. Duany, one of thousands of so-called Lost Boys left homeless by a Sudanese civil war that began in the 1980s, isn’t one to complain. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DUANY1/28DUANY1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DUANY1/28DUANY1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DUANY1/28DUANY1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DUANY1/28DUANY1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1013, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DUANY1/28DUANY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DUANY1/28DUANY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28DUANY1/28DUANY1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Longer Lost, He’s Taking the Lead ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Longer Lost, He’s Taking the Lead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Good Lie (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duany, Ger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T12:17:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Ito', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ito', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edfe9d3c-6d49-5e6c-852f-a47ff370930d', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edfe9d3c-6d49-5e6c-852f-a47ff370930d'}, {'abstract': '“The Big Chill,” out in a new dual-edition release, may have set out to lament the end of the hippie era but in some ways celebrated the arrival of the yuppie age instead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/movies/homevideo/the-big-chill-returns-in-a-dual-edition-release.html', 'snippet': '“The Big Chill,” out in a new dual-edition release, may have set out to lament the end of the hippie era but in some ways celebrated the arrival of the yuppie age instead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some movies are born significant, some achieve significance, and some have significance thrust upon them — not always in the way their makers would have wished. An intended lament for the death of the hippie, “The Big Chill” (1983), directed and written (with Barbara Benedek) by Lawrence Kasdan, celebrated the birth of the yuppie instead.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/arts/28HOBERMAN1/28HOBERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xla