ing a break from her tour to support her latest album, “I Never Learn.” A remix of the album track “Gunshot” appears exclusively here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/lykke-li-interview-latest-album-gunshot-song-stream/', 'snippet': 'The Swedish indie pop singer spoke during a break from her tour to support her latest album, “I Never Learn.” A remix of the album track “Gunshot” appears exclusively here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since bursting on the scene with her 2008 album “Youth Novels,” the Swedish chanteuse Lykke Li has carved out a niche with her mix of pulsating beats, hypnotic rhythms and coquettish vocals. But 2014 is serving as a banner year for the 28-year-old. In May, she released her third album, “I Never Learn,” which spawned the hit singles “No Rest for the Wicked” and “Gunshot” (a remix of which, by the Swedish producer Chords, premieres here). She also just kicked off a nationwide tour (which hits Radio City Music Hall on October 4) and is gearing up for an upcoming collaboration with the Swedish clothing line & Other Stories, which opens its first stateside store next month in SoHo. Here, Li talks about “I Never Learn,” appearing on U2’s new album and personal hygiene.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/t-magazine/24lykke-hyman/24lykke-hyman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/24/t-magazine/24lykke-hyman/24lykke-hyman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/24/t-magazine/24lykke-hyman/24lykke-hyman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'captio