o renew its agreement with the Confucius Institute, a global network of Chinese government-affiliated language and culture centers.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/university-of-chicagos-relations-with-confucius-institute-sour/', 'snippet': 'The University of Chicago has suspended negotiations to renew its agreement with the Confucius Institute, a global network of Chinese government-affiliated language and culture centers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The University of Chicago has suspended negotiations to renew its agreement with the Confucius Institute, a global network of Chinese government-affiliated language and culture centers, in a setback for the controversial program ahead of its 10th anniversary on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/world/26sino-CONFUCIUS/26sino-CONFUCIUS-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 15, 'width': 258, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/world/26sino-CONFUCIUS/26sino-CONFUCIUS-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 15, 'width': 258, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'University of Chicago’s Relations With Confucius Institute Sour', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese Language', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Changchun', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Confucius Institutes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Chicago', 'rank':