.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/27/fashion/paris-fashion-week-dior-lanvin-nina-ricci-rick-owens.html', 'snippet': 'Collections from Raf Simons at Dior, Alber Elbaz at Lanvin, Peter Copping at Nina Ricci and Rick Owens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — It’s hard not to wonder sometimes, as we sit idly by waiting for a show to start in, say, the Tuileries (where Nina Ricci was held) or the École des Beaux-Arts (Lanvin) or a hidden courtyard of the Louvre (Dior) or the Palais de Chaillot (Rick Owens) — or, indeed, any of the many historic French institutions where prêt-à-porter can be found — what Marine Le Pen, leader of the far-right National Front, preacher of “France for the French,” euro-skeptic and increasingly popular potential presidential candidate, would think.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/fashion/27dior-A/27dior-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/27/fashion/27dior-A/27dior-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/fashion/27dior-A/27dior-A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/fashion/27dior-A/27dior-A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1260, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/fashion/27dior-A/27dior-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images