baf6-f65d5f5cfcee', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82db37a5-9555-506c-baf6-f65d5f5cfcee'}, {'abstract': 'David Benjamin Sherry hauled his large-format 8-by-10 camera into Death Valley last year and to capture the desert light on film. One of the resulting images now illuminates the cover for the Sept. 28 Voyages Issue.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/under-cover-desert-voyages-in-colored-hues/', 'snippet': 'David Benjamin Sherry hauled his large-format 8-by-10 camera into Death Valley last year and to capture the desert light on film. One of the resulting images now illuminates the cover for the Sept. 28 Voyages Issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deserts are places for pilgrims and mystics, settings for odysseys and renewals, spaces to journey through and be changed by. You can see the light there. The photographer David Benjamin Sherry hauled his large-format 8-by-10 camera into Death Valley last year and brought back some of that light on film. Then he went into the darkroom and, using color, added his own light, his own emotions — “to instill fear or joy,” in his words. One of the resulting images now illuminates the cover for the Sept. 28 Voyages Issue. Sherry’s images belong to a larger body of work, “Wonderful Land,” for which he spent months visiting well-known vistas around the West. His landscapes, colorized with hues not seen in nature, conjure clarity and disorientation, making the familiar strange again — which just happens to be what all good voyages do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/magazine/28cover_type/28cover_type-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/magazine/28cover_type/28cover_type-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 731}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 