ittee make the report public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sepp Blatter, the president of FIFA, insisted Friday that an investigative report into the bidding for the 2018 and 2022 World Cups should remain private, despite growing pressure for its release from inside and outside soccer’s world governing body.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/sports/27fifa-1/27fifa-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/27/sports/27fifa-1/27fifa-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/sports/27fifa-1/27fifa-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/sports/27fifa-1/27fifa-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1409, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/sports/27fifa-1/27fifa-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/27/sports/27fifa-1/27fifa-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/sports/27fifa-1/27fifa-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'FIFA’s Sepp Blatter Says Corruption Report Will Remain Secret', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cup Report to Stay Private', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Michael J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blatter, Sepp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gulati, Sunil', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2018 (Soccer)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2022 (Soccer)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T18:48:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0f1d000-e407-536f-8946-1bee22f2f800', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0f1d000-e407-536f-8946-1bee22f2f800'}, {'abstract': 'In five seasons of playing Lucky Luciano on HBO’s “Boardwalk Empire,” Mr. Piazza never had to shoot scenes on a Sunday. A native of Queens, he currently lives in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/nyregion/vincent-piazza-40-blocks-from-home-but-a-world-away.html', 'snippet': 'In five seasons of playing Lucky Luciano on HBO’s “Boardwalk Empire,” Mr. Piazza never had to shoot scenes on a Sunday. A native of Queens, he currently lives in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In five seasons of playing Lucky Luciano on HBO’s “Boardwalk Empire,” Vincent Piazza never had to shoot scenes on a Sunday. “Sunday is a reflective day, a thoughtful day,” he said. Now, with the show heading toward a promised bloody end later this fall, Mr. Piazza has plenty to reflect on, including, as of earlier this year, a new neighborhood to call home. A native of Queens, Mr. Piazza, 38, speaks with a New York brio that makes a 40-block move sound like a journey across temperate zones. His new home, which he shares with his girlfriend of a year and a half and a miniature longhaired dachshund, is near the Ed Koch Queensboro Bridge. But Queens is not too far away. “It’s a pretty incredible thing to know I can walk across the bridge and end up there if I ever need to,” he said.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-thumbL