': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fddb1a4-9cc3-5bfd-b126-7882d819204b', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fddb1a4-9cc3-5bfd-b126-7882d819204b'}, {'abstract': 'The former New Yorker fell in love with the Rio Grande Valley, collecting the ballads and poems that embodied the land and its harsh beauty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/travel/in-new-mexico-on-the-cowboy-trail-of-jack-thorp.html', 'snippet': 'The former New Yorker fell in love with the Rio Grande Valley, collecting the ballads and poems that embodied the land and its harsh beauty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, when I pictured the Rio Grande, it was as the spindly, concrete-encased trickle that marks the dividing line between the United States and Mexico. In my mind, it was as much a military installation as a body of water. But the Rio Grande can roar. It can carve an 800-foot-deep gorge into the Southwestern plateaus. It can sustain vineyards, pecan orchards, pinto bean farms and lavender fields. It can drown riverside hot springs. It can flow so fast and full that its water turns the color of adobe.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/travel/28FOOTSTEPS5/28FOOTSTEPS5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/travel/28FOOTSTEPS5/28FOOTSTEPS5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/travel/28FOOTSTEPS5/28FOOTSTEPS5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/travel/28FOOTSTEPS5/28FOOTSTEPS5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/travel/28FOOTSTEPS5/28FOOTSTEPS5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/28/travel/28FOOTSTEPS5/28FOOTSTEPS5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/travel/28FOOTSTEPS5/28FOOTSTEPS5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In New Mexico, on the Cowboy Trail of Jack Thorp', 'kicker': 'Footsteps', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Along the Cowboy Trail of Jack Thorpe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moon, Freda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cowboys and Cowgirls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T19:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Freda Moon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Freda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18c1fef4-0071-5530-9f8c-af58b86fc04b', 'word_count': 1833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18c1fef4-0071-5530-9f8c-af58b86fc04b'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s special Voyages Issue includes pictures from a road trip through Georgia taken by the photographer Alec Soth and the writer Brad Zellar. Recently, Zellar talked about their state sojourns.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/interview-with-brad-zellar/', 'snippet': 'This week’s special Voyages Issue includes pictures from a road trip through Georgia taken by the photographer Alec Soth and the writer Brad Zellar. Recently, Zellar talked about their state sojourns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Sept. 28 Voyages Issue includes photographs from a road trip through Georgia that was taken by the photographer Alec Soth and the writer Brad Zellar. It was their seventh such expedition since 2012; they have also visited California, Colorado, Michigan, New York, Ohio and Texas. When Soth and Zellar are on the road — they spent two weeks in Georgia in July — they post photos and writings every day on their Tumblr, called The LBM Dispatch. Afterward, they print their version of a newspaper as a record of their trip. I recently talked to Zellar about their sojourns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/magazine/Soth-Dispatch-photo/Soth-Dispatch-photo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/26/magazine/Soth-Dispatch-photo/Soth-Dispatch-photo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/magazine/Soth-Dispatch-photo/Soth-Dispatch-photo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/magazine/Soth-Dispatch-photo/Soth-Dispatch-photo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'r