': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f2461f8-f6da-5f89-932f-cc2fb46d4253', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f2461f8-f6da-5f89-932f-cc2fb46d4253'}, {'abstract': 'The Blue Ridge Folklife Festival in Ferrum, Va., in October will feature sacred and string-band music.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/music-in-the-virginia-mountains/', 'snippet': 'The Blue Ridge Folklife Festival in Ferrum, Va., in October will feature sacred and string-band music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 41st Blue Ridge Folklife Festival, set for Oct. 25 in western Virginia, will showcase musicians dedicated to preserving the art and authenticity of regional folk music.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Music in the Virginia Mountains', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monroe, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T21:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charu Suri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92a37d7b-c304-5591-9753-50c444ea6287', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92a37d7b-c304-5591-9753-50c444ea6287'}, {'abstract': 'The former teenage prodigy is relaunching his namesake label with a show at Paris Fashion Week. Here, a first look at the spring/summer 2015 collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/esteban-cortazar-paris-fashion-week-spring-2015/', 'snippet': 'The former teenage prodigy is relaunching his namesake label with a show at Paris Fashion Week. Here, a first look at the spring/summer 2015 collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are fashion prodigies, and then there’s Esteban Cortazar. The designer debuted his first collection at New York Fashion Week at the age of 17 – the youngest person ever to do so – before moving to Paris at 23 to take the helm of creative director at Emanuel Ungaro, where he remained for two years. More recently, he has released capsule collections for Net-a-Porter under his own name, earning him countless “comeback kid” monikers in the press. Now 30, still living in Paris and armed with new backers, Cortazar is preparing for a full relaunch of his namesake line. And the spring/summer 2015 show, which will be held tomorrow at his spacious Marais studio, is shaping up to be one of Paris Fashion Week’s most anticipated events.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/t-magazine/26cortazar-hartman2/26cortazar-hartman2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/t-magazine/26cortazar-hartman2/26cortazar-hartman2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/t-magazine/26cortazar-hartman2/26cortazar-hartman2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/26/t-magazine/26cortazar-hartman2/26cortazar-hartman2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/t-magazine/26cortazar-hartman2/26cortazar-hartman2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Esteban Cortazar Returns to the Runway', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cortazar, Esteban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T21:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By sophia j. Gonzalez', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9279549-df07-53eb-b343-1bea8bafff71', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9279549-df07-53eb-b343-1bea8bafff71'}, {'abstract': 'Charting “Syro,” the first new Aphex Twin studio album as in 13 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/arts/music/breaking-down-syro-by-aphex-twin.html', 'snippet': 'Charting “Syro,” the first new Aphex Twin studio album as in 13 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard D. James, an electronic musician from Britain, is renowned for his lively yet mysterious dance music and his reclusive trickster persona. Since the early 1990s, he has made music under monikers like Aphex Twin, AFX and Caustic Window; the frenetic new “Syro” (Warp) is his first studio album as Aphex Twin in 13 years. With cryptic song titles like “minipops 67 (source field mix)” and “s950tx16wasr10 (earth portal mix),” “Syro” suggests that Mr. James remains his playful self. Here, I chart “Syro” and 41 of his other known solo releases. There may be even more.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/aphex/aphex-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1925, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/aphex/aphex-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1925}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/aphex/aphex-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 320, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/aphex/aphex-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/aphex/aphex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/aphex/aphex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/aphex/aphex-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Decoding a Trickster', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Decoding a Trickster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', '