e his many friendships in the food world.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/grant-achatz-april-bloomfield-anthony-bourdain-and-others-dish-on-the-plates-they-made-for-daniel-boulud/', 'snippet': 'The handmade items hang on the walls of Boulud’s new Washington, D.C., eatery to commemorate his many friendships in the food world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Daniel Boulud opened his 16th restaurant, DBGB Kitchen and Bar, in Washington, D.C., earlier this month, the occasion marked a homecoming of sorts for the French-born chef. “D.C. is where I spent my first two and a half years in America,” says Boulud, who arrived in 1981 and assumed his first stateside job cooking for the head of the European Commission. “DBGB is a restaurant I would have loved to open after a couple of years in D.C., but I couldn’t afford to,” he adds. “I didn’t have any money, nor did I have a name strong enough that I could raise money.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/t-magazine/26bouloud-neilson-slide-BVF3/26bouloud-neilson-slide-BVF3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/26/t-magazine/26bouloud-neilson-slide-BVF3/26bouloud-neilson-slide-BVF3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/t-magazine/26bouloud-neilson-slide-BVF3/26bouloud-neilson-slide-BVF3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/t-magazine/26bouloud-neilson-slide-BVF3/26bouloud-neilson-slide-BVF3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType':