: 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/06/fashion/06REVERSEPARENTING/0706-REVERSEPARENTING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/07/06/fashion/06REVERSEPARENTING/0706-REVERSEPARENTING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/06/fashion/06REVERSEPARENTING/0706-REVERSEPARENTING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Roosevelts Achieved Peace in Our House', 'kicker': 'Reverse Parenting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How the Roosevelts Achieved Peace in Our House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Franklin Delano', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T23:48:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Conlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Conlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fd5bbfc-9803-5b07-9569-46f2bd3507ec', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fd5bbfc-9803-5b07-9569-46f2bd3507ec'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cardona played percussion on hundreds of albums ranging from Latin and Santeria music to fusions by the likes of David Byrne, Paul Simon and Herbie Hancock.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/27/arts/music/milton-cardona-keeper-of-new-york-salsas-beat-dies-at-69.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cardona played percussion on hundreds of albums ranging from Latin and Santeria music to fusions by the likes of David Byrne, Paul Simon and Herbie Hancock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milton Cardona, a Puerto Rican percussionist who was a mainstay of New York salsa, a studio musician on hundreds of albums and a Santeria priest who introduced sacred traditional rhythms to secular audiences, died on Sept. 19 in the Bronx. He was 69. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/CARDONA-obit/CARDONA-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/CARDONA-obit/CARDONA-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/CARDONA-obit/CARDONA-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/CARDONA-obit/CARDONA-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/CARDONA-obit/CARDONA-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/CARDONA-obit/CARDONA-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/arts/CARDONA-obit/CARDONA-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Milton Cardona, Keeper of New York Salsa’s Beat, Dies at 69', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Milton Cardona, 69, Keeper of New York Salsa’s Beat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cardona, Milton (1944-2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Santeria Faith', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T23:52:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c4edc24-2e2a-5739-b05c-bbdc7dd0ea32', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c4edc24-2e2a-5739-b05c-bbdc7dd0ea32'}, {'abstract': 'He loses an attorney general, but takes an assertive stance at the United Nations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/opinion/sunday/in-the-homestretch-obama-comes-on-strong.html', 'snippet': 'He loses an attorney general, but takes an assertive stance at the United Nations.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The enemy of my enemy is my friend,” says the ancient proverb. But don’t tell that to President Obama, who is furiously bombing Bashar al-Assad’s enemies in Syria while insisting that Mr. Assad’s regime is also the enemy. Best also not to remind Mr. Obama about leading from behind, or of his arguments against being drawn into the Syrian civil war or getting embroiled in any Middle Eastern conflicts.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928SERGE/0928SERGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928SERGE/0928SERGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928SERGE/0928SERGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928SERGE/0928SERGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928SERGE/0928SERGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928SERGE/0928SERGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928SERGE/0928SERGE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Homestretch, Obama Comes On Strong', 'kicker': 'Quick History', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Homestretch, Obama Comes on Strong', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tohti, Ilham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mansouri, Mariam Al', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-26T23:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge Schmemann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmemann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/30fb9701-35ec-5739-aa59-4aa95162e172', 'word_count': 1017, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30fb9701-35ec-5739-aa59-4aa95162e172'}, {'abstract': 'The issue explores the power of refusal when it comes to interiors and important life matters.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/t-fall-2014-design-issue/', 'snippet': 'The issue explores the power of refusal when it comes to interiors and important life matters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T loves to say yes — to new people, places and ideas — but this issue is all about the power of restraint. Take the Scandinavian architects Claesson Koivisto Rune, who create warm, pared-back spaces that are low on embellishments but high on style, as evidenced by a Stockholm apartment distinguished by a single, spectacular brass cube. Or the couturier Stephan Janson, who years ago left the limelight in order to dress a more discriminating set of women. And after creating interiors for clients like Vera Wang and Anna Wintour, the decorator Stephen Sills passed up the opportunity to move into a palatial home, choosing instead to pour his heart and soul into a tiny, perfect apartment. Elsewhere in the issue, the Brussels-based designers Jorge Almada and Anna-Marie Midy forgo modern luxuries in favor of cowboy charm in their rustic Mexican casita; Jody Rosen gets twisted up in a convention as old as time — the humble knot — and meets one of its greatest champions; Malcolm Gladwell and Sarah Silverman politely decline cookies made of crickets, among other dubious temptations; and we examine the legacy of the legendary Braun designer Dieter Rams, whose career can be best summed up with the words “less but better.” See all stories from the issue >>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28FallDesign-Cover/28FallDesign-Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28FallDesign-Cover/28FallDesign-Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 727}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28FallDesign-Cover/28FallDesign-Cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 845, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/t-magazine/28FallDesign-Cover/28FallDesign-Cover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption':