 music I listen to over the course of a week comes from bands I discovered through his Tiny Desk Concerts. And here’s another — a young band that makes me want to drop acid and wear tie-died clothing, which is a great feeling when you’re 61.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Quilt', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-27T00:55:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ffc8cb6-531d-52fc-9d67-e7d299d031ac', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ffc8cb6-531d-52fc-9d67-e7d299d031ac'}, {'abstract': 'We asked readers of NYTimes.com to send us monarch butterfly photographs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/26/a-virtual-butterfly-hunt/', 'snippet': 'We asked readers of NYTimes.com to send us monarch butterfly photographs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the most recent N.Y.C. Nature column, Dave Taft wrote about the monarch butterfly and its migration. Unlike migratory birds, individual butterflies do not complete the trip from the northern United States to Mexico and back.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28BUTTERFLY2combo/28BUTTERFLY2combo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 161, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/nyregion/28BUTTERFLY2combo/28BUTTERFLY2combo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 161}}, {'rank': 0, '