wer and Chess Man, Forced Into an Unwanted Move', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibbs, Sonny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Street Vendors (Non-Food)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Florists', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Riverton Houses (Manhattan, NY, Apartments)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-27T01:45:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikita Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/506c07ec-bd6b-5e2a-a3c3-99f12fb1614e', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/506c07ec-bd6b-5e2a-a3c3-99f12fb1614e'}, {'abstract': 'The states have had plenty of time to figure out how to carry out the new rule. Further delay would only prolong the indefensible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/27/opinion/labor-rights-for-home-care-workers.html', 'snippet': 'The states have had plenty of time to figure out how to carry out the new rule. Further delay would only prolong the indefensible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new rule that will give home care workers basic labor protections is supposed to go into effect on Jan. 1, 2015. But several states are pushing for delay, s