with the stories of people who enacted change in vaccines, education, sanitation and water, and hope to end extreme poverty by 2030. Tamron Hall oversees this hourlong prime-time special; Chris Hayes and Alex Wagner will host preshow coverage starting at 3 p.m. on MSNBC, with Ronan Farrow and Joy Reid reporting from backstage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-27T05:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/49fc6879-8f7c-5d4e-a68a-60dab6a9091e', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49fc6879-8f7c-5d4e-a68a-60dab6a9091e'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on September 27, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/27/pageoneplus/corrections-september-27-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on September 27, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: September 27, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-27T06:10:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de2cc93b-9097-5bd4-adc6-8494db1d5e3a', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de2cc93b-9097-5bd4-adc6-8494db1d5e3a'}, {'abstract': 'It’s Saturday but no rest for the fashionably weary.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/27/paris-fashion-week-morning-report-comme-des-garcons-jean-paul-gaultier-haider-ackermann-viktor-and-rolf/', 'snippet': 'It’s Saturday but no rest for the fashionably weary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fashion week wheel, ever turning, is now spinning fast enough for the scene to blur. Yes, you may have to remind yourself, it is Saturday; it’s the weekend. That will give you something to chew over as you sit at Junya Watanabe’s show all the same, at the workweek hour of 9:30 a.m. No, there’s no rest for the fashionably weary. Saturday is packed. Haider Ackermann, the Colombian-born, Belgian-based specialist in louche luxe, follows at 10:30 a.m.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/fashion/27runway/27runway-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/27/fashion/27runway/27runway-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/fashion/27runway/27runway-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/fashion/27runway/27runway-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/27/fashion/27runway/27runway-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail