s state standards for access to health care are rarely enforced and that Medicaid patients may wait for months or travel long distances to see a doctor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Enrollment in Medicaid is surging as a result of the Affordable Care Act, but the Obama administration and state officials have done little to ensure that new beneficiaries have access to doctors after they get their Medicaid cards, federal investigators say in a new report.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Many New Medicaid Enrollees, Care Is Hard to Find, Report Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Many New Medicaid Enrollees, Care Is Hard to Find, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-27T16:42:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b303374-666b-5688-9efc-6c5f1a2d12c9', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b303374-666b-5688-9efc-6c5f1a2d12c9'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Columbine Goldsmith.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/27