abstract': 'Does spending on judicial elections corrupt the courts’ impartiality?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/sunday-review/judges-on-the-campaign-trail.html', 'snippet': 'Does spending on judicial elections corrupt the courts’ impartiality?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — FEDERAL judges are appointed for life and insulated from politics, and most of them do not think much of the distinctively American practice of electing judges. They make this clear by insisting that those elections, which take place in 39 states, be as political as possible.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928COURTsub/0928COURTsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928COURTsub/0928COURTsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 677}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928COURTsub/0928COURTsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928COURTsub/0928COURTsub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2031, 'width': 1799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928COURTsub/0928COURTsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/28/sunday-review/0928COURTsub/0928COURTsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum