orrections appearing in print on September 28, 2014', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: September 28, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T07:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47bee334-4bc5-54cb-be14-8d9cf93a0bb1', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47bee334-4bc5-54cb-be14-8d9cf93a0bb1'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: German troops are surprised in Belgium in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/1914-german-offensive-checked-in-belgium/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: German troops are surprised in Belgium in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANTWERP — The following communiqué has been issued here : ‘‘Yesterday [Sept. 26], a detachment of German troops, comprising a brigade of infantry, two regiments of cavalry and six batteries of artillery—two of which were heavy artillery—was surprised in its march from Brussels on Termonde, via Alost. Attacked in front and on their flank, the German troops retired in disorder toward Assche, leaving in our hands many prisoners and wounded as well as several caissons. To-day, apparently with the intention of avenging this defeat, Malines was bombarded by long-distance guns and important forces made a general movement along our front. Between Malines and Alost the several German attacks against us failed. Toward Alost, our division of cavalry succeeded in taking the German left wing in the rear. In short, the German attack has failed and our troops have without difficulty preserved the positions acquired from Antwerp to Malines. There, however, the station has suffered severely. Many houses have collapsed, others are on fire. A dozen civilians have been killed.’’\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 29, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-malines/29iht-oldsept29-malines-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-malines/29iht-oldsept29-malines-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 611}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-malines/29iht-oldsept29-malines-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 863, 'width': 848, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-malines/29iht-oldsept29-malines-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 863, 'width': 848, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-malines/29iht-oldsept29-malines-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-malines/29iht-oldsept29-malines-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-malines/29iht-oldsept29-malines-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1914: German Offensive Checked in Belgium', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46665214-bc32-5469-8aef-d7159b2366c7', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46665214-bc32-5469-8aef-d7159b2366c7'}, {'abstract': 'As Derek Jeter retires from the game he dominated, Barton Silverman looks back on his favorite moments photographing the Yankee star.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/indelible-photos-of-derek-jeter/', 'snippet': 'As Derek Jeter retires from the game he dominated, Barton Silverman looks back on his favorite moments photographing the Yankee star.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By his count, Barton Silverman has been blessed by the photo gods four times. They came in the form of larger-than-life subjects who can make or break a photographer’s career: Joe Namath, Wayne Gretzky, Michael Jordan and most recently, Derek Jeter, whose final innings on a Boston diamond today conclude a storied 20-year career.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indelible Photos of Derek Jeter', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'majo