n the Brazilian town of Ceres, a radio station reported today. It said it was believed the killing was for political motives. Brig. Shishakli had been living in Brazil for some four years and operated a rice plantation. The shooting occurred in mid-afternoon in the middle of the main street. The assassin was described as a dark-haired young man of medium height wearing dark glasses and a green shirt. Police said he had lunched with Brig. Shishakli in a restaurant shortly before the shooting. Restaurant witnesses said the assailant seemed to be a well-educated, well-mannered youth who had not been seen before in this sparsely-settled cowboy country west of Brasilia. Police said he fled the town in an automobile.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 29, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-syria/29iht-oldsept29-syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 333, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-syria/29iht-oldsept29-syria-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 333, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-syria/29iht-oldsept29-syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-syria/29iht-oldsept29-syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/blogs/29iht-oldsept29-syria/29iht-oldsept29-syria-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Ex-President Of Syria Slain in Brazil', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T12:50:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c2e1db1-38f6-5053-8fff-b08917456715', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c2e1db1-38f6-5053-8fff-b08917456715'}, {'abstract': 'The key to success in modern business is hiring and nurturing “smart creatives,” according to a new book co-authored by Eric Schmidt, former chief executive of Google.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/the-google-formula-for-success/', 'snippet': 'The key to success in modern business is hiring and nurturing “smart creatives,” according to a new book co-authored by Eric Schmidt, former chief executive of Google.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can Google’s winning ways be applied to all kinds of businesses? The authors of “How Google Works,” Eric Schmidt, Google’s former chief executive, and Jonathan Rosenberg, a former senior product manager at Google, firmly believe that they can.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/technology/29bits-google/29bits-google-articleLarge.png', 'height': 816, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/29/technology/29bits-google/29bits-google-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 816}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/technology/29bits-google/29bits-google-jumbo.png', 'height': 902, 'width': 663, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/technology/29bits-google/29bits-google-superJumbo.png', 'height': 902, 'width': 663, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/technology/29bits-google/29bits-google-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/29/technology/29bits-google/29bits-google-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/technology/29bits-google/29bits-google-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Google Formula for Success', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Page, Larry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Jonathan J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Eric E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T13:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eb76e4a-1dcd-56ce-97b0-c8deec5c3816', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eb76e4a-1dcd-56ce-97b0-c8deec5c3816'}, {'abstract': 'My 7-year-old son asked to stay home while I ran errands in our neighborhood. I agreed, and our experiment was a success — except to those who insisted on seeing encouragement of independence as a “tragedy waiting to happen.”', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/home-alone-at-7-safe-and-learning-to-stay-that-way/', 'snippet': 'My 7-year-old son asked to stay home while I ran errands in our neighborhood. I agreed, and our experiment was a success — except to those who insisted on seeing encouragement of independence as a “tragedy waiting to happen.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s that scene in the Pixar movie “The Incredibles” in which Elastigirl is flying a jet toward the island where her husband, Mr. Incredible, is being held by the evil Syndrome. Missiles are coming toward the jet, and with no other options, Elastigirl turns to her daughter, Violet, for help.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/us/motherlode-incredibles/motherlode-incredibles-jumbo.png', 'height': 135, 'width': 189, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/26/us/motherlode-incredibles/motherlode-incredibles-superJumbo.png', 'height': 135, 'width': 189, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit