nt': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/558cc34e-2215-5f8e-9e82-2906c43cc73a'}, {'abstract': 'The victims ranged in age from 11 to 25, according to a police spokeswoman, who said the shooting took place around 1 a.m. Sunday at a club about four miles north of downtown Miami.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/us/15-people-wounded-after-shooting-at-miami-nightclub.html', 'snippet': 'The victims ranged in age from 11 to 25, according to a police spokeswoman, who said the shooting took place around 1 a.m. Sunday at a club about four miles north of downtown Miami.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifteen people were shot and wounded, one critically, at a nightclub in Miami early Sunday, officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '15 People Wounded After Shooting at Miami Nightclub', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T16:33:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbf346ed-321d-5eb0-8d35-6d7a4e12beb6', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbf346ed-321d-5eb0-8d35-6d7a4e12beb6'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (13, 49) THE PARADISE, SEASON 2 Joanna Vanderham, above, returns as Denise Lovett, an ambitious country girl who last season took a job at a Victorian department store in a booming northern British city in this “Masterpiece Classic” adaptation of the 1883 Émile Zola novel “Au Bonheur des Dames.” Soon she had caught the eye of John Moray (Emun Elliott), the handsome if enigmatic owner of the establishment, whose affection was pursued by Lady Katherine Glendenning (Elaine Cassidy). But eventually Moray’s love for Denise won out, and he left Katherine at the altar. The new season picks up a year later as Moray pines away in Paris for Denise, who is back at the Paradise, their romance tested by the store’s regime of Katherine and her new husband, Tom Weston (Ben Daniels). In “Miss Marple, Season 7: Endless Night,” at 9, Agatha Christie’s spinster sleuth (Julia McKenzie) meets a chauffeur (Tom Hughes) who recounts his romance with an American heiress (Ms. Vanderham) and her death, foretold by a Gypsy, shortly after their marriage. And in “The Mystery of Agatha Christie With David Suchet,” at 10:30, Mr. Suchet, who starred in the long-running series “Agatha Christie’s Poirot,” ponders the writer’s life and legacy.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T16:44:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/72cff348-6234-5e3a-b11a-3fcc3fce793d', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72cff348-6234-5e3a-b11a-3fcc3fce793d'}, {'abstract': 'During a visit to Afghanistan, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo received briefings from military leaders that he said would inform his efforts to protect New York from terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/nyregion/andrew-cuomo-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'During a visit to Afghanistan, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo received briefings from military leaders that he said would inform his efforts to protect New York from terrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Invoking one tragedy to warn of the prospect of another, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo said on Sunday that the rise of the Islamic State had revived the trauma of the Sept. 11 attacks among New Yorkers while creating a fresh danger for their city.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/nyregion/29cuomo/29cuomo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/29/nyregion/29cuomo/29cuomo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/nyregion/29cuomo/29cuomo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/nyregion/29cuomo/29cuomo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/nyregion/29cuomo/29cuomo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/29/nyregion/29cuomo/29cuomo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '