rld.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama acknowledged in an interview broadcast on Sunday that the United States had underestimated the rise of the Islamic State militant group, which has seized control of a broad swath of territory in the Middle East, and had placed too much trust in the Iraqi military, allowing the region to become “ground zero for jihadists around the world.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Acknowledges U.S. Erred in Assessing ISIS', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Acknowledges That U.S. Made Errors in Assessing Militants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowlton, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '60 MINUTES (TV PROGRAM)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA IN MESOPOTAMIA', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T17:25:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker and Brian Knowlton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knowlton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/126087e2-12e7-55a3-b299-d5d9d97abd77', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/126087e2-12e7-55a3-b299-d5d9d97abd77'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Washington’s portrayal of a retired mercenary fighting Russian gangsters took in an estimated $35 million at North American theaters over the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/28/denzel-washington-and-the-equalizer-lead-box-office/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Washington’s portrayal of a retired mercenary fighting Russian gangsters took in an estimated $35 million at North American theaters over the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are few sure things in Hollywood, but Denzel Washington is certainly one of them. “The Equalizer” (Sony), starring Mr. Washington as a retired mercenary pitted against ultra-violent Russian gangsters, was No. 1 at North American theaters over the weekend, taking in an estimated $35 million. “The Equalizer,” which reteamed Mr. Washington with the director Antoine Fuqua, cost Sony and Village Roadshow roughly $55 million to make. Sony, which is counting on the film to make up ground from some under-performing summer releases like “Sex Tape,” boasted on Sunday of its “no-holds-barred marketing campaign” for “The Equalizer” and called the results “spectacular.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/29EQUALIZER/29EQUALIZER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/29EQUALIZER/29EQUALIZER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/29EQUALIZER/29EQUALIZER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/29EQUALIZER/29EQUALIZER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/29EQUALIZER/29EQUALIZER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/29EQUALIZER/29EQUALIZER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/29EQUALIZER/29EQUALIZER-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Denzel Washington and ‘The Equalizer’ Lead Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With ‘Equalizer,’ Denzel Washington Does It Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Denzel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Laika Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T17:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'midd