 the Queer New York International Arts Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dutch choreographer Jan Martens does not put on airs. At the Abrons Arts Center on Friday, he introduced himself to New York in shorts and sneakers, sitting onstage taking selfies with a laptop. The images were projected on the wall behind him, along with the words he typed: a list of 10 fairly simple things he was attempting in the solo he was performing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/MARTENS/MARTENS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/MARTENS/MARTENS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/MARTENS/MARTENS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/MARTENS/MARTENS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/MARTENS/MARTENS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/MARTENS/MARTENS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/MARTENS/MARTENS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Workouts for the Mind, Dressed in Cheeky Humor ', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Workouts for the Mind, Dressed in Cheeky Humor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martens, Jan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T21:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dcfe610-6ea0-5579-87f8-1237dc1f5c03', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dcfe610-6ea0-5579-87f8-1237dc1f5c03'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Wheeler spent decades as a lobbyist for the cable and wireless industries, experience from which he has drawn in creating highly scrutinized policy guidelines for ensuring equal access to online content.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/business/with-perspective-from-both-sides-of-his-desk-fcc-chairman-ponders-net-neutrality.html', 'snippet': 'Tom Wheeler spent decades as a lobbyist for the cable and wireless industries, experience from which he has drawn in creating highly scrutinized policy guidelines for ensuring equal access to online content.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As a lobbyist for the cable and wireless industries, Tom Wheeler played a role in shaping almost every major telecommunications policy and innovation over the last three decades.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/business/29WHEELER/29WHEELER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name