ism and foreign investment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/business/sectarian-violence-in-myanmar-threatens-the-livelihoods-of-muslims.html', 'snippet': 'Rioting causes small businesses owned by Muslims to suffer. Some worry that the violence could also affect tourism and foreign investment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANDALAY, Myanmar — It has been more than a month since Mandalay, Myanmar’s second-largest city, was rocked by deadly anti-Muslim riots. Broken windows and large dents in the facades of a dozen small Muslim-run businesses are the only visible reminders of when about 300 radical Buddhists rode into town wielding swords and bricks, killing two people.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sectarian Violence in Myanmar Threatens Livelihood of Muslims', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sectarian Violence in Myanmar Threatens Livelihood of Muslims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mandalay (Myanmar)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ooredoo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T22:02:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip J. Heijmans', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Heijmans', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dc49365-5508-5ac8-8ca7-433b7d22046b', 'word_count': 1221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dc49365-5508-5ac8-8ca7-433b7d22046b'}, {'abstract': 'Now in author mode, the young TV star and filmmaker Lena Dunham is promoting her book of essays on a tour that includes literary authors and performances by “remarkable, special weirdos.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/arts/turning-a-book-tour-into-a-literary-circus-and-a-hot-ticket.html', 'snippet': 'Now in author mode, the young TV star and filmmaker Lena Dunham is promoting her book of essays on a tour that includes literary authors and performances by “remarkable, special weirdos.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, the writer, actor and producer Lena Dunham started an ambitious project. Nearly 600 people responded to an open call for video auditions on her website, including a sand artist, a ukulele player, a cappella singers, gymnasts, performance artists and stand-up comics, even some exceptionally charismatic babies. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/DUNHAMTOUR/DUNHAMTOUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/DUNHAMTOUR/DUNHAMTOUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 776}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/DUNHAMTOUR/DUNHAMTOUR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/arts/DUNHAMTOUR/DUNHAMTOUR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2005, 'width': 1550, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ra