0:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Parens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b7b889c-3fd6-5996-81d3-7364e1c37c3c', 'word_count': 1566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b7b889c-3fd6-5996-81d3-7364e1c37c3c'}, {'abstract': 'At Madison Square Garden, Prime Minister Narendra Modi telegraphed a wish list while also deftly rallying an influential diaspora to his side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/world/asia/narendra-modi-madison-square-garden-obama.html', 'snippet': 'At Madison Square Garden, Prime Minister Narendra Modi telegraphed a wish list while also deftly rallying an influential diaspora to his side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Narendra Modi, the prime minister of India, sold himself on Sunday as a onetime tea vendor who wanted to lift India to glory by cleaning up the country, clearing the way for business and preparing its young citizens to be the work force of an aging world. His speech at Madison Square Garden telegraphed a wish list on the eve of his first meeting with President Obama, while also deftly rallying an influential diaspora to his side.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Narendra Modi Outlines Goals for India on Eve of a Visit With Obama', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Premier Outlines Goals for India on Eve of a Visit With Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian-Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T23:33:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b3ee0b6-38bb-5985-9840-41a84a202c29', 'word_count': 1312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b3ee0b6-38bb-5985-9840-41a84a202c29'}, {'abstract': 'Alexander Heffner, who succeeded his grandfather and mentor Richard D. Heffner, said “the importance of public broadcasting and elevating our discourse into something substantive and meaningful were values that were instilled in me.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/business/media/open-mind-host-continues-grandfathers-vision-for-new-generation-.html', 'snippet': 'Alexander Heffner, who succeeded his grandfather and mentor Richard D. Heffner, said “the importance of public broadcasting and elevating our discourse into something substantive and meaningful were values that were instilled in me.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This summer, Alexander Heffner, a 24-year-old journalist just a couple of years out of Harvard, became the host of a talk show on public television. But a new media venture this is not.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/business/hefner1/hefner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xl