ndra Modi, who spoke at Madison Square Garden on his first trip to the United States since being elected in May, was treated like a rock star.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They wore his face on their chests, waved it on posters, chanted his name and quoted his slogans, 19,000 fans drawn to a single star. His image stared down from the big screen at Madison Square Garden and emerged on canvas in a live speed-painting onstage. And when the man himself emerged, the capacity crowd on Sunday in New York’s most storied arena roared as one, as if all the Knicks, all the Rangers, Billy Joel and Bruce Springsteen had suddenly materialized.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/world/MODI-1/MODI-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/29/world/MODI-1/MODI-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/world/MODI-1/MODI-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/world/MODI-1/MODI-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1240, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/world/MODI-1/MODI-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/29/world/MODI-1/MODI-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/world/MODI-1/MODI-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Madison Square Garden, Chants, Cheers and Roars for Modi', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India’s Prime Minister Fills Arena With Fans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T23:53:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0175ed0f-ba15-5cbf-bf03-292a348890b8', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0175ed0f-ba15-5cbf-bf03-292a348890b8'}, {'abstract': 'The A.I.G. case is an opportunity to explain the Fed’s decisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/opinion/finally-the-truth-about-the-bailout.html', 'snippet': 'The A.I.G. case is an opportunity to explain the Fed’s decisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — TODAY is the start of the trial in Starr International Co. Inc. v. United States, the case alleging that the government’s 2008 bailout of A.I.G. amounted to an unconstitutional plunder of the company’s shareholders. Starr, a firm run by the former A.I.G. chief executive Maurice R. Greenberg, was the insurer’s largest single shareholder at the time. It saw the government grab almost 80 percent of its common stock amid the bailout (a proportion that eventually rose to 92 percent), and is asking for a cool $40 billion to make it whole.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/opinion/0929OPEDchayka/0929OPEDchayka-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1124, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/29/opinion/0929OPEDchayka/0929OPEDchayka-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1124}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/opinion/0929OPEDchayka/0929OPEDchayka-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 547, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/opinion/0929OPEDchayka/0929OPEDchayka-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1093, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/opinion/0929OPEDchayka/0929OPEDchayka-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/29/opinion/0929OPEDchayka/0929OPEDchayka-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/29/opinion/0929OPEDchayka/0929OPEDchayka-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finally, the Truth About the A.I.G. Bailout', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finally, the Truth About the Bailout', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Economic Stabilization Act (2008)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Maurice R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T23:54:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Scheiber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scheiber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c3a57d0-1bb1-5283-a062-5951a68c7e71', 'word_count': 949, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c3a57d0-1bb1-5283-a062-5951a68c7e71'}, {'abstract': 'WNYC, WNBC, WNJU and the New York Daily News will introduce a site with information in English, Spanish and Chinese, and with individual school pages that are easier to understand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/business/media/revamped-website-to-offer-news-on-new-york-city-public-schools.html', 'snippet': 'WNYC, WNBC, WNJU and the New York Daily News will introduce a site with information in English, Spanish and Chinese, and with individual school pages that are easier to understand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York public radio station WNYC and the commercial television station WNBC have forged an unusual relationship in recent months, sharing investigative coverage on air and online. Now the two are teaming up, along with WNBC’s Spanish-language sister station, WNJU, and The Daily News, on a reintroduction of SchoolBook.org, a WNYC-owned site offering news and data on the New York City public schools system. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Media Outlets Revamp Site for Schools', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Media Outlets Revamp Site for Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jensen, Elizabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WNYC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WNBC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Daily News', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SchoolBook.org', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-28T23:54:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f8d9d3d-938e-5791-902d-f9f54593ebe2', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f8d9d3d-938e-5791-902d-f9f545