g Kong’s ‘Umbrella Revolution’ Tell a Story', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APPLE DAILY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Central', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T05:34:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ea8925e-f40b-5558-ad75-7b58e5c18226', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ea8925e-f40b-5558-ad75-7b58e5c18226'}, {'abstract': 'Female designers, including Stella McCartney and Chitose Abe of Sacai, top the schedule for Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/paris-fashion-week-morning-report-stella-mccartney-sacai-giambattista-valli-hedi-sliman-saint-laurent/', 'snippet': 'Female designers, including Stella McCartney and Chitose Abe of Sacai, top the schedule for Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the risk of being controversial, Paris Fashion Week is not yet an equal playground for male and female designers. That’s not to say the city doesn’t have top female talent — just look at Phoebe Philo of Céline, the much-watched (and much-copied) designer, who scored her runway show Sunday with Kate Bush’s “This Woman’s Work” to underline the point — but the balance still tips to the guys’ side.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype':