ment_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nina Westervelt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Westervelt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e816f08c-6022-586b-a313-fffd06a6e662', 'word_count': 27, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e816f08c-6022-586b-a313-fffd06a6e662'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Fuller, The Times’s Southeast Asia correspondent, tells of an angle that did not make it into an article about testing the authenticity of Thai food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/09/29/a-match-com-for-thai-food/', 'snippet': 'Thomas Fuller, The Times’s Southeast Asia correspondent, tells of an angle that did not make it into an article about testing the authenticity of Thai food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Fuller wrote a front-page article for Monday about bad Thai food around the globe — or, rather, the Thai government’s effort to test the authenticity of the country’s food by using a soon-to-be unveiled robot. Here, Mr. Fuller, The Times’s Southeast Asia correspondent, tells of an angle that did not make it into the article. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Match.com for Thai Food?', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thai Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T15:07:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be70cce9-e039-52b3-afff-73ddec4c9e80', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be70cce9-e039-52b3-afff-73ddec4c9e80'}, {'abstract': 'The designer’s final ready-to-wear show had Champagne, cheers and confetti. It was a night when memories came flooding back.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/paris-fashion-week-jean-paul-gaultier-last-ready-to-wear-show/', 'snippet': 'The designer’s final ready-to-wear show had Champagne, cheers and confetti. It was a night when memories came flooding back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The first indication that Jean Paul Gaultier’s final show for his ready-to-wear collection would be just a little different came with the announcement of the site. The show would be staged not at his complex on the Rue St.-Martin but at the venerable movie theater Le Grand Rex on the Boulevard Poissonnière, raising expectations for an already eager audience that had marked this date on the calendar ever since Mr. Gaultier announced the show would be his last.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jean Paul Gaultier Gives a Good Party', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gaultier’s Life Takes Center Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September Fashion Week (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaultier, Jean Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Alexander', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T15:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Emmrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'l