 the American wife of a Thai diplomat, is to run on the West Coast in advance of a planned New York run in 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/waterfall-a-new-musical-with-thai-inspiration-aiming-for-broadway/', 'snippet': '“Waterfall,” which centers on a Thai student who falls in love with the American wife of a Thai diplomat, is to run on the West Coast in advance of a planned New York run in 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The veteran Broadway songwriters Richard Maltby Jr. and David Shire (“Baby,” “Big”) are teaming up with theater artists from Thailand on a new musical romance, “Waterfall,” that will have productions in Pasadena, Calif., and Seattle next year before a planned move to Broadway in 2016, the creators and producers announced on Monday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Waterfall,’ a New Musical With Thai Inspiration, Aiming for Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thai-Inspired ‘Waterfall’ Is Aiming for Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maltby, Richard Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T17:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73671aba-0071-571e-86e3-e4554c488abb', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73671aba-0071-571e-86e3-e4554c488abb'}, {'abstract': 'The barrister’s bespoke cream top and trousers evoked Bianca Jagger’s iconic marriage ensemble.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/amal-alamuddin-stella-m