, an illusionist and escape artist, once got him into business class and generated new business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY perspective of traveling is probably similar to that of other business travelers, except that I’m in a nontraditional career. I’m an illusionist and an escape artist. Houdini is my hero. When I started flying to give performances I thought it was really exciting. That lasted for about 30 flights. Now, flying is so routine I don’t even think about it much. It’s like brushing my teeth.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/business/Flier/Flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 933, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/30/business/Flier/Flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 933}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/business/Flier/Flier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 659, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/business/Flier/Flier-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1317, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/30/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/business/Flier/Flier-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Magic Opens Doors, No Tricks Required', 'kicker': 'Frequent Flier', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Magic Opens Doors, No Tricks Required', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magic and Magicians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Basso, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T17:55:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Basso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Basso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8979f789-3ff1-51a0-8eb6-3743fa9087b8', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8979f789-3ff1-51a0-8eb6-3743fa9087b8'}, {'abstract': 'How an outgunned Union force turned back the Confederate invasion of Missouri.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/the-thermopylae-of-the-west/', 'snippet': 'How an outgunned Union force turned back the Confederate invasion of Missouri.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the fall of 1862, Confederate armies under Robert E. Lee and Braxton Bragg invaded the slaveholding states of Maryland and Kentucky, but their ambition to conquer the border South was famously quashed at the battles of Antietam and Perryville. Two years later, in September 1864, a Confederate army under Sterling Price invaded another slave state, Missouri, likewise intending to wrest it from Union control. This, too, ended in failure. But while nothing in Price’s campaign reached the scale or importance of those previous battles, the pivotal engagement, at Pilot Knob, Mo., was noteworthy for the odds overcome by the vastly outnumbered Union – indeed, some called it “Thermopylae of the West,” recalling that ancient battle in which a small band of Spartan warriors held off an overwhelmingly larger Persian force.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Thermopylae of the West', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T17:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Etcheson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Etcheson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80e5b8ae-127c-52c2-96d8-492635318779', 'word_count': 1726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80e5b8ae-127c-52c2-96d8-492635318779'}, {'abstract': 'The once-staid activity has become a lot more physical, combining nature appreciation with zip-lining, paintball and off-road Segway tours.', 'we