me': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9c8773a-1982-5aa6-b241-4b3a95fa8a7d', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9c8773a-1982-5aa6-b241-4b3a95fa8a7d'}, {'abstract': 'Lucinda Williams explores obstacles to overcome in “Down Where the Spirit Meets the Bone”; Christopher Owens bypasses torment in “A New Testament.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/30/arts/music/new-albums-from-lucinda-williams-and-christopher-owens.html', 'snippet': 'Lucinda Williams explores obstacles to overcome in “Down Where the Spirit Meets the Bone”; Christopher Owens bypasses torment in “A New Testament.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lucinda Williams made her first album for her own label, Highway 20 Records, a magnum opus: two discs, 20 songs and a summation of what has endeared her to a large, loyal following. She’s pithy and penetrating, bruised but steadfast, proud of the grain and drawl of her voice. Her music places itself in a vanishing, idealized Southland where country, soul, blues and gospel all share a common spirit and a vocabulary of twang, and where life lessons can be delivered by a bar band.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/NEWMUSIC/NEWMUSIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/NEWMUSIC/NEWMUSIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/NEWMUSIC/NEWMUSIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/NEWMUSIC/NEWMUSIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/NEWMUSIC/NEWMUSIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/NEWMUSIC/NEWMUSIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/NEWMUSIC/NEWMUSIC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Twangy Homilies About Shouldering Through the Pain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twangy Homilies About Shouldering Through the Pain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Owens, Christopher', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Lucinda', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T21:35:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles and Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc21a3ef-4b98-558a-94a2-d6c5e8cebbe9', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc21a3ef-4b98-558a-94a2-d6c5e8cebbe9'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City Ballet all-Balanchine program brought out the best from Ashley Bouder, Wendy Whelan and Teresa Reichlen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/30/arts/dance/stars-variety-shines-in-city-ballet-balanchine-program.html', 'snippet': 'The New York City Ballet all-Balanchine program brought out the best from Ashley Bouder, Wendy Whelan and Teresa Reichlen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At New York City Ballet on Friday night, Ashley Bouder and Andrew Veyette kept bursting back onto the stage in “Donizetti Variations” with a twinkling, ebullient, heart-catching virtuosity that had seasoned audience members asking, “When was it last this good?” In the title role of “La Sonnambula,” Wendy Whelan paced through the sharply changing paths of her sleep with a bleak urgency that gave an unfamiliar darkness to this always amazing drama. And in “Firebird,” the contrasting capacities of Teresa Reichlen’s style for superhuman amplitude and quiet intimacy opened up fresh meanings in this ballet. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/firebird1/firebird1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/firebird1/firebird1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 590}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/firebird1/firebird1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/firebird1/firebird1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2012, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/firebird1/firebird1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/firebird1/firebird1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/firebird1/firebird1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Forces of Nature, Haunting, Changing and Just Plain Happy ', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Forces of Nature, Haunting, Changing and Just Plain Happy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouder, Ashley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whelan, Wendy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reichlen, Teresa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Balanchine, George', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch, David H, Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T21:40:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdfad4d4-1730-52af-aa21-771db1cc331b', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdfad4d4-1730-52af-aa21-771db1cc331b'}, {'abstract': 'Make no mistake, this is about politics and race.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/the-partisan-court-blocks-extended-voting-in-ohio/', 'snippet': 'Make no mistake, this is about politics and race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday afternoon the Supreme Court justices decided 5-4, on party (of-the-president-who nominated-them) lines, to block extended voting hours and days in Ohio, 16 hours before voting was to begin there. The decision affects everyone in the state but will disproportionately harm poorer and minority voters, who rely on weekend and evening hours to avoid forbiddingly long lines on Election Day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Partisan Court Blocks Extended Voting in Ohio', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preisse, Doug', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T21:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Wegman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wegman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b8ed743-4da7-5033-8a07-a2c39edfb652', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b8ed743-4da7-5033-8a07-a2c39edfb652'}, {'abstract': 'The actress-author of “Belfast Blues,” Geraldine Hughes, tells her story against images of Northern Ireland’s history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/30/theater/geraldine-hughes-returns-to-new-york-with-belfast-blues.html', 'snippet': 'The actress-author of “Belfast Blues,” Geraldine Hughes, tells her story against images of Northern Ireland’s history.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Belfast Blues” is full of impressive physical moments, when the flow of Geraldine Hughes’s words is either emphasized or countermanded by the casually coiled force of her body. On Saturday afternoon at the Barrow Street Theater, where the show has returned to New York for a limited engagement, one moment in particular stood out: Ms. Hughes standing very still and straight, embodying a British soldier.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Child of the ‘Troubles’ of Northern Ireland', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Child of the ‘Troubles’ of Northern Ireland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'La Rocco, Claudia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Belfast Blues (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Geraldine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T21:46:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/07968f5a-6d91-54ac-bc01-434d87223919', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07968f5a-6d91-54ac-bc01-434d87223919'}, {'abstract': '“Bright Star,” a new musical by Steve Martin and Edie Brickell, is having its premiere run in San Diego.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/30/theater/bright-star-is-steve-martin-and-edie-brickells-new-show.html', 'snippet': '“Bright Star,” a new musical by Steve Martin and Edie Brickell, is having its premiere run in San Diego.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — Darkness and light are blended in even proportions in “Bright Star,” a sepia-toned new musical by Steve Martin and Edie Brickell making its premiere at the Old Globe theater here. The characters in this musically vibrant if overstuffed show, set in the Blue Ridge Mountains of North Carolina during two separate decades of the 20th century, endure hardship, heartache and almost melodramatic loss. But, as the title suggests, their eyes remain fixed not on the black canopy of night but on the beacons of hope that pierce it. A telling song from the second act reminds us that no matter how gray the future seems, the “sun is gonna shine again.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/BRIGHT/BRIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/BRIGHT/BRIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/BRIGHT/BRIGHT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/BRIGHT/BRIGHT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/BRIGHT/BRIGHT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/30/arts/BRIGHT/BRIGHT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '