 Prime Minister Narendra Modi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/30/world/asia/indian-anchors-scuffle-in-new-york-draws-supporters-and-critics.html', 'snippet': 'Indian journalists rallied Monday in support of a television host who was harassed by supporters of Prime Minister Narendra Modi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Standing outside Madison Square Garden on Sunday, ahead of a rally for India’s new prime minister, Narendra Modi, the Indian television anchor Rajdeep Sardesai reminded viewers back home that the New York arena had been the site for many famous events, including "Muhammad Ali versus Joe Frazier.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Anchor’s Scuffle in New York Draws Supporters and Critics', 'kicker': 'Open Source', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sardesai, Rajdeep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gujarat State (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-29T22:54:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/164701b0-d93e-5892-bfb4-57bbbe500ec4', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/164701b0-d93e-5892-bfb4-57bbbe500ec4'}, {'abstract': 'A new report from the National Research Council found that the effect of climate cha