ion in settling to legitimate tribal claims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/30/opinion/delayed-justice-for-the-navajos.html', 'snippet': 'A $554 million agreement with the Navajo Nation is the latest and most encouraging development in a reversal by the Obama administration in settling to legitimate tribal claims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The long struggle of American Indian tribes to be fairly compensated for decades of federal mismanagement of their tribal lands’ resources reached an important point last week with an agreement by the largest tribe, the Navajo Nation, to accept $554 million in settlement of long-running litigation over breach-of-trust claims. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delayed Justice for the Navajos', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delayed Justice for the Navajos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Navajo Indians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norton, Gale', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-30T00:43:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/277f3e8f-13b6-543e-b3df-c73b2096db6f', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/277f3e8f-13b6-543e-b3df-c73b2096db6f'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Vestal’s collection of stories, “Godforsaken Idaho,” took home the $25,000 prize on Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/29/shawn-vestal-wins-penrobert-w-bingham-prize/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Vestal’s collection of stories, “Godforsaken Idaho,” took home the $25,000 prize on Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The PEN American Center on Monday announced that Shawn Vestal is the winner of this year’s $25,000 PEN/Robert W. Bingham Prize for Debut Fiction. Mr. Vestal earned the honor for “Godforsaken Idaho,” a collection of short stories. He received the prize from Louise Erdrich at a ceremony at the New School.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shawn Vestal Wins PEN/Robert W. Bingham Prize', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vestal, Shawn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PEN American Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-30T00:45:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b9f9a18-6d45-51db-95ae-48dd6cd1cfd4', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b9f9a18-6d45-51db-95ae-48dd6cd1cfd4'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration announced a plan to help reduce the overuse of antibiotics, but there are many details still to be filled in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/30/opinion/a-new-attack-on-antibiotic-resistance.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration announced a plan to help reduce the overuse of antibiotics, but there are many details still to be filled in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Antibiotic-resistant germs are an increasing threat, causing at least 23,000 deaths and two million illnesses in the United States each year, and requiring treatment costing $20 billion in direct medical expenses. The Obama administration announced some good measures this month that should help reduce the overuse of antibiotics in humans and much, though perhaps not all, of the overuse in animal husbandry that together are fueling the emergence of drug-resistant germs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Attack on Antibiotic Resistance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Attack on Antibiotic Resistance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Livestock', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factory Farming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 10, 'major'