n a different light. | EBay to spin off PayPal. | The dangers of fighting bad press. | A.I.G. trial begins in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/09/30/morning-agenda-lehman-revisited/', 'snippet': 'New accounts of events from 2008 are casting Lehman’s collapse in a different light. | EBay to spin off PayPal. | The dangers of fighting bad press. | A.I.G. trial begins in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Could Lehman Brothers have been saved? Government officials have argued that the Federal Reserve did not have the legal authority to rescue the big investment bank, leaving it instead to die overnight. Now, new accounts of events from 2008 are casting the firm’s collapse in a different light, James B. Stewart and Peter Eavis write in The New York Times. The decision not to rescue Lehman, in hindsight, let problems at one bank snowball into a full-blown panic. Why, given all that happened, was Lehman the only bank that was not too big to fail?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Lehman Revisited', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-09-30T12:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abb639f3-8400-5ee8-94ac-be7721795a27', 'word_count': 2209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abb639f3-8400-5ee8-94ac-be7721795a27'}, {'abstract': 'Federal agencies and private businesses and institutions are aligning their research with the Brain Initiative, which is studying the brain in action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/30/us/more-groups-join-project-on-the-brain.html', 'snippet': 'Federal agencies and private businesses and institutions are aligning their research with the Brain Initiative, which is studying the brain in action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration plans to announce Tuesday that it has recruited new federal agencies and a number of universities, foundations and businesses to help pursue the goals of the Brain Initiative, which the president started in 2013.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Groups Join Project on the Brain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Groups Join Project on the Brain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brain Initiative/Activity Map Project (US Health and Human Services)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-30T12:50:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abb8240c-0458-5dec-914f-cd66e97ae34d', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abb8240c-0458-5dec-914f-cd66e97ae34d'}, {'abstract': 'A new poll finds support for Internal Revenue Service efforts to regulate the activities of nonprofit groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/09/30/irs-political-groups-regulation-poll/', 'snippet': 'A new poll finds support for Internal Revenue Service efforts to regulate the activities of nonprofit groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Internal Revenue Service proposed new rules earlier this year to rein in political activity by nonprofits, it caused an unusual meeting of the minds between the right and the left in opposition to the proposal, which was eventually withdrawn by the agency.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Support Strong for Regulating Politics and Nonprofits', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hudson Institute', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Citizen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-30T12:53:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/311aa143-6950-57e4-869e-638e4bca5d33', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/311aa143-6950-57e4-869e-638e4bca5d33'}, {'abstract': 'Siri Hustvedt, Dinaw Mengestu, Roz Chast and Thomas Piketty are among the finalists for the first annual awards.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/09/30/kirkus-announces-finalists-for-book-prizes/', 'snippet': 'Siri Hustvedt, Dinaw Mengestu, Roz Chast and Thomas Piketty are among the finalists for the first annual awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The literary journ