old of professional careers into potential leaders and entrepreneurs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dallas Symphony Orchestra, in a partnership with the University of Texas at Dallas and several conservatories around the world, is starting an unusual program meant to turn music students on the threshold of professional careers into potential leaders and entrepreneurs in the music world. The D.S.O./Jaap van Zweden Scholars Program, as the enterprise is called, is named for the orchestra’s music director and is supported by a $10 million gift from Margaret McDermott, who also endows a scholar’s fund at the university.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dallas Symphony Aims to Develop Musical Leadership', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-09-30T18:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/678a549b-a398-5dab-bbf1-1848831adf5f', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/678a549b-a398-5dab-bbf1-1848831adf5f'}, {'abstract': 'Chrysler says it will double production of the Ram 1500 EcoDiesel pickup; Cadillac’s chief says production may decline to combat swollen inventory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/10/01/automobiles/wheelies-the-diesel-ram-edition.html', 'snippet': 'Chrysler says it will double production of the Ram 1500 EcoDiesel pickup; Cadillac’s chief says production may decline to combat swollen inventory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A roundup 